// The long texts of feats.js (same order), read after it. Built by tools/split_text.py; same licence as feats.js.
(function (r) { var P = r.SF2DATA = r.SF2DATA || {}, T = [["You have a keen interest in the origins of your people. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Crafting and Thievery. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Android Lore."],["You know sometimes a good tune is the best way to start a brawl. When you roll Performance for initiative, you grant yourself and all allies who can hear you a +1 status bonus to their initiative rolls and to saves against emotion effects during the first round of the encounter. You gain the Impressive Performance skill feat.\n\nCue the Music"],["Your inhibited or malfunctioning emotional processors make it difficult for you to feel strong emotions. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against emotion effects. If you roll a success on a saving throw against an emotion effect, you get a critical success instead."],["Your plates are reinforced even further, your soul hardening with it. Your Hellforged Armor is considered heavy armor instead of medium armor, its Strength requirement increases to +4, its item bonus to AC increases by 1, and it gains the bulwark trait."],["You appear not as an android, but a traditional organic creature. You become trained in Deception and gain a +2 circumstance bonus to checks to Impersonate living creatures as your biotech changes your body's shape or texture as part of the disguise. Creatures recognize you as a Biotech Android only if they succeed at a Perception check against your Deception DC, and you don't have to attempt a Deception check to interact with someone to conceal the fact that you're a biotech android; a check happens only if someone else tries to uncover your heritage."],["You retain instincts and fragmentary memories from the androids who previously occupied your body or from ancient programming embedded in your system. During your daily preparations, you can tap into these archived memories to become trained in one skill of your choice. This proficiency lasts until you prepare again. Since this proficiency is temporary, you can't use it as a prerequisite for a skill increase or a permanent character option like a feat."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou can use your nanites to create the perfect tool for a job. Outside of combat, you can have your nanites form a toolkit of a level no higher than half your level (minimum 0). The item lasts for 1 minute. Because your nanites must be actively working to provide the tool, you can't use other feats that require the use of your nanites while you're using them as a tool."],["You can quickly identify your surroundings, and you can use that information to your advantage while in the midst of danger or while in the process of piloting vehicles in hazardous situations. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Perception checks for initiative rolls and a +2 circumstance bonus to Piloting checks for initiative rolls."],["You don't just hum with dim light, you exude a burst of it. When you use Nanite Surge, you can choose to have your circuitry exude bright light in a 10-foot emanation and dim light 10 feet beyond that for 1 round. Creatures that start their turn in the area of your bright light must attempt a Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. On a failure, a creature is Dazzled for 1 round (or Blinded for 1 round and dazzled for 1 minute on a critical failure). A creature can spend a single Interact action to rub its eyes to remove the blinded condition.\n\nBursting Surge"],["You can cast Speak with Computers once per day as a 4th-rank arcane innate spell."],["*Helldrives* are unique tools of the hellforged, but your unique hardware means you can replicate the effects of a tool most adventurers rarely ever see: a *Helldrive*. You can spend a single Interact action to connect yourself to a starship. While you're connected, you gain +1 circumstance bonus to Piloting checks and can grant this circumstance bonus to the pilot of the vessel as well by spending a single action with the concentrate trait. Once per day, you can give a starship you're connected to the ability to travel long distances in space as if it had a Drift Engine.\n\nUnauthorized Helldriver"],["You refuse to surrender your autonomy and have erected mental bulwarks and technological protocols to safeguard your mind and memories. Whenever you attempt a Will save against a spell or effect that would give you the Confused or Controlled condition, roll that save twice and use the higher result (this is a fortune effect). If you would start your turn confused or controlled, you can immediately attempt a DC 5 flat check. On a success, you fight that mental control, becoming Paralyzed until the end of your turn rather than acting against your will. If you roll a 20 on this flat check, you immediately end the confused or controlled condition."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou change into a swarm of nanites for up to 1 minute or until you spend a single action to return to your normal shape. You become Huge, gain the swarm trait, and gain a fly Speed of 40 feet. As a swarm, you have the following characteristics.\n\n- You're immune to the Grabbed, Prone, and Restrained conditions.\n- You have weakness 5 to area and splash damage.\n- You can occupy the same space as other creatures and must do so to use your damaging ability.\n- As a 2-action activity, you can deal 10d6 acid damage to all creatures sharing your space (basic Reflex save with a DC equal to your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher).\n- You can't speak, Cast Spells, use manipulate actions requiring your hands, Activate magic items, or make any Strikes with your normal body.\n- You don't gain the swarm mind ability, so you're still affected normally by mental effects."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYour core pierces into the void and creates a black hole that tears apart the souls of everyone around you. All creatures within a 10-foot emanation take 8d6 void damage with a basic Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. A creature that fails this save is also pulled 5 feet toward you (or pulled 10 feet toward you and knocked Prone on a critical failure). For 1 minute, any creature that ends its turn within a 10-foot emanation around you takes 5d6 void damage (basic Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC).\n\nIf you aren't glitching, you can choose to become Glitching 1 when you use Synthesized Black Hole to increase the radius of the emanation from 10 feet to 30 feet. You can't reduce your glitching value for as long as Synthesized Black Hole is in effect, but you can Dismiss the effect."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou push your circuitry to its physical limits, maximizing your physical and mental capabilities. You become Quickened and Glitching 1 for 1 minute. You can use your extra action only to Stride or Strike. While quickened in this way, you gain a +2 status bonus to your AC, attack rolls, and saving throws. You can't reduce your glitching value until you lose the quickened condition."],["You can tap into your biotech's generative nature to don a new face or persona and better adapt to your surroundings. You physically modify your features to another creature of the same size category as yourself. Using Bionanite Skin counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception, and you gain a +2 status bonus to checks to Impersonate to pretend you're this other creature. You remain in this shape indefinitely and can shift into another shape by using this action again."],["You were created to fight other synthetic creatures. When you roll a critical hit against a creature with the tech trait, the target becomes glitching 1."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou can use your nanites to repair objects. You touch a common tech item with a level up to your level with the Broken or Glitching condition. It loses the broken condition until the end of your turn, allowing you to use the item as normal. You also reduce the glitching value of the item you touch by 1."],["You can internalize a large amount of information when connected to the infosphere. When you successfully Access Infosphere about a specific organization, culture, or region, you can adopt facets of the culture you researched into your personality unit to mimic their habits and sensibilities. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Charisma-based skill checks against creatures related to the culture for 1 hour after you Access Infosphere. You can only adopt the facets for one group of creatures at a time, and if you adopt facets from a new group, the effects of a previous one immediately end.\n\nCultural Consumption"],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou spin up your musical instruments to drop the bass and pick up the pace. All allies within 30 feet who can perceive you can Step, Stride up to half their speed, or Take Cover as a reaction."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou trigger your body's self-repair programming, stimulating your body's nanites to heal your wounds. You gain fast healing equal to half your level for 1 minute. While Repair Module is active, if you use Nanite Surge or Nanite Form, this fast healing ends."],["You've learned to channel your void inversion into another creature. You gain Void Seed as a 2nd-rank occult innate spell that you can cast once every 10 minutes."],["Choose an ancestry or heritage. You learn a new language available to that ancestry or heritage. You become trained in Society. If you're already trained in Society, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You also become trained in the Lore skill related to that specific ancestry or heritage, such as Android Lore or Ysoki Lore.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times, choosing a different ancestry or heritage each time."],["Your time spent in another skin has allowed you to shape your own body into a weapon. You gain a feat associated with a chosen ancestry or heritage that grants an unarmed attack. You can select ancestry feats that include that feat as a prerequisite as if you were a member of that ancestry or heritage. You can use the unarmed attack only when you're transformed into a member of that ancestry.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times, choosing a different ancestry or feat each time."],["You've learned how to use the traditional weapons of another ancestry. You gain the weapon familiarity feat associated with a chosen ancestry or heritage, even if you are not a member of that ancestry or heritage. You can select ancestry feats that include that feat as a prerequisite as if you were a member of that ancestry or heritage. You must meet all feats' prerequisites when chosen other than the ancestry or heritage.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times, choosing a different ancestry or feat each time."],["You can use Change Shape to transform into a specific individual. As long as you have studied the individual for at least 10 minutes, creatures you do not interact with will not suspect your disguise unless your behavior is markedly different, or the creature has an intimate familiarity with the individual."],["You emit the reeking smell of rotting meat when you disgorge your stomach. While you can thoroughly mask the scent by shapeshifting to eat like other species, disgorging your stomach to intentionally emit this vile odor can come in handy when you are trying to dissuade predators, whether they are hungry beasts or murderous mobsters. You become trained in Deception and gain the Lengthy Diversion skill feat as a bonus feat, even if you don't meet its prerequisites."],["**Trigger** You roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou can change at a moment's notice. You Change Shape and gain a +2 circumstance bonus on the triggering initiative roll if you used Deception to roll initiative."],["**Frequency** once per minute\n\n**Trigger** You use Change Shape.\n\n---\n\nYou renew and reinforce your body with elements of your new form. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to half your level (minimum 1) that last until the end of your next turn."],["You are a master at spotting other people in disguise. When you come within 10 feet of a creature that is disguised, transformed, or Impersonating a specific creature, the GM rolls a secret Perception check for you to realize that the creature is disguised, even if you didn't spend an action to Seek against that creature."],["Your malleable body makes it easier for you to reposition and rebalance yourself. Once every 10 minutes, when you Change Shape, you can gain the effects of the Reorient cantrip."],["You can easily contort and resize your limbs to squeeze into smaller spaces. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Acrobatics. If you are already trained in Acrobatics (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain the Quick Squeeze feat."],["When you Change Shape, you can Conceal an Object inside a cavity in your body or Interact to grab an object stored inside your body. You can store up to four items of light Bulk or less if you are Large, three items of light Bulk or less if you are Medium, or two items of light Bulk or less if you are Small. If you Change Shape into a smaller-sized body, the excess items fall to the ground in your square. None of these items can have a dimension longer than 1 foot."],["You Change Shape to sprout hundreds of suction cups across your limbs. You gain a 15-foot climb Speed as long as you're wearing light armor or no armor."],["You can Demoralize those around you by shifting your muscular and skeletal systems around. When you do, Demoralize loses the auditory trait and gains the visual trait, and you don't take a penalty if the creature doesn't understand your language."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou force your body to produce an excess of powerful corrosive digestive enzymes that you can use to spray in a 30-foot cone, dealing 7d6 acid damage (basic Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC). A creature that gets a critical failure on this Reflex save is also Sickened 1."],["You can flatten your body completely to avoid getting hurt. Change Shape and Drop Prone to Take Cover by hunkering down. You can Hide and Sneak due to the greater cover and don't lose the benefits of Take Cover when you Sneak."],["You've studied certain creatures enough that you can transform into them. If you are a master in a Lore skill that can be used to identify a category of creatures, you can use Change Shape to transform your appearance to that of a Small or Medium creature of that category."],["You rapidly shift the colors of your skin to throw off the senses of those around you. Attempt a Deception check against the Perception DCs of all creatures within melee reach. On a success, the creature becomes Clumsy 1 until the end of your turn (Clumsy 2 on a critical success). Regardless of the result of your check, each creature is then temporarily immune to Prismatic Display for 10 minutes."],["You've learned to grow additional eyes all over your body, enhancing your visual processing and the range of your eyesight. When you use Change Shape, you can choose to gain all-around vision until you change forms again. During this time, you take a –3 circumstance penalty to Deception checks and Deception DCs to Impersonate a different ancestry, unless the ancestry you are Impersonating normally has seven or more eyes."],["You can stretch your body into long tentacular limbs to strike enemies from further away. For 1 minute, increase your reach when you're delivering touch range spells and making unarmed Strikes to 10 feet. This doesn't change the reach of your melee weapon attacks."],["You can take the form of a terrifying aberration. When you Change Shape, you can choose one of the following: gain the effects of a 4th-rank Enlarge spell and 6th-rank Eldritch Bond spell; gain the effects of a 2nd-rank enlarge spell and 6th-rank eldritch bond spell granting three abilities; or gain the effects of a 6th-rank eldritch bond spell granting four abilities. This effect lasts for 1 minute or until you shift back, whichever comes first."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYour body can repair damaged cells and even regrow missing limbs. You gain regeneration equal to half your level for 1 minute. During this time, you can't die from damage and your dying condition can't increase to a value that would kill you, though if your Wounded value becomes 4 or higher, you stay Unconscious until your wounds are treated. Each time you regain Hit Points from regeneration, you also regrow one damaged or ruined organ (if any), and you can reattach severed body parts by spending an Interact action to hold the body part to the area it was severed from."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou can use Change Shape to split two of your identities into two different bodies, each using a unique form and identity. Each copy Strides to an unoccupied square. Both you and your copy act on your turn and use the same pool of actions, the same multiple attack penalty, and the same pool of Hit Points, but if both forms take damage from the same effect, such as from an attack or spell with area damage, you apply the damage only once. In the case of an effect with a save that affects both forms, you take the worse result and apply it to both forms. When this effect ends, you choose one of the two forms as your actual form and the other version of you Strides once toward you before becoming an arm that melds with your body as soon as it occupies the same square as you. If you can't retrieve your arm, you lose the ability to Change Shape into that copy's form and lose the use of that limb until it regrows in 1 week. This effect automatically ends if you are reduced to 0 Hit Points, if you occupy the same square as your copy, or after 1 minute."],["**Frequency** once per minute\n\n**Trigger** You're targeted by a mental effect.\n\n---\n\nYou can shield your consciousness by blocking one of your neural networks from the others, cutting yourself off from the identity until it's safe. You Change Shape and become immune to the triggering mental effect. You are no longer immune and the mental effect continues to affect you if you Change Shape into any form that shares an ancestry with that form before the duration of the mental effect expires."],["You have enough practice with your natural form that you can utilize more of your limbs than usual. You have six arms, which allows you to wield and hold up to six hands' worth of weapons and equipment. If you use more than four of these arms, your land Speed becomes 5 feet. At any time, one pair of hands is designated your active hands. You can change this designation from one pair of hands to another by taking the Switch Hands action, which is a single action. You can only perform actions with your active hands. This feat allows you to use up to six arms when you use Change Shape to take a form with multiple arms, such as a kasatha or skittermander."],["Once per day, when you Change Shape, you can instead gain the effects of Animal Form, heightened to half your level rounded up, for 1 minute or until you shift back, whichever comes first."],["The malleable nature of your body dulls the impact of physical ailments. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against diseases, poisons, and radiation. If you roll a success on a saving throw against one of these effects, you get a critical success instead."],["You disgorge your stomach out of your mouth in a disturbing display of your aberrant heritage. Attempt a single Intimidation check to Demoralize each enemy within 30 feet. Regardless of the results of your check, each creature is then temporarily immune to Frightening Display for 1 minute."],["**Trigger** You become Grabbed or Restrained by another creature or you grab or restrain another creature.\n\n**Requirements** You can use Change Shape to assume the appearance of that creature.\n\n---\n\nYou Change Shape to assume the appearance of the other creature. All other creatures must use the Seek action to attempt a Perception check against your Deception DC to determine which creature is real and which is an imitation. A creature who doesn't know which creature you are must succeed at a DC 11 flat check when targeting either of you with an attack, spell, or other effect. If the check fails, the attack, spell, or effect targets the other creature instead.\n\nAbilities such as telepathy or the mystic's group chat feature may automatically allow a creature to determine which creature is which, but an aware creature must still use the Point Out action to indicate to others which creature is which. An imitated creature might have a signal or phrase that indicates to their allies which creature is which, but doing so in the din of battle is an action with the auditory or visual trait."],["You suddenly change your appearance to create an opening for your next attack. Change Shape and Feint. You gain a circumstance bonus to your Deception check to Feint equal to the number of steps between your sizes when you Change Shape (+1 if you are one size smaller or larger, +2 if you are two sizes smaller or larger, and so on). Regardless of the results of your check, each creature who observes you Change Shape is temporarily immune to Shifter's Feint for 1 minute."],["You use the explosive momentum of shifting to help push a creature away from you. Change Shape into a larger size and Shove. You gain a circumstance bonus to your Athletics check to Shove equal to the number of steps between your sizes when you Change Shape (+1 if you are one size larger, +2 if you are two sizes larger, and so on)."],["**Trigger** A creature targets you with an attack.\n\n**Requirements** You are aware of the attack and are not Off-Guard to the triggering attack.\n\n---\n\nYou quickly Change Shape into a smaller size to avoid getting hit. You gain a circumstance bonus to AC, Fortitude DC, and Reflex DC against the triggering attack equal to the number of steps between your sizes when you Change Shape (+1 if you are one size smaller, +2 if you are two sizes smaller, and so on)."],["Each of your forms has unusually thick skin. Your DC on flat checks to end persistent bleed damage is reduced from 15 to 10, or from 10 to 5 after receiving especially appropriate assistance.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can use the Restorative Shapeshifting feat to attempt an additional flat check to end persistent bleed damage, but this is not considered especially appropriate assistance."],["You can wriggle your way around tight spaces without much difficulty, making it hard for others to pin you down. You can ignore difficult terrain caused by moving through tight spaces that aren't tight enough to force you to Squeeze. If you roll a success to Squeeze, you get a critical success instead. Ignore any penalties to Speeds conferred by the suppressed condition."],["You shift the color and texture of your skin to match your surroundings. You Change Shape, but instead of taking on the form of another creature, you blend in with your environment. As long as an observer is at least 20 feet away from you, you don't need cover from that observer to Hide or Sneak. This lasts as long as you stay in your new form or until you move to an area with substantially different terrain."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou speed up your body's metabolism and respiration by changing yourself at a cellular level. You become Quickened for 1 minute and can use the extra action each round only for Strike and Stride actions."],["Contorting your limbs as though you were transforming allows you to fit through tight spaces. You can move at full Speed while Squeezing."],["You disgorge your stomach to attack your opponents with powerful enzymes. You gain a stomach unarmed attack that deals 1d8 acid damage damage, has the analog and unwieldy traits, and is in the corrosive weapon group."],["Even if you are forced to reveal your natural appearance, you have an additional layer of security in the form of a backup shapeshifting identity. Choose one form during your daily preparations. Waving away your ability to transform as some unrelated magic or technology, you gain a +3 circumstance bonus to Deception checks to Lie that the chosen form is your true form. You can tell lies that protect your identity even against magical spells, and effects like truesight reveal the chosen form as your true form. You revert to this form if you become the target of a spell or effect that causes you to unwillingly shift back to your true form."],["You can adjust your body's size and shape to take advantage of obstacles on the battlefield. Change Shape into a Small-sized form and Take Cover; you can Take Cover to gain standard cover if you would have lesser cover from a creature after you Change Shape; if you would have standard cover from a creature, you gain greater cover instead."],["You exemplify the favored studies of the atraxids. You become trained in Crafting and Thievery. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills, you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Atraxid Lore."],["You benefit from having extra legs, as anyone trying to trip you quickly learns. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Fortitude DC to avoid being Tripped, and you gain the Multi-Legged Recovery reaction."],["You might have three left feet, but you also have three right feet. You have spent years perfecting traditional atraxid dancing. You become trained in Performance. You gain the Impressive Performance feat. When you attempt a Performance check to [[/act make-an-impression]] on a creature with more than two legs or hands, if you roll a critical failure, you get a failure instead."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** An ally within 30 feet becomes frightened.\n\n---\n\nYou'll never quite understand why non-atraxids find your appearance unsettling, but at this point you're used to it. You're adept at using subtle body language to keep others calm, which comes in handy when your friends are frightened due to any source. The value of your ally's frightened condition is reduced by 1."],["You have trained in numerous areas of crafting, learning how many different kinds of useful items are put together. You are trained in Crafting. You gain the Specialty Crafting feat, and you can choose two specialties from the list instead of one."],["Like many atraxids, you have spent a great deal of time building and repairing starships. You can Recall Knowledge about starships using Crafting instead of Piloting. When you critically fail a Crafting check to Recall Knowledge about starships, you get a failure instead."],["You have studied szandite crystals extensively, and you can tap into their power. You gain the Additional Lore general feat for Szandite Lore. By focusing for 1 minute, you know the direction and approximate distance to the nearest szandite crystal within 500 feet."],["**Frequency** once per minute You create a silk balloon that allows you to fly a short distance.\n\n---\n\nYou Fly up to 35 feet. If you aren't on solid ground at the end of this movement, you fall."],["You are a highly skilled crafter, and you can make larger batches than normal in the same time. When you Craft consumables or ammunition, you increase the quantity that you can craft at one time by one half; for example, you can make six of a given consumable at a time instead of four. You must still pay the costs for the raw materials of the additional items."],["You have spent so much time learning about how things work that you have also learned how to break them in the most efficient manner possible. You can cast Overload Systems as a 5th-rank arcane innate spell once per day."],["You have a great deal of experience with a wide variety of people and languages, and you can pass your skills along to others. You can cast Translate as a 2nd-rank arcane innate spell at will."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You fail or critically fail a saving throw or skill check at the same time that an ally within 30 feet succeeds or critically succeeds at the same save or check.\n\n---\n\nYou, like many atraxids, are highly competitive, and you can't stand to see one of your friends succeeding while you are failing. Reroll the triggering check, but you must use the new result, even if it's worse."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nWhile your fangs aren't suitable for biting, you still produce a dangerous venom. You spit your venom onto a melee weapon or into the magazine of a ranged weapon you're holding. Your next Strike or use of Auto-Fire with the chosen weapon until the start of your next turn that deals bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage also deals an additional 1d6 poison damage.\n\nAtraxid Venom"],["You have spent substantial time around the other peoples of the Szandite Collective, and you know their cultures as well as that of atraxids. Select binnaquid, fonqugon, hardor, mecanaic, ord, or phasorq. You can select ancestry feats from the chosen ancestry, in addition to your character's own ancestries, as long as the ancestry feats don't require any physiological feature that you lack, as determined by the GM. When you select this feat, you additionally gain one 1st-level ancestry feat from your chosen ancestry."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** A creature fails a saving throw against your spell or other ability.\n\n---\n\nYou are quite competitive and rub it in that your enemy failed. That enemy takes a –1 circumstance penalty to their next saving throw, skill check, or attack roll made before the end of their next turn.\n\nRub It In"],["You have an eye for the ideal jewelry needed for any occasion. In 10 minutes, you can craft the perfect accessories for one creature for one social event. The accessories confer a +2 item bonus to Diplomacy checks to [[/act make-an-impression]] at that event. A creature can only have one set of accessories per day, and they go out of style after 24 hours and can no longer be used. The accessories have negligible monetary value.\n\nAtraxid Jewelry"],["You can reach even the highest levels of atraxid cities in no time. Your climb Speed increases to 30 feet."],["You have experimented with mind-altering substances enough that drugs and poisons of all kinds have a harder time affecting you. You gain poison resistance equal to half your level."],["You have spent so much time in zero-g that you can control your own personal gravity. You gain Personal Gravity as a 3rd-rank primal innate spell that you can cast once per day."],["You quickly shout a mind-bending brainteaser at one creature within 30 feet. That creature must attempt a Will saving throw against your choice of your Deception or your Crafting. Regardless of the result, the creature is then temporarily immune to your Puzzling Outburst for 24 hours.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature figures out your riddle so fast that your ego is bruised. You cannot use Puzzling Outburst for 10 minutes.\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature is stumped and becomes Stupefied 1 for one minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is completely stumped by your riddle and is Stupefied 2 for one minute."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You fail, but do not critically fail, a skill check with the chosen skill.\n\n---\n\nYou have worked hard to become one of the greatest talents in a particular area, and your reputation simply wouldn't stand if you were seen failing. When you select this feat, choose a skill that you're a master in. You can reroll the triggering check, but you must use the new result, even if it's worse.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once, choosing a different skill each time. You can What, Me, Fail? once per hour for each skill you've chosen."],["You cruise around your adversaries at top speed.\n\nYou become trained in Acrobatics. If you would automatically become trained in Acrobatics (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You can [[/act tumble-through]] any number of enemies, not just one. Your movement ends only when you critically fail an Acrobatics check to Tumble Through an enemy's space (or when you lack the Speed to move all the way through its space). You still trigger reactions on a failure to Tumble Through."],["Your jeweled orb has a lattice to process magic that can automatically troubleshoot and correct calculations in magical formulas to prevent mishaps when using unfamiliar magic.\n\nYou become trained in a skill matching the tradition of the innate spell you gained with the jeweled orb bantrid heritage. The relevant skills are Arcana for arcane, Nature for primal, Occultism for occult, or Religion for divine. If you were already trained in the relevant skill, you become trained in another one of those skills. You gain the Trick Magic Item skill feat."],["Your magnetic foot orb picks up loose metal objects that you can retrieve later. Whenever you leave a square, you can pick up one unattended object of 1 Bulk or less that is mostly made out of metal with your foot orb. Your foot orb can hold 4 Bulk of items, and the first 2 Bulk of these items don't count against your Bulk limits. These items are considered stowed and must be drawn in order to be used."],["You've lived your life chasing the thrill of high speeds, so driving fast vehicles was a natural fit. You become trained in Piloting. If you are already trained in Piloting, you become trained in a Lore skill related to vehicles, such as Gambling Lore, Starship Lore, Travel Lore, or Vehicle Lore. You gain the Express Driver skill feat."],["Nothing will stop you from moving forward. Each time you use an action with the move trait, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to saves against effects that would impose the Fatigued, Immobilized, Paralyzed, Slowed, or Suppressed conditions until the end of your next turn. When you would be fatigued, immobilized, paralyzed, slowed, or suppressed for at least 2 rounds, reduce that duration by 1 round."],["You might not remember your past, but some part of you has an innate understanding of the basic layout and user interfaces of ancient pre-Gap technology. You become trained in your choice of Computers or Crafting. If you're already trained in both, you instead become trained in a Lore skill related to technology. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Recall Knowledge checks using Computers, Crafting, or Piloting to identify ancient technology designed before the Gap."],["You've made your foot orb into a living work of couture art, becoming what young bantrids often call a baller. Whether you've incorporated it into stunning performances as a diva or use it to impress others who might not have even encountered a bantrid before, people can't help but admire your taste and style.\n\nYou either become trained in Diplomacy and gain the Group Impression skill feat, or you become trained in Performance and gain the Impressive Performance skill feat. If you're already trained in one of these skills, you must take the other one and can choose from either skill feat. If you're trained in both skills, you become trained in a different skill of your choice instead and can choose from either skill feat."],["**Requirements** You have at least one hand free.\n\n---\n\nWhile you're unable to accelerate as quickly as most vehicles, you can keep up with them by hanging onto them. Attempt an Acrobatics or Athletics check with a DC equal to the vehicle's AC. On a success, you hang onto that vehicle and remain adjacent to the vehicle as it moves, and you can Board the vehicle without an additional check. You can let go of the vehicle at any point without spending an action; if you do, you gain a circumstance bonus to your land Speed equal to the vehicle's Speed until the end of your next turn. Each time you move farther than your land Speed without this bonus, you must succeed at a Fortitude saving throw or lose control and move in a straight line up to your land Speed."],["Inspired by the anatomy of other species in the Pact Worlds, you've augmented yourself with humanoid arms, whether cybernetic or biotech, that would put even world-class bodybuilders to shame.\n\nYou gain a second pair of arms. At any time, one pair of hands is designated as your active hands. You can take the Switch Hands action to change your active hands. Add the All Hands on Deck and Double Draw ancestry feats to your list of standardized ancestry feats."],["You become a blur when you push yourself to move as fast as you can. When you Stride while Quickened from Need for Speed, you gain Concealment until the start of your next turn. As usual for concealment involving an obvious visual manifestation, you can't use this concealment to Hide or Sneak."],["**Requirements** You have at least one hand free.\n\n---\n\nYou swoop down, use your strong cilia to grab your friend, and fly them off to safety. Fly twice. At any point during this movement, you can [[/act grapple]] one willing ally within reach. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Athletics check to Grapple your ally if you have two free hands or they have a free hand and are aware of you. The Grabbed condition ends once you have completed your movement."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** You would become Fatigued, Immobilized, Paralyzed, Slowed, or Suppressed.\n\n---\n\nYou refuse to stop moving, pushing yourself beyond effects that would stop most creatures. You delay the effects of the triggering condition until the end of your next turn. Each time you use a move action while the condition is being delayed, you continue to delay the condition an additional round, up to 6 rounds. If the condition has a duration, the duration begins to elapse only after the delay. You can't further delay or prevent the condition after this ability ends."],["Your foot orb has become a reflection of all of creation, allowing you to zoom in and project scenes from across the cosmos upon its crystalline surface. You can cast Scrying twice per day as a 6th-rank innate spell of the same tradition as the cantrip chosen for your jeweled orb bantrid heritage. Any visual information you receive through *scrying* this way appears within your foot orb, and any auditory information is emitted as sound out from the surface of your foot orb."],["Even the natural limitations of your own biology won't get between you and your need for speed! You can use Need for Speed once per hour, rather than once per day."],["You weave and veer between the legs of your enemies, causing them to fall over as you race across the battlefield. Stride twice, each in a straight line. You can move through the spaces of creatures that are at least one size larger than you, attempting to [[/act trip]] each creature whose space you enter. All attacks count toward your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until after you've made all of them. You can attempt to Trip the same creature only once in a single Underfoot Stampede!"],["By landing your foot orb directly on the ground, you can use your momentum to bounce yourself forward. If you land on the ground at the end of a jump (whether performing a [[/act high-jump]], [[/act long-jump]], or Leap), you can use High Jump or Long Jump as a single action, but you don't get to Stride as part of the activity.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Quick Jump skill feat, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Athletics check for your second High Jump or Long Jump."],["You position yourself to rapidly spin your foot orb without moving, kicking up a thick plume of dust. Until the end of your next turn, any creature in your square (including yourself) becomes Concealed, though they can't use this concealment to [[/act hide]] or [[/act sneak]], as normal for concealment where your position is still obvious. If you are in a sterile environment without significant dirt or dust on the floor, you have to instead rely on a reserve of detritus stored in your cilia. You cannot use this action again for 10 minutes, or until you Step or Stride into a dirty square."],["By quickly reversing the polarity on a portion of your magnetic foot orb, you can launch items attached to you at your enemies. You gain a magnetic projectile unarmed attack in the sling weapon group with a range increment of 30 feet that deals 1d4 bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage—as appropriate for the object you hurled. You must have a metallic object of at least light Bulk attached to your foot orb as ammunition for this attack, but no specific traits or magic properties of the thrown item affect the attack or the damage."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You would become Clumsy, Enfeebled, Slowed, or Suppressed.\n\n---\n\nFaced with helplessness, you channel your restlessness into a relentless desire to always move faster even when you are feeling sluggish. You gain a +20-foot status bonus to all your Speeds for 1 round."],["The slopes and roads of Hibb are kept in phenomenal condition, and you've mastered the bantrids' method for cleaning the roads for one another. You Stride. You clear through any squares of non-magical difficult terrain (but not greater difficult terrain) in which the source of the terrain could be crushed, such as dense undergrowth, or swept aside, such as debris or rubble."],["Your above-average control over your foot orb offers you the extra spin you need to coast effortlessly. When you Step, you can move 10 feet instead of 5. This enables you to Step into and within difficult terrain as long as you can meet the extra movement cost."],["Whether you adjusted your diet or used augmentations, you've adapted your foot orb to take on special qualities without compromising the integrity and utility of your original body. You gain the mechanical benefits of the Bouncy Orb, Jeweled Orb, Magnetic Orb, or Hollow Orb bantrid heritage. This does not allow you to take feats or gain any benefits that require a specific bantrid heritage."],["By quickly spinning your magnetic orb while channeling primal energy through it, you can create a tether of electricity that can pull objects and creatures across the battlefield, including yourself.\n\nYou can cast Electrotether as a 3rd-rank primal innate spell twice per day, but the target becomes \"one creature, unattended object, or metal structure.\"\n\nIf you target an unattended object, you immediately pull the object into your square and can grab the item if you have a free hand. If you target a metal surface, such as the side of a starship or building, you are immediately moved to the structure (this movement doesn't trigger reactions based on movement) and [[/act climb]]."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou're always spinning your wheel, and you can strain your body and mind to push yourself beyond your normal limits. You become Quickened for 4 rounds. You can use the extra action each round only to Stride."],["You can slowly inject a serum or *spell ampoule* into your foot orb as a 1-minute activity, storing it to be absorbed by your body later. You can have only one serum or *spell ampoule* in your body at a time. You can activate and consume the absorbed fluid by squeezing your orb with your cilia without needing a free hand. An injected serum or *spell ampoule* left in your foot orb is gradually absorbed by your body and is consumed without any effect after 24 hours."],["You grow sturdy lower limbs that allow you to walk on land. Increase your Speed to 20 feet. Additionally, you gain the Adaptive Locomotion action."],["You've learned how to wield nearly any weapon effectively while underwater. You don't take the –2 penalty for making melee slashing or bludgeoning Strikes while underwater. Your ranged attacks aren't affected by being underwater. You can use weapons that deal fire damage underwater."],["From your upbringing, you've learned the ways of your people while also seeking to expand your own mind in the fields of creation. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Crafting and Medicine. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Barathu Lore."],["You've explored the darkest regions of space and found ways to adapt. You gain darkvision."],["Spiky protrusions jut from your body, which you can use to wound your attackers. Your Fortitude DC against Athletics checks to Grapple or Shove you increases by 1. Additionally, you gain the Piercing Spikes reaction."],["Your extensive database of knowledge and experiences enables you to readily break codes and crack passwords. You become trained in Computers and can use Computers to [[/act decipher-writing skill=computers]]. You gain the Digital Ambassador skill feat and can successfully communicate using the feat with a DC 12 flat check (DC 8 if you're legendary in Society or Computers)."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou can Stride and move through spaces of any creatures in your path. Any creature your size or smaller whose space you move through can attempt a Reflex save against your Athletics DC to avoid being engulfed. A creature unable to act automatically critically fails this save. If a creature succeeds at its save, it can choose to either be pushed aside or pushed in front of you at the end of your movement. You can only attempt to Gooey Engulf the same creature once per turn. You can contain as many creatures as can fit in your space.\n\nA creature that fails its save is pulled into your body. It is Grabbed and Slowed 1, and it must hold its breath or start suffocating. The creature takes 1d6 acid damage at the end of each of its turns while engulfed (this damage can be improved by hardlight handwraps as though it were an unarmed attack). An engulfed creature can get free by [[/act escape dc=athletics]]{Escaping} against your Athletics DC. An engulfed creature can attack you but only with an unarmed attack or weapons of light Bulk or less. You're Off-Guard against these attacks. If you take piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding one fourth of your remaining Hit Points from a single attack or spell, the engulfed creature cuts itself free. A creature that gets free by either method can immediately breathe and exits your space. If you fall asleep, are knocked Unconscious, or die, all creatures you've engulfed are automatically released."],["You've adapted more of your tendrils and limbs with complex musculature and cellular structures, improving articulation and fine motor skills. Increase your number of arms by two. At any time, one pair of your hands is designated as your active hands. You can change this designation from one pair of hands to another by taking the Switch Hands action, which is a single action. You can only wield items with your active hands.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat multiple times."],["Through careful experimentation and selective adaptation, you've manipulated your immune system and internal chemistry to better fight off illness and infection. You gain the Fast Recovery skill feat and the Targeted Immunization action."],["You have spikes extending from your external shell. These spikes deal 1d4 piercing damage to a creature that Grapples you or hits you with an unarmed attack."],["You might blend into the background, but your allies can use your bulk as cover. When you [[/act hide]], one adjacent ally your size or smaller can use a reaction to Step and Hide behind you, gaining the Concealed condition until either one of you moves."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou create a cloud of vapor around yourself. This vapor lasts for 1 minute or until you move. You become Concealed within the mist, and other creatures outside the mist become concealed to you."],["You grow a tentacle that can lash out like a whip. You gain a tentacle unarmed attack that deals 1d6 bludgeoning damage. Your tentacle is in the brawling weapon group and has the barathu, finesse, reach, and unarmed traits."],["You can control causticity as you vent your gases. When you Vent Gas, increase the area of your emanation to 10 feet. You can choose to make the gas you vent caustic. If you do, any non-barathu creature that enters the emanation or starts its turn in the area takes 3d6 acid damage, with a basic Reflex save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. On a critical failure, a creature additionally takes 1d4 persistent acid damage. At 17th level, the acid damage increases by 2d6, and the persistent acid damage increases by 1d4."],["You've lived among other creatures and cultures for most of your life, and you can alter your body and demeanor to precisely mimic a humanoid.\n\nYou can cast Humanoid Form as a 5th-rank occult innate spell once per day, except the duration is increased to 1 hour."],["You tweak your anatomy and bodily systems to metabolize pharmaceuticals more efficiently. Regain additional Hit Points equal to half your level when you restore Hit Points to yourself using a consumable item with the healing trait."],["You attune to the brain waves of living creatures and can sense the presence or absence of thought in others.\n\nYou gain thoughtsense as a precise sense with a range of 30 feet, allowing you to detect thinking creatures. As thoughtsense only detects thinking creatures, a creature that doesn't think or is otherwise immune to mental effects (such as many oozes and robots) can't be perceived using your thoughtsense, regardless of how precise it is."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou temporarily merge your body with that of an adjacent willing creature, overlaying yourself atop them to better shield them from harm. This transformation lasts for 10 minutes. You can Dismiss this effect. When you do, you emerge in a space adjacent to the target you merged with. While combined, you and your target each take your own turns as normal and must be targeted separately for the purposes of abilities and other effects. Additionally, you and your target gain the following benefits.\n\n- If the target is Medium or smaller, their size increases to Large and their reach increases to 10 feet.\n- You occupy the target's space and can't take actions with the move trait. If the target moves, you move with them.\n- For each Speed you possess, compare it to that of your target. If your Speed is faster, or they lack that Speed, they gain your Speed.\n- Your body shields the target from harm, granting them greater cover, though you don't gain cover. Your body doesn't obscure the target's vision or block line of sight."],["You've cataloged the genetic code from countless ancestries you've encountered, and you can draw upon any of them to enhance and evolve your body. Increase the number of ancestries you can select with Convergent Evolution to six. You gain two additional ancestry feats you qualify for of 13th level or lower, chosen from among the ancestries selected with Convergent Evolution. You can retrain one or both of these selected feats once per day during your daily preparations."],["You can emit sound waves and sense your environment as it's reflected by objects around you. When you take the [[/act seek]] action, you can use hearing as a precise sense with a range of 40 feet until the start of your next turn. You can also use this sense while you Search."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** An enemy scores a critical hit against you with a Strike.\n\n---\n\nYour anatomy adjusts to distribute damage from vital areas. The triggering attack deals only the damage it would deal on a hit (typically normal damage instead of double damage). Any other effects of the attack caused by a critical hit still occur, such as critical specializations effects. Until the beginning of your next turn, you're Off-Guard against the triggering enemy."],["You've learned how to maintain your ooze form, allowing you to experience the glory of your primordial form more frequently. You can use Become Ooze with a frequency of once per 10 minutes, rather than once per day. If you fall asleep in your ooze form, you remain in that form until you wake up."],["You can quickly access your genetic database of knowledge and experiences. Choose a skill you're expert in that has the Recall Knowledge action. You gain the Assurance and Automatic Knowledge skill feats for the chosen skill.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times, choosing a different skill each time."],["You can reshape your body to provide a safe means of undersea travel for trusted allies. When another PC rides you as a mount while you're using the Living Submersible ability, your expert coordination allows them to take three actions at the start of their turn rather than the two they normally could take while riding another PC. You still gain only two actions at the start of your turn, instead of three, as you spend one action keeping your rider safely contained within a protective foam layer on your back."],["You modify your body's genetics to resist certain damage types. You gain resistance to acid, bludgeoning, cold, electricity, fire, piercing, poison, slashing, or sonic damage equal to half your level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat multiple times. Each time you do so, select a different damage type."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou can transform your body into a gaseous vapor. In this state, you're amorphous. You lose any item bonus to AC and all other effects and bonuses from armor, and you use your proficiency rank in unarmored defense. You gain resistance 8 to physical damage and are immune to precision damage. You can't cast spells, activate items, or use actions that have the attack or manipulate trait. You gain a fly Speed equal to your normal fly Speed and can slip through tiny cracks. This form lasts for 5 minutes or until you Dismiss it."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou vent gas to propel yourself forward. All squares in a 5-foot emanation become filled with gas. All creatures in the gas become Concealed, and all creatures outside the gas become concealed to creatures within it. This gas disperses at the beginning of your next turn.\n\nYou gain a +10-foot circumstance bonus to all your Speeds until the start of your next turn. Then you Stride."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYour body stores cellular kinetic energy as a static charge. You discharge this electricity in a 10-foot emanation (15 feet if you're in a body of water). All creatures in the area take 5))d6 electricity damage (basic basic Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC). On a critical failure, a creature becomes Immobilized for 1 round. At 13th level, the damage increases to 8d6. At 17th level, the damage increases to 11d6."],["You sample the genetics of creatures and people you've made contact with and mimic them. When you take this feat, select up to three different ancestries with which you've had significant contact. You can select ancestry feats from the ancestries you chose, in addition to barathu ancestry feats. Additionally, you gain one ancestry feat you qualify for of 5th level or lower from one of the selected ancestries. You can retrain the selected feat once per day during your daily preparations."],["Your reinforced tentacles wrap together to burrow through the ground. You gain a burrow Speed of 15 feet for as long as your tentacles are wrapped together, and then you Burrow. You take a -10-foot status penalty to your land and fly Speeds until you unwrap your tentacles as a free action."],["Your songs become more complex and tinged with greater magic. Each day during your daily preparations, you can choose one common 2nd-rank spell from the occult spell list. You can cast this spell as an occult innate spell once before your next daily preparations."],["Your molecular structure is more resistant to certain damage types. You gain additional resistance to the damage type chosen with Molecular Modification. Your resistance to the chosen damage type equals your level, instead of half your level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you've taken Molecular Modification multiple times, you can take this feat multiple times, each time gaining additional resistance to a different damage type chosen with Molecular Modification."],["You worship the ancestral deity of Czelle, the great ocean spirit Aspalasch, seen as the protector both of binnaquids and all other life on the planet. You gain the Additional Lore general feat for Aspalasch Lore.\n\nAdditionally, Aspalasch grants you magical gifts. Choose one divine cantrip from Forbidding Ward, Guidance, Message, and Summon Instrument. You can cast that cantrip as an innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["You have learned the traditional hunting techniques of your people. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Stealth and Survival. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Binnaquid Lore."],["You can force water out through the protrusion on top of your head and blast an enemy with a stream of water. You gain a blowhole ranged unarmed attack with a range increment of 30 feet and the water trait that deals 1d6 bludgeoning damage. On a critical hit, you knock the target back 5 feet from you. Blowholes do not add critical specialization effects."],["You have spent your life watching out for hidden dangers in the murky waters of Czelle. How could a city ever catch you by surprise? You are trained in Survival and gain the Urban Survivalist skill feat. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Survival checks to detect hazards when using Urban Survivalist."],["You are a star dakeshar player, easily slipping past the opposing team to swim as many laps as possible. You have learned to use this skill in other settings. You gain the Underwater Marauder skill feat, even if you don't meet its prerequisites. If you are Tumbling Through an enemy's space while underwater, you do not consider the enemy's space to be difficult terrain. Additionally, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to all Acrobatics checks made while underwater."],["You spend enough time moving around in swamps that they don't slow you down, and you've grown accustomed to having to keep an eye out while inhabiting those swamps. You ignore difficult terrain due to water and mud. You can see twice as far in murky water as a normal creature would, and you can see as far in clear water as you would be able to in air."],["You have spent enough time in the deepest, darkest waters of Czelle that your vision can penetrate anything. You gain greater darkvision, enabling you to see through magical darkness even if it normally hampers darkvision. You automatically succeed at the DC 5 flat check to target a Concealed creature if that creature is concealed only by ink, mud, silt, or other particulates underwater."],["**Trigger** A foe hits you with a melee weapon or unarmed attack that deals physical damage.\n\n---\n\nYou relax yourself the instant you are hit to minimize the damage it deals to your body. You fall Prone and are Stunned 1. Attempt a DC 6 flat check. On a success, you take minimum damage from the attack, and on a critical success, if the attack was a critical hit, you don't take double damage."],["You have spent a lot of time using weapons underwater, and you know how to modify them to function as well as they would on land. By spending 10 minutes with a weapon, you alter it to function better underwater for the next 24 hours. If it is a bludgeoning or slashing weapon, the wielder no longer takes a –2 circumstance penalty to attack rolls with it. If it is a ranged weapon, its range increment is no longer halved."],["**Trigger** You gain the dying condition.\n\n---\n\nYou have spent a lifetime quietly waiting underwater, barely even breathing. When most necessary, you can slow down your body's functions to give your allies time to help you before you succumb to your injuries. As you lose consciousness, you slow down your bodily functions to stave off death a little longer. Your dying condition cannot increase for any reason until after your next turn (including a failed recovery check)."],["You understand the power of waiting for the opportune moment. When you would roll initiative, you can choose to forgo rolling and instead receive a result of 1. If you do, you are Quickened during the first round of combat. You can use the extra action only to Stride or to Strike."],["You have continued in your worship of Aspalasch, and the ocean spirit has granted you greater powers. Choose a spell from air bubble, create water, and sanctuary. You can cast that spell as a 1st-rank divine innate spell once per day. You may choose each morning which cantrip you would like to cast from Aspalasch Worshipper.\n\nIf you select this feat at 9th level, you can additionally choose from Environmental Endurance, Water Breathing, and Water Walk. You can cast that spell as a 2nd-rank divine innate spell once per day.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. If you do, you must select a different spell."],["You love your pets and you take excellent care of them. When you restore Hit Points to a pet, animal companion, or other creature with the minion trait under your control, you increase the Hit Points restored by 2. At 12th level, you instead increase the Hit Points restored by 5."],["You are among the strongest swimmers on Czelle. Your swim Speed increases to 40 feet."],["You grew up in a germy swamp, giving you an excellent immune system. You retch in an attempt to recover from the sickened condition. On a success, you reduce your sickened value by 2 (or by 4 on a critical success). On a failure, you reduce your sickened value by 1."],["You have spent enough time honing your psychic skills with telepathic messages that you can now manipulate objects using only your mind. You gain Telekinetic Maneuver as a 2nd-rank occult innate spell that you can cast once per day."],["You excel at underwater sports, and you are now particularly adept at feats of strength while unburdened by gravity. You can use this to your advantage in combat. When you successfully [[/act grapple]] a creature while underwater or in zero gravity, your target must attempt a saving throw against the higher of your class DC or Athletics DC. On a failure, the target is Enfeebled 1 until the end of its next turn."],["Your coloration camouflages you nicely in aquatic environments, and you know how to take full advantage of that. While underwater, you can [[/act sneak]] without attempting a Stealth check as long as you move no more than 5 feet and do not pass within 10 feet of an enemy during your movement.\n\nYou can move at full Speed while using the [[/act avoid-notice]] exploration activity in an aquatic environment, and you can use another exploration activity that does not attract unnecessary attention while Avoiding Notice."],["Your skin is always moist, covered in a layer of secretions that keep your body from drying out. These secretions are powerful enough to partially neutralize any acid that comes into contact with your skin. You gain acid resistance equal to half your level."],["Vampires have nothing on your ability to draw blood with every bite. When you successfully hit with your jaws unarmed attack, your target takes 1 persistent bleed damage, or 1d4 persistent bleed damage on a critical hit."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nWith a sacred word of gratitude, you drink some water and allow it to channel vitality into your body. The water functions as your choice of an advanced medpatch or hypopen. At 13th level, it functions as a superior medpatch or hypopen. At 17th level, it functions as an elite medpatch or hypopen."],["**Frequency** once per minute\n\n---\n\nYou have an ominous presence that unnerves the living. You have learned to harness this sinister aura to your own advantage and can scare your foes with a focused glance. Focus your ill intent at one living creature within 30 feet. The target must succeed at a Will save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC, or become Frightened 1 (Frightened 2 on a critical failure) and Stupefied 1 as long as it's frightened. Once you've used Baleful Gaze against a creature, it's temporarily immune for 24 hours."],["Since your resurrection, you've learned a lot about yourself, your place in the cycle of souls, and other undead. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Intimidation and Religion. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Borai Lore."],["You exist on the boundaries between life and death, and you can channel your own imbalanced spiritual essence into magical spells. Choose one of the following cantrips: Vitality Lash or Void Warp. You can cast this spell as a divine innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat twice. Each time, you must select a different cantrip."],["You became a borai through a botched resurrection attempt—perhaps a magic spell was disrupted, a religious rite went awry, or faulty technology went haywire, resulting in your condition. Your soul is loosely tethered to your body, allowing you to temporarily shield your living form from the ravages of the void. You gain the Soul Shield reaction."],["You became a borai through your own stubborn willfulness. When you died, you refused to accept your death and clung to your corpse, forcing your soul back into your body and regaining life along with it. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Will saving throws against fear and effects that would make you Confused or Controlled and to your Will DC against attempts to Demoralize you."],["You became a borai intentionally through necromantic experimentation conducted by yourself or someone else before you died. This experimentation has strengthened your defenses against death but has also made you look more like a corpse than a living being. You gain the Diehard feat, and death effects no longer kill you if they reduce you to 0 Hit Points. This keeps you from being automatically killed or from having your dying value automatically decrease, but it doesn't make you immune to other parts of the spell or effect. For example, you can still take mental damage and become frightened by a vision of death spell, you just don't instantly die from it."],["Your living body is flush with vitality, which easily hides your ichor-filled veins from sight. You don't have to attempt Deception checks against a creature's Perception DC to successfully Impersonate yourself as a living member of your ancestry or hide your borai heritage, nor do you require a disguise kit for such Impersonations. This is a non-magical effect that doesn't protect against detection, revelation, or scrying effects. Additionally, when a creature actively attempts a Perception check against you, you gain a +4 circumstance bonus to your Deception DC, but only for the purposes of seeing through your disguise when you're Impersonating yourself as a living member of your ancestry or otherwise attempting to hide your borai heritage."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou enjoy embracing new experiences and have a knack for picking up new skills and talents, sometimes over the course of countless lifetimes, as your semi-dead nature grants you a wider perspective. Choose a skill that you're untrained in. Until the beginning of your next turn, you become trained in the chosen skill."],["You're willful and stubborn, and you refuse to accept your own failure—traits that have served you well in life and after death. When you critically fail a saving throw against a mental effect, you get a failure instead. Additionally, you gain the Deny Failure reaction."],["You've learned to unleash the anger and malice you've built up over the course of your life and restless undeath against multiple foes at once, creating a potent effect around yourself. You can choose to use Baleful Gaze as a 2-action activity, rather than 1. When you do, Baleful Gaze gains the divine trait, loses the visual trait, and affects each living creature in a 30-foot emanation, rather than a single living creature."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You have the dying condition and are about to attempt a recovery check.\n\n---\n\nYou have died once before and have no intention of dying ever again; your soul stubbornly resuscitates your body when you would otherwise perish. You are restored to 1 Hit Point, lose the dying and Unconscious conditions, and can act normally on this turn. You increase your wounded condition as normal."],["Thanks to your life-altering brush with death, your living body is better protected against the weaknesses of the flesh. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Fortitude saves against disease and poison."],["Your soul is radiant and can sustain your living body indefinitely, without the need for outside nourishment. You don't need to eat or drink, and you count your Constitution modifier as one higher while determining how much you heal from resting."],["Some element of your borai nature gives you flashes from the beyond: visions from the afterlife you were intended for or might still one day obtain. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Religion. If you're already trained in Religion, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Additional Lore feat for a Lore subcategory about a specific plane tied to your afterlife (such as Heaven, Hell, Nirvana, or Outer Rifts Lore)."],["The ichor pulsing through your veins is infused with void energy, and it protects your body and soul from the same sinister power. You have void resistance equal to half your level."],["You release a pulse of spiritual energy into one weapon you're holding, making it resonate with immaterial soul stuff. Until the beginning of your next turn, your weapon gains the effects of the ghost killer weapon fusion. At 17th level, it deals an additional 1d6 spirit damage."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** An enemy's Strike or targeted effect would hit you, and you weren't already Concealed, Hidden, or undetected to that enemy.\n\n---\n\nYour mere presence attracts restless spirits, haunted objects, spiritually active substances, and fragmented souls, like a magnet attracts metal. You manifest these spirit shards in a chaotic whirlwind around you that you barely control with your thoughts. You become concealed until the beginning of your next turn, and the flat check for concealment applies to the triggering Strike or effect that would've hit you. If the flat check fails, the Strike or effect misses you."],["You unleash a portion of your spiritual essence—either the vitality of your living body or the void of your undead soul—in a violent burst around you. You deal 5d6 untyped damage of your selected type (see below) to all adjacent creatures (basic Reflex save using your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher). At 11th level and every 2 levels thereafter, this damage increases by 1d6.\n\nWhen you take this feat, choose either vitality or void. Once chosen, this selection can't be changed. Unleash Pneuma deals the chosen damage type and gains the chosen trait.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat twice, but you must select a different damage type each time. If you do, Unleash Pneuma's frequency becomes once per day per damage type, rather than once per day."],["You are adept at carrying objects in your armpit pockets. You can store up to four objects of negligible or light Bulk in your pockets. Stored objects are protected from environmental damage, including water. You can stow or remove an object as an Interact action, or drop all stored objects to the ground as a free action. When you become Unconscious, all stored objects are dropped."],["You lock arms with one or more adjacent allies as an Interact action, which supports them while swimming. Any number of additional allies equal to half your level (minimum 1) can lock arms with another ally in the raft as an Interact action. As an exploration activity, you can Swim at half your typical swim Speed and carry your allies with you. If you're using Community Raft at the start of an encounter, you and your interlocked allies can usually roll an Athletics check instead of a Perception check to determine your initiative.\n\nAny member of the Community Raft can stop locking arms at any time without spending an action. Allies can still use interlocked arms for other purposes, such as wielding weapons or using unarmed Strikes while part of a Community Raft.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can form a Community Raft in zero-g. All members of the raft lose the Untethered condition if at least one member of the raft does not have the untethered condition. If the raft is moved, every member of the raft floats at the same time. If every member of the raft is untethered, the entire raft floats at the end of each round rather than the end of each member's turn."],["Your whiskers instinctively twitch and provide you with feedback about a target's current disposition. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to [[/act sense-motive]] for targets within 30 feet of you that are not immune to emotion or mental effects."],["**Requirements** You are adjacent to an ally.\n\n---\n\nYou learned that supporting members of your pair or pod also makes you stronger. You join hands with an adjacent willing ally, which occupies one of each of your hands. For 1 round, while you remain adjacent to that ally and holding hands, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC. Additionally, you and your ally gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your saving throws against attempts to [[/act demoralize]], [[/act reposition]], [[/act shove]], or [[/act trip]] either of you.\n\nHold Hands"],["**Requirements** You are Blinded or Dazzled with a duration of 1 minute or less.\n\n---\n\nYou have a well-developed nictitating membrane, which you use to see underwater and clear out obstructions. If you are dazzled due to an effect other than Nictitating Membrane, reduce the flat check DC to target a creature with Concealment caused by your dazzled condition from 5 to 3 until the end of your next turn. If you are blinded, attempt a DC 10 flat check. On a success, you remove the blinded condition and gain the dazzled condition instead for the same duration as the blinded condition. You cannot use this to remove a permanent blinded condition."],["You have an object that comforts you, such as a favorite rock, a childhood stuffed animal, or another trinket. While you hold your personal trinket, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus on saving throws and to Will DCs against fear effects. If your personal trinket is ever lost or destroyed, you can gain another one by spending 1 week of downtime searching for a suitable replacement.\n\nAdditionally, you gain the Self Soothe action."],["**Trigger** You fail at an attempt to [[/act demoralize]] a creature.\n\n---\n\nYou bare your teeth in aggression at your target. It loses temporary immunity to your attempts to Demoralize it until the end of your next turn, and its attitude toward you decreases by one step. The creature then becomes immune to Take Me Seriously for 24 hours."],["You release a loud shriek meant to draw attention or raise alarm. All enemies within 60 feet must attempt a Will save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. The targets are then temporarily immune to your Alarming Scream for 24 hours.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target becomes Frightened 1.\n\n**Failure** The target becomes Deafened for 1 round and Frightened 2.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target becomes deafened for 1 minute and Frightened 4."],["Your whiskers buzz with energy as empathic pulses collect within them that you can unleash in a burst of intense emotions. You can cast Vibe Check four times per day as a 2nd-rank occult innate spell, selecting a different emotion each time. You can cast *vibe check* as a 4th-rank spell by using two daily uses of the spell, but you still only project a single emotion when you cast *vibe check* this way."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nOne of your personal trinkets carries your memory of eager early mornings and the rush of energy to start a task. You grasp a personal trinket and allow it to invigorate you with a pleasant memory. You become Quickened for 1 minute and can use the extra action each round for only Strike and Stride actions."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You are about to attempt a skill check, attack roll, or saving throw.\n\n---\n\nIn this world, there are few things more noble than a personal sacrifice. You use one of your personal trinkets to empower yourself. You do not roll the triggering check but instead earn a critical success. When you use this ability, the personal trinket is destroyed."],["◆ to ◆◆◆\n\nBrenneris often live and work in pairs to take advantage of different areas of expertise, inspired by the old adage that says two heads are always better than one. You stick close to your companions so you can help one another in a jam. You gain an extra reaction at the start of each of your turns that can only be used to Aid."],["**Trigger** You attempt a Diplomacy check.\n\n---\n\nYou attempt to Recall Knowledge about the target of the triggering check as you reach into your memories of your negotiation preparation files. If you succeed at the Recall Knowledge attempt, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the triggering Diplomacy check (+2 on a critical success)."],["Some trinkets are useful for medicinal purposes. You have found another trinket of light Bulk that can serve as a tool for certain traditional medicinal uses and can Conceal an Object of negligible Bulk inside of it. You can use your Medicinal Trinket as a medkit when you Treat Wounds. The first time each day you use the Medicinal Trinket to use Battle Medicine or Treat Wounds on yourself, you gain additional temporary Hit Points equal to your level that last for 1 hour, regardless of the result of the attempt.\n\nMedicinal Trinket"],["**Trigger** You become Grabbed, Immobilized, or Restrained.\n\n---\n\nYour slick fur assists you in sliding out of narrow crevices, slipping restraints, or evading the crushing jaws of predators. You attempt to Escape."],["**Trigger** An ally attempts a Diplomacy or Intimidation check to [[/act coerce]] or [[/act make-an-impression]].\n\n---\n\nBrenneri ambassadors refer to alternating tones in negotiations as soft paw, sharp claw. If the triggering check is a Diplomacy check, you attempt an Intimidation check, and vice versa. Your ally uses the higher of the two results for their triggering check."],["You have adapted to swimming gracefully among the stars. You are not clumsy or Off-Guard while moving in zero-g environments. Additionally, you can move in zero-g using your swim Speed as though it were a fly Speed and you had the cosmic trait."],["A lack of shared language can be a pernicious challenge for negotiations, interrogations, and diplomatic relations. As part of your ambassador corps training, you learned how to quickly establish linguistic connections with others.\n\nYou can attempt a Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation check with the linguistic trait that targets a creature that does not share a language with you. These attempts take a −4 circumstance penalty to the check. Furthermore, you can translate for your ambassador partner when they attempt any Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation check with the linguistic trait as a reaction with the auditory trait."],["One of your personal trinkets has seen you through a long illness, recovery from an injury, or days aboard a ship dealing with motion sickness. Holding on to the object fills you with memories of being treated with tender care. You suppress the Sickened condition for 10 minutes."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nOne of your personal trinkets has aged from years of love and wear. Looking at it reminds you of times when you were safe and filled with joy, such as when you were a child listening to stories of heroic triumph. When you use the Self Soothe action, you also reduce your Doomed value by 1. You cannot use this to reduce a permanent doomed value."],["**Requirements** You have access to an infosphere, library, or similar reference collection.\n\n---\n\nWhat might take other minds a lifetime to master, you can temporarily absorb through a brief, intense study session. During your daily preparations, you can review literature to gain the trained proficiency rank in one skill of your choice. This proficiency lasts until you prepare again. Since this proficiency is temporary, you can't use it as a prerequisite for a skill increase or a permanent character option (like a feat)."],["After extensive study of historical records, legends, and myths, you have absorbed the essential teachings of contemplative society. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Arcana and Occultism. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Contemplative Lore."],["For all their practicality, broader fields of study don't capture your imagination when there are more specialized disciplines you might explore. Choose two Lore skill subcategories. You gain the Additional Lore general feat for both skills.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat three times. Each time you do, you gain the Additional Lore general feat for a new subcategory of Lore, and you become trained in one other Lore skill subcategory of your choice."],["Through rigorous mental exercises or natural talent, your psychic senses extend farther than average. Increase the ranges of your limited telepathy and thoughtsense by 10 feet each."],["You've honed your thoughts into a deadly weapon that can shatter a foe's mind. You gain a psychic shock ranged unarmed attack with a range increment of 30 feet and the agile trait. The weapon deals 1d4 mental damage and is in the mental weapon group."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYour brain can process complex calculations subconsciously and save the answers for when they're needed most. You gain 1 Focus Point. If you don't spend this Focus Point by the end of this turn, you lose it."],["You read the subtle cues of a target's brainwaves to anticipate the mental state of a single creature within range of your limited telepathy that you can detect with thoughtsense. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Deception checks and Intimidation checks targeting the creature, to saves against the target's effects that have the fear trait, and to your Will DC against the target's Intimidation skill actions, such as Demoralize. If you deal mental damage to the target, increase this bonus to +2.\n\nYou can Telepredict the actions of only one creature at a time. Telepredict ends if you use it on a different creature or the creature leaves the range of your limited telepathy."],["**Trigger** A Telepredicted creature uses an effect that requires a Reflex save or attempts to Disarm or Trip you.\n\n**Requirements** You have a bonus against the target using Telepredict.\n\n---\n\nBy reading cues and analyzing probability outcomes, you smoothly predicting your opponent's next move. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Reflex save or Reflex DC against the triggering action. Increase this bonus to +2 if you've dealt mental damage to the target since the last time you used Telepredict."],["You can track the minds around you with astonishing precision. Your thoughtsense becomes a precise sense."],["You effortlessly juggle an assortment of gear with your telepathy, giving you the appearance of a solar cerebellum orbited by planetoid items. You gain a second set of telekinetic hands, per Mind Over Matter, granting a typical contemplative six hands total. While at least one of your telekinetic hands is empty, you can deflect incoming attacks, granting your fist attack the parry trait. You gain the Eccentric Orbit free action."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nCommunication via mere words is a limitation of lesser minds. Your thoughts weave meaning from words, feelings, mental imagery, and ineffable stimuli for 10 minutes, during which you can communicate using your limited telepathy without sharing a language.\n\nAt 17th level, you can activate this feat at will."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nIn an instant, your mind becomes a psychic supercomputer. You become Quickened for 1 minute. You can use your extra action only to Recall Knowledge, make psychic shock Strikes, activate your psychic shock's boost trait, Seek, Sense Motive, or activate abilities with the contemplative trait."],["With unparalleled focus, you can tap into and sift through the memories of every contemplative who has come before. You can cast the Collective Memories ritual once per week as the primary caster. When you do so, you can ignore the rare incense cost; if you do so, you become Drained 2 after completing the ritual."],["**Trigger** A Telepredicted creature targets you with a mental effect.\n\n**Requirements** You have a bonus against the target using Telepredict.\n\n---\n\nYou gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Will saving throws against the triggering effect. Increase this bonus to +2 if you've dealt mental damage to the target since the last time you used Telepredict. If you roll a critical success on the saving throw, the target takes 5d4 mental damage and becomes Stupefied 1 until the end of your next turn."],["**Trigger** You succeed at a check to Recall Knowledge to identify a foe within range of your limited telepathy.\n\n---\n\nUpon carefully analyzing a creature, you helpfully send it a telepathic lecture regarding its physiological and psychological inadequacies. For inexplicable reasons, doing so tends to aggravate the creature rather than educate it. The creature must attempt a Will save against your class DC. If you critically succeeded at the triggering check to Recall Knowledge, the target takes a –1 status penalty to its Will save. The creature is then temporarily immune for 24 hours.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** You accidentally overshare, exposing your own foibles. The creature gains a +1 circumstance bonus to its next attack roll against you, as long as that attack is made within 1 minute.\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature is Stupefied 1 for [[/gmr 1d4 #rounds]]{1d4 rounds}.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is Stupefied 2 for 1 round, after which it is stupefied 1 for [[/gmr 1d4 #rounds]]{1d4 rounds}."],["Your psychic awareness expands, granting you sharper perception at close range and a wider sensory field overall. Increase the range of your vague thoughtsense by 10 feet. In addition, you gain thoughtsense as an imprecise sense with a range of 5 feet.\n\nAt 9th level, your vague thoughtsense becomes an imprecise sense."],["You muster myriad minutiae that you subsequently use to overwhelm a creature's mind with pointless trivia. Attempt a check to Recall Knowledge against the Will DC of a creature you're aware of within 60 feet; you can use any skill for which you can Recall Knowledge, not just a skill associated with the target's traits. Rather than remembering useful information, you recite facts at the target. Regardless of your result, the creatures within 60 feet become temporarily immune to your attempts to Infodump with that skill for 24 hours.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is Stupefied 2 for [[/gmr 1d4 #rounds]]{1d4 rounds}.\n\n**Success** The target is Stupefied 1 for [[/gmr 1d4 #rounds]]{1d4 rounds}.\n\n**Failure** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Critical Failure** You trip over your own thoughts, becoming stupefied 1 until the beginning of your next turn.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can Infodump using speech or limited telepathy. If you Infodump through speech, this ability gains the auditory trait."],["Your telekinetic capabilities extend beyond personal levitation, allowing you to handle nearby objects with precision. Your telekinesis grants you the equivalent of two additional hands, following the rules for characters with more than two hands as detailed in Starfinder Player Core. However, each of the telekinetic hands can wield only items of 1 Bulk or less. The Switch Hands action gains the contemplative trait when you switch to or from your telekinetic hands."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYour incredible processing power and near-perfect recall allow you to refocus even in stressful situations. You regain 1 Focus Point, up to your usual maximum."],["You can focus your mental Strikes with truly devastating precision. Whenever you critically hit using your psychic shock unarmed Strike, you get its critical specialization effect. The first time each round you hit an enemy you can sense with your thoughtsense using a psychic shock Strike, you deal an additional 1d4 persistent mental damage to your target."],["No matter how engrossed you are in other tasks, part of your mind can't help but stay curious about your surroundings.\n\nYou become trained in a Lore skill about a specific environment, planet, plane, or settlement. You can move at full Speed while using the Investigate activity.\n\nChoose one of the following: Arcana, Nature, Occultism, Religion, or Society. While using any other exploration activity, you also Investigate your surroundings, though only to Recall Knowledge using the chosen skill and any Lore skills you have."],["You have honed your telekinetic maneuverability, enabling greater bursts of speed. Increase your fly Speed by 5 feet. In addition, you gain the Telekinetic Sprint action."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou swiftly calculate and cross-reference several subjects at once. You instantly use up to three Recall Knowledge actions. If you have any special abilities or free actions that would normally be triggered when you Recall Knowledge, you can't use them for these actions. At 13th level, you can instead use up to four Recall Knowledge actions. At 17th level, you can instead use up to five Recall Knowledge actions."],["You focus your telepathic attacks further, broadcasting your psychic power with greater range and area. Your psychic shock unarmed attack gains the boost (1d6) trait, requiring no battery to boost your attack. By spending 10 minutes in intense concentration, you can reconfigure your mind to apply one of the following benefits to your psychic shock. This benefit lasts until you reconfigure to another benefit.\n\n- **Extended Shock:** Increase the range increment of your psychic shock by 15 feet.\n- **Mind Crusher:** Your psychic shock gains the fatal d8 trait.\n- **Peer Pressure:** Your psychic shock gains the arc trait, but it deals mental damage rather than electricity damage.\n- **Psychic Wave:** Your psychic shock gains the splash trait."],["Having overcome countless challenges in your rise to power, your self-confidence isn't just bluster and brains; it's supported by empirical evidence! Your Shielding Arrogance reaction can now also trigger whenever a foe within range of your thoughtsense critically fails an attack against you or critically fails a skill check attempted against you (such as an Intimidation check to Demoralize you or an Acrobatics check to Tumble around you). Increase the number of temporary Hit Points you gain from Shielding Arrogance to 2d8 plus your character level. Increase this by 1d8 at 13th level and by an additional 1d8 at 17th level."],["Straining every neuron, you briefly supercharge your telekinetic abilities. Choose Charisma, Intelligence, or Wisdom when you activate this ability. For 1 minute, you can carry Bulk equal to 7 + the chosen attribute modifier before becoming encumbered, and you can hold and carry a total Bulk of 12 + the chosen attribute modifier. Your telekinetic hands can hold and wield objects heavier than 1 Bulk, and you ignore the effects of your atrophied ability. Finally, you gain the Telekinetic Lift action. When the duration ends, you become Fatigued for 1 minute, and your telekinetic hands drop any objects they can no longer hold."],["Like copaxi warriors of old, you've grown particularly sturdy and threatening copi antlers instead of the elegant ones favored by most modern copaxis. You gain an antlers unarmed attack that deals 1d4 piercing damage. Your antlers are in the brawling group and have the finesse and unarmed traits."],["You've grown an armored copi exoskeleton—far sturdier than most copaxi exoskeletons—to protect the rest of your body from harm. Your exoskeleton grants a +3 item bonus to AC, has a Dex cap of +1, a check penalty of –2, and a Strength threshold of +3, and has the comfort and exposed traits. You're trained in your exoskeleton. You can wear a Flight Suit, but you can't wear other armor. You can't install armor upgrades or etch armor runes onto your exoskeleton."],["During your adventures—most likely offworld—you've honed your ability to adapt to one of the predominant ancestries around you. You gain the Adopted Ancestry general feat, and you also gain one 1st-level ancestry feat from the ancestry you chose for the Adopted Ancestry feat."],["You've taken on a role as a diplomat, whether as an official government agent, an ecological activist seeking allies, a frequent visitor to other worlds, a petitioner for Pact Worlds protectorate status, or simply as someone who recognizes the need to strengthen bonds between interstellar communities.\n\nYou gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks to [[/act gather-information]] and [[/act make-an-impression]] against sapient creatures as well as to Perception checks to Sense the Motives of such creatures."],["Your polyps are especially sensitive to hormones and other chemicals. You gain imprecise scent with a range of 30 feet."],["**Trigger** You attempt a saving throw against a spell or magical effect, but you haven't rolled yet.\n\n---\n\nYou've spent your life learning to react with extreme wariness to all things mystical. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your saving throw against the triggering effect, which increases to a +2 circumstance bonus if the effect changes gravity or can cause you to fall Prone."],["You've grown especially sturdy fists. Your fist unarmed attacks no longer have the nonlethal trait and gain the shove trait."],["You've grown an additional pair of arms beyond the pair that most copaxis have. Your four arms allow you to wield and hold up to four hands' worth of weapons and equipment. At any time, one pair of hands is designated as your active hands. You can change this designation from one pair of hands to another by taking the Switch Hands action. You can wield items only with your active hands."],["You've grown more legs than a typical copaxi, or your legs are especially long, increasing the length of your strides. Your Speed increases by 5 feet."],["By making minor adjustments to gravitational forces on your body, you make a controlled descent instead of falling. You glide slowly toward the ground, 5 feet down and up to 25 feet horizontally through the air. As long as you spend at least 1 action gliding each round and haven't yet reached the ground, you remain in the air at the end of your turn. If you use Steady Descent in zero gravity, you instead move up to half your fastest Speed in a direction of your choice."],["You have remarkable control over the polyps on your body. When you cast Telekinetic Hand, as long as you have line of effect and line of sight to your hand, you can use your *telekinetic hand* as the origin point for your spells that have a line or cone area. Additionally, you gain the Polyp Print activity."],["Your polyps can absorb hostile magic and repurpose it to fuel your body. Whenever you succeed at a saving throw against a spell or magical effect, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to double the spell's rank, or equal to the level of the magical effect if it isn't a spell. These temporary Hit Points last until the end of your next turn."],["Like the ancient copaxis who occupied your planet's majestic sky cities, you've become connected to the cosmic forces of gravity. You gain a permanent fly Speed equal to your land Speed. You gain the cosmic trait. You can use your fly Speed to Fly normally in a vacuum or zero-gravity environment. You're still susceptible to effects that require breathing while in normal atmosphere."],["You've reconnected with some of the primal cosmic power of Tabrid Minor's copi, and it infuses the polyps of your body with energy. You can cast Sound Body and Unfettered Movement as 7th-rank primal innate spells. You can cast each of these primal innate spells once per day."],["Your connection to the gravitational forces of copi allows you to temporarily alter gravity's effects on your body. You treat gravity as being one step higher or lower (for example, low gravity becomes standard gravity, or standard gravity becomes high gravity), but you can't Adjust Gravity to extreme or zero gravity. This only affects you, your gear, and your movement. This lasts until the end of your next turn if you adjust from extreme or zero gravity; otherwise, it lasts 1 hour, until you Adjust Gravity again, or until you enter an environment with a different gravity, whichever comes first.\n\nAt 13th level, you can adjust gravity to zero gravity or extreme gravity. At 17th level, you can lower or raise the gravity level by up to two steps."],["You've enhanced your exoskeleton with cybernetics or biotech to make it even sturdier. The item bonus to AC from your exoskeleton increases to +4. You can use the Install Upgrade activity to install armor upgrades into your exoskeleton; your exoskeleton has two upgrade slots."],["Your body can adapt and change even faster than most other copaxis. You can retrain using your Regenerative Evolution feature over 1 week of downtime instead of 1 month. At 13th level, you can use regenerative evolution to retrain one feat or skill increase during your daily preparations. You can't use regenerative evolution to retrain Heightened Metabolic Adaptation."],["The polyps that form your exoskeleton adapt and regrow more quickly than usual. Reduce the DC of flat checks to end persistent damage on you by 2."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You're struck by a critical hit that deals physical damage.\n\n---\n\nYour body's polyps respond to an injury by immediately shedding wounded or dead polyps and regrowing new ones. Attempt a DC 17 flat check. If you're successful, the attack becomes a normal hit."],["You're so accustomed to being wary around magic that you've undergone physiological changes that make your body resistant to it. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against spells and magical effects. Increase the bonus you gain from Copaxi Superstition to a +2 circumstance bonus (or a +3 circumstance bonus if the effect changes gravity or can cause you to fall Prone)."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou can manipulate the effects of gravity on your own body enough to allow you to fly. You gain a fly Speed equal to your land Speed for 10 minutes."],["Thanks to your focus on your body's health as it grows new polyps, your polyps are especially resilient. Increase your maximum Hit Points by your level. When you have the Dying condition, the DC of your recovery checks is equal to 9 + your dying value (instead of 10 + your dying value).\n\nIf you also have the Toughness feat, the Hit Points gained from it and this feat are cumulative, and the DC of your recovery checks is equal to 6 + your dying value."],["You've learned to manipulate the forces of vitality and void to cheat death. Choose one of the following cantrips: Forbidding Ward or Stabilize. You can cast this spell as a divine innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat twice. Each time, you must select a different cantrip."],["A transformation after death twisted your body, elongating your teeth into fangs or sharpening your appendages into claws. When you select this feat, you gain one of the following unarmed attacks of your choice: claw or jaws. Both of these attacks are in the brawling weapon group and have the listed damage die and traits.\n\n**Claw** 1d6 slashing (agile, finesse, unarmed)\n\n**Jaws** 1d6 piercing (grapple, unarmed)\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these attacks, you get its critical specialization effect.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat two times. Each time you do, select a different attack from the options listed above."],["Becoming undead has given you unique insight. You learn how to speak and understand the Necril language, and you become trained in Undead Lore, a skill that allows you to Recall Knowledge about all kinds of undead regardless of subtype. At 5th level, your proficiency in Undead Lore increases to expert."],["Through experimentation, manipulation, or perhaps just due to natural wear and tear of your limbs, you are able to use your natural weaponry in more creative ways than just bashing, stabbing, or biting. Select two of the traits from the following list and add them to your ancestry's unarmed attacks: backstabber, backswing, concussive, disarm, forceful, parry, shove, sweep, and trip.\n\n---\n\n**Special** Partial corpsefolk characters may apply this feat's benefit to the knives they create with their lineage ability."],["Your long existence has given you time to train and insights worth several mortal lifetimes. You become trained in two skills of your choice."],["You died from massive traumatic injuries that caused you to lose body parts, or you rotted for a long time before you were brought back as an undead. There is no hiding your undead nature from onlookers unless you are wholly disguised, but you can manipulate your broken shards in creative ways. Your reduced mass gives you a +5-foot status bonus to your land Speed. In addition, you can spend 1 action that has the manipulate trait to break off a jagged piece of your own body to create a commercial Knife. You can create a number of knives at a time equal to your Constitution modifier. They can't be sold and don't function for others. Effects that enhance your natural attacks, such as hardlight handwraps, apply their effects to a commercial knife created in this way while you're wielding it."],["Your eyes burn with a red hue and glow like embers when in areas of darkness or shade. You gain darkvision."],["Most creatures mistake you for a mindless, shambling zombie or even a lifeless corpse, and you've learned how to use your sepulchral appearance to your advantage. You gain the Feign Death feat, even if you don't meet the prerequisites. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus when using Deception to roll initiative if you are Impersonating a corpse when combat begins."],["When you died, your muscles and sinew knotted themselves together more tightly than when you were alive, allowing for more tightly controlled and rapid movements. You gain a +5-foot status bonus to your land Speed."],["For you, other undead creatures are easy to read, and you have a knack for dealing with them that others lack. You can influence mindless undead and communicate rudimentary orders to your minions. You can use Diplomacy to [[/act make-an-impression]] on mindless undead or make simple requests of them. If the undead creature currently is already in the thrall of a creature whose level is higher than yours, you typically need to roll a critical success (at GM discretion)."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou break off a piece of your anatomy and fling sharp bone shards at your enemies. You gain a bone shards unarmed attack that deals 1d8 piercing damage. Your bone shards are in the projectile group and have the area (cone) trait with a range of 15 feet. This effect lasts 1 minute."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You are reduced to 0 Hit Points and would gain the dying condition.\n\n---\n\nYou're not ready for the Boneyard. Roll a DC 11 flat check. On a success, you remain standing with 1 Hit Point instead of being reduced to 0 Hit Points with the Dying condition."],["You force yourself to metabolize more flesh, gristle, and bone than you can normally stomach, gorging on as much of your grisly meal as possible to bolster your body's necromantic healing processes. When you Consume Flesh, you gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to 10 plus half your level, rounded down. These temporary Hit Points last for 10 minutes.\n\nGorge"],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You take damage from an effect that deals vitality damage.\n\n---\n\nYou draw upon precious memories from your life to shield you against the energies that would nominally purge undead creatures from the universe. You gain resistance to the triggering damage equal to your level."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** Your last action was a successful Strike with an unarmed attack or commercial knife you created using your lineage.\n\n---\n\nBy tapping into the latent necromantic energies that surround you, you leech vitality from nearby living creatures, healing your own body in the process. You cast Vampiric Exsanguination as a 7th-rank divine innate spell, but the spell affects only the target of your last Strike."],["Your ability to sense living and undead energies improves, and you learn how to differentiate between entities you can sense in an area. Your lifesense becomes a precise sense with a range of 60 feet."],["You refuse to let anyone control you. Whenever you attempt a Will save against a spell or effect that would give you the Confused or Controlled condition, roll twice and use the higher result. If you would start your turn confused or controlled, you can immediately attempt a DC 5 flat check. On a success, you fight that mental control, becoming Paralyzed until the end of your turn rather than acting against your will. If you roll a 20 on this check, you immediately end the confused or controlled condition."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** You are adjacent to the corpse of a Small or larger creature who has died in the last day.\n\n---\n\nYour undead metabolism has evolved in ways that allow you to gain some small measure of sustenance and healing from the consumption of the recently dead. This might be the act of eating their flesh, fusing their bones with yours, or a combination of other activities that your companions might find to be gruesome. Regardless, it nourishes and replenishes you. You regain 1d6 Hit Points for every level you have ((level)d6 healing)."],["Without nerve endings, you can put your body up against hazards and obstacles without caring about bruising. Stride twice. Once during this movement, if you pass through or end adjacent to a door, window, wall, or similar obstacle, you can attempt an Athletics check to [[/act force-open options=dead-nerves]] that obstacle with a +1 circumstance bonus to the roll. On a failure, your movement immediately ends."],["◆◆ or ◆◆◆\n\n---\n\nYour magically preserved corpse can plow through obstacles and ignore strain in ways the living cannot. Stride twice, or three times if you spent 3 actions to Death's Advance. During this movement, you ignore difficult terrain and greater difficult terrain. Once per day, you can choose to ignore all circumstance and status penalties to your Speed when you use Death's Advance."],["You're a mountain of flesh, having managed to increase your girth in irreversible ways. Perhaps you absorbed enough physical material to do so, or maybe you've completed mysterious, inexplicable necromantic rituals. Increase your size category to Large, and increase your reach by 5 feet."],["You learn to prepare your natural weapons much more quickly than before. Breaking off knives from your body loses the manipulate trait and becomes a free action instead of a 1-action activity, and your unarmed attacks are now treated as though they had the advanced weapon improvement."],["Your skull plates or teeth have grown sharper over time, or you have painstakingly carved them to do maximum damage when using them in combat. Your unarmed jaws attack now inflicts 1d6 persistent bleed damage on a successful hit (double on a critical hit). If your weapon damage ever increases, the number of dice for your bleed damage also increases by the same amount."],["Your senses changed and improved after you died. Now you can feel the vitality energy radiating from living creatures and the void surrounding other undead entities like you. You gain lifesense as an imprecise sense with a range of 10 feet, allowing you to pinpoint the locations of (and distinguish between) living and undead creatures, but not other unliving beings such as constructs."],["Your blood coagulates into sludge, making your body more resilient against attacks that rip and shred. You gain resistance to bleed and precision damage equal to your level. The DC of your flat checks to recover from persistent bleed damage is 13 rather than 15. This reduces to 8 rather than 10 when receiving appropriate assistance."],["Your skin and bones have weathered down to the point where certain types of damage no longer have the same effect on them as when you were counted among the living. You gain resistance to a specific damage type equal to half your level. Biting corpsefolk gain resistance to slashing damage, partial corpsefolk gain resistance to piercing damage, and shambling corpsefolk gain resistance to bludgeoning damage."],["You infuse your attacks with necromantic or radiant energies from beyond the material Universe. You infuse your attacks with spiritual energy for 1 minute. All weapons you're wielding and your unarmed Strikes become magical and either deal 1 additional spirit damage and gain the unholy trait against living creatures, or deal 1 additional spirit damage and gain the holy trait against undead."],["Whether through atonement, supernatural evolution, or mutation, your internal organs have regrown and reconnected to your soul in such a way that you can gain pleasure from eating and drinking once again, giving you a flushed, healthy appearance. This gives you a +1 status bonus on Deception checks to appear as a non-undead creature. You can also now receive healing from items with the vitality trait that are eaten, ingested, absorbed, or injected (such as serums or oils), but you only receive half the normal amount of healing (rounded up)."],["You laugh at holy symbols and delight in the sound of faltering prayers. You are more in tune with your existence as an undead than many other corpsefolk are, and you can now leverage that to hold off those who would wield religious energies to try and unmake you. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to all saving throws against divine effects and spells."],["Whether working as a spy or just tired of losing your comm unit at night, your optical receptors have been upgraded to see in poor lighting conditions. You gain low-light vision. If you already have low-light vision, you instead gain darkvision.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat twice."],["Your olfactory system has been enhanced with a more powerful and precise sense of smell. You gain imprecise scent with a range of 30 feet. This means you can use your sense of smell to determine a creature's location. The GM will usually double the range if you're downwind from the creature or halve the range if you're upwind.\n\nIn addition, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to [[/act seek]] a creature or object within the range of your scent."],["Your frame is better equipped to deal with the vacuum of space, making you an ideal starship pilot or space explorer. You aren't clumsy while Untethered. In addition, you gain the cosmic trait, meaning you don't need to breathe while in space or a vacuum and are immune to the harmful environmental effects of being in space."],["The GG-OS frames were designed for military and corporate espionage applications, yet cyborgs in the seedier parts of society naturally gravitate to these builds as well. A few of these cyborgs find their way into athletic competitions. Your augmentations are sleek and subtle, and your frame is inherently faster than most other frames due to the lightweight materials used in its construction. You gain the Fleet general feat."],["You can temporarily download additional skills from the infosphere or an external memory unit. During your daily preparations, you become trained in one skill of your choice. This proficiency lasts until you prepare again. Since this proficiency is temporary, you can't use it as a prerequisite for a skill increase or a permanent character option like a feat.\n\nAt 9th level, you become an expert in the chosen skill. At 17th level, you instead become a master in the chosen skill."],["Your augmentations are hidden under sheets of lab-grown flesh or synthetic alternatives, enabling you to pass as an unaugmented being without arousing suspicion. You become trained in Deception. If you're already trained in Deception (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. In addition, creatures perceive you as an unaugmented member of your ancestry and don't realize you're a cyborg or you have the tech trait. A creature that succeeds at a Perception check to [[/act seek dc=deception]] against your Deception DC notices the tech, but unless they get a critical success or are specifically looking for a cyborg, they are likely to assume you simply have augmentations."],["Thresher models were developed with durability in mind and are built to be rugged, powerful, and festooned with defensive attachments. Your frame might have been constructed for combat, salvage, recovery operations, or heavy construction. Your sturdier design elements allow you a measure of protection not found in other frames. You treat your Strength modifier as 2 higher for the purposes of meeting the Strength requirements of armor.\n\nIn addition, you gain an integrated commercial dermal plating augmentation that doesn't count against your total implant limit and doesn't cost you any credits. You can improve the grade of this augmentation as normal by paying the difference in credits between its current grade and the intended grade."],["The X-Hat frame's encrypted blueprints were anonymously published on the infosphere for the keen-eyed to decipher and alter. A handful of infosphere sleuths traced various parts of its design to organizations that peddle in digital espionage. You become trained in Computers. If you would automatically become trained in Computers (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain the Phreaker skill feat."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You fail an Acrobatics check, Athletics check, or Reflex save.\n\n---\n\nMany of your muscles have been replaced with a densely woven fiber empowered by nanites, and you can push these muscles to function well beyond their usual limits in your moment of need. Reroll the triggering check or save, and use the better result."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou reroute power to your limbs to launch yourself through the air like a rocket. You [[/act leap]] to an unoccupied space of your choice within 60 feet. When you land, all adjacent spaces become difficult terrain as your impact shatters the ground, and you can make a melee Strike against a creature of your choice within reach. On a hit, the target is additionally knocked Prone by the force of your blow."],["You can draw energy from other parts of your body to power your limited use augmentations. During your daily preparations, select up to two augmentations installed in your body that have an activation frequency of once per day. Until your next daily preparations, increase the frequency of the selected augmentations to twice per day."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou activate a magitech crystal integrated in your body, causing it to shoot a 120-foot-long line of otherworldly energy that tears the fabric of space and time. You deal 10d6 force damage to creatures in the line. Each creature in the area must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage, and you teleport the creature up to 15 feet into an unoccupied space of your choice along the line's area.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage, and you teleport the creature up to 30 feet into an unoccupied space of your choice along the line's area.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage, becomes Stunned 1, and you teleport the creature to any unoccupied space of your choice along the line's area."],["You've replaced or augmented nearly your entire body, becoming one with your artificial components and crossing the threshold of true cybergenesis. You cease aging, and you no longer need to sleep, eat, drink, or breathe. The first time each day that you would die, you don't. Instead, your body automatically resuscitates itself; you regain a number of Hit Points equal to your level, and you don't increase the value of your wounded condition due to losing the dying condition."],["Despite the cybernetics, you are still very much a living being and within your soul beats the indomitable spirit of mortality that lets you exceed the limits of both flesh and steel. Once per day you can cast Moment of Renewal as an 8th-rank primal innate spell, targeting up to 6 living creatures within 100 feet who can hear the primal bellow affirming the nature of your heart and soul, including yourself."],["You can use your internal uplink to swiftly augment your own mind and memory by rapidly accessing databases. You gain the Open-Source Research skill feat. Your Open-Source Research has a frequency of once per 10 minutes, rather than once per hour."],["Your body is coated in microscopic plates specially treated to resist a specific kind of damage. You gain resistance equal to half your level to one damage type of your choice from the following options: acid, bludgeoning, cold, electricity, fire, piercing, slashing, or sonic."],["Your body has a hardpoint, hidden away in an internal compartment within one of your arms, that can hold one weapon. You gain a tactical hideaway limb for free that doesn't count against your total implant limit, except it can only hold one weapon, and this weapon must be a one-handed weapon of light Bulk or less. When you Draw this weapon, the weapon drawn is integrated into your body and can't be disarmed, dropped, or stolen. These effects last until you stow the weapon in the hideaway compartment.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Thresher KO-1 Frame lineage feat, the weapon can instead be a one-handed weapon of 1 Bulk or less."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYour limbs are fitted with advanced hydraulic pistons to increase their power, allowing you to exert more force using your arms, legs, and other appendages. You gain the Quick Jump skill feat, even if you don't meet its prerequisites. In addition, your fist gains the boost d4 and tech traits, and you don't take the normal –2 circumstance penalty when making a lethal attack with your fist. When you get a critical hit with your fist, you gain the critical specialization effects of unarmed attacks."],["**Trigger** You impose the glitching condition on a tech creature, hazard, or tech equipment with a camera.\n\n---\n\nYou know how to use technological glitches and malfunctions to your advantage to disguise your presence. You become Concealed to the triggering creature, hazard, or creatures using the glitching tech item to perceive you as long as it has the glitching condition.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the X-Hat Firewalker Frame lineage feat, you become Invisible, rather than concealed."],["Through a comprehensive upgrade to your frame's operating system, your cybernetic components have been systematically replaced with biotech components cloned from your own genetic markers. You lose the tech trait and gain the biotech trait. All cybernetic augmentations you've installed in your body, and that you install in yourself in the future, lose the tech trait and gain the biotech trait."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou activate a sensor mask program installed in your body that distorts digital recordings of you. Select one of the following effects.\n\n- You become the target of a 3rd-rank Illusory Disguise spell, except the *illusory disguise* is only visible to tech creatures, tech hazards, and tech visual sensors and recording devices (such as security cameras).\n\n- You become Concealed to tech creatures, tech hazards, and tech visual sensors and recording devices (such as security cameras) for 10 minutes. You can't use this concealment to [[/act hide]] or [[/act sneak]]."],["◆to◆◆\n\n**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou move at incredible speeds, covering great distances in the blink of an eye thanks to your mostly mechanical body. Stride twice. You can increase the number of actions this activity takes to 2 to instead Stride up to four times.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the GG-OS Frame lineage feat, you additionally gain a +10-foot status bonus to your Speeds for the duration of Uncanny Dash."],["Your draconic body is a weapon. When you select this feat, you gain one of the following unarmed attacks of your choice: claw, horn, jaws, or tail. Each of these attacks is in the brawling weapon group and has the listed damage die and traits.\n\n- Claw 1d6 slashing (agile, finesse, unarmed)\n- Horn 1d6 piercing (finesse, unarmed)\n- Jaws 1d6 piercing (grapple, unarmed)\n- Tail 1d6 bludgeoning (sweep, trip, unarmed)\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these attacks, you get its critical specialization effect.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat four times. Each time you do, select a different attack from the options listed above."],["Your exhalations are infused with energy, like your dragon ancestors of old. You can exhale a 15-foot cone that deals ceil(level/2)d4 @actor.flags.system.dragonkinBreath.damageType damage (basic Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC). After using this attack, you can't use it again for 1d4 rounds. At 3rd level and every 2 levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d4.\n\n---\n\n**Special** When you select this feat, choose your breath's damage type and weapon group: acid (corrosive), bludgeoning (hammer), cold (cryo), electricity (shock), fire (flame), piercing (spear), slashing (knife), or sonic (sonic). This choice is permanent. This ability has the trait associated with the type of damage it deals."],["You're trained in skills passed down through generations of dragonkin. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Athletics and Society. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Dragonkin Lore."],["You wield weapons favored by the Skyfire Legion. You are trained with the skyfire sword, flamethrower, and machine gun. In addition, you gain access to all uncommon weapons with the dragonkin trait. For the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["You're as fearsome as a dragon. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Intimidation. If you would automatically become trained in Intimidation (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Intimidating Glare skill feat."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** You have less than one-quarter of your Hit Points remaining.\n\n---\n\nYou fight fearlessly for your friends. You gain temporary Hit Points equal to your level for 1 minute. As long as you have these temporary Hit Points, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Will saves against fear effects and a +2 circumstance bonus to your Will DC against attempts to Demoralize you."],["Your desire to protect the people you care about from harm has kindled the spark of magic in your soul, and you can share that spark with others. You can cast the Guidance and Forbidding Ward cantrips as divine innate spells at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up. Whenever you cast one of these spells on your bonded partner, you increase the range of the spell to 60 feet, rather than 30 feet."],["Your scales automatically change color to match your current temperament. This has the same effect as a Moodskin augmentation, though it doesn't count as an augmentation and doesn't count toward your implant limit. When you select this feat, you can decide which colors correspond to each mood. Your keen awareness of your mood grants you a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against emotion effects. If you roll a success on a saving throw against an emotion effect, you get a critical success instead."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail a saving throw.\n\n---\n\nIn times of great stress, you can still feel the flickers of your deceased partner's heartbeat pounding in time with yours, steering you to safety or girding your mind from assault. Their spirit still protects you from beyond the grave. You can reroll the triggering saving throw and use the better result."],["You and your bonded partner have learned to physically shield one another from harm. If you would grant lesser cover to your bonded partner (including when your partner is using you as a mount), or your bonded partner would grant lesser cover to you, standard cover is granted instead."],["There's nothing you love more than soaring through the air. When you fly, you don't count moving upward (straight up or diagonally) as moving through difficult terrain. This does not apply to flying with equipment or vehicles, such as jet packs and hover boards."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes.\n\n**Trigger** Your bonded partner is within 40 feet and would be damaged by an enemy.\n\n---\n\nInstinctively sensing your bonded partner is in danger, you swoop in to save them from harm. You and your bonded partner immediately swap places with one another, teleporting into one another's locations. The damage that would be dealt to your bonded partner is dealt to you instead."],["While some claim you're incapable of forming a partner bond as deep as other dragonkin can, it's undeniable that you have more flexibility and freedom when it comes to bonding. You can maintain any number of partner bonds at once. Your bonded partners don't automatically count as being bonded with one another."],["**Requirements** You are adjacent to an ally or your ally is riding you and you have one or more hands free.\n\n---\n\nYou use your innate strength to hurl an ally across the battlefield. Pick up an adjacent ally of your size or smaller and throw them to an unoccupied space you can see within 20 feet, or within 40 feet if you throw your bonded partner. Their movement doesn't trigger reactions. Your ally ends this movement on their feet and treats the fall as 20 feet lower, or 40 feet lower if you throw your bonded partner."],["When push comes to shove, you're more than willing to give your life in place of an ally's. You gain Spirit Link as a 3rd-rank divine innate spell. You can cast this spell once per day. If you cast this spell on your bonded partner, spirit link is heightened to 4th-rank and you can increase the range of spirit link to 60 feet, rather than 30 feet."],["You trust that your deceased bonded partner is with you, even from beyond the grave. You can use Spirit's Protection once per hour, rather than once per day."],["**Trigger** You and your bonded partner roll the same skill for initiative, but get different results.\n\n---\n\nYou and your bonded partner act in utter synchronicity with one another, reacting to danger and entering battle as one. You and your bonded partner use the higher result between your initiative rolls, but use the lower Perception or skill modifier."],["When you use Dragonkin Breath, a creature who fails or critically fails its saving throw takes 2d6 persistent @actor.flags.system.dragonkinBreath.damageType damage of the same type. On a critical failure, the flat check to remove persistent damage increases to DC 20 (or DC 15, if the flat check would be reduced because the creature has an appropriate type of help). If you apply a critical weapon specialization effect that also deals persistent damage of the same type, apply this persistent damage in addition to the base persistent damage."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Requirements** You and your bonded partner are on the same planet.\n\n---\n\nWith a centering breath, you fill your mind with thoughts of your bonded partner and will yourself to their side. You teleport into an unoccupied space of your choice adjacent to your bonded partner. If there is no adjacent space available, you teleport into the closest unoccupied space."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou undergo a rapid physical change, increasing in size to rival dragonkin of the ancient past. You grow to size Huge. Your equipment grows with you, but it returns to its natural size if removed or dropped. Your reach increases by 5 feet (or by 10 feet if you are a shipborn dragonkin), and you gain a +4 status bonus to melee damage. This transformation lasts for 10 minutes. You can end this transformation early as a single action that has the concentrate trait."],["The intensity of your draconic breath lays waste to the environment and your foes. When you use Dragonkin Breath, the area of your breath becomes difficult terrain for 1 minute. Any creature that enters the area of your dragonkin breath or is occupying your breath's area at the end of its turn takes 4d6 @actor.flags.system.dragonkinBreath.damageType damage of the same type (basic Reflex save against the same DC as your dragonkin breath)."],["**Requirements** You have a bonded partner.\n\n---\n\nSince becoming bonded with your partner, you've learned a lot about them, and you're beginning to pick up their habits, interests, and knowledge. You gain the Adopted Ancestry, but you must select the ancestry of your bonded partner. You also gain one 1st-level ancestry feat from the ancestry you chose for Adopted Ancestry.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You must have a permanent partner bond to select this feat, meaning you can't be a mercurial dragonkin."],["Whether by catching a current or pushing yourself beyond your limits, you fly forward incredibly fast. Fly up to three times. If you are a stormrider dragonkin, instead you Fly up to four times."],["You've adapted your own body to suit your needs. The total number of augmentations you can install is increased by two."],["You and your bonded partner have learned the ancient art of dragonriding. Your bonded partner can ride you if they are one size category smaller than you (Medium size, for most dragonkin), rather than needing to be two size categories smaller. When your bonded partner rides you as a mount, your synchronicity enables them to gain three actions at the start of their turn, rather than the two they normally would for riding another PC. You still gain only two actions at the start of your turn, rather than three."],["**Requirements** You're adjacent to at least two of your allies.\n\n---\n\nYou instinctively understand how your allies act and move, and use that knowledge in the heat of combat to adopt a defensive formation that better shields you from harm. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC and Reflex saving throws. If one of these adjacent allies is your bonded partner, that bonded partner gains the same benefit that you do. This benefit lasts until you are no longer adjacent to at least two of your allies."],["Your mind and body have the resilience of your dragon progenitors. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against fear effects, sleep effects, and effects that would cause you to become Paralyzed. This bonus increases to +2 against spells and magic items that have these effects."],["Like the heroes who inspire you, you rally yourself to persevere against death itself. When you use Heroic Last Stand, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to twice your level for 1 minute, rather than equal to your level for 1 minute."],["**Requirements** Your last action was a successful Shove.\n\n---\n\nYou use your size and strength to push and position your enemies around the battlefield. You attempt to Trip the creature you successfully Shoved, even if the target is no longer in your reach. If you have a tail attack, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Trip attempt."],["**Trigger** You, your bonded partner, or both you and your bonded partner would roll a Will saving throw against a spell or effect that could impose the Confused or controlled condition.\n\n**Requirements** You and your bonded partner are within 60 feet of one another, and are willing.\n\n---\n\nYou and your bonded partner are two halves of the same spirit, entwined together in different bodies. Both you and your bonded partner roll the triggering Will saving throw. The triggering creature (or creatures) uses the higher result. Both you and your bonded partner are affected by the triggering spell or effect, even if it would normally only affect one of you."],["Your ability to fly through the skies under your own power is unparalleled. Your fly Speed increases by 10 feet."],["You have an impressive sense of smell, passed down through the generations from a dragon ancestor. You gain imprecise scent with a range of 40 feet. The GM might double the range if you're downwind from the creature or halve the range if you're upwind, at their discretion."],["You fight hardest when the odds are at their most dire, and the specter of death looms over you. As long as you have temporary Hit Points from Heroic Last Stand, your Strikes and spells deal additional damage. You gain a status bonus to damage with your Strikes equal to the number of weapon damage dice. Spells you cast from spell slots gain a status bonus to damage equal to the level of the spell; this bonus applies only to spells that deal damage and don't have a duration."],["The magical spark you use to protect others grows in power. You can cast Share Life and Status as 2nd-rank divine innate spells, once per day each."],["As long as you and your bonded partner are on the same plane of existence and both alive, you can communicate telepathically together and both remain aware of one another's present state, general direction and distance from one another, and if they are conscious, Unconscious, or dying. You both know any conditions affecting one another, except those that the affected character does not know about."],["Your ability to bear your bonded partner into battle has further improved, and you act as one body and one mind. When your bonded partner rides you as a mount, you gain three actions at the start of your turn, rather than the two you normally would."],["Your ability to breathe energy is unparalleled. The area of your Dragonkin Breath increases to a 30-foot cone and the damage dice are d6s instead of d4s. If you have the critical specialization effect of any weapon, a creature that gets a critical failure on their Reflex save against your dragonkin breath are affected by its corresponding critical weapon specialization effect."],["Your magical spark wards your allies, protecting them from attacks. You can cast Sanctuary as a 1st-rank divine innate spell once per day. You can cast the spell as a reaction triggered when your bonded partner is the target of an attack, as long as your partner is within 40 feet and you can perceive them and their attacker. If you do, the spell has a range of 40 feet and can target only your bonded partner."],["You've learned to carry additional supplies using your talons. You gain the Hefty Hauler skill feat. If you already have this feat, instead increase your maximum and encumbered Bulk limits by 2. While floating or flying you may use your feet as an additional pair of hands, but only to carry up to 4 Bulk of creatures or items beyond your maximum encumbrance."],["Dwarves who have spent their lives aboard orbital clanholdings or Star Citadels find themselves at ease in low gravity environments. You aren't Off-Guard or Clumsy due to being Untethered in zero-g. At 13th level, you gain a climb Speed of 20 feet while in low gravity or zero-g."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nIn a universe of optimists, dwarves can be down-to-earth grumps. If you spend more than 1 minute grumbling or grousing, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the next skill check you make within a minute of your continued grumbling."],["Your squat form and low center of gravity make you remarkably sturdy. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to [[/act force-open]], [[/act reposition]], and [[/act shove]] as well as to your Fortitude DCs against attempts to Reposition and Shove you. When you succeed at an Athletics check to Reposition or Shove, you get a critical success instead."],["You have learned magic common among questbound dwarves that focuses on Torag's lessons and the New Quest for Sky. You gain the ancestry feats Ancestral Cantrip (divine; Seek the Stars) and Ancestral Cantrip (divine; Shield)."],["You know how to effectively hurl yourself like a cannonball directly into your opponents. You Stride twice in a straight line, dealing 4))d8 bludgeoning damage to each creature in your path (basic Reflex save against your class or spell DC, whichever is higher). You move until you meet an obstruction or finish Striding twice. The damage increases to 6d8 at level 16 and 8d8 at level 19.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have Dwarven Zero-G Familiarity, enemies have a –2 circumstance penalty to their Reflex saves against your Gravity Hammer in low or zero gravity. You can also Push Off instead of Striding, using a creature in the line to Push Off."],["You drill through the earth with great speed. During your daily preparations, select an implement you use for mining, like a pick, drill, laser, or razing weapon. You gain a burrow Speed of 15 feet while holding or wielding the item, or 20 feet if the item expends ammunition or charges when used."],["Your clan crystal glows and expands, coating you in the ores found in the crust of the planet you were born nearest to.\n\nYou can cast Cairn Form twice per day as a 6th-rank primal innate spell. You resemble the statue found on your clan crystal when you do so. While in cairn form, increase the damage die size of your clan crystal weapon by one step, and double your resistance to laser weapons and effects with the light trait."],["Heightened gravity barely affects you thanks to your sturdy body. Ignore the effects of high and extreme gravity on your carrying capacity, falling damage, jumping distance, and Speed.\n\nYou don't take bludgeoning damage every minute in extreme gravity. Additionally, while in high gravity, your first weapon Strike each round that uses a melee weapon that deals bludgeoning, slashing, or piercing damage gains a status bonus to damage equal to the number of weapon damage dice (or twice the number of weapon damage dice in extreme gravity)."],["The universe is nothing like the simulation you once lived in, but you refuse to stay in the past. You gain the Untrained Improvisation general feat. In addition, you can attempt skill actions that normally require you to be trained even if you're untrained."],["The Quest for Sky caused many wars between orcs and dwarves in the past, but now, you're the only ones who can truly understand each other. You've spent time around orcs and learned from them, and you proudly count yourself among their friends.\n\nYou gain the Adopted Ancestry general feat and must select orc as the feat's chosen ancestry. You also gain one 1st-level Orc ancestry feat."],["You're a creditor who has done business with many, many debtors. You can Earn Income using Intimidation as long as you're in a settlement or other area where your debtors have access to you. When you Earn Income using Intimidation, you spend no time gathering money; instead, it's delivered to you by a debtor at the end of the day, allowing you to simultaneously perform other downtime activities as long as you can still spend a few minutes every hour interacting with your debtors (such as Earning an Income by running a bar or Retraining at a gymnasium).\n\n---\n\n*SFS Note:* This feat can be used in downtime, but takes the normal amount of downtime."],["Honor is the pillar of traditional dwarven ideals. When someone Lies to you, you automatically roll a secret Perception check to [[/act sense-motive]] against them. You also gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks to [[/act make-an-impression]] on creatures that value truth and respect the honor of your word.\n\n---\n\n**Special** Hryngar culture cares less for honor but teaches to capitalize on its absence. If you have the Deep Space Hryngar heritage, you instead gain the bonus to Make an Impression on individuals who value crime and deceit."],["You remember tales of legendary dwarven heroes who battled spacefaring dragon raiders, and you keep their epic deeds alive in your heart.\n\nSelect a magical tradition. When you successfully Strike against a dragon, you gain a circumstance bonus to your damage equal to the number of weapon damage dice. This bonus increases to double the number of weapon damage dice if your target dragon has the trait associated with the magical tradition you selected when you gained this feat."],["You don't plan to die—instead, you're going to exist forever as a necrovite. You live by the Song of Silence and have spent time investigating undead organizations and studying the processes required to make the final transition into undeath. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus on checks to Recall Knowledge about undead creatures, the Corpse Fleet, and Eox. You also learn the Necril language."],["You recite a memorable catchphrase or monologue delivered by a famous media character. Attempt a Media Lore or Performance check against the Will DC of a single enemy within 30 feet.\n\nYou can target up to two targets within range if you have expert proficiency in Media Lore or Performance, four if you're a master, and eight if you're legendary.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target takes a –1 status penalty to Perception checks and Will saves for 1 minute.\n\nDramatic Reading (Critical Success)\n\n**Success** The target takes a –1 status penalty to Perception checks and Will saves for 1 round.\n\nDramatic Reading (Success)\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is temporarily immune to Dramatic Reading for 1 hour."],["You enhance your performances with delightful magical tricks, going far beyond normal sleight of hand. Choose one cantrip from the following list: Adhere, Figment, Prestidigitation, or Telekinetic Hand. You can cast this cantrip as an arcane innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. If you do, you must select a different cantrip."],["Your people's dwindling numbers hasn't stopped you from learning everything there is to know about your ancestral past. You are trained in Arcana and Society. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Elebrian Lore."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nAll the world is a stage and you know the script—you anticipate the direction of the scene and then change it up on your opponents. You can choose to roll twice and take the better result, substituting Performance for the statistic you would normally use for initiative."],["Life often imitates art, and you've learned to deploy your dramatic training in dangerous situations, whether it's using your talent for pratfalls to cushion a real drop or faking out an enemy with your improv antics. You gain the Feign Death feat, ignoring the prerequisites. In addition, you can use Performance instead of Deception to [[/act create-a-diversion skill=performance]]."],["You like to live as the character you're playing, which makes your performances incredibly convincing. Whenever you would critically fail a Deception check to Impersonate, you fail instead."],["You've practiced enough with prop replica weapons that you can draw on these experiences in a real fight. Select a common advanced or martial weapon. You have familiarity with this weapon for the purposes of proficiency, and you treat this advanced weapon as a martial weapon, or martial weapon as a simple weapon.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with this weapon, you get its critical specialization effect."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou've played many roles and picked up a surprising amount of eclectic knowledge while preparing to play them. Roll any [[/act recall-knowledge skill=performance]] check using Performance instead of Lore."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You're about to roll a saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYou've performed countless risky stunts and flashy tricks for an audience, and your uncanny luck always seems to keep you safe. For the triggering saving throw, you can roll twice and take the better result."],["Performing for an audience has made you aware of your surroundings. You're always looking for ways to use the scenery to your advantage, setting yourself up to show your best angle to the world—or hide it! You always gain an additional +1 status bonus when you Take Cover."],["Your intense magical studies have taught you how to watch out for signs of magic even when looking for other things. When you're Searching, you also gain the benefits of the Detect Magic exploration activity unless you choose not to."],["Thanks to years of practice, you know how to use every inch of the stage and give a fantastic performance even in tight quarters. While you can act, you aren't Off-Guard to Hidden, Undetected, or flanking creatures of your level or lower."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou played a leading role in a long-running, popular production, and you frequently like to fall back on this character to get through difficult situations. You can roll a Performance check in place of a skill check to accomplish any other task."],["You've reached the pinnacle of necrovite training available to living creatures. You've crafted an electroencephalon, a type of high-tech soul cage designed to preserve your existence, and you've begun your mystical preparations for your final transition into undeath. You gain void healing and immunity to death effects, disease, and poison. You gain resistance 5 to cold and physical damage. When you die, your soul immediately transfers to your electroencephalon."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou consistently rehearse your best bits so that you're always ready for an encore. During this turn, the next action you take can be an ability with a frequency of once per day and that you've used only once today. This doesn't allow you to reuse spell slots or abilities from 20th-level feats or features."],["Your arcane aptitude grows as you learn how to better entrance an audience with magic. Choose one 1st-rank spell from the following list: Charm, Glow Up, Illusory Disguise, or Ventriloquism. You can cast this spell as an arcane innate spell once per day.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. If you do, you must select a different spell."],["Your stage experience has taught you how to improvise in just about any situation, and you know how to share your insight with others. You gain the Untrained Improvisation general feat. In addition, you gain the Once More with Feeling action."],["Your studies as a necrovite have progressed, and you've learned how to influence mindless undead. You can use Diplomacy to [[/act make-an-impression]] on mindless undead or [[/act request]] simple tasks of them. If the undead creature is controlled by a creature with a higher level than yours, you typically need a critical success on your Diplomacy skill check."],["Just like giving an encore performance of one of your most iconic roles, you learn how to better use your training off the set. You can now use Role Repertoire once per hour instead of once per day."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYour training has enhanced your memory for magic, and spells linger in your mind. You can cast one spell you've already cast today without expending a spell slot."],["Choose one 3rd-rank or lower arcane spell. You can cast that spell as a 3rd-rank arcane innate spell once per day. If this is your 13th-level ancestry feat, instead choose a 5th-rank or lower arcane spell, and you can cast it as a 5th-rank arcane innate spell once per day. If this is your 17th-level ancestry feat, instead choose a 7th-rank or lower arcane spell, and you can cast it as a 7th-rank arcane innate spell once per day.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. If you do, you must select a different spell."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** You're critically hit by an attack.\n\n---\n\nWhen Eox's atmosphere burned, necrovites crafted devices called electroencephalons in order to house their souls and transition themselves into undead beings who could survive the eons since that cataclysmic event. You've learned the basics of this technology and have crafted a similar device. Attempt a DC 10 flat check. On a success, the triggering hit becomes a normal hit."],["Whether through magical training, a technomagical body rig, or superior escape and evasion training, you've managed to learn how to fade from plain sight. You can cast Invisibility as a 2nd-rank arcane innate spell twice per day, but the spell has a duration of only 5 minutes each time."],["You've trained hard to tackle physical challenges of all types as part of your entertainment career. You gain a climb Speed or a swim Speed equal to your land Speed.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once."],["By activating your arcane sensory organ and analyzing ancestral memories and arcane lore, you can communicate with all kinds of people, animals, and even plants. You gain Speak with Animals, Speak with Plants, and Translate as 3rd-rank arcane innate spells. You can cast each spell once per day."],["You're one of the forlorn, and the centuries you've spent away from Castrovel have helped you understand how other species live and how to move among them without drawing undue attention.\n\nYou become trained in Society. If you would automatically become trained in Society (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain the Blend In skill feat."],["You conceal your face behind a mask while in mixed company, showing yourself only among other elves. The blank expression of your mask makes it difficult for others to read into your motives.\n\nYou become trained in Deception. If you would automatically become trained in Deception (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain the Lie to Me skill feat."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You're about to attempt a saving throw against an enemy's ability.\n\n**Requirements** You believed the triggering enemy was your ally within the last hour.\n\n---\n\nYou understand deeply that others can never be trusted. Reroll the triggering saving throw. You must use the second result, even if it's worse.\n\n---\n\n*SFS Note:* Change the last sentence to “You roll the triggering saving throw twice and use the better result.”"],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail a skill check or saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYou were alive during the Gap, but like everyone else, you remember nothing from that time. You're haunted by centuries of lost experiences that shaped you into a form you can't identify. Reroll the triggering check, but you must use the new result, even if it's worse. You become Frightened 1."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou Step and create a burst of brilliant, scintillating light in a 5-foot burst centered on one corner of your previous space. Other creatures in the area must attempt a Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. On a failure, a creature is Blinded and Dazzled for 1 round. On a critical failure, they're blinded for 2 rounds and dazzled for 1 minute."],["When your enemies have you cornered, you become ever more vicious. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that deals damage to a single target, and if that spell doesn't have a duration, you gain a circumstance bonus to its damage equal to twice the sum of your Frightened and Wounded conditions (to a maximum of +12) if you have one or both conditions."],["**Trigger** You Swear Vengeance.\n\n---\n\nYou riposte as you're almost brought low. Make a single Strike against the triggering creature. If this Strike brings a foe to 0 Hit Points, the triggering activation of Swear Vengeance doesn't count against its frequency, and your Wounded condition decreases by 1."],["You can ride the waves of energy left in the wake of your spells. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that targets a creature within 60 feet, you teleport to an open space adjacent to the spell's target."],["You have spent more of your life away from elven communities than you have within them and have grown accustomed to living surrounded by other species. You've buried more non-elven friends than most elves will make across their entire lifetimes, and you will carry the memories of these friends for centuries.\n\nDuring your daily preparations, you can reminisce about a lost friend, gaining the Assurance skill feat for one skill you're trained in. This lasts until you prepare again. Since this skill feat is temporary, you can't use it to satisfy a prerequisite for a permanent character option."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou don't trust others and are always ready to move when a situation sours. You Stride up to half your Speed."],["The hottest socials on the infosphere might change with time, but the way those spaces fill up with drama and gossip is a truth that lasts forever. Luckily, you've been saving every embarrassing holo and compromising remark you've found on the infosphere to your personal archives for centuries.\n\nYou can roll a Computers check instead of an Intimidation check when you use the [[/act coerce skill=computers]] action, threatening to share copies of an embarrassing infosphere moment from the target's past. On a success, in addition to the normal effects of Coerce, the target is temporarily immune to any additional Coerce attempts from you for 24 hours. On a failure, they're instead immune for 1 week, and on a critical failure, they're immune for 1 month."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You're damaged by an attack.\n\n---\n\nElves might be under attack from all sides metaphorically, but you don't intend to let that be the case for you literally. You Step away from the triggering attacker. If an effect with an Escape DC prevents you from Stepping, you can attempt to [[/act escape]] the effect instead."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You would be reduced to 0 Hit Points but not immediately killed by a creature you're aware of.\n\n---\n\nYou swear vengeance against the creature who almost brought you down, committing yourself to their destruction. You avoid being knocked out and remain at 1 Hit Point, and your Wounded condition increases by 1. You also become Quickened for 1 round and can use the extra action to Stride toward or make a Strike against the triggering creature."],["Your body's natural secretions cover your tracks. Outside of an urban environment, you're always considered to be Covering Tracks, even if you chose a different activity in exploration mode. You take a –2 circumstance penalty to Cover Tracks in an urban environment due to your messy footsteps."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou can Stride and move through spaces of any creatures in your path. Any creature your size or smaller whose space you move through can attempt a Reflex save against your Athletics DC to avoid being engulfed. A creature unable to act automatically critically fails this save. If a creature succeeds at its save, it can choose to either be pushed aside or pushed in front of you at the end of your movement. You can only attempt to Gooey Engulf the same creature once per turn. You can contain as many creatures as can fit in your space.\n\nA creature that fails its save is pulled into your body. It's Grabbed and Slowed 1, and it must hold its breath or start suffocating. The creature takes 1d6 acid damage at the end of each of its turns while engulfed (this damage can be improved by hardlight handwraps as though it were an unarmed attack). An engulfed creature can get free by [[/act escape dc=athletics]]{Escaping} against your Athletics DC. An engulfed creature can attack you but only with an unarmed attack or weapons of light Bulk or less. You're Off-Guard against these attacks. If you take piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding one fourth of your remaining Hit Points from a single attack or spell, the engulfed creature cuts itself free. A creature that gets free by either method can immediately breathe and exits your space. If you fall asleep, are knocked Unconscious, or die, all creatures you've engulfed are automatically released."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail a Will saving throw against a mental effect.\n\n---\n\nYou bolster your host's mental defenses. Reroll the triggering saving throw and use the better result."],["You've awakened dormant psychic abilities in your host by unlocking atrophied sensory and nervous organs. Choose one cantrip that has the fungus or plant trait or is from the occult spell list. You can cast this cantrip as an occult innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["You can grow into an enormous fungal beast. Once per day, you can cast Plant Form as a 5th-rank primal innate spell. When you reach 17th level, you can heighten the spell to 6th rank when you cast it. When you cast this spell, you gain the following special abilities:\n\n- **Speed** 30 feet\n\n- **Resistances** acid 10, poison 10\n\n- **Melee** ◆ tendril (reach 20 feet), **Damage** 2d6 bludgeoning plus Grab.\n\n- Targets Grabbed by your tendril take 2d4 persistent poison damage."],["You can permanently merge with a willing or destroyed creature with the tech trait. If the creature is mindless, it gains awareness and can choose whether to accept the symbiosis (depending on the circumstances gauged by the GM or determined by a DC 10 flat check).\n\nIf you succeed, you can no longer use Tactical Symbiosis, but you gain basic environmental protections, protection against extreme cold and extreme heat, and a +3 status bonus to saves against disease, poison, and radiation. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Disguise yourself as the creature you merged with, and you can communicate with your host's kin and other compatible models likely serving the same function or built by the same manufacturer, as though you'd cast Speak with Computers."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You're reduced to 0 Hit Points and would gain the Dying condition or would otherwise die.\n\n**Requirements** You have a willing host.\n\n---\n\nIn a final act of bravery and gratitude, your host has decided that preserving your gift of intelligence is more important than preserving itself. Your host prevents you from dying and takes the brunt of whatever force would cause you to die, allowing your body to absorb its rapidly decaying form and regain Hit Points equal to 6d8 plus half your level. If the cause of your death was a condition or effect that would still cause you to die after regaining Hit Points, such as a high value on the doomed condition, you lose the condition or effect as the host creature dies in your stead. You lose the benefits of your heritage and any ancestry feats that require your heritage or having a host until you can find and merge with another host."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou use some of your host's energy to trigger immense growth in your mycelium network, growing a protective layer of tough, oozy fungus. For 1 minute, you gain a +2 status bonus to AC and resistance 10 to physical damage, and are Clumsy 1. If you gain Hit Points or temporary Hit Points while this ability is active, until the end of your next turn, you deal an additional 2d6 poison damage with all your unarmed melee Strikes."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Requirements** You're adjacent to the corpse of a foe who has been dead for no longer than 1 minute.\n\n---\n\nYou gain nourishment from consuming decaying matter. You gain temporary Hit Points equal to the creature's level that last for 1 minute."],["You allow your spores to spread. The ground in your square becomes difficult terrain for all non-fungi creatures for 1 minute. If you're already in a square affected by Entangling Mycelium, the fungus spreads and all non-diagonal adjacent squares become difficult terrain for 1 minute."],["The fungal caps all over your body release toxic spores when disturbed. Each time you become Grabbed by a creature or an adjacent creature hits you with an attack, you deal 2)))) poison damage to that creature. This damage increases to 3 at 9th level, 4 at 13th level, and 5 at 17th level."],["You can connect with other minds, even if they aren't your host's. You can cast Mindlink as a 1st-rank occult innate spell twice per day."],["You can instantly merge with a creature you summon. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that summons a minion, you merge with the minion instead of summoning them. This works like Animal Form, except your form's Size, Speeds, AC, senses, attacks, and Athletics modifiers are identical to the summoned creature (you don't gain temporary Hit Points). If you're reduced to 0 Hit Points while merged with your summoned minion, the effect ends, and you return to your normal self with half as many Hit Points as you originally had when you first merged with your summoned minion."],["**Requirements** Your target is larger than you.\n\n---\n\nYou cling to a target with a sticky grasp. Attempt an Athletics check against the target's Fortitude DC.\n\n**Critical Success** The target is Blinded until the end of your next turn, unless you move or your target Escapes. If the target moves, you move with them.\n\n**Success** The target is Dazzled until the end of your next turn, unless you move or your target Escapes. If the target moves, you move with them.\n\n**Failure** You miss the target.\n\n**Critical Failure** You miss the target and land Prone."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou spew a dense cloud of fungal spores. Plants and fungi are immune to this effect, but all other creatures in a 10-foot emanation must attempt a Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC with the following results.\n\n**Critical Success** No effect.\n\n**Success** The creature is Dazzled for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The creature is dazzled and can see only 10 feet away for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is Blinded for 1 round."],["Your potent psychic powers have steadily grown as you and your host's minds merge and evolve, granting you additional magic. Choose one 1st-rank or 2nd-rank spell with the fungus or plant trait or from the occult spell list. You can cast that spell as a 2nd-rank occult innate spell once per day."],["**Requirements** You're holding or adjacent to an unattended tech object.\n\n---\n\nYou have learned how to adapt your thought patterns to that of a tech device and can merge with a tech object to understand what it knows. This allows you to learn what the computer knows as if you spent an hour scanning the computer or engaging it in a conversation using Speak with Computers. You can [[/act hack]] the computer to access protected systems without needing a hacking toolkit and can Hack using [[/act hack skill=diplomacy]]{Diplomacy} or [[/act hack skill=nature]]{Nature} instead of Computers. If the targeted object is an augmentation, you implant the augmentation."],["While you've got just as many emotions as other people, you've got an entire brain dedicated to keeping them under control so they don't interfere with the rest of your brains. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saves against emotion effects, and if you roll a success on a save against an emotion effect, you get a critical success instead."],["You've dedicated a few extra brains to control more than the typical number of armlike appendages for a fonqugon. You have four \"arms,\" which allows you to wield and hold up to four hands' worth of weapons and equipment. At any time, one pair of \"hands\" is designated as your active hands. You can change this designation from one pair of hands to another by taking the Switch Hands action. You can wield items only with your active hands."],["You've got a brain or two that can control especially long or nimble \"legs\" or otherwise give you increased locomotion. Your Speed increases by 5 feet."],["Your knowledge of a specific subject is especially reliable thanks to the brain you've dedicated to thinking about it. You gain the Additional Lore feat and the Assurance feat for the chosen Lore. Once per day when you forgo rolling a skill check using Assurance for the associated Lore, you can choose to receive a result of 13 + your proficiency bonus (instead of 10 + your proficiency bonus)."],["While all fonqugons are children of the fonqon trees, you're a rare fonqugon whose gestation took place over the course of 17 days instead of the typical seven, which often occurs when a fonqon tree is in especially dire circumstances. As such, you're much more connected to the trees' primal magic than a typical fonqugon. Choose one cantrip from the primal spell list. You can cast this cantrip as a primal innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up.\n\nFonqugons must adapt to meet any challenge or threat that arises, and your magic is equally adaptable. By spending 1 day of downtime in a natural environment with any trees, you can change the cantrip you chose with this feat to a different primal cantrip.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat only at 1st level, and you can't retrain into this feat."],["You have an entire brain just for processing scents. You gain imprecise scent with a range of 30 feet. This means you can use your sense of smell to determine the location of a creature. The GM will usually double the range if you're downwind from the creature or halve the range if you're upwind. In addition, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks whenever you're trying to locate an Undetected creature that's within the range of your scent."],["Your body is notably resilient, even for an ooze. You gain the Diehard general feat."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You are attacked by a foe but haven't rolled yet.\n\n---\n\nIn an emergency, your especially oozy body has adapted to split into multiple pieces to survive danger. A piece of you splits off to ward off a harmful blow. The triggering attacker must attempt a DC 13 flat check; on a success, the attack targets you normally; if they fail, the attack targets the piece of you that split off, destroying it. You become Stupefied 1 and Clumsy 1 for 1 minute, after which time your body regrows the split-off part."],["You're among the most powerful scions of the fonqon trees. Choose one 3rd-rank primal spell and one 4th-rank primal spell. You can cast each of these spells once per day as primal innate spells."],["**Trigger** You're struck by a critical hit that deals energy damage or critically fail a saving throw against an effect that deals energy damage.\n\n---\n\nYou're used to taking serious amounts of damage from all kinds of extreme Rodnarth weather, from acid quakes to lightning waves. Attempt a DC 15 flat check. On a success, the triggering attack becomes a normal hit, or you fail the saving throw against the triggering effect instead of critically failing."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou put all your brains in a hyperactive state to process dangers. You become Quickened for 1 minute and can use your extra action only to Recall Knowledge, Stride, or Strike."],["When anyone asks how tough you are, all you have to say is, \"I'm from Rodnarth.\" You've survived more extreme disasters than most can count, and your body has adapted to danger by storing a small reservoir of primal energy from the fonqon trees. The first time each day you would die because of the Dying condition, your body draws on this reservoir, and you instead survive. Your remain at 1 Hit Point, and your dying value becomes 0, but you gain a wounded value equal to 1 less than the dying value that would normally kill you (typically Wounded 3)."],["Your brains are just as oozy as the rest of your \"body.\" You can move through a gap at least 2 inches wide without Squeezing and can [[/act squeeze]] through a gap at least 1 inch wide. When you're struck by a critical hit that deals physical damage, roll a DC 20 flat check. On a success, the hit becomes a normal hit."],["Even while otherwise preoccupied, you can dedicate some of your brains to scanning your environment for threats. You can cast Scan Environment as a primal innate cantrip at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up. You can cast this innate cantrip even while performing other tasks, such as resting, traveling, talking, fighting, or even casting other spells, but not while sleeping or otherwise Unconscious. Additionally, once per day when you cast *scan environment*, you can change its casting time to 1 round instead of 10 minutes."],["You can precisely control your oozy body's coagulation when you're wounded to prevent unwanted seepage. Your DC on flat checks to end persistent bleed damage is reduced from 15 to 10, or from 10 to 5 after receiving especially appropriate assistance."],["Your body is very sticky. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Fortitude and Reflex DCs against attempts to [[/act reposition]], [[/act shove]], or [[/act trip]] you. This bonus also applies to saving throws against spells or effects that attempt to force you to move or knock you Prone. In addition, if any effect would force you to move 10 feet or more, you're moved only half the distance."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou can coagulate your oozy body to respond to different types of ongoing harm. Attempt a DC 15 flat check; on a success, you recover from any ongoing persistent damage. Additionally, you gain resistance to each type of persistent damage you had when you used Adaptive Coagulation equal to half your level for 1 minute."],["You're used to threats coming out of nowhere, and you react by thinking very quickly. Attempt up to three Recall Knowledge checks. If you have any special abilities or free actions that would normally be triggered when you Recall Knowledge, you can't use them for these actions. At 13th level, you can instead attempt up to four Recall Knowledge checks. At 17th level, you can instead attempt up to five Recall Knowledge checks."],["As someone who tends to the upper branches of fonqon trees, you spend much more time climbing than most fonqugons and are much better at it. Your climb Speed increases to 20 feet, and you can Climb with your \"legs\" rather than your hands, so you have free use of your hands while Climbing and can perform tasks such as using tools or firing weapons."],["You've honed your primal connection to the fonqon trees. Choose one 1st-rank primal spell and one 2nd-rank primal spell. You can cast each of these spells once per day as primal innate spells."],["You were born from a fonqon tree that was especially suffused with primal energies. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against primal spells and effects."],["You're always prepared to help others succeed in their callings. You gain a +4 circumstance bonus on checks to Aid."],["You grew up in a colony that builds structures along the coast and in the oceans, and you've adapted to life underwater. You become trained in Athletics. If you would automatically become trained in Athletics (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain a swim Speed of 5 feet and the amphibious trait, allowing you to breathe underwater as well as in the air.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you take the Swimming Specialist ancestry feat, you gain a swim Speed of 30 feet instead of 20 feet."],["All formians use pheromones as a supplementary form of communication, and you've become especially adept at detecting scents. You gain imprecise scent with a range of 30 feet. In addition, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks whenever you're trying to locate an Undetected creature that's within the range of your scent."],["You're part of a colony that builds inside massive trees rather than below the ground. You become trained in Nature and Survival. If you would automatically become trained in Nature or Survival (such as from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain a climb Speed of 5 feet.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you take the Climbing Specialist ancestry feat, you gain a climb Speed of 30 feet instead of 20 feet."],["You understand the intricacies of architecture, especially the construction of sturdy tunnels and buildings. You become trained in Crafting. If you're already trained in Crafting, you instead gain the Specialty Crafting skill feat for architecture.\n\nYou also gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to notice dangerous structures. This bonus applies to checks to discover mechanical and environmental traps incorporated into walls, doors, ceilings, or other parts of a structure.\n\nIf you aren't using the Seek action or Searching, the GM automatically rolls a secret check for you to notice hazards incorporated into a structure anyway. This check doesn't gain your normal circumstance bonus."],["When you're stumped, you can reach out through your hive mind to access the shared knowledge of your colony. Once per day, when you attempt to Recall Knowledge with a skill you aren't trained in, you can treat your level as your proficiency bonus. Additionally, you can roll twice on the check and take the better result.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Hypertelepathy feat, you can use the skill modifier of a willing ally within range of your telepathy even if it's a skill you aren't trained in."],["Whether with subtle telepathy or your natural leadership skills, you're able to link up and move with allies more efficiently. You can March! as a single action instead of two actions."],["Except for queens, most formians possess little in the way of inherent magical ability. You're no queen, but you're in close proximity with your queen as a member of her court, and she often channels her magic through your close telepathic bond.\n\nYou can cast Force Barrage and Translocate as 4th-rank primal innate spells once per day each. For 1 minute after casting either spell, the range of your Limited Telepathy quadruples."],["You have six highly coordinated legs, so it's easy to get around the battlefield. You Step up to three times."],["You've practiced using your sensilla so much that they've developed into a permanent sensory organ. You have imprecise tremorsense with a range of 20 feet. When you Activate Sensilla, instead of its normal effect, you increase the range of your tremorsense to 100 feet until the start of your next turn."],["Formian queens are famous for their ability to psychically call upon the various components of their hive to fight, defend, or flee as they desire. You can channel your queen's telepathic power to motivate your own allies into a battle frenzy. Up to 10 willing allies within range of your telepathy become Quickened for 1 minute and can use the extra action only to Stride or Strike. While quickened in this way, they have a +2 status bonus to saving throws against mental effects.\n\nFor the Queen!"],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** An enemy within 10 feet attempts to Cast a Spell or Activate a magic item.\n\n---\n\nYou emit a burst of disruptive telepathic waves that disrupt the triggering creature's magic. Attempt a counteract check against the triggering effect; your counteract rank equals half your level (rounded up), and for the roll, use your attack roll modifier with your mageslayer claw."],["You unleash powerful telepathic feedback to assail the minds of your foes and render them unwell. Any number of enemy creatures you can sense within range of your Limited Telepathy take 14d6 mental damage with a basic Will save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. You can choose for any of these creatures to take nonlethal instead of lethal damage from Telepathic Onslaught. On a failure, creatures are also Sickened 1 (or Sickened 2 on a critical failure)."],["The Call led you far away to another planet. You gain the Adopted Ancestry general feat, and you also gain one 1st-level ancestry feat from the ancestry you chose for the Adopted Ancestry feat or the Unconventional Weaponry standardized ancestry feat."],["When you first heard the Call, you began to truly understand the meaning of beauty. Once per day, when you fail a Crafting check, Performance check, or a Lore check related to art or crafting, you can reroll the check and take the higher result."],["The Call led you to help others, whether members of your ancestral colony or friends you've made after years of swashbuckling adventures. At the start of your turn, you gain one additional reaction, which you can use only to Aid."],["The Call led you to war, whether on Castrovel or another world. When wielding a weapon you aren't proficient with, treat your level as your proficiency bonus. At 11th level, you become trained in all weapons."],["Your body generates a special biotoxin that you can deliver with your jaws. Your jaws unarmed attack deals an additional 1d4 persistent poison damage. Additionally, on a critical hit with your jaws Strike, the target must succeed at a Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC or be Enfeebled 1 for 1 round (or 1 minute on a critical failure)."],["You form up with allies and move in unison. Stride once. You can choose up to two willing allies adjacent to you at the start of your movement to move with you as a reaction. All allies end their movement adjacent to you, but not adjacent to one another, forming a line or triangle. Creatures moving with March! can't move further than the lowest Speed used by any other creature in that march."],["**Requirements** You're standing on a solid surface.\n\n---\n\nYou listen for vibrations through your legs' sensitive hairlike fibers. You gain imprecise tremorsense with a range of 20 feet until the start of your next turn."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nHelping others comes so naturally to you that you instantly prepare yourself to help your ally with a task. This counts as preparing to help an ally for the purpose of using the Aid reaction. You must still explain to the GM exactly how you're helping."],["The queen and other members of your colony are ever-present in your mind. When you roll a success on a saving throw against an effect that would directly control your actions, you get a critical success instead.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Queen's Court Formian heritage, when you roll a critical failure on a saving throw against an effect that would directly control your actions, you get a failure instead."],["Your connection to a hive mind gives you even greater telepathic potential than most other telepathic species can even dream of. Increase the range of your Limited Telepathy to 200 feet. Once per day, when you Recall Knowledge, you can use the skill modifier of a willing ally within range of your telepathy instead of your own."],["As a result of generational war between your peoples, you've trained in special antimagic techniques to battle elven and lashunta spellcasters. You gain a mageslayer claw unarmed attack that deals 1d6 slashing damage, is in the brawling weapon group, and has the finesse, primal, and unarmed traits. A creature you Strike with your mageslayer claw must attempt a Will save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. On a failure, the creature becomes Stupefied 1 for 1 minute (or Stupefied 2 on a critical failure)."],["You were born Gap-touched, have long since acclimated to your strange affliction, and can wield it more effectively than most of your peers. When you Step, you can flicker in and out of reality, causing your Step to gain the teleportation trait and allowing you to Step into Difficult Terrain."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You fail or critically fail a save against a mental effect.\n\n---\n\nThe immediate past slips from your mind, giving you some additional mental protection. Reroll the triggering save and take the second result."],["Sometimes, people forget about you, and it's happening more and more lately. Increase the DC of attempts to Gather Information on you by 1 for each Gap-touched feat you have. Additionally, you gain a +1 status bonus to Stealth checks to [[/act avoid-notice]]."],["**Frequency** once per turn\n\n---\n\nYou've learned how to harness the mechanics of the Gap to disrupt technology. You touch an adjacent object or creature with the tech trait. If the target is an unwilling creature or is held by an unwilling creature, the creature attempts a Reflex save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. On a failure, the target becomes Glitching 1. On a critical failure, the target becomes Glitching 2."],["People and machines both struggle to discern your features, making you difficult to keep track of in a crowd. You become trained in Society (or another skill of your choice if you're already trained) and gain the Blend In skill feat."],["You present evolutions distinct from any other members of your species, like your ancestors developed for an environment different than your peers, but no records indicate how or what happened to necessitate your variance. Genetic or temporal attempts to trace your family history or lineage find nothing.\n\nYou gain one 1st-level ancestry feat you qualify for from an ancestry different from yours. That ancestry feat has the Gap-touched trait for you."],["You have a deep and innate understanding of the foundations of communication as a whole. You learn an additional language. You get a +2 status bonus to Decipher Writing and can make such attempts even if you're untrained."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nWith focus, you remove yourself from videos and pictures, leaving only pixelated images and static behind. You become Concealed to all technological visual sensors, such as security cameras, ocular cybernetic augmentations, and the visual processors of technological constructs, for 1 minute."],["**Frequency** once every 2 rounds\n\n---\n\nYou forget how many shots you've taken, and for a second, so does reality. Make a Strike with a weapon you're wielding. This Strike doesn't use any ammo or battery usage. You don't apply any benefits from special ammunition to this Strike."],["You've trained to use your reality issues to your advantage in a fight. When you use Flickering Existence, you can make one Strike before or after the movement."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou can wield the Gap to muddle a creature's existence, potentially deleting them as thoroughly as if you killed them. Choose one creature within 30 feet. The target must attempt a Will save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is Slowed 1 for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The target is slowed 1 for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, and the target must attempt a Fortitude save against the same DC. If it fails, it dies. All records and memories of the creature become hazy, similar to those of the Gap. This critical failure effect has the death trait."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou vanish from existence, severing your connection to reality for a moment. You cease to exist and disappear from your space, ending all ongoing conditions or effects on you. You return to the same space (or the closest unoccupied space if the same space is then occupied) immediately before the start of your next turn. When you return, you regain any ongoing conditions or effects from before you disappeared."],["You can speak a truth about the Gap that causes you to vanish from others' perceptions temporarily. You gain Disappearance as an 8th-rank occult innate spell that you can cast only on yourself once per day."],["**Frequency** once per minute\n\n---\n\nSuddenly, you vanish and reappear in a flash of static. You Step, moving up to 10 feet instead of 5 feet."],["The distant memories of your heritage, once lost and long forgotten, begin to manifest physically. You gain a heritage from your ancestry in addition to this versatile heritage. If an ability from this new heritage conflicts with an ability from your versatile heritage, you choose which of the conflicting abilities your character has, as normal. You count as having that heritage for the purposes of qualifying for feats."],["You can manipulate and disrupt technology at a greater range. You can use Glitching Memory at a range of 60 feet."],["You understand your affliction enough to wield your inability to communicate certain things as a shield against prying eyes, adorning yourself with imagery of pre-Gap truths that are obscured to most people. You can cast Invisibility as a 2nd-rank occult innate spell three times per day, but the spell's duration becomes \"until the end of your next turn.\""],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** You become Frightened.\n\n---\n\nYou let your memory forget the immediate past to better move beyond its trauma. Reduce your frightened value by 1."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** An enemy's Strike or targeted effect would hit you.\n\n---\n\nYou try to time your temporal displacement to avoid attacks. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your AC against the triggering attack, potentially causing a successful hit into a miss or a critical success into a success. If this changes the result of the attack, you can Step up to 10 feet."],["You scrub your presence from your enemies' minds in a blast of psychic static that disorients them. You become Concealed against any number of observable creatures of your choice within 30 feet for 1 round."],["Your internal chemical balance is adaptable, allowing you to control the composition of your normally flaming expulsions. When you use Fire Breath, you can choose to deal acid or cold damage instead of fire damage.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you're a mystic with the Elemental connection, you can also choose bludgeoning, electricity, or poison damage instead of fire damage."],["You've traveled out into the stars and adapted to the void of space, allowing you to survive in lifeless conditions and operate more effectively in zero-gravity environments. You can breathe in a vacuum without environmental protection and ignore the Clumsy condition imposed by being Untethered in zero-g."],["You channel the fluids you expel into a concentrated blast of flame. When you use Fire Breath, you can choose to have it be a 30-foot line instead of a 15-foot cone."],["**Trigger** A creature targets you with a Strike, and you can see the attacker.\n\n---\n\nYou've learned a particular way of moving to disorient your foes. You scuttle to the side and gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack. If the Strike is a failure or critical failure, you can Step."],["Your shell is etched with markings that grant you a connection with the underlying truth of the cosmos. Choose one cantrip from the divine spell list. You can cast this cantrip as a divine innate spell at will. You can also cast the Implant Data cantrip as a divine innate spell at will, except when you do, the target becomes \"your shell,\" and data implanted on your shell can be accessed by any creature that knows the G'folian language. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["Your body has developed a reserve of extra chemicals that can be used to produce smaller expulsions. You gain a flame belch ranged unarmed attack with a range increment of 30 feet that deals 1d4 fire damage. When you critically succeed at a flame belch Strike, the target takes persistent fire damage equal to half your level (minimum 1). Flame belches don't add critical specialization effects. You take a –2 circumstance penalty on attacks with your flame belch if you can't use your Fire Breath.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have Admixture Breath, you can use it to change the type of damage you deal with Flame Belch."],["You constantly accumulate knowledge about philosophies and multiversal understanding. During your daily preparations, you can call upon that knowledge and gain the trained proficiency rank in two Lore skills of your choice related to philosophies, religions, or the cosmos. You might select something like Abaddon Lore and Prophecies of Kalistrade Lore or Pharasma Lore and Boneyard Lore. This proficiency lasts until you prepare again. Since this proficiency is temporary, you can't use it as a prerequisite for a skill increase or a permanent character option like a feat."],["**Trigger** You lose the Unconscious condition.\n\n---\n\nNatural instincts take over as you wake from a torpor or unconsciousness. You Stand. This movement doesn't trigger reactions."],["Your legs can bend and retract to let you make ample use of odd sources of cover. You can [[/act take-cover]] as though you were Prone even while standing."],["The writing on your shell has evolved to become a divine script, either to a deity or to a philosophy unto itself. Depending on the spell you selected for Repository of Divinity, you become sanctified and gain either the holy or unholy trait (holy for Summon Celestial, or unholy for Summon Fiend). Your Fire Breath gains the sanctified trait, and you can choose to deal spirit damage instead of fire damage."],["Your stomach contents can become especially toxic to outsiders. When you use Fire Breath, you can choose to deal poison damage instead of fire damage. If a creature fails its Reflex save against your Fire Breath when it deals poison damage, it becomes Sickened 1 (Sickened 2 on a critical failure).\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have Purge Stomach, you can still use your Fire Breath while under the effects of Purge Stomach as long as you choose to deal poison damage."],["Your immense shell has the capability to mount weapons of destructive power like other species might wield in their arms. You count as having an additional pair of arms that can only be used to hold a single two-handed weapon. This weapon is implanted as an augmentation but doesn't count toward your implant limit and can be removed with an Interact action."],["You vent the contents of your stomach while spinning in place, unleashing a cloud of your internal gases in a 30-foot emanation. This functions as Fire Breath, except that the damage dice are d10s instead of d4s. Creatures that fail their Reflex saves against this effect are also Dazzled for 1 round. You can't use Fire Breath for 1 minute."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou channel your internal chemicals to enhance your shell, turning it into an additional layer of temporary protection. For 1 minute, you gain a +2 status bonus to AC and resistance 10 to physical damage, but you take a –10-foot status penalty to your Speeds."],["Your understanding of the underlying nature of the multiverse allows you to call into question the existence of other beings. Once per day, you can cast Death Sentence as an 8th-rank divine innate spell."],["Your massive pincer can crush your foes and never let go. Your pincer unarmed attack deals 1d8 damage instead of 1d6 and gains the versatile S trait."],["Your shell is structured in such a way to allow for easier movement of objects. Increase your maximum and encumbered Bulk limits by 4. You can rest normally while wearing medium armor."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You gain the Sickened condition or fail a save against an ingested poison.\n\n**Requirements** You can use Fire Breath.\n\n---\n\nThanks to control of your stomach, you can expel foreign substances in your body with ease. Reduce your sickened condition by 2, and immediately attempt a saving throw with a +2 circumstance bonus against any ingested poisons you've been exposed to within the last minute. You can't use Fire Breath for 1d4 rounds."],["**Trigger** A creature fails its Reflex save against your Fire Breath.\n\n---\n\nYour flames are a fearsome sight to behold, blazing through all who oppose you. Choose one creature that failed its Reflex save against your Fire Breath. Attempt an Intimidation check to [[/act demoralize]] that enemy; you don't take a penalty for not sharing a language."],["Your exoskeleton shell has further merged with your body, granting you more bodily space for enhancements. Increase the number of augmentations you can have implanted by 2."],["Increase the circumstance bonus to AC for Crab Walk to +2. In addition, when you Crab Walk, you can Stride up to half your Speed instead of Stepping if the triggering attack fails to hit you, and when you do, Crab Walk gains the traversal trait."],["You can protect yourself against effects associated with the fundamental foundations of the cosmos. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to all saving throws against divine effects."],["The writings on your shell expand to include a vast array of knowledge about the entities found across the multiverse. Choose either Summon Celestial or Summon Fiend. Once per day, you can cast the chosen spell as a divine innate spell heightened to half your level rounded up. The creature summoned must match the theme of the philosophical treatises marked on your shell, such as a creature with the angel trait if your treatise is on enlightenment achieved through virtuous acts."],["The flame from your Fire Breath now lingers on targets. When a target fails its save against your Fire Breath, it also takes 1d6 persistent fire damage. The damage increases to 2d6 at 13th level and 3d6 at 17th level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you use Admixture Breath to change the damage type of your Fire Breath, the persistent damage changes to match the new damage type."],["You overexert your internal hydraulics for a burst of speed. You Stride with a +10-foot circumstance bonus to your Speed. When your movement ends, you become Suppressed until the end of your next turn. You can't use this feat while suppressed."],["You mix your resin with other chemicals to make yourself repellent to specific attackers. When you select this feat, choose one trait from among animal, beast, celestial, dragon, elemental, fey, fiend, fungus, giant, ooze, plant, spirit, undead, or any ancestry trait, such as human or ysoki. Any creature with that trait that starts its turn within a 10-foot emanation of you or attacks you with a jaws attack must succeed at a Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC or become Sickened 1 (Sickened 2 on a critical failure). A creature that succeeds at its save is temporarily immune to all foul fragrance auras for 24 hours. You can change which trait you choose by spending 1 day of downtime adjusting your internal chemistry."],["You are closely connected to ancient gnarefuroid colonies and know how your species survived eons in a hostile universe. You become trained in Crafting and Survival. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Gnarefuroid Lore."],["You've incorporated detritus and adhesive resin to your body to build temporary layers to your shell. As part of your daily preparations, you create either one commercial Compact Shield or one commercial Carbon Shield from detritus and your excretions. This shield can't be sold, repaired, upgraded, or altered in any way, and it disintegrates when you next make your daily preparations. You can use the Shield Block reaction with this shield."],["You produce abundant adhesive resin. You become trained in Athletics. If you're already trained in Athletics (from your background or class, for example), you become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Fortitude or Reflex DC against attempts to [[/act shove]] or [[/act reposition]] you. Additionally, you gain the Goo Grab reaction."],["Your tendrils have barbs that can deliver toxins. You gain a tendril unarmed attack that deals 1d6 poison damage in the dart weapon group and has the agile, finesse, injection, and unarmed traits.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with this attack, you get its critical specialization effect."],["Your time spent stuck to the hull of a traveling starship has made you hypersensitive to even the faintest traces of light. You gain darkvision."],["Your body instinctively integrates foreign materials. You gain the Augmented Body general feat. If the chosen augmentation deals damage, increase that damage by 1 for every two augmentations you have (minimum 1). If the chosen augmentation gives you resistance to damage or has Hardness, increase it by 1 for every two augmentations you have (minimum 1)."],["Your resin contains a protective hardening reagent activated by stress. Whenever you're Clumsy, Drained, or Enfeebled, you gain resistance equal to the value of the condition against physical damage. This doesn't apply to conditions caused by beneficial effects, such as the Enlarge spell."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nA mixture of resin and corrosive slime oozes from you and trails behind you as you move. You Climb or Stride twice. You leave a trail of slime in each square you leave as part of this movement, and each square adjacent to those squares, except the square where you end your movement. Each square containing slime becomes difficult terrain as well as hazardous terrain, dealing 2 acid damage for each square a creature moves through. The slime dries out, ending these effects, after 1 minute.\n\nAt 17th level, the hazardous terrain deals 6 acid damage."],["Your temporary shells are dangerous if shattered. If a creature breaks or destroys your shield with an unarmed attack or melee weapon without the reach trait, it takes 1d6 bleed damage from the shrapnel."],["You trigger a dormant survival instinct to temporarily turn into your species' ultimate evolution. You can cast Animal Form as a 5th-rank primal innate spell once per day, except instead of choosing an animal, your battle form is an aberration with a Speed of 30 feet and climb Speed of 30 feet, resistance 10 to acid and poison damage, darkvision, precise scent 60 feet, and an unarmed tentacle Strike (reach 15 feet) that deals 2d10 bludgeoning damage plus 2d6 acid damage. You can spend an action after you hit a creature with your tentacle to Grab the target. You also gain the Gunk Spray ability while in this battle form.\n\nGigafuroid Form"],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYour cirrisensors regenerate and help you shrug off afflictions. Attempt to counteract an effect of your choice imposing one of these conditions on you: Blinded, Dazzled, Deafened, Sickened, or Stupefied. This counteract check uses your Fortitude modifier against the target's DC, and your counteract rank is equal to half your level rounded up. If you didn't counteract the effect, but you would have if its counteract rank were 2 lower, you instead suppress the effect until the beginning of your next turn. The effect's duration doesn't elapse while it's suppressed in this way.\n\nThis effect can't cure curses, diseases, or other long-term afflictions with these conditions as part of their normal state, but it can temporarily remove the condition. If the underlying affliction isn't treated, any counteracted conditions return after 24 hours."],["Your shell represents an incredible collection of priceless objects, but your life is worth more than your precious baubles. If you have a shell and would die, you instead gain temporary Hit Points equal to twice your level that last for 1 minute. Your shell breaks, leaving hazardous terrain in a 10-foot emanation centered on you that deals piercing damage equal to half your level ((floor(level/2)) piercing) for each square a creature moves through. Whether you use the shards of your broken shell or new materials, rebuilding a new shell is a downtime activity that takes 8 hours.\n\nSacrificial Shell (Gnarefuroid)"],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYour sticky resin flows into your wounds or the wounds of an adjacent creature currently taking persistent damage, helping to repair cellular damage. For the next minute, reduce the DC of any flat check the target rolls to recover from persistent damage as though it were being assisted. The target immediately rolls a flat check to see if it recovers from each ongoing source of persistent damage.\n\nAssistive Goo Gush"],["Where others see garbage and slime, you see bandages and disinfectants. Your become an expert in Medicine. If you were already an expert in Medicine or would automatically become expert from another source, you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain the Unusual Treatment skill feat, and you can apply its benefit to [[/act treat-disease]] and [[/act treat-poison]] actions in addition to Treat Wounds."],["Your acute taste boosts your immunities. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to saves against effects with the disease, ingested, olfactory, or poison traits. Any disease you contract with a level lower than your own loses the virulent trait."],["Nothing turns your stomach. When you succeed at a Fortitude save to retch, reduce your sickened value by 2 (or by 3 on a critical success). Any disease you contract with a level lower than your own loses the virulent trait."],["You resist the most common hazards of your unsavory habitat. Choose one damage type: acid, piercing, or poison. You gain resistance equal to half your level to that damage type.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat multiple times. Each time you do, select a different damage type."],["You build more durable temporary shells. The shield you create with Scrap Shield is tactical grade. You can create an advanced shield at 9th level, a superior shield at 13th level, and an elite shield at 17th level. In addition, you can use Scrap Shield to create a Riot Shield."],["You mix your sticky, corrosive resin with certain weapons and spells. The next time this turn you Strike with a spell or weapon, one creature that takes non-persistent acid damage from the Strike becomes Clumsy 1 until the start of your next turn, then becomes immune to Adhering Acid for 24 hours."],["A starship hull can be a dangerous place. When the need arises, you can use your internal hydraulics to launch yourself to safety. You gain a fly Speed equal to your land Speed for 10 minutes."],["You've acclimated to constantly using multiple cirrisensors in all directions as a defense mechanism. You can't be flanked by creatures of your level or lower."],["You expand the ways organisms can thrive in adverse settings. You can cast Entangling Flora and Verdant Code once per day each as 3rd-rank primal innate spells."],["You gain the Barricade general feat. You can Barricade using resin and hazardous debris from your own body. Any attack that fails to hit you while you have cover from this barricade destroys it, dealing 4d8 acid damage to each creature in a 20-foot cone originating from the barricade with a basic basic Reflex save against the higher of your class or spell DC. You must spend 10 minutes collecting new debris and resin before you can make another barricade in this way.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can use Adhering Acid on your barricade to make any creature that fails a Reflex save against your barricade Clumsy 1 until the start of your next turn."],["You secrete enough poisonous chemicals to afflict other creatures. As part of your daily preparations, you create two doses of gnarefuroid toxin. These poisons can't be properly used by any other creature, have no value, and become inert when you next make your daily preparations. The poison's save DC uses the higher of your class or spell DC.\n\n**Gnarefuroid Toxin** (injury, poison)\n\n**Saving Throw** Fortitude\n\n**Maximum Duration** 6 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** 1d6 poison damage and Enfeebled 1 (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** 1d6 poison damage, enfeebled 1, and Clumsy 1 (1 round)\n\n**Stage 3** 2d6 poison damage, enfeebled 1, and clumsy 1 (1 round)"],["You comfortably slither through mounds of loose debris. You gain a burrow Speed of 15 feet."],["You've met all kinds of people in your long and varied life and have steeled your mind with caution. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saves against mental effects and a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to Sense Motive."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a melee weapon that deals bludgeoning damage.\n\n---\n\nSometimes the only way to take care of a haywire prototype or malfunctioning doodad is to give it a good old-fashioned wrench-thrashing. Make a Strike with the required weapon against a creature that is glitching. On a hit, instead of dealing the weapon's normal damage, you deal 1 bludgeoning damage and reduce the target's glitching value by 1 (or by 2 on a critical hit)."],["You use your encyclopedic knowledge about a foe like a cudgel, energetically castigating and criticizing them with your quick wit and knowledge. You [[/act demoralize]] a target using a skill that could be used to Recall Knowledge about that target instead of using Intimidation. If you succeed, in addition to the effects of Demoralize, you gain information about the target as though you had succeeded at a check to Recall Knowledge about them with the skill you used in place of Intimidation."],["A common way to try to stave off the Bleaching is to experiment with substances. As a result, each new generation of gnomes becomes more inured to toxic and hazardous materials. You gain poison resistance equal to half your level as well as a +1 circumstance bonus to Fortitude saves against diseases and poisons."],["When a topic draws your interest, you learn all you can about it but can just as easily shift to a new subject at the drop of a hat. Gain the Additional Lore feat. During your daily preparations, if you have access to the infosphere or any relevant learning material, you can swap the Lore skill you have selected with your Additional Lore feat (including any additional skill increases applied to that Lore skill using Additional Lore). Since the proficiency from this selection is temporary, you can't use it to satisfy a prerequisite for a permanent character option (like a feat)."],["Radiation and electricity are simply natural phenomena, which might explain your fey-like connection to things others see as science. You can cast Discharge, Electrotether, and Irradiate once per day each as 3rd-rank primal innate spells."],["You're notorious for your discipline to the point that you can leverage your fame to ask favors of fans and colleagues. You can use the Lore skill that you gain from Voracious Reader to Gather Information. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks to [[/act make-an-impression]] on people interested in your chosen discipline. If you're legendary in the Lore skill, this circumstance bonus increases to +4."],["As far removed as you might be from your First World ancestry, some spark of it still beats within you, giving you a supernaturally powerful connection to life. You Stride twice and can pass through other creatures' spaces without needing to [[/act tumble-through]]. Creatures of your choice whose space you pass through recover level healing Hit Points equal to your level. A creature with void healing treats this as a void effect. You gain temporary Hit Points equal to your level at the end of your movement. These last for 1 minute."],["Your photonic magic is flashy and disorienting to behold. When a creature fails or critically fails a save against a spell you cast that has the light trait, they also become Dazzled for 1 round."],["You've learned to cast some simple energy manipulation spells to help get additional versatility out of your and your allies' weapons. You can cast Infuse Vitality and Shifting Surge once per day each as 1st-rank arcane innate spells."],["Your attention to detail makes you stand out in your field, and your work comes to you automatically at the direst times. Gain the Assurance feat for a skill of your choice. When you make an attack with a weapon that has the professional trait for a skill for which you have Assurance, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the attack roll."],["You have an obsession with augmentations and take pride in discovering new things for your enhanced body to do. You gain the Augmented Body general feat. Once per day, when you attempt a skill check as part of using the augmentation you gained from this feat, you can gain a +1 item bonus to the check."],["You're obsessed with animals and communicating with them, consuming countless videos, recordings, and first-person accounts to hone your ability to speak with them. When you attempt a Diplomacy check to [[/act make-an-impression]] on or make a [[/act request]] of an animal, roll twice and take the better result."],["An innate wellspring of protective magic guards you from unexpected environmental danger. You can cast Life Seal once per day as a 3rd-rank primal innate spell. You can target only yourself, but the duration increases to 10 minutes."],["Goblin stories are legendary. When you spend 1 minute telling a story, you can attempt a Performance check against up to 5 creatures' Will DCs to enrapture them. On a success, the creature listens incredulously, becoming Fascinated for the duration."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou can craft technology quickly at the expense of safety. Once per day, you can Craft an Item you know the formula for with the consumable and tech traits. You can reduce the time it would take to finish Crafting the item to 10 minutes instead of 4 days, and you reduce the materials needed for each 10 minutes of Crafting taken as you seek out more scrap (so by about half). On a critical failure, you cause an explosion and take 1d6 fire damage per item level, destroying the raw materials."],["Your mutations are manifold. You gain one mutation from the Mutant Goblin heritage.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times."],["Picklecore, a blend of improvised jug band music, electronica, and power tools, is your jam. Attempt a Performance check against the Will DC of a single enemy or willing ally within 30 feet. This has all the usual traits and restrictions of a Performance check to sing. This can affect up to two targets within range if you have expert proficiency in Performance, four if you have master proficiency, and eight if you have legendary proficiency.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** If the target doesn't have the goblin trait, they become Off-Guard until the start of your next turn or the next time they're hit by a Strike, whichever comes first. If the target has the goblin trait, they instead gain a +5-foot status bonus to its Speeds for 1 round.\n\nPicklecore Music (Critical Success)\n\n**Success** If the target doesn't have the goblin trait, they become off-guard against the next attack that you attempt against it before the end of your current turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** You accidentally perform conventional music. As critical success, except goblins are affected as if they were non-goblins and vice versa."],["Maybe it was your environment, genetics, or even something you ate, but you've developed a resistance to radiation. You gain resistance to fire and poison damage from radiation effects equal to half your level and a +1 circumstance bonus to Fortitude saves against radiation."],["You're a sneaky stowaway who knows that vents are the best way to get around aboard a ship or station. You become trained in Acrobatics. If you would automatically become trained in Acrobatics (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain the Quick Squeeze skill feat."],["You love to cook anything you find, even if you really shouldn't. You gain the Additional Lore feat with Cooking Lore. You can spend thirty minutes preparing and serving a meal for up to 5 living creatures; when you do so, partaking creatures must attempt a Fortitude save against your Cooking Lore DC. Your targets are then temporarily immune to xenogourmand for 1 day.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature feels nourished; they're full for the day and gain temporary Hit Points equal to your level for 1 day.\n\nXenogourmand (Critical Success)\n\n**Success** The creature is full for a few hours and gains temporary Hit Points equal to your level for two hours.\n\nXenogourmand (Success)\n\n**Critical Failure** Your meal doesn't sit well with the creature's stomach. Unless they're goblins, they're Sickened 1 and can't reduce their sickened value for 10 minutes."],["You like to tinker with your weapons so that they can spit fire. During your daily preparations, you can tinker with one tech weapon, using an upgrade slot to apply a chem tank to the weapon until your next daily preparations. The weapon deals fire damage and gains the boost 1d6 and critical (flame) traits. If it already dealt fire damage, it gains the boost 1d8 trait instead. Each time you boost the weapon, it expends 1 chem.\n\nFlamespewer"],["One gobbo's junk heap is your own hot ride. You learn the formula for four tech vehicles of your level or lower. Vehicles you Craft gain a Pickle Switch."],["For one reason or another, machines around you often spontaneously break down. Whenever an enemy starts its turn adjacent to you, it must attempt a Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. On a failure, the target's wielded tech items (or the target itself if it has the tech trait) becomes Glitching 1 (Glitching 2 on a critical failure) as long as it remains adjacent to you. Regardless of the result of the save, the creature is then temporarily immune to your Malfunction Aura for 24 hours."],["With a flash of nuclear fire, you suddenly transform into a radioactive monster, gaining the effects of a 7th-rank Elemental Form for 1 minute. You gain immunity to radiation in this form. Creatures struck by your tendril must attempt a Fortitude save against mild radiation sickness. This radiation uses the higher of your class DC or spell DC in place of the radiation's normal Fortitude DC, has an immediate onset, and the interval between each stage is 1 round (but it doesn't cause glitching).\n\n---\n\n**Saving Throw** Fortitude\n\n**Stage 1** 1d4 poison and Sickened 1 (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** 1d6 poison and Sickened 2 (1 round)\n\n**Stage 3** 1d6 poison and Sickened 3 (1 round)"],["Your gobbing is renowned across the galaxy's infospheres, making you something of an urban legend. You gain the Combat Hack skill feat. Hackers and frequent infosphere users against whom you succeed at a Battle Gobbing or Combat Hack check recognize your handiwork, granting you a +1 status bonus to Deception checks to Lie, [[/act create-a-diversion]], or Legendary Troll those creatures for 1 minute."],["The quickest way to stop a machine, in your experience, is to bite it over and over. Your melee unarmed Strikes gain the razing trait."],["You've watched enough vids of vehicle crashes to know how to create the perfect collision. When you Run Over or Ram a creature in a vehicle, you can use your Piloting DC as the vehicle's collision DC."],["You're a vicious fighter. When you succeed at a melee weapon Strike against a Frightened enemy, that enemy can't reduce their frightened condition below 1 until the beginning of your next turn."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You're about to attempt a skill check or saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYour reckless tactics surprise others when they occasionally work. You roll twice and take the better result. If you destroy a consumable item of half your level or higher in the process, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the triggering roll."],["Your caustic stomach is the safest place to hide your goods. You Interact to eat an item of 1 Bulk or less. The item takes 1d6 acid damage every hour it stays in your stomach. You're Sickened with a value equal to the total Bulk of items you have in your stomach and can't reduce your sickened value below that total while they remain there. You can regurgitate any number of items as a single action into your hands or your square."],["You continue to mutate your body further to gain even more strange powers. You gain one mutation from the Mutant Goblin heritage.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have Mutanter Goblin, you also gain the Augmented Body general feat but must choose a biotech augmentation."],["You've been exposed to so much radiation that you become radioactive. When a creature Strikes you with a melee unarmed attack or Grabs you, it takes 1d4 persistent poison damage."],["You're of the school of thought that an alert halfling is a halfling who stays alive, and you keep your head on a swivel out of habit. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks made as initiative rolls."],["Halfling musicians have a magical trick handed down from artist to artist, so they're always prepared for an impromptu gig. You become trained in Performance. If you would automatically become trained in Performance (from a background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. Additionally, you gain Summon Instrument as an occult innate cantrip. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["You tell fibs so naturally that even as you're pulling the wool over their eyes, people see the best in you. You become trained in Deception. If you would automatically become trained in Deception (from a background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain the Charming Liar skill feat."],["You've learned to make good use of your diminutive stature and angle your attacks when fighting larger enemies. If you critically hit a Large or larger enemy with a ranged Strike while using a weapon that fires projectile ammo, you knock them Prone. A creature knocked prone by your unusually angled shots learns how to brace for impact, becoming immune to The Bigger They Are for 24 hours."],["Your exemplary courage and mental fortitude carry you through the most daunting of situations. When you roll a success on a saving throw against a fear effect, you get a critical success instead. In addition, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Will saves against fear effects and a +2 circumstance bonus to your Will DC against attempts to [[/act demoralize]] you."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nLacking the additional protections and advantages granted by augmentations that many others take for granted, you have nurtured a habit of being prepared for every eventuality. You swap the skill feat granted to you by Homegrown Skills for another skill feat you qualify for."],["**Trigger** You become Frightened.\n\n---\n\nWhen the going gets tough, the best choice is often to find somewhere safe to hide quickly. You Step or Stride."],["**Trigger** A Large or larger creature within your melee reach is hit by a melee attack from one of your allies.\n\n---\n\nYou have become accustomed to dealing with creatures much larger than you, and you know very well how to use their size against them. The triggering creature must attempt a Reflex save against the higher of your class or spell DC. On a failure, the creature falls Prone and takes 1)) bludgeoning damage equal to half your level."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You become Immobilized, Grabbed, or Restrained.\n\n---\n\nYou're at your fiercest when fighting against being constrained. You cast Unfettered Movement as a 4th-rank occult innate spell targeting yourself."],["You have become a master at manipulating the ebb and flow of fortune's fickle tide. When you gain the Lucky Break reaction, you only become immune to Unlucky for Some for 10 minutes."],["You eschew physical augmentations beyond what's necessary, avoiding superfluous enhancements on your body. During your daily preparations, choose a skill that you're at least trained in. Until your next daily preparations, you gain the Assurance feat for that skill."],["You have an affinity for riding animals of all shapes and sizes, and you haven't met a mount that you aren't willing to ride. You become trained in Nature. If you would automatically become trained in Nature (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain the Ride general feat and gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Command an Animal if the target is trained as a mount."],["You're a quick study when it comes to breaking things, even with minimal equipment. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Computers and Crafting checks to Disable a Device if the device has the tech trait. Additionally, while wielding a weapon from the knife group, you can treat it as an Infiltrator's Toolkit when attempting to Disable a Device or Pick a Lock."],["Your quick reflexes and impeccable balance assist you in zero gravity. You can Push Off in zero-g without needing a free hand. You also ignore the Off-Guard and Clumsy penalties while Untethered in zero gravity."],["**Requirements** Your last action was a Strike that critically hit a Large or larger creature.\n\n---\n\nPeople think you're just lucky, but in truth, you're simply always prepared to seize an opportunity when it presents itself, even in the face of seemingly impossible odds. Automatically [[/act shove]] the target 10 feet away from you. The target is Off-Guard until the end of your current turn."],["By avoiding relying on superfluous augmentations, you have sharpened your senses and your skills. During daily preparations, when choosing a skill for Assurance, you can also choose an additional skill feat that you qualify for in that same skill."],["**Frequency** Once per day\n\n**Trigger** You're about to roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nYour quick reflexes and cautious nature combine to keep you hidden when trouble finds you. You Step. If you have cover, greater cover, or concealment after you Step, you can roll Stealth for initiative as if you were Avoiding Notice."],["**Trigger** You critically fail a saving throw or an enemy's Strike against you is a critical hit.\n\n**Requirements** You don't have the Lucky Break reaction.\n\n---\n\nYou gain the Lucky Break reaction for 24 hours or until the next time you use it, and you become immune to Unlucky for Some for 24 hours."],["You've spent a great deal of time in Dorjo's deserts at night, or in otherwise dark environments. You gain darkvision."],["Your spines aren't just for show; they're sturdy enough to use as weapons. You gain a spine unarmed attack that deals 1d6 piercing damage. Your spines are in the brawling group and have the finesse, hardor, and unarmed traits."],["With your build, and that collection of brutal-looking spines, you don't need to say much to frighten your opponents. You're trained in Intimidation (or another skill of your choice if you were already trained in Intimidation). You gain the Intimidating Glare skill feat."],["Your wide, powerful build and experience carrying massive loads of equipment from job to job have left you surprisingly nimble while burdened. You gain a +5-foot circumstance bonus to your Speed while you have any penalty to your Speed."],["You've spent enough time around the machines your people build to understand all manner of contraptions, often by sight alone. You're trained in Crafting (or another skill of your choice if you were already trained in Crafting). You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Crafting checks to Recall Knowledge about a tech item you can see."],["When you get your powerful legs moving, it's very difficult to stop you. Increase your land Speed by 5 feet. If you move at least 20 feet on your turn, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to attempts to [[/act shove]] or [[/act tumble-through]] an opponent's square until the end of that turn. You can attempt to Shove a creature up to two sizes larger than you, or up to three sizes larger than you if you're legendary in Athletics."],["The cellular walls that make up your hardened exterior have adapted to protect you from a multitude of threats. Choose one of the following energy damage types: acid, electricity, fire, or sonic. You gain resistance equal to half your level against the damage type you chose.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat multiple times. Each time you do so, select a different damage type."],["**Requirements** An adjacent ally is dying.\n\n---\n\nYou give a substantial piece of yourself to bring an adjacent ally back from the brink, breaking a part of your body off to use your restorative body chemistry for emergency aid. Don't increase the value of the target's wounded or dying condition for 1 minute due to the results of recovery checks or losing the dying condition. The targeted creature immediately rolls a recovery check. The target is then immune to Part of Me for You for 24 hours.\n\n---\n\n**Special** The frequency of Restorative Tissues becomes once per 10 minutes rather than once per day."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You are reduced to 0 Hit Points but not immediately killed.\n\n---\n\nYou never want to depend on the ground beneath your roots, but in desperate times it can be your most reliable ally. Your roots reach deep into the ground and draw enough life-giving nutrients to give you one last chance. You are not knocked out and regain Hit Points equal to 6d8 plus half your level. Your wounded condition still increases by 1 as though you had been dying and recovered. You cannot move until you take an Interact action to draw your roots back to the surface."],["Your face lacks most of the expressive features other creatures use to read nonverbal cues, and combined with your silence, this works to your advantage in social situations. You're trained in Deception (or another skill of your choice if you were already trained in Deception), and you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Deception checks to Lie to non-plant creatures and to Deception DCs against [[/act sense-motive]] checks."],["Your spines are sturdy enough to serve double duty. Your spine unarmed attack gains the parry trait. The circumstance bonus to your AC from parrying increases to +2 against any target you hit with a Strike using your spine this turn."],["Forged by the blowing sands of Dorjo and the teeth of thousands of microscopic predators, your skin has become calloused and strong. You gain piercing resistance equal to half your level (minimum 1)."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail a Fortitude saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYour hardiness has reached almost supernatural levels. Reroll the triggering saving throw and use the better result."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** You are hit with an unarmed Strike or an adjacent creature hits you with a melee weapon Strike.\n\n---\n\nYour long, sharp spines and tough, spiked ridges protect your body. You defend yourself by reflexively Striking the triggering creature with your spine unarmed attack."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nCompounds that occur naturally within your leaves have healing effects on other creatures, and you're always finding new ways to harness them. You coat an adjacent willing creature's wounds in your own blood. You lose 1 Hit Point for every 2 levels you have. This damage can't be resisted, prevented, or negated in any way. The target creature regains 1d6 healing Hit Points for every Hit Point you lost."],["You embrace ultimate adaptation by integrating cutting-edge augmentations into your body. Choose one common augmentation with an item level of 1 or less. You begin with this augmentation already installed in your body (you don't need to pay the credits to purchase this starting augmentation). This augmentation doesn't count toward your implant limit."],["Many humans like to experiment when it comes to sampling alien flavors, and you consider yourself a connoisseur. As a result of you treating the galaxy like a smorgasbord, you've developed a strong immune system.\n\nYou gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against diseases and poisons. You reduce the DC of flat checks to recover from persistent poison damage from 15 to 10."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You critically fail a saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYou were taught not to give up, even in a situation as dire as the end of your home world. You treat your critical failure as a failure. If you begin Dying as a result of the failure, your first recovery check has a DC equal to 5 + your current dying value."],["Your personality shines bright in a galaxy of stars. You become trained in Performance (or another skill if you're already trained in Performance), and you gain a +3 circumstance bonus on checks to Aid for Deception, Diplomacy, Intimidation, and Performance checks."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** You roll a saving throw.\n\n**Requirements** You're adjacent to two allies.\n\n---\n\nHerd mentality is strong in humans, but it's also a survival mechanism that has stood the test of time and served them well. You roll the saving throw twice but must use the second result, even if it's worse.\n\n---\n\n*SFS Note:* Change the trigger to “You fail a saving throw.” and the last sentence of the feat to “Reroll the triggering saving throw. You must use the new result, even if it's worse.”"],["You can utilize your powers with enough force to grab items held by other creatures. You can [[/act disarm]] or [[/act steal]] from a creature up to 15 feet away instead of only adjacent creatures."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nWhen you must endure times of extreme stress and pain, you dig deep and draw on the memories or stories of your lost ancestral home world of Golarion, tapping into inner reserves of power to pull off just one more miracle. You regain 1 Focus Point."],["While humans lacks the innate magic of other ancestries, they makes up for it with the ability to learn the mystical arts and protect themselves from magical threats.\n\nChoose one of the four spell traditions in which you're an expert in its corresponding skill (arcane for Arcana, primal for Nature, occult for Occultism, and divine for Religion). You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to all saving throws against spells and effects with the corresponding tradition's trait. If you are or become a master in a skill corresponding to a previously chosen spell tradition, you can choose another tradition in which you're trained in its corresponding skill. You can repeat this process until you've chosen all four spell traditions."],["Pioneers have overcome many of the wastelands' dangers, gaining both resilience and the skills needed to survive there. You gain resistance to cold and fire damage equal to half your level. You can disable environmental hazards using [[/act disable-device skill=survival]] instead of Athletics or Thievery. If you're a master in Survival, you can disable environmental hazards that require a proficiency rank of master or lower in Athletics or Thievery."],["Your legendary abilities set you apart from the rest of humanity, and you can project an air of majesty that inspires compliance in those around you.\n\nOnce per day, you can cast Command as a 7th-rank occult innate spell using the higher of your class DC or spell DC (Will). Because you're projecting your presence more so than words, this effect loses the linguistic trait."],["You always believe in yourself. You can use Confident Actualization once per hour, rather than once per day."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You would die.\n\n---\n\nYou return from the brink of death, hauling yourself back to consciousness through exhaustion and pain. If you have the dying or Unconscious conditions, you lose the dying and unconscious conditions. If you're at 0 Hit Points, you have 1 Hit Point. Increase the value of your wounded and doomed conditions by 1. You can use this reaction while unconscious."],["Humans have traveled across the galaxy and seen a little bit of everything on every imaginable type of planet. Many of your ancestors' stories have percolated down through storytellers and community records, allowing that knowledge to spread.\n\nYou can attempt one additional Recall Knowledge check to yield more information about a specific creature even if you failed the check once. If you're an expert in the relevant skill, you can use this ability even if you failed the same check twice."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You're about to attempt a saving throw or skill check.\n\n---\n\nYour utter confidence in your own abilities helps you push yourself to reach your desired goals. Roll the triggering check or save twice and use the better result."],["Winning friends and influencing people are among the things that humans do best, and you know that objective is best accomplished using your innate magical empathy.\n\nYou gain Mindlink as a 1st-rank occult innate spell at-will. When you cast this spell, you can allow the willing target of the spell to impart information to you instead. After you cast this spell, the target is temporarily immune to your mindlink innate spell for 24 hours."],["Your training with an unconventional weapon has taught you the basics of how to use that weapon for its original nonviolent purpose. While wielding a weapon with the professional trait, you become trained in one skill listed for that weapon's professional trait. If you were already trained in that skill, you become an expert instead. You also gain Assurance in that skill while wielding the weapon."],["You integrated yourself completely into another culture, whether through honest immersion or duplicitous subterfuge. As a result, you've adopted the mannerisms of your hosts. You gain the Adopted Ancestry general feat and your choice of a 1st-level common ancestry feat from the chosen ancestry."],["Given how most humans don't have ancestral home worlds of their own, many must scrape and scavenge to get by. You become trained in Crafting and your choice of Arcana, Nature, Occultism, or Religion. If you were already trained in Crafting, you become an expert instead. If you were already trained in Arcana, Nature, Occultism, and Religion, you become an expert in one of those skills instead. You can Repair items that have both the magic and tech traits without a repair toolkit and without taking a −2 circumstance penalty, improvising tools from whatever you have at hand."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** Your turn begins, and you have the Wounded condition.\n\n---\n\nLike your hard-luck ancestors, you somehow always recover from near-death experiences with astounding resilience and determination. Reduce your wounded condition by 1."],["You can leverage your forgettable appearance to escape your pursuers. You gain Invisibility as a 2nd-rank arcane innate spell once per day, targeting yourself only.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Face in the Crowd skill feat, you can cast invisibility twice per day instead of once per day."],["Humans familiar with low-gravity environments are also better trained at dealing with the complete loss of gravity. At the end of each round in which you're Untethered, attempt a DC 11 flat check. On a success, you ignore the Clumsy and Off-Guard conditions imposed by being in zero gravity for 1 round and can increase or decrease the number of squares you move by up to 10 feet (up to 20 feet on a critical success)."],["**Requirements** You have at least one hand free, and the target is an item you can hold in one hand that's unattended or that you're carrying in a bag, pack, pouch, or other container.\n\n---\n\nYour concentrated center of gravity has evolved to form a supernatural aura of sorts that you can leverage to your advantage. By focusing on this personal gravity field, you can call a single item into your hand from up to 30 feet away."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail a saving throw\n\n**Requirements** You're adjacent to at least one ally.\n\n---\n\nYou fly better with a copilot or a trusted ally you've formed a tight bond with. Reroll the triggering saving throw and use the better result. If your ally also rolled a saving throw against the same effect, they can reroll the triggering saving throw and use the better result."],["You've learned to split your focus between multiple classes with ease. You gain a 2nd-level multiclass dedication feat, even if you normally couldn't take another dedication feat until you take more feats from your current archetype."],["**Requirements** You aren't Encumbered.\n\n---\n\nWhether expelling air or water, your siphons enable quick bursts of speed. You Leap, Stride, or Swim in a straight line, gaining a +10-foot status bonus to your Speeds during that movement. After you use Jet, you can't do so again for 1d4 rounds. You can't Jet in a vacuum and similar environments that lack air or fluid you can expel."],["Powerful muscles anchor your beak, enabling you to take devastating bites out of any target you can immobilize. You gain a beak unarmed attack that deals 1d8 slashing damage. Your beak is in the brawling group and has the backstabber, grapple, razing, and unarmed traits. However, the beak is awkward to deploy as a weapon. You take a –2 circumstance penalty to beak Strikes against targets that aren't Grabbed, helpless, Prone, or Restrained. Even if an effect increases your melee reach, your beak's reach can't exceed 5 feet."],["The minerals constituting your mantle gradually absorb primal energy that you can extrude and shape. Choose one cantrip from the primal spell list. You can cast this cantrip as a primal innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["**Requirements** You have at least one hand free.\n\n---\n\nYour powerful limbs help anchor you to surfaces, allowing you to pull yourself through shallows and even lean your body almost parallel to the ground without falling over. You can choose to fall Prone. You then either Crawl 10 feet (if prone) or Stride up to your Speed (if not prone), ignoring difficult terrain caused by shallow water. If you're prone, you can then Stand.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If an ability (such as the Nimble Crawl skill feat) allows you to Crawl more than 10 feet as an action, you can instead Crawl up to that distance when you Shore Scuttle."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nA special gland near your siphons produces a viscous ink that you can squirt at a foe within 15 feet. The target must attempt a Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. The target then becomes immune to your Spray Ink for 1 minute.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The target is Dazzled until the end of your next turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is Blinded until the beginning of your next turn and dazzled until the end of your next turn."],["Your mineralized mantle and practiced stoicism ensure that others sense your emotions only when you want them to. Other creatures take a –2 circumstance penalty to Perception checks to [[/act sense-motive]] against you. In addition, if you roll a success on your saving throw against an emotion effect, you get a critical success instead."],["**Trigger** Your turn begins, and you're Grabbing or Restraining a creature within your reach.\n\n---\n\nDirected by the sensitive nerves entwined within each of your limbs, your tentacles reflexively cling onto whatever you're grappling, even if your attention is directed elsewhere. Attempt a DC 16 flat check. If you succeed, you can extend the duration of the grappled creature's grabbed or restrained condition until the end of your next turn. If you have any special abilities or free actions that would normally be triggered when you Grapple a creature, you can't use them as part of this action."],["Your brain efficiently processes each of your eyes' input, creating composite images that reveal what would otherwise remain hidden. When you Seek or use the Search exploration activity, you gain the benefits of the See the Unseen spell until the end of your next turn."],["◆ or ◆◆◆\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** You have at least one hand free.\n\n---\n\nYou carefully balance with the aid of only a few arms, freeing the rest to snag anything around you. As you do, your limbs elongate and writhe. Until combat ends, you're knocked out, or you Dismiss All-Grabber Stance, you can make lashing limb Strikes. These deal 3d6 bludgeoning damage, are in the brawling group, have the grapple and unarmed traits, and have a reach of 15 feet. You can also use the Hug the World activity. If you spent 3 actions to use All-Grabber Stance, you can immediately Hug the World."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nA typical ijtikri's leviathan transformation is their last act in life, irreversibly swelling to immense size before seeding the sea with new life. You aren't typical; you can transform into a Gargantuan ijtikri leviathan battle form for 1 minute. You can Dismiss this effect. When the effect ends, the revitalizing gases from your leviathan body fill a 30-foot emanation, restoring 5d8 healing Hit Points to living creatures in the area. You gain the following statistics and abilities.\n\n- AC = 22 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.\n- 10 temporary Hit Points.\n- Speed 10 feet, fly 40 feet, swim 60 feet\n- The following unarmed melee attacks. You're trained with this attack, and your attack modifier is +25. This attack is Strength based. If your unarmed attack modifier is higher, you can use it instead. **Melee** ◆ tentacle (backswing, grapple, reach 30 feet), **Damage** 3d10+15 bludgeoning; **Area Fire** ◆◆ wail (60-foot cone), **Damage** 3d10+15 sonic (basic Reflex save versus the higher of your class DC or spell DC)\n- Acrobatics modifier of +15 and Athletics modifier of +25, unless your own modifiers are higher."],["Your ancestors served the Veskarium for countless generations. You've incorporated vesk traditions into your own life, and the Veskarium has freely shared its secrets with you.\n\nYou gain the Adopted Ancestry general feat and must choose vesk. You gain a 1st-level Vesk ancestry feat for which you qualify, and your mantle grows tougher. Increase your resistance to precision damage by 2."],["You adapt to new hierarchies with ease and find reassurance in a reliable command structure. When using the Follow the Expert activity in exploration mode, you gain a +3 circumstance bonus if the ally you're following is an expert and a +4 circumstance bonus if your ally is a master. In addition, if you roll a success on your saving throw against a mental effect that would make you Controlled, you get a critical success instead."],["**Trigger** An attack, spell, or effect would deal damage to you.\n\n**Requirements** Your shell isn't Broken.\n\n---\n\nAn ijtikri's shell is tough enough to discourage foes from striking vital organs, but you're brave enough to literally block attacks head-on. You gain resistance equal to your Constitution modifier plus your level against all damage from the triggering attack or effect. After resolving the effect, your shell is broken, during which time you are Clumsy 1 and lose your resistance to precision damage granted by your Mantle ability. The first time per day that someone successfully uses the Medicine skill to Treat your Wounds while your shell is broken, their efforts also repair your shell. Your shell is also repaired fully when you rest for 8 hours."],["Your limbs' myriad suckers provide you unrivaled grip strength. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to [[/act force-open]], and you don't take an item penalty when Forcing something Open for not having a crowbar or other suitable tool. When you roll a success on a check to Force Open, you get a critical success instead. In addition, while you're in contact with a floor or other solid surface, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Fortitude and Reflex DCs against attempts to [[/act disarm]], [[/act reposition]], [[/act shove]], or [[/act trip]] you."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou vent most of your ink all at once, filling a small area with obscuring droplets. You create a stationary cloud of ink in a 10-foot emanation centered on your current location. Creatures are Concealed while inside the cloud, and creatures outside the area are concealed to creatures inside the cloud. The ink dissipates at the start of your next turn. This ability functions equally effectively above or below water."],["**Trigger** You're about to Demoralize with the visual trait while you're in an area of bright light.\n\n---\n\nYou focus your mantle's reflective properties to overwhelm not just your target's will but also its senses. Attempt your [[/act demoralize dc=reflex traits=visual]]{Intimidation} check against the target's Reflex DC instead of its Will DC. If you critically succeed, the target is Dazzled until it's no longer Frightened."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** A creature that you can see targets you with an attack.\n\n**Requirements** You aren't Encumbered.\n\n---\n\nWith a reflexive burst from your siphons, you try to flit away from the attack. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack. If the attack fails or critically fails, you can also Stride or Swim up to 10 feet as part of the reaction.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Spray Ink feat, you can also expel a puff of ink as part of this reaction. In addition to the circumstance bonus to AC, you're Concealed against the triggering attack."],["**Requirements** You used your last action this turn to Grapple a creature within your reach.\n\n---\n\nYou bring additional limbs to bear, ensuring that you either ensnare your target or wrap your captured prey in additional tentacles. Attempt to [[/act grapple]] the target, but the attempt's multiple attack penalty is only –3 if it's your second attack on your turn or –6 if it's the third or subsequent attack. If the target is already Grabbed or Restrained by you, replace Grapple's effects with the following.\n\n**Critical Success** If your target was grabbed, it's now restrained until the end of your next turn unless you move or your target Escapes. Until the end of your next turn, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Athletics DC to resist the target's attempts to [[/act escape]].\n\n**Success** You wrap additional limbs around the target. Until the end of your next turn, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Athletics DC to resist the target's attempts to Escape, and you increase the DC 7 flat check DC it must attempt when attempting a manipulate action to 7.\n\n**Failure** You fail to wrap additional limbs around your target, but it remains grabbed or restrained."],["Venomous glands near your mouth can give your saliva toxic properties. Your beak unarmed strike deals an additional 1 persistent poison damage. This increases to 2 persistent poison damage if your beak deals at least three weapon damage dice. In addition, you gain the Toxic Tear action."],["You've served as, or are training to become, a brood-minder responsible for rearing and educating dozens of hatchlings. It's a multi-year job requiring extreme endurance. You become trained in Society. If you would automatically become trained in this skill (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. In addition, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus on saves to resist becoming Fatigued."],["You grew up without a brood. Whether you were a lone survivor, became lost, or were raised offworld, you've learned to survive alone. You become trained in one of the following skills of your choice: Deception or Thievery. If you would automatically become trained in both of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. If you selected Deception, you gain the Charming Liar skill feat. If you selected Thievery, you gain the Subtle Theft skill feat."],["You may be small, but your body is a dangerous weapon, sporting either long talons, razor-sharp teeth, or curving horns. When you select this feat, you gain your choice of a claw unarmed attack, a horn unarmed attack, or a jaws unarmed attack. These attacks are in the brawling weapon group.\n\n- A claw unarmed attack deals 1d6 slashing damage and has the agile, finesse, ikeshti, and unarmed traits.\n- A horn unarmed attack deals 1d6 bludgeoning damage and has the disarm, ikeshti, shove, and unarmed traits.\n- A jaws unarmed attack deals 1d6 piercing damage and has the grapple, ikeshti, and unarmed traits.\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these attacks, you get its critical specialization effect.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat up to three times. Each time you do, select a different attack from the options above."],["You're determined to amass a fortune and send a portion of the profits back home. You gain the Additional Lore general feat for one Lore skill of your choice—the Lore you choose must be related to your business or profession, such as Accounting Lore, Corporate Lore, or Legal Lore. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus on checks to Earn Income with your chosen Lore. In addition, whenever you successfully Earn Income, you earn an additional 10%. This additional income is transferred directly to your home community's accounts and can't be accessed or used by you in any way."],["Life on Akiton is hard, but thanks to your brood-minder, you learned the skills necessary to thrive. You become trained in Crafting and Survival. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Ikeshti Lore."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You attempt to Escape.\n\n---\n\nYou rapidly shed a layer of your skin and slip away from a tight or sticky situation, living to fight (or flee) another day. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus on the triggering Escape, and on all attempts to Escape for 3 rounds. If the triggering Escape was successful, you can additionally Stand or Step (or Stride up to your Speed on a critical success)."],["Your scales are marked with tiny sigils. When you select this feat, choose if you were blessed by a god or by an aberrant force. You can tap into the latent magic in your scales to cast a cantrip as an innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up.\n\nIf you are blessed by a god, choose one cantrip from the divine spell list. You can cast this cantrip as a divine innate spell at will.\n\nIf you are blessed by an aberrant force, choose one cantrip from the occult spell list. You can cast this cantrip as an occult innate spell at will.\n\nWhenever you cast an innate spell granted by your Sigiled Scales or a feat that lists Sigiled Scales as a prerequisite, the sigils on your scales glow with magical energy, shedding bright light in a 10-foot radius for a number of minutes equal to the spell's rank."],["You have a deep understanding of emotions and mental health. You become trained in one of the following skills of your choice: Diplomacy or Medicine. If you would automatically become trained in both of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. In addition, if you roll a critical failure on a Will save against an emotion effect, you get a failure instead."],["You squirt blood from one of your eyes at a creature within 30 feet. The target must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher, with the following results.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is disgusted by the display, becoming Sickened 1.\n\n**Failure** The target is struck in the face, becoming Dazzled for 1 round, or until they Interact once to clean the blood away.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is struck in the face, becoming dazzled for 2 rounds, or until they Interact twice to clean the blood away."],["You never lose your cool. When you become Frightened or Stupefied, you immediately reduce the value of the condition by 1. When you would gain the Confused or Controlled condition, you can attempt a DC 16 flat check. On a success, you don't get the confused or controlled condition."],["Your scales blend in with the rocks and rubble of your home world. While you're outdoors on Akiton or a similar planet, and you're in a desert, mountain, or plains terrain, you don't need cover to Hide or Sneak from creatures at least 10 feet away from you."],["You've learned which survival tactics work best for you and rely on them frequently. Select one of the following feats or abilities you possess: Puff Up, Shed Skin, Squirt Blood. You can use the selected ability once per 10 minutes, rather than once per hour.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat more than once, selecting a different ability each time."],["You can divine the future. You can cast Read Omens and Vision of Death each once per day as 4th-rank spells. The tradition of this spell matches the tradition of the cantrip you gained from Sigiled Scales.\n\nAt 17th level, the rank of *vision of death* increases to 6th."],["**Trigger** You would be reduced to 0 Hit Points.\n\n**Requirements** You have a tail.\n\n---\n\nIn an embarrassing act of desperation, you sacrifice your tail to save your life. You're reduced to 1 Hit Point, rather than 0 Hit Points, and don't gain the Unconscious or wounded conditions. Your tail falls off and flails around wildly, distracting your foes. You Stride up to your Speed, and don't trigger reactions due to this movement. Your tail grows back over 24 hours. While your tail is regrowing, you don't have a tail, your Speed is reduced by 5 feet, and you take a –2 status penalty to Acrobatics checks."],["You've mastered your anger and can maintain the rivener transformation indefinitely. You permanently become Large, and your reach increases by 5 feet. You can use Enter Rivener State once per hour, rather than once per day. When you Enter Rivener State, your size and reach don't increase, you don't become stupefied, and you don't become Fatigued when the transformation ends. You still gain the bonus to damage."],["You see now; you understand. Your powers come with a price, and your fate is not your own. You're a part of something greater—a pawn in motion within a vast and complex pattern, executing commands long planned and twice foreseen. You're beholden to a higher power, and it has plans for you.\n\nIf your innate spells are divine, you can cast Divine Decree once per day as a 7th-rank divine innate spell.\n\nIf your innate spells are occult, you can cast Warp Mind once per day as a 7th-rank occult innate spell."],["You catch periodic glimpses of the immediate future and can use your insight to predict your foes' moves before they make them. Once per day, you can cast Bless or Sure Strike as a 1st-rank spell. The tradition of this spell matches the tradition of the cantrip you gained from Sigiled Scales."],["You have a colossal appetite for a creature your size, and you find that a good meal always hits the spot. Once per day, you can eat a snack or meal as a 10-minute activity. When you do, you regain a number of Hit Points equal to 1d6 plus your level (1d6 + level healing)."],["You take great delight in breaking down objects to their component parts so they can be rebuilt into something new. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus on Thievery checks to Disable Device and Pick Lock. Whenever you successfully Disable Device, you harvest useful parts from the device for future use, gaining a +1 circumstance bonus on your next Crafting check to Craft or Repair. If the device you disabled was of a level higher than your own, this bonus increases to +2.\n\nScrapper's Ingenuity"],["**Trigger** You are about to roll a Reflex save against a hazard\n\n---\n\nYou've learned to react to Akiton's dangers at a moment's notice, and you trust your instincts to see you through. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the triggering saving throw."],["You use your body's built-up toxins to enhance your natural attacks, making them poisonous. Whenever you deal damage with an unarmed Strike you gained from Compact Predator, you deal an additional 1 poison damage per weapon damage die of the attack. Whenever you Puff Up or Squirt Blood, you additionally deal poison damage equal to half your level."],["**Requirements** Your most recent action was a success on a melee Strike against a creature who is at least one size larger than you.\n\n---\n\nYou know that being small only means you need to be more vicious to survive and have learned to use your size to your advantage against larger foes. Attempt an Athletics check to Shove or Trip the target, ignoring the size requirements. If you roll a critical failure, you get a failure instead."],["Your experience as a brood-minder has hardened you, and you can function fully with little to no rest. You require only two hours of sleep to get a full night's rest, rather than eight. You can use exploration activities when Fatigued."],["Your survival instincts are honed by a life of danger and scarcity, and you've learned to never let your guard down. You are not Off-Guard against Hidden or Undetected creatures. In addition, you can use Survivor's Instincts anytime you would attempt a Reflex save."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You fail a Will saving throw against a mental effect.\n\n---\n\nYou refuse to allow others to influence or manipulate your emotions. Reroll the triggering saving throw and use the better result."],["You embrace your anger, willingly entering a controlled rivener state and maintaining your mental faculties. Your body grows and expands, becoming Large. Your equipment grows with you, but returns to its natural size if removed. Your reach increases by 5 feet, and you gain a +2 status bonus to melee damage. You become Stupefied 1. This transformation lasts for 10 minutes, or until you choose to end it early as a single action that has the concentrate trait. When your transformation ends, you become Fatigued for 10 minutes.\n\nAt 13th level and 17th level, the bonus damage increases by 2"],["Your magical scale markings give you insight into the future. You can cast Augury twice per day as a 2nd-rank spell. The tradition of this spell matches the tradition of the cantrip you gained from Sigiled Scales."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Requirements** You are in an area of severe, extreme, or incredible heat, or you were dealt fire damage within the last round.\n\n---\n\nYour body has adapted to convert ambient thermal energy into kinetic energy to boost your speed. You Stride up to double your Speed. In addition, you become Quickened until the end of your next turn. You can only use the extra action from quickened to Stride."],["As one of the izalguuns who created the advanced technology of Izalraan, you have a deep understanding of engineering practices. You become trained in Crafting. If you would automatically become trained in Crafting (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Electrical Engineer skill feat."],["Your middle arms have grown in bulk and strength from the time you've spent running on all fours. While in quadrupedal posture, your land Speed is 35 feet. You can't hold any items in your middle limbs or designate them as your active hands, even in bipedal posture."],["You've perfected the skill of moving around on four limbs while holding on to objects or weapons in your middle hands. While in quadrupedal posture, you can still hold one object or weapon of light Bulk in each of your middle limbs. You can't designate these hands as your active hands until you've returned to bipedal posture with Change Posture."],["You have a deep understanding of plants, and you rarely make mistakes about them. You become trained in Life Science Lore and Nature. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. If you get a critical failure on a Life Science Lore or Nature check to Recall Knowledge about plants, you get a failure instead."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou use the shot of your weapon to help your allies hunt down prey. Strike a creature Undetected by one or more of your allies, but not undetected to you. If you hit the target, you Point Out the creature to your allies."],["You're entrusted with keeping your society's advanced technology a secret. You can modify one item with the tech trait as a 1-hour activity. Once modified, a creature must use a Seek action to attempt a Crafting or Perception check against your Crafting DC to recognize that the item has the tech trait. Otherwise, it appears as an item with the analog trait, even if they see it used. The disguised item must appear to be the same general type of item, such as disguising a Fangblade as a greatsword or a Hypopen as an herbal remedy. Some items might be too high-tech to disguise as an analog item and can be disguised as a magic item instead, but doing so allows other creatures to use Arcana, Nature, Occultism, or Religion to attempt to determine the item's true nature."],["You're highly skilled at making a succulent meal out of whatever you find lying around. You gain the Additional Lore feat for Cooking Lore. You can use Cooking Lore in place of Survival to [[/act subsist skill=cooking-lore]]. Additionally, you gain the Seasoned skill feat."],["You spread the strain of your fall throughout your large build, cushioning the impact. Treat falls as 20 feet shorter. If you're an expert in Athletics, treat falls as 50 feet shorter, and 100 feet if you're a master. If you're legendary in Athletics, you always land on your feet and don't take damage, regardless of the distance of the fall. If you land Prone, you also land in quadrupedal posture regardless of your posture at the beginning of the fall and drop anything you were holding in your middle arms, unless you have Galloping Grip or another ability that allows you to hold objects in quadrupedal form."],["You sleep in quadrupedal posture with the rest of your body mostly upright, allowing you to easily sleep in armor. You can sleep in armor overnight without being Fatigued the next day. If you were already fatigued before sleeping, the armor doesn't prevent you from recovering from being fatigued."],["Your eyes are set particularly far apart, even relative to other izalguuns, and with some focus you can keep track of all the threats around you. You gain all-around vision until the start of your next turn. This lets you see in all directions and prevents you from being flanked."],["You use your middle arms as feet so much that you've lost the ability to use them as arms. You lose the Change Posture action, and you can no longer be in bipedal posture. Your land Speed increases to 40 feet. You gain the Solid Stance feat. If you already had the Solid Stance feat, you can retrain that feat to another ancestry feat when you select this feat."],["**Requirements** You have a creature Grabbed or Restrained using one or more active limbs.\n\n---\n\nYou use all of your available limbs to hold on tight. You use your second pair of arms to hold on to the grabbed or restrained target. If you're in quadrupedal posture, you automatically Change Posture to bipedal as part of this action. The grabbed creature takes a –2 circumstance penalty to Escape being grabbed by you until the end of your next turn.\n\nMulti-Armed Grab"],["**Requirements** You're in quadrupedal posture.\n\n---\n\nYou trot forth, crushing your enemies under your feet! You Stride up to double your Speed and can move through the spaces of creatures at least one size smaller than you, trampling each creature whose space you enter. You can attempt to trample the same creature only once in a single Trampling Stride. You deal bludgeoning damage equal to your fist unarmed attack against these creatures with a basic Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC."],["Your physique is so impressive that your acts of strength astound your foes. When you succeed or critically succeed at an Athletics check to [[/act grapple]], [[/act reposition]], [[/act shove]], or [[/act trip]], you can, as a free action, attempt an Athletics ([[/act demoralize skill=athletics]]) or Intimidation ([[/act demoralize skill=intimidation]]) check to Demoralize one creature within 30 feet. You also gain the Intimidating Glare skill feat, even if you don't meet the prerequisites."],["You're astonishingly good at keeping secrets. You gain a +4 circumstance bonus to Deception checks to Lie when it involves protecting a secret you believe is only known by 10 or fewer people. When you use Deception to [[/act lie]], you don't take a penalty to Deception checks while subject to a spell or effect that would compel you to tell the truth. Whenever you're subject to an effect that attempts to extract a secret from you, including any effect that would read your thoughts or make you controlled, you can attempt to counteract the effect using your Deception modifier as the counteract modifier, with a counteract rank equal to half your level (rounded up). You can attempt to counteract each effect only once per round."],["You can process enough visual information that you can see in all directions at once. You permanently gain all-around vision, meaning you can't be flanked. Additionally, you can [[/act seek]] in two directions at once."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail or critically fail a saving throw against a divine spell or effect.\n\n---\n\nYour resistance to the god Kadrical has manifested in the form of great resilience against divine influence. You reroll the triggering saving throw and use the second result."],["**Trigger** You fail, but don't critically fail, an attempt to Escape.\n\n---\n\nYou writhe wildly to get out of your predicament. You reroll the triggering attempt to [[/act escape]] and use the second result."],["You use your multiple limbs to play two or more instruments at the same time, creating your own melodies, counter-melodies, and harmonies to impress your audience. You gain the Virtuosic Performer skill feat and can apply its benefits to keyboards, percussion, strings, synths, and winds."],["When you take the Change Posture action, you can Switch Hands and put away or swap any number of items between your hands."],["**Requirements** You're in bipedal posture.\n\n---\n\nYou can use the momentum of shifting your form to quickly gallop into battle. You Change Posture from bipedal to quadrupedal and Stride up to your Speed."],["**Requirements** You're in quadrupedal posture.\n\n---\n\nYou use the momentum from lifting yourself up into bipedal posture to propel yourself into a high leap. You Change Posture from quadrupedal to bipedal and High Jump or Leap with a +2 circumstance bonus to Athletics. You don't automatically fail if you don't Stride as part of the activity. You remain in bipedal posture when you land.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Quick Jump skill feat, this activity is also reduced to 1 action."],["You are ever vigilant and refuse to be caught unaware, always watching for enemies. Whether agents of Kadrical or corporate spies come after you, you'll be ready to move quickly if they appear. When you roll initiative while using the Scout exploration activity, you can roll twice and take the better result."],["When you stand on four legs, you dig into the ground firmly, making yourself particularly difficult to move. While in quadrupedal posture, you gain a +4 circumstance bonus to your Fortitude or Reflex DCs against attempts to [[/act reposition]], [[/act shove]], or [[/act trip]] you. This bonus also applies to saving throws against spells or effects that attempt to move you or knock you Prone. When you move, except to Stand, you lose the benefits of this feat until the beginning of your next turn."],["**Requirements** You're in quadrupedal posture.\n\n---\n\nYou're deft enough at using your middle limbs in both postures to immediately use them when changing. You Change Posture from quadrupedal to bipedal posture, Switch Hands from your top hands to your middle hands, and can Strike using a weapon in your middle hands or an unarmed attack."],["**Requirements** You're in bipedal posture.\n\n---\n\nYou squat down from bipedal posture to quadrupedal posture with enough force to send tremors through the ground around you. You Change Posture from bipedal posture to quadrupedal posture. Each creature within 10 feet of you must attempt a Reflex saving throw against the higher of your class DC or spell DC.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is Off-Guard until the end of your turn.\n\n**Failure** The creature falls Prone.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature falls prone and takes 1d6 bludgeoning damage."],["Your eyes glow like bioluminescent lamps, and you have learned how to focus them into a directional beam. Your eyes shed light in a 30 foot line in any direction you're looking.\n\nYou can suppress or restore this light as a free action. In addition, while this light is active you can take the Point Out action to indicate a creature within the area of your bioluminescence without making any noise, in which case it loses the auditory and manipulate traits. Finally, after you use an action to Hide or Sneak, you can send predetermined signals with your lights to alert all allies you can see to your location as a free action."],["Your body is your canvas, and you've taken body modification to a whole new level. You gain an augmentation at no cost. The augmentation must be your level or lower. This augmentation doesn't count against the maximum number of augmentations you can implant, and each time you gain a new ancestry feat, you can upgrade this augmentation to a new augmentation of your level or lower at no cost, representing your continued exploration in body modification."],["You've poured all your creativity into making your weapon truly eye-catching. Choose one weapon you own to decorate in your own style. While wielding your chosen weapon, add the weapon's tracking value as an item bonus to Deception checks to Feint and Intimidation checks to Demoralize. You can only have one such weapon active at a time. You can spend 24 hours customizing a new weapon, at which point your connection with your previous weapon is lost."],["You've studied the history of the Deep Current Alliance, and you understand the value of turning an enemy into a friend. When you succeed on a Diplomacy check to Make an Impression against an opponent that's hostile, you critically succeed instead."],["You're descended from a long line of deepspeakers, dating back to an ancestor who served as liaison for a linnorm. You've been chosen to carry on the tradition, learning secrets passed down through generations of your people. You become trained in Performance and gain the Impressive Performance skill feat."],["The sensory tentacles covering the lower part of your face are sensitive enough to detect toxins. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against ingested or inhaled poisons.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat only at 1st level, and you can't retrain out of or into this feat."],["You are accustomed to floating free in the wide ocean and don't lose your cool when you have nothing within reach. You don't gain the clumsy or Off-Guard conditions when untethered."],["Growing up among the blooms and glowing spires of Kalo-Mahoi has instilled in you a deep appreciation of the beauty around you, both natural and constructed. You're trained in Crafting and Nature. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Kalo Lore."],["Your ancestors swore allegiance to a linnorm long ago. Though your family is no longer bound to serve the creature, a bit of its influence remains in you, manifesting in particularly long and sharp teeth. You gain a jaws unarmed attack that deals 1d6 piercing damage. Your jaws are in the brawling group and have the finesse and unarmed traits."],["Stalking great finned beasts through the kelp forests of Kalo-Mahoi has taught you to move silently and smoothly through the cover of foliage. While sneaking, you ignore difficult terrain caused by foliage and underbrush and treat greater difficult terrain caused by foliage or underbrush as difficult terrain. In addition, you can move at your full swim Speed when you Sneak while swimming. If you have another ability that allows you to move at full speed while Sneaking, you also gain a +2 status bonus to checks to Sneak while Swimming."],["Through diligent training, you've learned to stretch your ability to remain out of the water for extended periods. You gain the amphibious trait."],["People have noticed the originality and quality of your artistic creations, and you've started moonlighting as a professional artist. You become trained in Crafting or a Lore skill related to art (such as Art Lore or Sculpture Lore). When you succeed or critically succeed on a check to Earn Income using Crafting or a Lore skill related to art, calculate the amount you earn as if you'd attempted a check one level higher."],["After years of meritorious military service, you were chosen for the elite Bloomguard, where you underwent rigorous training that honed your defenses against the tricks of First World creatures. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Will saving throws and Will DCs against mental effects and effects created by fey, and once per day, you can roll twice and take the better on a save against a mental effect or an effect created by a fey."],["Years of careful attention to your look have given you a deep understanding of the interplay between color, texture, and light, and you know how to make your outfit catch anyone's eye. You gain Vibrant Pattern as a 6th-rank primal innate spell that you can cast once per day. At 17th level, increase the area of your vibrant pattern innate spell to a 20-foot burst."],["The membranous webbing between your limbs and torso grows strong enough to function as true wings when you're floating. When you're in low or zero gravity, you gain a Fly speed equal to your Swim speed."],["Through years of practice, you've honed your ability to see through tricks and illusions of the First World. Once per day, you can cast Truesight as a primal innate spell; use the higher of your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher, minus 10 for any associated counteract checks."],["The surge of Kalo-Mahoi's ever-present tides courses in your blood, and you can feel their pull wherever you go. You gain Unfettered Movement as a 4th-rank primal innate spell that you can cast once per day."],["The freezing power of your bite becomes irresistible. The cold damage dealt by your jaws Strike increases to 2d6 untyped damage and ignores an amount of the target's cold resistance equal to your level. A creature's immunities are unaffected."],["**Requirements** You aren't in a vacuum.\n\n---\n\nYou take inspiration from schools of hunting manta rays, creating a vortex to draw in your foe before striking. You spin in place and can attempt an Athletics check against the Fortitude DC of all creatures within 20 feet of you (or 40 feet if you and the target are in water). On a success, that creature is moved adjacent to you. On a critical success, it's also knocked Prone. If a creature is within melee reach of you after this check is resolved, you can Strike that creature."],["You perceive your surroundings as much by echolocation as by your other senses. Your echolocation becomes a precise sense to a range of 60 feet (or 120 feet underwater), in addition to the imprecise sense out to 120 feet (or 240 feet underwater)."],["You have a mystical connection to the powerful currents of Kalo-Mahoi and their interactions with the blooms, and you've learned to call upon them to wash powerful outsiders away through portals between planes. You gain Banishment as an 8th-rank primal innate spell that you can cast once per day. You can cast the spell targeting up to 10 willing creatures, who treat the results of their Will save as two degrees of success lower."],["Through practice, you've learned how to increase the intensity of your bioluminescence. The range of your bioluminescence increases to 50 feet. Your dazzling glare misleads your foes, allowing you to use the Feint action against a creature within the range of your bioluminescence, and applies to ranged attacks."],["The muscles that control your membranous wings are particularly well developed, and you know how to use them to catch enemies off guard with their power. Once per day while in an area of atmosphere, you can flap your wings to cast Gust of Wind as a primal innate spell. If you're submerged in liquid, you can instead cast Hydraulic Push. After you've cast the spell, you can move up to half your Speed (or half your swim Speed if submerged) as a free action."],["Your Homeguard training has prepared you for anything. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to initiative rolls, and when you tie an adversary's initiative roll, you always go first."],["You spent time exploring the icy caves of Kalo-Mahoi's crust, and climbing comes nearly as easily to you as walking. You gain a Climb speed of 25 feet, and you treat difficult terrain from ice and snow as normal terrain."],["By imitating your ancestors' diet, taking synthetic supplements, or unlocking your genetic potential with magic, you've enhanced your bioelectrical network. All your Strikes or spells with the attack trait that deal electricity damage gain the arc trait. If you're wielding an active forcefield, it regenerates twice its normal HP for 1 round after you hit an enemy with an arc attack."],["You earned your space legs in the Skyguard, Kalo-Mahoi's space navy. You become trained in Piloting, and you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Piloting checks to Navigate and Stunt. If you're already trained in Piloting, you become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Stunt Maneuver skill feat, even if you don't meet the prerequisites of the feat."],["You've learned how to wield nearly any weapon effectively while underwater. You don't take the –2 penalty for making melee slashing or bludgeoning Strikes while underwater. Your ranged attacks aren't affected by being underwater. You can use weapons that deal fire damage underwater."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** A creature Grabs you or successfully Strikes you with an unarmed melee strike or a non-reach melee weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou flex the spines running down the back of your head and neck as a defensive response. The attacking creature takes (floor((level + 1) / 3 + 1))d6 piercing damage, with a basic Reflex save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. On a critical failure, the target also takes (floor((level + 1) / 3 + 1)) persistent bleed damage. At 8th level and every 3 levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d6, and the persistent bleed damage increases by 1."],["You are known for your astounding custom outfits and pride yourself on designing versatile and reconfigurable garments, allowing you to create nearly any look in a matter of moments. You can use the Crafting skill rather than Deception to Impersonate another person, and can do so in 1 minute rather than the usual 10 minutes. You don't need a disguise kit to Impersonate a specific person when using Crafting to do so, and a maker's toolkit grants a +1 item bonus to the check."],["You propel yourself up like a whale breaching the surface of the ocean, then crash back down with thunderous force. Leap. When you land, all opponents within 10 feet of you must succeed at a Fortitude save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher, or be knocked Prone.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Quick Jump feat, you can High Jump or Long Jump when using Breach."],["You've learned to quiet your other senses and focus your attention on your echolocation. The range of your echolocation imprecise sense doubles to 60 feet (or 120 feet underwater), and you gain the Focus Senses action."],["Your linnorm heritage has begun to manifest more as you've become more powerful. Your jaws Strike deals an additional 1d6 cold damage. On a critical hit, the target is also Suppressed until the end of your next turn, unless it succeeds at a Fortitude save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher."],["The winglike membranes that stretch between your arms and torso let you maneuver while floating without a solid point to push off from. While in low gravity or zero gravity, you can take the Push Off action without having a solid surface within reach.\n\nIn addition, when falling in such an environment, you can move 5 feet horizontally in the direction of your choice for every 20 vertical feet you fall. Subtract this distance moved horizontally from the distance you fell when calculating fall damage."],["You have trained in the ceremonial art of combat mounted upon a manta and can apply your experience to other forms of mobile combat. Reduce the penalty when attacking from a vehicle that has moved within the last round to 0 (or –2 if the vehicle is uncontrolled or any action in the last round had the reckless trait). You don't take a penalty to Reflex saves while mounted."],["You maintain a calm demeanor even when facing mortal peril. When frightened, at the end of your turn, reduce your frightened condition by 2 instead of 1."],["**Trigger** An ally within 30 feet attempts to Aid and rolls a failure.\n\n---\n\nYou're always able to help in a pinch. Attempt a skill check or attack roll of the same type attempted by your ally and replace the result of the failed Aid with your result, even if you didn't prepare to help."],["You've spent a significant amount of time living in the desert and learned to control your thirst and move swiftly through shifting sands.\n\nYou can ignore difficult terrain caused by desert terrain (such as loose sand or gravel). In addition, you're less susceptible to dehydration. You don't take damage from dehydration until you've gone without water for double the usual duration of your Constitution modifier + 1."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou've studied ancient kasathan martial techniques of using a combatant's own bodyweight against them to gain the upper hand in battle.\n\nYou [[/act grapple skill=acrobatics]] a target, using Acrobatics against the target's Fortitude DC instead of Athletics. You can continue to use Acrobatics instead of Athletics for further attempts to Grapple the target until they Escape or are otherwise freed from being grappled by you."],["Exposure to low levels of cosmic radiation over a long period of time has made your cells more resilient. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Fortitude saving throws against poison; this bonus increases to +2 against radiation."],["You've studied the kasathan traditions of balance and harmony. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Diplomacy and Society. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Kasatha Lore."],["You have a respect for melee combat, and you've trained to wield a few more elegant examples in battle. You gain access to all uncommon weapons with the kasatha trait. You have familiarity with weapons with the kasatha trait plus the dueling sword, plasma sword, shock truncheon, and singing spear—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["You have an exceedingly precise control over your body. When you succeed at a check to [[/act balance]], you get a critical success instead. If you roll a critical failure at a check to Balance, you get a failure instead."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail an Acrobatics check or Reflex saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYou have an almost supernatural control of your movements, which can sometimes save you in dangerous situations. You can reroll the triggering skill check or saving throw, using the second result even if it's worse."],["You've studied the dense and interconnected network of kasathan Great Families. You know all their major achievements, and you can use this knowledge either to flatter or to find the right person for a job, depending on what the situation calls for.\n\nYou become trained in Society and gain the Streetwise skill feat. In addition, when you're in a settlement with a significant kasatha population, you can request help or expertise by meeting with a member of a Great Family; when you do so, you gain a +2 status bonus to Society checks to Gather Information."],["You have studied the art of adat—the kasathan mystical technique of preserving a slice of brain from a deceased intelligent creature and establishing a technomagical link to the creature's soul. The kasathan Doyenate use these to preserve the wisdom of their ancestors, and you've adapted their technique for use in the field to draw important information out of a target or send disorienting messages to a target's mind.\n\nYou gain Holographic Memory and Void Whispers as 3rd-rank divine innate spells. You can cast each spell once per day, and when you cast *holographic memory*, you can extract a memory of up to 10 minutes instead of 5 minutes."],["While it pales in comparison to the powers of a true solarian, you are a devoted disciple of the Cycle and can temporarily manifest control over the powers of the cosmos. You gain Entropy Strike and Skyfire Wings as 3rd-rank occult innate spells. You can cast each of these occult innate spells once per day."],["You've become so soaked in void energies from your studies that you're empowered by them. You gain void healing until you Dismiss the effect."],["You've come closer to finding balance between two extremes of energy, learning how to expel or draw in excess heat when necessary. You gain resistance 5 to cold and fire. Additionally, you gain the Redirect Energy reaction."],["You've forged a strong relationship with your ancestors through years of shared customs and fellowship. You feel so close to them that by simply recalling the story of their life and enacting one of their cherished traditions, you can channel a portion of their wisdom into yourself.\n\nChoose one skill to emulate for 10 minutes. You gain a +2 status bonus to that skill and can attempt any skill check that normally requires you to have master proficiency in that skill, and if you're untrained in that skill, your proficiency bonus to untrained skill checks is equal to your level."],["Through your knowledge of traditional kasathan healing rituals and meditative practices, you've learned to cleanse the body and mind of the ill or troubled. You gain Cleanse Affliction and Sound Body as 4th-rank occult innate spells. You can cast each of these occult innate spells once per day."],["You have exceptional control over your body. You can use Natural Grace once per hour, rather than once per day."],["You're taller than the average kasatha—which is saying something. Your height combined with your long limbs and natural dexterity allow you to target foes even when your allies are in the way. You ignore lesser cover when Striking an enemy with a ranged weapon if that lesser cover is caused by an ally."],["Kasathan combat training tends to focus on grace instead of economy of movement. Certain forms and gestures are passed down both for their beauty and their capacity to distract an unfocused foe. Once per turn, when you Switch Hands you can [[/act feint]] as a free action."],["You become trained in a Lore skill of your choice. You can spend 10 minutes checking your notes or research materials to Recall Knowledge about a piece of history with any Lore skill in which you aren't trained, using your highest Lore skill modifier instead of your modifier with that skill."],["You've learned how to adapt your martial expertise to wield other weapons. When wielding a weapon you aren't proficient with, treat your level as your proficiency bonus.\n\nAt 11th level, you become trained in all weapons."],["Your masked face prevents others from scrutinizing your appearance, and you've learned to leverage this uncertainty to your advantage in social situations. While your mouth is covered, increase the DC of any Perception check to Sense Motive against you by 2. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Lie, make a Request, or Make an Impression."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYour experience living with undead has helped you understand the necromantic energies that animate the undead brain and the intrinsic forces that keep such creatures animate. You sense the void energy that makes up a mindless undead foe's consciousness. One mindless undead foe within 60 feet must attempt a Will saving throw against the higher of your class DC or spell DC.\n\n**Failure** The undead creature loses immunity to mental effects until the beginning of your next turn.\n\nUndead Understanding (Failure)\n\n**Critical Failure** The undead creature loses immunity to mental effects for 1 minute.\n\nUndead Understanding (Critical Failure)"],["**Requirements** You're Untethered in zero gravity.\n\n---\n\nYou have learned kasathan techniques that takes advantage of your extra arms for increasing your defense in zero gravity. You curl yourself into a tight ball, using one set of arms to balance and one set of arms to protect yourself. You lose the Off-Guard condition from being untethered, and you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC and Reflex saves for as long as you're untethered or until you use an action with the manipulate trait.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you're a Void Acolyte Kasatha, you don't lose the benefits of Weightless Defense by using an action with the manipulate trait."],["Your affinity with the plant life of Kasath has made it so that you can summon it from nearly anywhere.\n\nYou gain Verdant Code as a 2nd-rank arcane innate spell you can cast once per hour. You gain a +2 status bonus to your basic Reflex saves to avoid the piercing damage from your *verdant code*."],["Your relationship with death has progressed such that you are empowered when you feel it near. You can use the Doomsayer's Litany reaction as often as you like.\n\nIn addition to its usual trigger, you can use Doomsayer's Litany whenever an ally's Dying value increases. When you use the reaction, the +2 status bonus applies to any recovery checks or saving throw the ally attempts until the end of their next turn, instead of just the triggering recovery check.\n\nWhenever you use your Doomsayer's Litany reaction, you gain a status bonus equal to your Doomed value or the doomed value of the triggering ally to attack rolls and saving throws until the end of your next turn."],["You know that there's no such thing as a true zero-gravity environment. You're sensitive to the ebbs and flows of microgravity and can use it to propel yourself even when you're floating Untethered. When you're in an area of zero gravity, you gain a fly Speed of 30 feet, and you can Fly in zero gravity.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can use the Weightless Defense feat while Flying in zero gravity, even if you're not untethered. The benefits end if you stop Flying or leave zero gravity."],["You've cataloged countless customs, histories, and traditions. You can cast hypercognition once per day as a 3rd-rank occult innate spell. You can use your modifier for the Lore skill you chose for Historian in place of any other skill modifier when attempting a Recall Knowledge check while casting Hypercognition."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou have a particular interest in the inconsistencies of reality and the material universe that you've read about in philosophical texts. You overload a technological foe's logic processes by posing a paradoxical problem to them. The tech creature must have an Intelligence modifier of –3 or higher, and they must understand the language you speak. The creature attempts a Will saving throw against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. Any creature targeted by Logical Paradox becomes immune to it for 24 hours, no matter the result of their saving throw.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature's logic processes are strong enough to understand your logical paradox, and it has no effect.\n\n**Success** The creature becomes Glitching 1.\n\n**Failure** The creature becomes Glitching 2.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature becomes glitching 2 and is also Stupefied 2 for as long as it remains glitching."],["You are in tune with your surroundings and can instinctively sense when danger is near. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks for initiative rolls. If your initiative roll result is tied with that of an opponent, you go first, regardless of whether you rolled Perception or not. The first time each day that you roll Perception for initiative, you roll initiative twice and use the higher result."],["Whether in isolation or in communion with others of your kind, you've contemplated the nature of your ancestry for many years. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Nature and Survival. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore feat for Khizar Lore."],["You have an empathic understanding of nature and can use your limited telepathy to communicate with plants and fungi, even if you don't share a common language. You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with plants and fungi. In most cases, wild plants and fungi will give you time to make your case. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your checks to Make an Impression on plants and fungi."],["You can become virtually indistinguishable from a common tree or tangled vines. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Stealth checks when you're in a natural area that contains flora, and you can use Deception to Impersonate plant life, including stationary plants like shrubs or plant creatures like ksariks. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to these checks."],["Your limbs and trunk grow strong and thick enough to shield your allies from danger. You can share your space with up to one willing ally. While an ally is sharing space with you or occupying an adjacent square, your ally gains the benefits of lesser cover. The ally can Take Cover to increase the bonus to standard cover."],["You've grown a stout vine that you can use to bludgeon enemies. You gain a vine unarmed attack, which is in the brawling weapon group, deals 1d6 bludgeoning damage, and has the khizar, sweep, trip, and unarmed traits."],["Once per day, you can deploy your seedpod as a single action, which has the concentrate trait. When deployed this way, your seedpod can travel up to 200 feet away from you, with a fly Speed of 20 feet. Moving the seedpod is a free action, which you can take once per turn, and you can sense through it in all directions as if using your normal senses. After 1 minute, the seedpod returns directly to you at its normal Speed."],["**Trigger** You become Unconscious, dying, or dead while standing.\n\n---\n\nYou fall like a mighty tree, dealing 7d6 bludgeoning damage to each creature in a 10-foot line originating from your square with a basic Reflex save against your class DC; on a critical failure, a medium or smaller creature falls Prone and is Immobilized until your body is removed."],["Your flowering is a reservoir of incredible vitality energy. Once per day, you can cast Breath of Life as a primal innate spell."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** You're exposed to natural sunlight.\n\n---\n\nYour body regenerates by taking in nutrients from natural sunlight. You gain regeneration 20 for 1 minute."],["You can draw on a wellspring of primal power to cast Energy Aegis as a 7th-rank primal innate spell once per day."],["When you die, a seed sprouts from your body. The seedling is a copy of you lacking any of your memories, though it has vague memories of your relationships and might feel fond of your allies or distrustful of your enemies. Over 1d6 weeks, the seedling grows into a miniature version of you with the same attributes and abilities (but Small instead of Medium). Over 1d6 months, you grow to your original size. A new seedling germinates in you over 10 years; if you die again before then, the seedling dies too."],["Once per day as an Interact action, you can siphon nutrients from a dead creature. You consume part of a creature that hasn't been dead for more than 24 hours, and you heal 3d8 Hit Points, plus 1d8 for every 2 of your levels beyond 5th ((ceil(level/2)d8) healing)."],["You're an unstoppable transplant who has adapted to thrive in brutal environments vastly different from the lush forests of Castrovel. You always count as adapted to a planet's environment, and you always take half damage from environmental effects such as from cold, heat, or corrosive atmospheres."],["Your body has two primary \"trunks,\" one of which has diverged in nature from the other. Choose one khizar heritage that you don't already have; you gain that heritage and its benefits."],["The vines you use to move—what others call your limbs—are extra long. Increase your land Speed and climb Speed by 5 feet."],["You grow a floating secondary seedpod you can use to fool other creatures. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Create a Diversion or Feint. Once every 10 minutes, you can deploy this lure as a move action. It remains deployed for 1 minute or until you Dismiss it. Any creature targeting you with an attack must attempt a DC 5 flat check; on a failure, the creature hits the seedpod lure instead of you, destroying it. A new one grows after 10 minutes of rest."],["You can detect the vital essence of creatures. You gain lifesense as an imprecise sense with a range of 30 feet. This means you can sense the vital essence of living and undead creatures within range. You can distinguish between the vitality energy animating living creatures and the void energy animating undead creatures, much as sight distinguishes colors."],["The sticky sap produced by your vined body has healing properties. You produce 1d4 vials of sap each day when you are exposed to natural sunlight for at least 4 hours. A creature that drinks a vial of the sap as an Interact action restores 2d8 Hit Points. This effect has the healing and vitality traits."],["You influence others with pheromones, even when you lack other means of communication. You can use Diplomacy to Make an Impression on creatures with whom you don't share a language and to make simple Requests of them. This could include getting directions or getting the target to pick a specific individual out from a crowd. When you do, Make an Impression and Request lose the linguistic trait and gain the olfactory trait."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail a Will saving throw against a mental effect.\n\n---\n\nYou center your thoughts and focus your mind, shaking off emotional turmoil and harmful mental intrusions. Reroll the triggering saving throw and use the better result."],["You can leverage your alluring pheromones to soothe ill will and take the edge off your threats, turning your attempts at coercion into acts of leadership. When you Coerce a creature, if your target would become unfriendly (and they aren't already unfriendly or hostile), they become indifferent instead."],["You've studied the lives and achievements of other lashuntas who have improved both their psychic powers and their communities. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Occultism and Society. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Lashunta Lore."],["You learned to manipulate your pheromones in compensation for a lack of telepathy. You can [[/act make-an-impression traits=olfactory]] with your pheromones, which causes your attempt to lose the auditory and linguistic traits and instead gain the olfactory trait. If you use your pheromones to enhance your speech (by retaining the auditory and linguistic traits while also adding the olfactory trait to the action), you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to this check. When modified in this way, a failure on a check to Make an Impression becomes a critical failure instead."],["You honed your negotiation skills from balancing the triad of elves, formians, and lashuntas on Castrovel. When you attempt to [[/act make-an-impression]], you can choose two non-ally targets. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your check against one target, and a –2 circumstance penalty against the other target. If you succeed against both targets, you critically succeed against both instead."],["Your psychic abilities manifest in a supernatural connection to the natural world, particularly the jungles on Castrovel and on planets with similar environments. You gain the Tangle Vine and Scan Environment cantrips as primal innate spells at will. These cantrips are heightened to half your level."],["You can sense changes to flora and fauna within the range of your limited telepathy. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to find living environmental hazards. Even if you aren't Searching, you can attempt to find living environmental hazards that normally require you to be Searching."],["You attempt to smooth over an erupting conflict or at least make one target less likely to hurt you. You Stride twice, then attempt to [[/act make-an-impression]]. If you end your Strides closer to a target, use the outcome one degree of success worse than the result of your check, and if you end your Stride further from a target, use the outcome one degree of success better than the result of your check. Instead of the normal results of Make an Impression, use the following.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** For the next minute, or until you perform a hostile action toward the target or one of the target's allies, the creature takes a –2 circumstance penalty to attack rolls and to its save DCs for any hostile actions that include you as a target or include you in the area.\n\nDiplomatic Retreat (Critical Success)\n\n**Success** As critical success, but it only lasts until the end of your next turn.\n\nDiplomatic Retreat (Success)\n\n**Critical Failure** Until the end of your next turn, the creature gains a +1 circumstance bonus to attack rolls and save DCs for any hostile actions that include you as a target or include you in the area.\n\nDiplomatic Retreat (Critical Failure)"],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou can purposefully deploy your pheromones to manipulate the reactions of those around you. If your next action is to attempt a Deception check to Create a Diversion, a Diplomacy check to Request, or an Intimidation check to Demoralize, roll that skill check twice and use the better result."],["You can use your telepathic abilities to quickly assess your circumstances or subtly glean information from the minds of others. You can cast Hypercognition and Mind Reading as 3rd-rank occult innate spells. You can cast each of these occult innate spells once per day."],["As your connection grows, you become adept at pulling energy out of the world around you. You gain Discharge and Earthbind as 3rd-rank primal innate spells. You can cast each of these primal innate spells once per day."],["You know your own mind and instinctively resist attempts to unbalance your thoughts or control your emotions. You can use Center Thoughts once per hour, rather than once per day."],["Your embrace of the role of damaya helped you become a lifelong learner. You gain the Additional Lore skill feat twice and the Legendary Professional skill feat."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou know that changing your body is cheap, but gear is expensive. When you Invest an Item that has the apex trait, you can change the attribute your apex item increases to another attribute of your choice."],["You have perfected what it means to be a korasha and embody lashunta values around physical strength and might. Increase your maximum Hit Points by your level. When you succeed at an attempt to [[/act shove]] or [[/act trip]], you critically succeed instead."],["**Trigger** A creature Casts a Spell with the mental trait.\n\n**Requirements** You have at least 1 Focus Point.\n\n---\n\nWhen a foe Casts a Spell that has the mental trait and you can see or otherwise detect its manifestations, you use your psychic powers to disrupt it. You expend 1 Focus Point to counter the triggering creature's casting of the spell. You then attempt to counteract the triggering spell using your spellcasting attribute modifier plus your spellcasting proficiency bonus as your counteract modifier and half your level, rounded up, as your counteract rank."],["Your psychic abilities have grown stronger. Choose one common 6th-rank spell from the occult spell list. You can cast that spell as an occult innate spell once per day."],["Your psychic connection to the environment stretches to the ground below and manipulates lava as though it were alive. You gain Wall of Fire and *Uncanny Eruption* as 7th-rank primal innate spells. You can cast each of these primal innate spells once per day."],["You defined self-perfection and will let no other voices influence you. Your control over your mind is resolute, allowing you to shake off the worst effects your foes impart.\n\nWhenever you attempt a saving throw against an ability that would impart the Confused or Controlled condition you roll twice and take the better result; this is a fortune effect.\n\nIf you have the confused or controlled condition, you can attempt a Will save to end the effect at the start of each of your turns."],["Navigating the jungles of Castrovel is a task fit for an adrenaline junkie. When you attempt a Stunt while Piloting a vehicle, you reduce the penalty to your check by 1 (minimum 0)."],["**Frequency** once per minute\n\n---\n\nYou learn to crowd the minds of other creatures with your psychic static and emit it as a protective field. Each adjacent creature attempts a Will save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.\n\n**Failure** The target is Off-Guard against the next melee or ranged attack that you attempt against it before the end of your current turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is off-guard against melee and ranged attacks that you attempt against it until the end of your next turn.\n\n---\n\n**Special** As a 10-minute exploration activity, you can make any number of allies temporarily immune to this ability for 24 hours. Creatures that can't access telepathy, such as other static mind lashuntas, are immune to Deployed Static."],["Your connection to the psychic energy of the natural world grows and anchors your abilities. You gain Cellular Stimulant and Gentle Landing as 1st-rank primal innate spells. You can cast each one of these primal innate spells once per day."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou bark a simple command to spur your allies to action. Select Stride, Strike, or Step. Your allies who can perceive your command can use their reaction to take the action you selected. This action gains the auditory trait if you shout, but not if you use telepathy."],["You can leverage your telepathic abilities to influence the minds of others, imparting orders or inflaming fears. You can cast Command and Fear as 1st-rank occult innate spells. You can cast each of these occult innate spells once per day."],["You can transfer vast amounts of information to the minds of others in mere moments. You can cast Mindlink as a 1st-rank occult innate spell twice per day."],["Your mastery of your psychic powers makes your targets more susceptible to later spells. When a creature fails or critically fails a saving throw against one of your innate spells gained from an ancestry feat, they take a –1 status penalty to saving throws against your other innate spells until the end of your next turn.\n\nPsychic Wedge"],["Your antennae are covered in fine hairs that make them more sensitive to psychic vibrations than most. You gain thoughtsense as a vague sense with a range of 30 feet. This means you can use your antennae to determine if a creature is within range. Your thoughtsense detects only thinking creatures, so a creature that's unthinking or otherwise immune to mental effects can't be perceived using your thoughtsense. This doesn't give you the ability to read or understand their thoughts.\n\nAt 9th level, this becomes an imprecise sense."],["Your psychic abilities continue to expand as your mind starts to meld with the world around you. You gain Entangling Flora and Verdant Code as 2nd-rank primal innate spells. You can cast each of these primal innate spells once per day."],["Your psychic training allows you to block attempts to read your thoughts. Any effect that specifically attempts to read your mind to glean information must succeed at a counteract check against the higher of your class DC or your spell DC to do so successfully; otherwise, it gains no information. The counteract rank is equal to half your level rounded up."],["Your psychic abilities stimulate growth in the world around you. If the next action you use is to Cast a primal innate Spell, you make plants grow around you in a 15-foot emanation. Other creatures treat this area as difficult terrain for 1 minute."],["Your psychic abilities have grown stronger, allowing you to tap into entirely new dimensions of psychic power. Choose one common 2nd-rank spell from the occult spell list. You can cast that spell as an occult innate spell once per day."],["**Trigger** You roll Diplomacy or Intimidation for initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou know negotiations fail and aren't afraid to resort to force when they do. You attempt to [[/act demoralize]] a foe you were observing and engaged in conversation with for at least 1 minute."],["During your daily preparations, you can piece together fragmentary memories of your past lives to gain the trained proficiency rank in one skill of your choice. This proficiency lasts until you prepare again. Since this proficiency is temporary, you can't use it to satisfy a prerequisite for a skill increase or a permanent character option like a feat."],["You were either created in a densely populated area such as a city or have spent significant time in one. As a result, you've learned to apply your intuition and knowledge from the wilderness to the streets of metropolises and the narrow corridors of massive starships alike. You become trained in Survival (or another skill if you're already trained in Survival), and you gain the Urban Survivalist skill feat."],["You gather organic plant or fungal matter to your body, permanently increasing your size. You become Large.\n\nOnce per day as a two-action activity with the concentrate trait, you can grow a burst of foliage that further reinforces your body, increasing your reach by 5 feet, granting you a +2 status bonus to melee damage rolls, and making you Clumsy 1 for 10 minutes.\n\nAgglomerate Leshy"],["Your body contains polymers that you can rapidly reconfigure to resist extreme temperatures. You treat environmental cold and heat effects as if they were two steps less extreme (incredible cold becomes severe, extreme cold becomes mild, and so on).\n\nAdditionally, you gain resistance equal to half your level to your choice of cold or fire. You can change your choice during daily preparations, as well as with the Instantaneous Adaptation reaction."],["You conjure plants from every surface to ensnare your foes. You can cast Tangling Creepers once per hour as a 6th-rank primal innate spell."],["You can blend effortlessly into nature. You can [[/act hide]] in natural environments even without cover or concealment, and you don't become automatically Observed in a natural environment if you end your [[/act sneak]] without cover or concealment."],["The plant or fungus your body is based upon has a penchant for becoming a multi-planetary invasive species. When you're not on your home world, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against diseases and poisons. When you succeed at a saving throw against an affliction that's benefiting from this bonus, you improve your condition by 2 stages (or by 1 stage if the affliction is virulent)."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou channel extra spores into one of your spore pods, preparing it to choke your target. Make a spore pod Strike. If it hits, you deal spore pod damage as normal and your target must succeed at a Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC or become Clumsy 1 for 1 minute (or Clumsy 2 on a critical failure). You also gain the critical specialization effect for your spore pod Strike."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYour body is covered in thorns, spines, or other sharp protrusions, which you can position defensively. For 1 minute, adjacent creatures that hit you with a melee attack, as well as creatures that hit you with melee unarmed attacks, take level piercing damage equal to your level."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** Your last action was a successful tentacle Strike against a living creature.\n\n---\n\nYou absorb fragments of the genetic code and psychic energy of living creatures through your tentacles to temporarily augment your abilities.\n\nPick one damage type that your target is resistant or immune to. You gain resistance to that damage type equal to half your level for 1 minute. If the creature has a compound resistance or immunity, pick one damage type; for example, if a creature is resistant to all physical damage, you could pick bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing.\n\nIf you don't know the target's resistances or immunities, you gain a resistance chosen at random. If the target has no immunities or resistances, you gain no resistance, and this use doesn't count against Adaptive Resistance's frequency."],["You can activate the energy within technology and spur it into new, blossoming life. You can cast Verdant Code as a 2nd-rank primal innate spell once per hour."],["Light is nourishment for you, even if it comes in the form of highly concentrated beams. You gain resistance 5 against laser weapons and effects with the light trait. You can also use the Photon Accelerator activity."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYour digestive enzymes can break down just about any organic material into food. You eject a spray of digestive enzymes in a 20-foot cone, dealing (ceil(level/2)+1)d6 acid damage plus 1d6 acid damage for every 2 levels beyond 9th (to a maximum of 11d6 at 19th level), with a basic Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. The digestive slurry remains liquid for 1 hour. As long as at least one living creature in the cone failed its saving throw, the slurry contains nutrients that you can absorb to restore your body. If you spend 10 minutes absorbing the liquid slurry through your roots, you regain level*6 healing Hit Points equal to 6 times your level."],["You surge your internal light in a brilliant flash, disorienting everyone nearby and revealing anything that would try to hide from your sight. You can cast Revealing Light as a 2nd-rank primal innate spell once per hour, except it doesn't dazzle moonflowers and moonflower leshies."],["Your core can levitate, enabling your hardlight body to fly. You gain a fly Speed equal to your Speed. When you Disable Hardlight Projector, your core hovers in place 3 feet above the ground, rather than falling to the ground.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you're a hover ad living hologram, you instead gain a fly Speed equal to your Speed + 10 feet."],["You've tapped into the captivating magical power of emoji. You can cast *emoticon* as an occult innate cantrip at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["You've installed an algorithm that uses a refraction of your hardlight to allow you to see in the absence of any other light. You gain low-light vision.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat a second time. When you do, you gain darkvision."],["You have a unique weapon integrated into your hardlight body, perhaps a bladed arm, a shoulder-mounted cryo cannon, or a kiss attack that fires sparkling cartoon hearts. When you select this feat, you gain one of the following unarmed attacks of your choice. Each of these attacks has the unarmed trait.\n\n- A melee unarmed attack that deals 1d8 damage.\n\n- A melee unarmed attack that deals 1d6 damage and has the agile and finesse traits.\n\n- A ranged unarmed attack that deals 1d6 damage and has a range increment of 30 feet.\n\n- A ranged unarmed attack that deals 1d4 damage and has a range increment of 60 feet.\n\nOnce you make this decision, select the type of damage your weapon deals and an associated weapon group from among the following options: acid (corrosive weapon group), bludgeoning (brawling, club, or hammer weapon group), cold (cryo weapon group), electricity (shock weapon group), fire (flame or laser weapon group), piercing (brawling, knife, or spear weapon group), slashing (brawling, knife, or sword weapon group), or sonic (sonic weapon group).\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with your hardlight weapon, you get its critical specialization effect."],["You're perpetually online, surfing the infosphere, chatting with friends, and scrolling your social feeds. Your core has an integrated comm unit you can operate by thought alone, even making calls without audibly speaking. At 5th level, this functions as a Commercial Hacker's Toolkit and an Advanced Hacker's Toolkit at 8th level. This doesn't count as an augmentation and is immune to the glitching condition."],["You reprogram the appearance of your hardlight body over the course of 10 minutes. As part of this activity, you can change your size to one of the following of your choice: Small, Medium, or Large. You maintain this size and appearance until you next Reprogram Appearance."],["You can roll your core around with surprising mobility, allowing you to move without a projected body. Add Step and Stride to the list of actions you can take while you aren't projecting your hardlight body."],["Your hardlight projectors are adjusted to provide you with flexible defensive capabilities. You can cast Shield as an arcane innate cantrip at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou've added automated repair subroutines to your core in case of extreme damage. You Disable Hardlight Projector and gain fast healing 10 for 1 minute or until you Project Hardlight Body, whichever happens first."],["Instead of directing your hardlight at a single foe, you cause it to flash impossibly bright all around you. Whenever you use Trick of the Light, you can choose to have it affect every creature in a 15-foot emanation rather than a single target."],["You've got a favored routine you perform repeatedly and have learned how to do so efficiently without risk. Select one of the following actions: Anti-Glitch Response, Let Me Hear You Cheer, or Light Hop. The frequency of the selected action becomes once per 10 minutes, rather than once per day.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat more than once, selecting a different action each time."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou overclock your core and its movement subroutines to move so fast that everything else seems to slow down. For 1 minute, you gain a +10-foot status bonus to your Speeds, and you become Quickened. You can use the extra action each round only to Stride.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Light Hop feat, you can use the extra action gained from Fast Forward to Light Hop or Stride; when you Light Hop in this way, it doesn't count toward Light Hop's frequency."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nAs a living hologram, you know how to blend in with other forms of light and how light can be used to your advantage to distract or misdirect those who aren't as experienced manipulating light. These lived experiences have made you aware of the little clues that can give away the position of someone trying to avoid notice. You heighten your senses, gaining the effects of a Truesight spell."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail or critically fail a flat check you attempted due to the glitching condition.\n\n---\n\nAfter much trial and error, you've programmed your core to diagnose and repair glitching systems. Reroll the triggering flat check, and use the better result."],["You can stretch your arms extra far! When you Cartoonish Stretch, you increase your reach by 10 feet, rather than 5 feet.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat three times. The second time you do, you increase your reach by 15 feet when you Cartoonish Stretch, rather than 5 feet. The third time you do, you increase your reach by 20 feet when you Cartoonish Stretch, rather than 5 feet."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nFor the briefest of moments, you're able to move as a beam of light. You teleport yourself (and any items you're wearing and holding) to an unoccupied space you can see within 60 feet."],["Your core projects incredibly lifelike holograms. Your holographic body is no longer semi-translucent and doesn't look like a hologram.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Reprogram Appearance feat, you don't require a holoskin to Impersonate, and if you critically fail a Deception check to Impersonate, you get a failure instead."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou redirect some of your hardlight at a creature's eyes in an attempt to dazzle them. One creature of your choice within 30 feet must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.\n\n**Failure** The creature is Dazzled for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is dazzled for 3 rounds."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYour integrated toolkit repairs a touched common tech item with a level up to your level with the broken or glitching condition. It loses the broken condition until the end of your turn, allowing you to use the item as normal. You also reduce the glitching value of the item you touch by 1."],["**Frequency** three times per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail a Reflex saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYou take advantage of your hardlight body's malleability and shape by turning sideways or flattening your body in an attempt to avoid incoming danger. You reroll the triggering save and use the better result."],["You've improved your core's manipulation routines, enabling more of your holographic limbs to function. Your hardlight body gains one additional pair of arms.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat multiple times, gaining one additional pair of arms each time."],["You take advantage of your hardlight body by bending light around your core to hide in plain sight. You can cast Invisibility twice per day as a 2nd-rank arcane innate spell."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou swiftly change size, becoming Small, Medium, or Large. If you became smaller, you can Create a Distraction or [[/act hide]] as part of this action. If you became larger, you can [[/act demoralize]] as part of this action. You remain this size until you next Reprogram Appearance or Zoom In, Zoom Out."],["You ensure that you can dutifully perform your assigned role to the best of your abilities, whether that be for the Virtuum or for yourself. You gain a 1st-level class feat for your class. You must meet the prerequisites, but you can select the feat later in the character creation process in order to determine which prerequisites you meet."],["You ensure that your knowledge in a task is absolute. You gain the Additional Lore feat and the Assurance feat for the chosen Lore. When you forgo rolling a skill check using Assurance for the associated Lore, you receive a result of 11 + your proficiency bonus (instead of 10 + your proficiency bonus)."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYour extra thumb allows you to quickly shift control of weapons that normally require more concentration to manage. You Interact to change your grip on an item you're holding from one-handed to two-handed or vice-versa."],["Your blood works to assist you and even helps others who try to heal your wounded form. You can use Battle Medicine and Treat Wounds without a medkit, and your allies don't need a medkit to use Battle Medicine on you or Treat your Wounds. The first time each day, when someone rolls a failure or a critical failure on a check to use Battle Medicine on you or Treat your Wounds, the magic in your blood coagulates to assist and increases the degree of success by one step, even if you're Unconscious."],["Your hands maintain a firm grip on anything they hold. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Reflex DC when defending against checks to [[/act disarm]] you. A creature that succeeds at a check to Disarm you gains only a +1 circumstance bonus on further attempts to Disarm you, and you take only a –1 circumstance penalty to attacks with the held item."],["Your blood consumes arcane magic. Whenever you successfully save against a foe's harmful spell or magical effect, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to the spell's rank or equal to the level if the magical effect isn't a spell (double the number of temporary Hit Points you gain if the spell or trait is arcane). You gain these temporary Hit Points before the effect is resolved, and they last until the end of your next turn."],["You channel a portion of your blood into your weapon to empower your next Strike. The first time you successfully Strike a creature before the end of your turn, your target becomes tinged with your blood for the next minute. Double the range of any of your spells that target any creature tinged with your blood. In addition, you don't need line of sight to target them with spells, though you still need line of effect.\n\n---\n\n**Special** Blood-tinged Attack is a free action if you're taking persistent bleed damage."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou invoke your arcane blood so that it can revitalize and energize your body. You regain 6d6 healing Hit Points. You also gain the Quickened condition until the end of your next turn and can use the extra action to only Stride or Strike."],["As you've progressed through life, you've taken your role as a stalwart worker to heart, and your bloodline surges to support you in your duties. You can use Madrosarai Tenacity with a frequency of once per hour, rather than once per day."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou accelerate the blood in your veins, charging latent magical energies within. For 1 minute, any adjacent creature that touches you, deals piercing or slashing damage to you, or hits you with a melee unarmed attack takes 3d6 fire damage."],["By exerting absolute control over your emotions, you stay perpetually composed. You diffuse any effects related to emotions that impact you, making you immune to emotion effects."],["Once per month, when you die, you can choose to invoke your devotion to a single willing living creature you know. Your life essence becomes inextricably bound to that creature, letting you survive beyond death. Your body immediately disappears, and after 1 month, you return to life at maximum Hit Points, appearing within 30 feet of the target of your devotion. If the target of your devotion dies, then you immediately die. If you die and choose not to use this ability, your spirit might return as a ghost or other spirit under the GM's control."],["Your golden blood grants you access to powerful magic that lets you better lead and threaten those around you. You gain Command and Fear as 1st-rank arcane innate spells. You can cast each of these arcane innate spells once per day."],["Your magical blood resists being spilled. Your DC on flat checks to end persistent bleed damage is reduced from 15 to 10, or from 10 to 5 after receiving especially appropriate assistance."],["Your extra set of eyes allows you to constantly be aware of your surroundings. You aren't Off-Guard to flanking creatures of your level or lower."],["**Trigger** You roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nWhether by patient analysis or a moment of inspiration, you're prepared for combat. You can Interact to draw a weapon, or you can Step."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou channel some of the power of your blood into your spellcasting abilities to help support them. You regain 1 Focus Point, up to your usual maximum."],["You're exceptionally difficult to kill. The DC of your recovery checks is equal to 9 + your Dying value, or 8 + your dying value if you have the Toughness general feat. In addition, whenever someone returns you to life using magic that would normally leave you debilitated for a week (such as Raise Dead or the Resurrect ritual), you don't suffer that condition."],["You unleash your contained anger at a situation. Your size increases to Large, and you're Clumsy 1. You gain a +1 status bonus to melee damage. This doesn't change your Speed, reach, or other statistics except as noted here. Your worn equipment automatically resizes to suit your new form, though it immediately returns to its original size if it leaves your possession. These effects last for 1 round. You can Sustain for up to 10 minutes, though you must then spend at least 10 minutes in your natural form before using Unleashed Anger again.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you're a Red-Blooded Madrosarai, you can use Controlled Rage as a free action right after using Unleashed Anger. If you do, you gain a +2 status bonus to melee damage."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You attempt a saving throw against an area effect with the arcane trait.\n\n---\n\nYou attempt to absorb some of the magic of an incoming spell into your blood. Attempt a counteract check against the triggering effect; your counteract rank equals half your level (rounded up), and for the counteract check, use the higher of your spell attack modifier or your class DC minus 10. If you counteract the triggering effect, you end the effect for all other creatures in the area, but you become Drained 1 for 10 minutes as your body struggles to contain the transfusion of magic."],["You can pull a chunk of the ethereal realm of dreams into reality, providing you and allies with a measure of safety. You can cast Cozy Crashpad as a 3rd-rank arcane innate spell once per day, except it comes with a vendor constructed entirely based on your desires (though once chosen, it can't be changed). You can order items from this attendant, with an item level equal to or less than half your level (rounded up). As long as you pay for these items, they appear at the end of the 12-hour duration or when you Dismiss the spell."],["You hone your anger into a prolonged duration, allowing you to overcome foes in the heat of battle. Your Unleashed Anger lasts for 10 minutes without the need to Sustain it. While in this form, increase your reach by 5 feet."],["Your psychic potential expands, encouraged by your blood. Choose one 1st-rank occult spell and one 2nd-rank occult spell. You can cast each of these spells once per day as occult innate spells."],["With arcane blood in your veins, you can deflect the worst effects of magic. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against arcane spells and effects."],["You've developed a healthy appreciation for your prehensile tail. It's hard to imagine life without it—you'd probably fall over all the time. Luckily, yours is there to help keep your balance, even in the trickiest situations. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Acrobatics checks to Balance and a +1 circumstance bonus to your Reflex DC against attempts to Trip you. As long as your tail isn't holding an item, you aren't Off-Guard while on a narrow surface or uneven ground."],["Though cutting-edge technology has only recently arrived in your home world, you've proven yourself to be a natural with new trinkets and devices the moment you get your hands on them. You become trained in Crafting. If you would automatically become trained in Crafting (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus on Crafting checks to [[/act recall-knowledge skill=crafting]] about tech items."],["The key to a good jump isn't speed, and it isn't technique. It's a powerful set of legs, and you've got some of the strongest. You gain the Powerful Leap skill feat, even if you don't meet the prerequisites. You treat all falls as if they were 10 feet less than the actual distance traveled, or 40 feet less if you're falling immediately after you Leap."],["Though your surroundings might have changed, you're adept at bending them to your purposes: you grab whatever is close at hand and build your own tools, shelters, and in this case, protection. Where others might struggle to find cover from enemy fire, you can piece together safety from the most meager supplies. You gain the Barricade general feat. If you construct a barricade in a natural environment, it falls apart after two turns instead of at the end of your next turn."],["To navigate the wilds of Marata, you ask more of your body than most. You become trained in Athletics. If you would automatically become trained in Athletics (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. When you fall, you can Grab an Edge using your tail with an Athletics ([[/act grab-an-edge skill=athletics]]) check instead of Acrobatics."],["When outside technology started streaming into Marata, industrious maraquois didn't simply accept it: they wanted to learn how it worked. You love taking new toys apart to see what makes them tick—but unlike most, you can always put them back together. You become trained in Crafting. If you would automatically become trained in Crafting (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Crafting checks to Craft a formula by reverse engineering it from an item you possess."],["Years of darting between cactus-like plants, climbing the twisting, gnarled trunks of kvashes, and leaping across giant chasms have paid off. Your Speed increases by 5 feet."],["Years of practice leaping from kvash to kvash, kicking off of walls, and racing your peers through the canopy weren't just good fun, they've translated wonderfully into close combat. You gain the Wall Jump skill feat. You can use Wall Jump to make additional jumps off of creatures your size or larger as if they were walls. Once per turn, when you make an additional jump off a creature in this way, you can also attempt to [[/act shove]] or [[/act trip]] that creature as a free action.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have Leaping Expertise, you can jump off a wall to increase your fly Speed by 10 when using a Jetpack or Jump Jet."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You would fail a save against a spell or effect with the void trait.\n\n---\n\nThe darkness between the stars isn't simply a void for your people, it's a storehouse for a great reserve of energy, built by generation after generation of maraquois. When the darkness threatens to take hold of you, the power of that ancestral wellspring swells forth and lifts you up. You reroll the triggering saving throw with a +1 status bonus. You must use the second result, even if it's worse."],["For a maraquoi, hearing is a full-body experience. While most of your kind can use their hypersensitive hearing to track the world around them with great precision, you've taken the ability to the next level. By concentrating on the vibrations rolling across thousands of receptors on your skin, you can pick up on the slightest movement and use it to find hidden enemies. Your Dermal Hearing becomes a precise sense."],["Through study and meditation, you've found a powerful link to the great gifts your ancestors have prepared for you. Through your connection with the ancestral wellspring, you have access to the combined wisdom of thousands of generations. From their place between the stars, they can guide your actions and tell you things about the world around you that you'd never learn on your own. You are permanently Quickened and can use that extra action only to Recall Knowledge."],["You can jump from enemy to enemy and never have to touch the ground. Instead of being able to [[/act shove]] or [[/act trip]] a creature once per turn, you can Shove, Strike, or Trip a creature you use as a wall for Wall Jump up to three times per turn, but only once per creature per round."],["You've gone a step further than most and upgraded your body with built-in data access. You always count as having a Comm Unit available, even if you don't have a comm unit equipped.\n\nYou can use a 1-minute activity, which has the manipulate trait, to integrate a single Datapad into one of your arms. You can draw or stow this item as an Interact action. Creatures don't automatically see this integrated item when it's stowed and must actively [[/act seek]] to find it. They take a –2 circumstance penalty to any checks to do so. While you're wielding the item, it can't be Disarmed, and you can't drop or Release it; you must Interact to store the item and free that hand. A creature determined to retrieve the item can do so, but it requires either 1 minute to remove the item or extreme violence to your arm—such as physically removing portions of the limb. You can have only one integrated datapad at a time, though you can use the 1-minute activity to replace the datapad or swap the arm in which it's stored."],["Controlling your body as you fly through the air has become second nature. You can Leap greater distances horizontally by spending additional actions. If you do, increase the limit on how far you can Leap by 5 feet for each additional action spent. Additionally, you can [[/act long-jump]] in a different direction than the direction you were Striding.\n\n---\n\n**Special** When you Fly using a Jetpack or Jump Jets while your feet are on the ground, you can spring upward to increase your fly Speed by 10 feet for the duration of the move action."],["Few places are as hazardous to run through as the scrublands of Marata, and few people spend as much of their time running as young maraquois. You've gained an otherworldly expertise in placing your feet just right to rush over even the roughest ground. When you Stride, ignore the first 10 feet of non-magical difficult terrain, or treat 10 feet of non-magical greater difficult terrain as difficult terrain."],["You've trained your tail to move with incredible precision, practicing a specific set of underhanded skills until they become second nature. When you attempt to [[/act disable-device options=thiefs-tale]] or [[/act pick-a-lock options=thiefs-tale]], if you're holding no items other than tools to help you Disable a Device or Pick a Lock, you can spend an additional action to use your tail to help with the attempt. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your check to Disable a Device or Pick a Lock. On a success or critical success, you achieve an additional success if the device or lock requires more than one success."],["A well-trained maraquoi hunter can launch themself at their prey from any perch, in any direction. You [[/act high-jump]], [[/act long-jump]], or [[/act maneuver-in-flight]] to Fly your fly Speed. If you move at least 10 feet and end in a square adjacent to a target, make a melee Strike or attempt to [[/act shove]] the target. If you rolled a critical success on your Athletics check to High Jump or a success on your Acrobatics check to Maneuver in Flight, your target is Off-Guard to this attack."],["You extend your powerful membranes and flap your powerful arms in carefully controlled patterns, creating enough lift to carry you through the air. You gain a fly Speed of 20 feet."],["You've trained yourself to exploit the extra reach of your prehensile tail and can use that particular detail to your advantage. You can Interact to pick up, pass, or take items with your tail up to 5 feet further than your usual reach with your hands. You can Release items held by your tail into an adjacent square. Tailblades you wield gain the reach trait."],["Marata's fiercest predators are also some of its most cunning hunters, leaving little sign when attempting to remain unseen. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to [[/act hide]] and [[/act sneak]] in natural terrain and a +1 circumstance bonus to Survival checks to Cover Tracks and [[/act track]] in natural terrain. You're always considered to be Covering Tracks, even if you chose a different activity in exploration mode."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nSometimes, you need to ignore your own limits and run just a little bit faster. When circumstances are dire, you can draw on an inner strength and push your body to go even faster than usual. You gain the Quickened condition for 3 rounds. You can use the extra action only to [[/act long-jump]] or Stride."],["Your life has a strict time limit, and it makes every moment more valuable. It's incumbent upon you to go to great lengths to ensure that none of your time is wasted. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks for initiative."],["It might have taken you a bit longer to find your niche than most of your ilk. After a couple extra internships and some trial and error, you're a bit of a mecenaic-of-all-trades. You gain the trained proficiency rank in two skills of your choice."],["On Xofirth, you're one of the smallest sentient life-forms, and you've had to develop techniques to avoid much larger predators in a variety of situations. You become trained in Athletics or Survival. If you're already trained in both of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. Choose one kind of terrain from the following list: muddy, rocky, sandy, sloped, undergrowth. You ignore difficult terrain or uneven ground of that type."],["When you need extra mobility, you can leave your cumbersome, protective shell behind. When you don't have your shell, your Speeds increases by 5 feet; you gain a +2 status bonus to Acrobatics, Stealth, and Thievery checks; and you gain weakness to physical damage equal to half your level (rounded up). You can't use any actions that require a shell until you return to your shell by using Shed Shell again. Regrowing a new shell takes 1 week of downtime, but a variety of prosthetic shells are available, as Prosthetic Limb."],["There's no difference between front and back for a mecenaic. You can look, move, and point your arms in either direction interchangeably. You aren't Off-Guard when flanked and gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Perception checks for initiative."],["**Trigger** An enemy critically hits you with a Strike.\n\n---\n\nThe importance of preserving your body, and your time, has been drilled into your head your entire life. Now that you have more experience in the field, you're able to combine that mentality with quick reflexes to protect yourself against the most dangerous threats. You Make a Tiny Target."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** You're damaged by an enemy's attack.\n\n---\n\nPreserving your time is the most important thing you can do. You summon a primal form of desperation to protect yourself. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to half your level rounded up that last for 1 round. You can immediately Stride up to your Speed but must end your movement further away from the triggering enemy."],["You've scheduled your life down to the minute, prioritizing your strict deadlines to the point of manifesting mysterious powers that maximize your entire team's the productivity. You gain Haste as an 8th-rank occult innate spell that you can cast once per day. When you cast this innate *haste* spell the first time each day, you can choose to cast it as a 3rd-rank occult innate spell instead of 8th-rank. If you do, you can cast it two more times that day as a 3rd-rank occult innate spell."],["You might be Tiny, but your pliable anatomy allows you to stretch and contort to simulate the reach of a larger creature. When you wield a melee weapon that requires two hands and doesn't have reach, you can change between a typical two-handed grip and an extended two-handed stretch using an Interact action. Weapons wielded in your extended stretch gain a reach of 5 feet."],["Predators have treasured your people for centuries, and you've learned how to use your unique anatomy to slip out of their grasp. Your pliable body, lack of bones, and protective shell make you extremely hard to hold on to. You can attempt a Stealth check to Escape in addition to the existing options (but this action still has the attack trait). You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your first attempt to Escape each round.\n\n[[/act escape skill=stealth]]"],["You pull your limbs and other vulnerable body parts in tight, hiding mostly inside your protective shell. You gain resistance to physical damage equal to half your level (rounded up) until the end of your next turn. However, with your limbs in your shell, it becomes difficult to move. You gain the Immobilized condition until the end of your next turn."],["Other psychic ancestries find the aberrant nature of your prowess to be unusual, and it can be difficult for them to adapt to contact with your mind. You gain mental resistance equal to half your level (minimum 1)."],["The giant, ravenous, and persistent predators of Xofirth can follow even the weakest trail. By adapting your travel regimen, you've learned to hide any trace of your passing from beasts and intelligent beings alike. When you [[/act avoid-notice]], you also gain the benefits of Cover Tracks unless you choose to forgo them."],["You don't have time to let your emotions control your actions. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against emotion effects. Additionally, if you roll a success on a saving throw against an emotion effect, you get a critical success instead."],["The shell that protects most of your body has always been a part of you, and it has taught you valuable lessons in improving your defense and mobility when wearing armor. You gain the armor specialization effect of light armor. If you're trained in medium or heavy armor, you gain the respective armor specialization effects of those armors as well and reduce the Speed penalty of medium and heavy armor by 5 feet."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** An enemy's Strike against you is a critical hit.\n\n---\n\nYou position your fortified crystalline hair to absorb some of the blow from an otherwise lethal attack. The triggering attack deals only the amount it would deal on a hit (typically full damage instead of double damage). Any other effects caused by a critical hit still occur. It takes a day for your shattered hair to regrow, and until it does, you take a –2 circumstance penalty to Diplomacy checks with other moyishuus."],["You've learned to open your mind to the wavelengths of those around you, beyond merely sensing their emotions. You gain Limited Telepathy. You can communicate mentally with creatures within 30 feet that share a language with you, and they can mentally respond. This doesn't give you any access to their thoughts and communicates no more information than normal speech would."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** An enemy critically fails a melee Strike against you.\n\n---\n\nThe uncanny movements you make to avoid the incoming Strike confuse and distract your assailant. The triggering creature is Off-Guard to the next Strike made against it by any ally before the start of your next turn.\n\n---\n\n**Special** The frequency of Uncanny Wonder is once per minute as long as your soulfeel is attuned to wonder."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** An enemy causes you to become frightened or take persistent mental damage.\n\n---\n\nThe depth of your sorrow causes the negativity coming from others to cascade back at them. The triggering creature becomes Frightened 1, and that enemy can't reduce their frightened condition below 1 until the beginning of your next turn.\n\n---\n\n**Special** The frequency of Unfathomable Sorrow is once per minute as long as your soulfeel is attuned to sorrow."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** You critically succeed at a Strike.\n\n---\n\nViolence further fuels your fury and resilience. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to your Charisma modifier until the end of your next turn.\n\n---\n\n**Special** The frequency of Unforgiving Fury is once per minute as long as your soulfeel is attuned to fury."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** You're Frightened or taking persistent mental damage.\n\n---\n\nYour outlook on life is full of boundless hope. Reduce your frightened condition by 1. If you're taking persistent mental damage, roll a DC 15 flat check to see if you recover from that persistent mental damage.\n\n---\n\n**Special** The frequency of Unrelenting Joy is once per minute as long as your soulfeel is attuned to joy."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou pause and take a quick breath to stabilize your emotions. Choose any emotional state for your soulfeel.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can Center Your Emotions as a free action if you're a Court of Dance Moyishuu who chooses joy, a Court of Fields Moyishuu who chooses wonder, a Court of Flames Moyishuu who chooses fury, or a Court of Song Moyishuu who chooses sorrow."],["You sense others' baseline emotional states from afar. When you Feint using Absolute Empathy, you can do so at a range of up to 60 feet, instead of just melee reach. If you succeed, the opponent is Off-Guard against your melee and ranged attacks."],["Your understanding of your own emotions and soul deepens profoundly. You gain additional benefits depending on your current soulfeel attunement.\n\n**Fury:** You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Athletics checks.\n\n**Joy:** You gain a fly Speed of 20 feet.\n\n**Sorrow:** You gain a burrow Speed of 10 feet.\n\n**Wonder:** You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Perception checks.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have Mascot Power!, the summoned minion gains the same benefits of Soulfire as you."],["By allowing yourself to drown in ambient emotions, you can cause them to spill over and erupt around you in a cathartic flow of primal energy. You can cast Vibe Check as a 4th-rank primal innate spell four times per day. You must select a different emotion each time you Cast the Spell in a day, and the emotion must match your current soulfeel (or wonder, if you select fear)."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYour performances, vocal or otherwise, can tap into the same riotous primal energy as that of the First World, warping reality to the whimsy of your soul's emotional spectrum. Roll 1d20 and consult the table below for your result. If the result's emotion doesn't match your current soulfeel, attune your soulfeel to that emotion. If the effect requires a saving throw, use the higher of your class DC or spell DC.\n\n| d20 | Emotion | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1–3 | Fury | All enemies within 30 feet must attempt a Will save. If they fail, they become Confused for 3 rounds (or 1 minute on a critical failure), and their latent anger causes them to deal an additional 3d4 persistent bleed damage with all Strikes against allies. |\n| 4–6 | Joy | You and all allies within 30 feet reduce your Frightened conditions by 1, end any persistent mental damage, and gain 25 temporary Hit Points that last until the end of your next turn. |\n| 7–9 | Sorrow | All enemies within 30 feet become Suppressed until the end of your next turn and must attempt a Will save. If they fail, they become Slowed 1 for 3 rounds (or 1 minute on a critical failure). |\n| 10–12 | Wonder | All enemies within 30 feet become Dazzled until the end of your next turn and must attempt a Will save. On a failure, they become Stupefied 2 for 3 rounds (or 1 minute on a critical failure). |\n| 13+ | Current soulfeel | Select the effect that corresponds to your current soulfeel attunement. |"],["You find the feelings of your foe to better understand them. You attempt to Feint against a creature. Unlike a normal Feint, use Diplomacy ([[/act feint skill=diplomacy dc=will]]) instead of Deception. You attempt your check against the creature's Will DC instead of its Perception DC."],["Your connection to the First World is strong. Whenever you meet a fey creature in a social situation, you can immediately attempt a Diplomacy check to [[/act make-an-impression]] on that creature rather than needing to converse for 1 minute. You take a –4 circumstance penalty to the check. If you fail, you can engage in 1 minute of conversation and attempt a new check at the end of that time rather than accepting the failure or critical failure result. In addition, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to both Perception checks and saving throws against fey."],["Your crystals grant you a resonant defense against certain effects, though they often disrupt your soulfeel. You gain resistance 5 to sonic damage. In addition, if you critically fail a save against a damaging sonic effect, you can change your soulfeel to a different emotion as a free action."],["You're as fickle as the inhabitants of the First World. When you use an action with both the emotion and moyishuu traits, you must immediately attune your soulfeel to a different emotion. If the action had a duration, it becomes until the end of your turn. You can attempt to keep the same emotional attunement by succeeding at a DC 15 flat check, but if you fail, the frequency of the action becomes once per hour."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nBy touching a friend and concentrating, you can draw in harmful effects negatively impacting their emotions. Attempt a Counteract check using your Perception modifier and a counteract rank equal to half your level (rounded up). If you succeed, the target gains temporary Hit Points equal to your level for a number of rounds equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1 round).\n\nAbsorb Vibe\n\n---\n\n*SFS Note:* For the purposes of this feat, \"harmful effects that negatively affect their emotions\" are \"one emotion effect affecting the target or one of the following conditions: Frightened, Fleeing.\""],["You've attuned your senses beyond their natural limits. Your Emotionsense becomes a precise sense, and its range increases by 10 feet (this is cumulative with the Enhanced Senses standardized ancestry feat). The range of your Limited Telepathy increases to the range of your emotionsense."],["Your soulfeel has attracted and bound the spirit of a creature to you. When you select this feat, choose Summon Animal or Summon Fey. You can cast the chosen spell as a primal innate spell once per day, heightened to half your level rounded up."],["**Trigger** You would take fire damage.\n\n---\n\nYou incorporate fire that washes over you into your own flame, burning brighter and hotter for a short time. Until the beginning of your next turn, the area of your solar luminance is doubled, and your next Strike deals additional fire damage equal to half your level (rounded up)."],["You have an innate knowledge of suns, stars, and stellar forces. You become trained in Nature. If you would automatically become trained in Nature (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Additional Lore feat for Physical Science Lore and one other space-related lore of your choice, such as Astrophysics Lore, Astronomy Lore, Star Lore, or Sun Lore."],["You can seize and move objects from afar using your gravitational field, although your control is clumsy, and you can't perform actions with these objects. You grasp one unattended object of light Bulk or less within 30 feet and move it slowly 15 feet in any direction, up to a maximum distance of 30 feet away from you. You can Sustain Gravity Grasp for up to 1 minute, moving the object an additional 15 feet each time. If the object is in the air when this effect ends, it falls.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you're a Black Hole Novian, Dense Novian, or Massive Novian, you can grasp one unattended object of 1 Bulk or less, rather than light Bulk or less."],["You've learned to exert your gravitational field not only over objects but other creatures. You become trained in Athletics. If you would automatically become trained in Athletics (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Titan Wrestler skill feat, and you gain a +1 circumstance bonus on Athletics checks to [[/act disarm]], [[/act grapple]], [[/act reposition]], [[/act shove]], and [[/act trip]]."],["Forged in a sun's flames, your body is a living furnace that releases an abundance of thermal energy. You become inured to high temperatures, and your body sheds a pleasant heat that can stave off the cold. You gain resistance 4 to fire. You and creatures within 20 feet of you treat environmental cold effects as if they were one step less extreme (incredible cold becomes extreme, extreme cold becomes severe, and so on)."],["You can focus your light, shining it onto a specific location or target like a mobile spotlight to ensure no detail passes unseen. You shine a focused, bright light in a 5-foot burst within 40 feet (within 120 feet if you're a Bright Novian). You [[/act point-out]] one creature in your spotlight. Creatures gain a +1 circumstance bonus on Perception checks to [[/act seek]] within the area of this focused light.\n\nSpotlight lasts a number of rounds equal to half your level (minimum 1 round). While Spotlight is active, and for an hour after Spotlight ends, the area of your Solar Luminance is halved."],["You vent copious amounts of thermal energy as you fly, burning anyone in your path. Whenever you use Shooting Star, you can choose to vent thermal energy. If you do, you deal (ceil(level/2)-4)d6 fire damage to all creatures in the spaces you move through, with a basic Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. On a critical failure, a creature additionally catches fire, taking 1)d4 persistent fire damage.\n\nAt 15th level and every 2 levels thereafter, the fire damage increases by 1d6, and at 17th level, the persistent fire damage increases by 1d4."],["You have the soul of a true sun and are impervious to even the hottest flames. You become immune to fire."],["**Trigger** You take damage from an enemy or hazard.\n\n**Requirements** Satellites are currently orbiting you due to Pull Into Orbit.\n\n---\n\nYou exert precise control over the debris that's orbiting you, purposefully placing it between you and harm to shield your body. You gain resistance equal to half your level against the triggering damage. Pull into Orbit immediately ends."],["You have excellent light control and can strobe so fast that it makes would-be attackers sick. If a creature fails its flat check to hit you due to Concealment caused by Strobe Light, it becomes Sickened 1."],["You know that energy is eternal—changing, shifting, and reforming, but never truly extinguished. Just as you were born from the death of a star, so too are you born again upon your own death. If you would die, your body explodes in a miniature burst of energy, and you're reborn as a microscopic, slumbering novian, which grows to your full size (usually Tiny) over the course of 24 hours. At the end of this time, you awaken fully healed in the space you died."],["You exude a much stronger gravitational field than most novians, enabling you to exert your personal gravity upon your surroundings from a farther distance. Your reach increases to 10 feet. In addition, you double the range of all the following novian feats you possess: Gravity Grasp and Gravity Swipe."],["Your ability to compress and store objects within your own body is unparalleled. The amount of material you can store in the extradimensional space within your body increases to 50 Bulk."],["You're the inheritor of your progenitor star's stellar glory. Your mere presence terrifies your enemies and emboldens your allies. You gain a +1 status bonus to Diplomacy and Intimidation checks. This bonus increases to +4 against novians. In addition, you gain the Unleash Majesty action."],["You don the darkness like a mantle—a crown inherited from the black hole that bore you—and can disappear in its depths. Whenever you Absorb Light, you become Concealed until the beginning of your next turn. You can't use this concealment to [[/act hide]] or [[/act sneak]]."],["Your gravitational field has strengthened, and your ability to manipulate objects within it has improved. Your gravitational field grants you two additional hands, following the rules for characters with more than two hands. The Switch Hands action gains the novian trait when you switch to or from any of your gravity hands.\n\n---\n\n**Special** A novian with Extra Hands can select the All Hands on Deck and Double Draw standardized ancestry feats."],["When you use Gravity Grasp, the range at which you can move objects increases to 60 feet. In addition, whenever you use Gravity Grasp, you can choose to pull the target object directly into one of your free hands from up to the maximum range of Gravity Grasp. You also gain the Seize Object action."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou can launch a ball of plasma and stellar ejecta across the battlefield that explodes on impact, raining plasma and flame in a small area. Launch Plasma deals ceil(level/2)d6 fire damage in a 5-foot burst within 60 feet. Each creature in the area must attempt a basic Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. On a critical failure, a creature also takes (ceil(level/2)) persistent electricity damage.\n\nAt 7th level and every 2 levels thereafter, the fire damage increases by 1d6, and the persistent electricity damage increases by 1. At 17th level, the area increases to a 10-foot burst.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you're a Volatile Novian, Launch Plasma and Mini-Nova's damage dice are both increased to d8s."],["**Frequency** twice per day\n\n---\n\nYou suffuse your natural glow with healing light. You regain Hit Points equal to your level (level healing). All allies within the light of your Solar Luminance gain temporary Hit Points equal to half your level for 1 minute.\n\nLife-Giving Light"],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou exert your gravitational field upon your surroundings, causing small objects, debris, and stellar ejecta from your own body to orbit you like miniature satellites. These satellites grant you lesser cover until the beginning of your next turn.\n\nAt 9th level and every 4 levels thereafter, your satellites remain in orbit for 1 additional round, up to a maximum of 4 rounds at 17th level."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou launch yourself across the battlefield, emulating the brightest shooting stars. You Stride up to twice your Speed in a straight line. You're Concealed during this movement."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** A creature hits you with an attack.\n\n**Requirements** You're aware of the attack and not Off-Guard against it.\n\n---\n\nYou strobe and pulse your brilliant light erratically, throwing off your attacker's aim at the last second with a display worthy of the hottest nightclubs and starriest skies. You become Concealed against the triggering attack."],["You have impeccable control over your natural flames and wield them to excellent effect during battle. You gain the critical specialization effects for your burning tendril and solar flare unarmed attacks (whichever you possess). In addition, you gain one of the following benefits of your choice.\n\n- **Broad Flame:** Your burning tendril gains the sweep trait.\n- **Empowered Flame:** Your burning tendril gains the boost 1d8 trait.\n- **Explosive Flare:** Your solar flare releases a small burst of flame on a hit, dealing 1 fire damage per weapon damage die to all creatures adjacent to the target.\n- **Long-Range Flare:** Your solar flare's range increment increases by 15 feet.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat twice, selecting from the benefits you haven't yet chosen."],["Your body is a literal black hole, capable of absorbing and compressing material within yourself. The amount of material you can store in the extradimensional space within your body increases to 2 Bulk."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou are the prime inheritor of your progenitor star's power and can don this star's lost legacy as a crown, growing in size and power, resplendent in glory. You become Small (or Medium, if you're a Massive Novian). Your equipment grows with you but returns to normal size if removed. You gain a +2 status bonus to melee damage and Intimidation checks, and the area of your Solar Luminance (and Absorb Light, if you're a Black Hole Novian) is doubled. This transformation lasts for 1 minute. You can end this glorious transformation early as a single action, which has the concentrate trait."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nLike the star or supernova you wish to emulate, you've learned to focus and release bursts of radiation. All non-novian creatures in a 10-foot emanation must attempt a Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is Sickened 1 for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The creature is Sickened 2 for 2 rounds.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is sickened 2 for 1 minute."],["Your penchant for understanding other beings and gathering information allows you to quickly assess anyone before you. You can cast the Analyze Target cantrip as an occult innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up. Once per day, as part of Casting the Spell, you can attempt a Recall Knowledge check as a free action on the target, or a single creature among the targets if you cast it on multiple creatures."],["Your true feelings and thoughts are tucked away in the twisting corridors of your mind, such that you and, more importantly, others have difficulty accessing them. When you roll a success on a saving throw against an emotion effect or a Mind Reading spell, you get a critical success instead."],["You constantly wander the maze of life, moving from one interest to the next; as a result, it's easy to forget past passions while delving into others. You gain the Additional Lore feat, as well as the benefits of Unmistakable Lore for that Lore subcategory, even if you don't meet the prerequisites. You can retrain Maze Lost to a different Lore skill subcategory with 1 day of downtime."],["Your stature cuts a threatening figure, such that even a forceful breath can feel like a threat to smaller beings. You become trained in Intimidation. If you're already trained in Intimidation (from your background or class, for example), you become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Intimidating Glare skill feat. You also gain a +1 circumstance bonus to [[/act demoralize]] targets that are smaller than you."],["Nuars are no strangers to wandering the stars and exploring alien worlds, meeting other nuars along the way. You possess an innate sense of location that never leaves you truly lost. You become trained in Piloting and Survival. If you're already trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Nuar Lore."],["Your focus is so powerful that it's easy for you to lose track of self care, but fortunately, you've trained to endure periods of stress. You're never Fatigued as a result of hunger or starvation as long as you spend time during your daily preparations solving or creating a puzzle or riddle. You only need to sleep for 2 hours a day, and you need only 4 hours of rest between your daily preparations. Choose a Lore skill related to the puzzle or riddle you worked on. Until your next daily preparations, you become trained in that skill, and if you roll a critical failure on a check to Recall Knowledge with that Lore skill, you get a failure instead."],["Your ability to focus on your interests encourages rapid talent growth, allowing you to leap ahead in your studies. You gain the Assurance feat for up to two Lore skills you're trained in. You can retrain Preternatural Skill to gain Assurance for one different Lore skill with 1 day of downtime."],["Who says topics can't be randomly connected? Whenever you attempt a check to Recall Knowledge, you can roll the Lore skill you gained from Maze Lost with a –3 circumstance penalty instead of rolling with a normally applicable skill."],["Pain is in the mind as well as in the body, which your horns make abundantly clear on contact. Your unarmed horns attack deals an additional 1d6 mental damage. On a critical hit, the target also becomes Stupefied 2 until the beginning of your next turn."],["Your unnatural relationship with gravitational forces allows you to manipulate its flow to your will. You can cast Gravity Field as an 8th-rank occult innate spell once per day."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou extend your innate ability to alter your personal gravity to harm another creature within 120 feet, the intense pressure buckling their bones. You deal 10d8 bludgeoning damage to the creature with a basic Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. On a failure, the creature also becomes Suppressed and Slowed 1 until the beginning of your next turn."],["The depth of your knowledge is matched only by your ability to recall it at a moment's notice. You gain the Automatic Knowledge general feat and can apply it to any skill you're expert in as long as you have Assurance in that skill. You can also cast Hypercognition as a 3rd-rank occult innate spell once per day."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou attempt a check to Recall Knowledge about a single creature you can sense. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Recall Knowledge check if you use the same skill you're using to roll initiative. This bonus increases to +2 if you're a master in that skill."],["Your wide build allows you to carry crushing weights. Increase your maximum and encumbered Bulk limits by 4. You ignore the penalty to attack rolls using weapons with the kickback trait as if you had +2 Strength, regardless of your actual modifier."],["You've begun to develop your personal legend about nuar history, tailored from your own study and interests. While not necessarily factual, the legend is captivating when you tell it. You can use any Lore skill in which you're trained to [[/act make-an-impression]] or [[/act create-a-diversion]], instead of using Diplomacy and Deception respectively. You take a –2 circumstance penalty to your Diplomacy checks using Lore if the target isn't interested in or trained in the same or a related Lore skill (creatures are trained in the skills listed in their stat blocks)."],["You can leverage your size to extend your reach. When you wield a melee weapon that requires two hands and doesn't have reach, you can change between a typical two-handed grip and an extended two-handed stretch using an Interact action. Weapons wielded in your extended stretch gain a reach of 10 feet."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** An adjacent enemy deals damage to you with an unarmed melee Strike.\n\n---\n\nWith an angry bellow, you lean into your horns to gore the offending opponent. Make a horns Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a success, the creature takes an additional 2d6 bleed damage."],["Focusing latent power from your distant minotaur cousins, you expand quickly in size. You can cast Enlarge on yourself as a 2nd-rank occult innate spell once per day. At 13th level, this spell is heightened to 4th rank."],["Gravitational forces are always accessible to you, even in a vacuum. You can cast Personal Gravity as a 3rd-rank occult innate spell once per day. The first time each day that you cast this spell while in a vacuum, that casting doesn't count toward this limit."],["You use the momentum of your body to charge at your opponent with your horns. Stride twice or Push Off once, then make a horns Strike. If you moved at least 20 feet from your starting position, your horns Strike also deals 1d6 persistent bleed damage."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nWith a short moment of introspection, you can reposition yourself within the maze of life to find a new vocation. You can spend 10 minutes to Retrain the Lore skill you chose with Maze Lost to a different subcategory."],["An object in motion stays in motion, and a person of your mass is rarely acted upon by an outside force. You Stride twice or Push Off once, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to your AC against any reactions triggered by your movement. A creature that attempts such a reaction and fails its attack roll becomes Off-Guard until the beginning of your next turn."],["You've been trained in a traditional orc combat style called the Broken Hand Technique. The style originates from a tale that claims the orc who invented it was said to have driven off an invasion with two broken hands. This fighting style emphasizes close-quarters combat, grappling, trips, and pins, and uses the knees, elbows, feet, and shoulders to maneuver the enemy into a more advantageous position regardless of their size.\n\nYou become trained in Athletics. If you would automatically become trained in Athletics (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Titan Wrestler skill feat."],["You adjust quickly to changing circumstances in battle, whether from intense training or some intrinsic knowledge. As a result, you're able to shake off effects that are intended to distract or cloud the mind.\n\nYou gain a +1 status bonus to saving throws against emotion effects and a +1 to your Perception DC against attempts to Create a Diversion and Feint."],["Your hold has worked as laborers for generations, and as a result you've become an expert not only at the work that you do, but commanding respect and fair treatment from your employers.\n\nYou become trained in a Lore skill of your choosing. In addition, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks to Gather Information when consulting other professionals related to the chosen Lore skill."],["You're experienced in moving through spaces that are too small for you. This might be from the caverns of Apostae or a similar world.\n\nYou become trained in Acrobatics. If you would automatically become trained in Acrobatics (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Quick Squeeze feat."],["You have spent time working in zero gravity and are able to keep your stomach even when floating freely. The interior of asteroids or ships that have lost power are easily navigable for you.\n\nYou can use your legs to Push Off while in zero-g without needing a free hand. You can ignore the Clumsy and Off-Guard penalties while Untethered in zero gravity."],["Your attacks have become so powerful that they can shatter armor and shields. When you Strike a creature that has hardness (such as a construct with construct armor) or an enemy using an action such as Shield Block, you deal additional damage to that creature or shield equal to your level or the target's hardness (whichever is lower)."],["You've managed to hone your prior experience in the tunnels of Apostae and can employ them when faced with almost any hazard or environmental threat. You can use your Apostae delver heritage to reroll on traps every hour instead of every day. In addition, you can use this reroll against any effect caused by a hazard, instead of just traps."],["**Requirements** You're adjacent to a creature that isn't immune to bleed damage and died within the last minute.\n\n---\n\nYou dip your fingers into the gushing wounds of the fallen, using their ichor to mask your face in a visceral ritual that pays homage to the fallen while calming yourself for in the din of battle. For 1 minute, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Intimidation checks to [[/act demoralize]], a +1 status bonus to Will saves against emotion effects, and at the end of your turn, reduce your Frightened condition by 2 instead of 1."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You reduce a creature to 0 Hit Points.\n\n---\n\nYou effortlessly enter a state of flow in combat. When you use Battle Focus and each time you reduce a hostile creature to 0 Hit Points in the next minute, you regain level healing Hit Points equal to your level. If you're Wounded, you can reduce the wounded condition by 1 instead of regaining Hit Points."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** A creature you can sense critically succeeds on a Strike against you.\n\n---\n\nYou can't stand being shown up in battle, and those who best you face your swift retribution. You Strike the triggering creature."],["You've layered alloys over your fists and tusks to improve their efficiency in dispatching certain foes. This enhancement might be voluntary or part of some unwanted evolution or experimentation. Choose cold iron or silver. Your melee unarmed attacks have the special properties of a weapon made of that metal. If you're at least 13th level, you can choose adamantine instead of just cold iron or silver."],["You verbally boast before you Strike, further pressing your advantage by rubbing some salt into their wounds. Make a Strike. If you critically hit your target, attempt an Intimidation check with a +2 circumstance bonus to [[/act demoralize]] your target."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail a saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYour mental and physical fortitude allow you to resist disastrous harm. You reroll the triggering check, but you must use the new result, even if it's worse than your first roll. Unless you roll a critical success, you become Suppressed until the end of your next turn as you shake off the ill effects."],["You focus your energy and concentrate on your target to find cracks and flaws you can exploit before you Strike. Make a Strike. This Strike gains the razing trait, dealing additional damage to objects equal to double the number of weapon damage dice. On a critical hit, a targeted tech item becomes Glitching 1."],["You take great pride in the mastery of your craft. Gain a skill feat in for a skill that you're at least a master in. You also gain Assurance in that skill."],["You have experience surviving in some of the most extreme situations in the galaxy. You gain the Forager skill feat. In addition, you can perform other downtime activities while you Subsist as long as they're feasible in your environment, such as finding raw materials to Craft or Earning Income using Survival by live streaming your foraging."],["**Trigger** You're struck by a critical hit that deals damage.\n\n**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nThough Torag fails to answer the prayers of his followers, you know that in your most trying moments, his gaze sometimes falls upon you. Attempt a DC 15 flat check. If you're successful, the attack becomes a normal hit."],["You're well-versed in the artistic history of your people and found a way to make it your own. You might not even be a musician, but an actor, comedian, or other kind of performer—the fact remains that the show is in your blood, and you're good at what you do. You gain the Virtuosic Performer feat with the specialty of your choice. Your background in entertainment has left you shrewd, and you know exactly how to get a reaction out of a crowd. When you roll Performance to Earn Income, treat your task's level as 1 higher for the purposes of determining income earned, but don't increase the DC."],["You are adept at reading nonvisual social cues and quickly use this to your advantage when a conversation is going awry. You gain the Just Kidding! skill feat even if you don't meet the prerequisites and can use Deception instead of Performance when you're Just Kidding!"],["**Trigger** An enemy you can observe damages your ally.\n\n---\n\nIf one of your own is harmed, it awakens the monstrous side of you. When one or more of your allies takes damage from an enemy, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Deception checks to [[/act feint]] and Intimidation checks to [[/act demoralize]] the triggering enemy until the end of your next turn."],["You've learned to stretch your legs and adjust your posture, allowing your strides to cover more ground. Your Speed increases by 5 feet."],["More lurks in the tunnels than most understand. You've taken the time to study the strange and otherworldly things that lurk in the shadows. You become trained in Occultism. If you would automatically become trained in Occultism (from your background or class, for example), you can instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Decipher Writing or Identify Magic with Occultism."],["It might seem a bit cowardly, but sometimes having a living shield is practical and advantageous for both parties. You can use your smaller allies for cover while gaining an offensive advantage as well. When you [[/act take-cover]] behind an ally between you and a target you can reach, you gain the benefits of standard cover, even if your ally is smaller than you. If your ally is also threatening the target, you're both considered to be flanking the target."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** A creature within 30 feet attempts a ranged Strike against you.\n\n---\n\nYou exclaim suddenly, creating a powerful jolt to the triggering creature's nerves and potentially disrupting its attack. The creature must attempt a Will save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. Regardless of the result, it becomes immune to Shocking Howl for 1 hour.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The triggering attack roll takes a –1 status penalty.\n\n**Failure** The triggering attack roll takes a –2 status penalty.\n\n**Critical Failure** The shot is completely disrupted and automatically misses."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou've embraced your aberrant nature to a terrifying degree. You rise up to your full height, drawing the howling winds through your ear canals and your mouth, and create a terrifying cacophony with a matching display. You attempt to [[/act demoralize]] all creatures within 20 feet; you don't take a penalty when you attempt to Demoralize a creature that doesn't understand your language. You can use Performance in place of Intimidation when you use Howl of the Deep.\n\n[[/act demoralize skill=performance]]"],["The strange music that lurks inside you is always straining to get out. You can harness it more readily than most, much to the dismay of any enemies standing in your way. The frequency of Hypnotic Melody and Shocking Howl becomes once per round. Creatures that fail their Will saves against your Hypnotic Melody or Shocking Howl become Enfeebled 1 (Enfeebled 2 on a critical failure)."],["Though many of the tunnels on your home world appear to be too small for a towering person like you, you've worked out strategies to bend, twist, and balance your way through the tightest spots. You gain the Quick Squeeze skill feat. When you critically fail an Acrobatics check to Squeeze, you get a failure instead."],["Many find your size, and the aberrant nature of your appearance, intimidating. You've learned to use that to your advantage, frightening smaller foes without ever opening your mouth. You gain the Intimidating Glare skill feat. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to [[/act demoralize]] a target that's smaller than you."],["Without eyes to pierce the darkness, you've developed new, more creative ways to track your foes. You have a finely honed ability to feel other creatures moving through vibrations in the ground. You gain tremorsense as an imprecise sense with a range of 30 feet."],["Your mind's functions are alien to most creatures, giving you natural psychic defenses. Any effect that specifically attempts to read your mind to glean information must succeed at a counteract check against the higher of your class DC or your spell DC to do so; otherwise, it gains no information. The counteract rank is equal to half your level rounded up."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou command the attention of those who can hear you with a truly haunting song. Attempt a Performance check and compare it to the Will DC of each creature in a 15-foot emanation. Regardless of the result, each creature then becomes immune to your Hypnotic Melody for 24 hours.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is Fatigued and Fascinated with you for 1 round as your song seems to lull them to sleep.\n\n**Success** The target is fatigued for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The target is unaffected."],["The water is a second home to you. You've grown used to weightlessness, to being carried by the flow or your own inertia, and it's not so different from moving in zero gravity. When you Push Off, you can move your full Speed. You aren't clumsy due to being Untethered in zero gravity."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You take acid, cold, electricity, fire, poison, sonic, or void damage.\n\n---\n\nYou've recently developed a new mutation: flesh that rapidly adapts to hazardous environments—for a time. You gain resistance 5 against the triggering damage type for 1 hour."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** You're wielding a weapon that deals physical damage.\n\n---\n\nYou coat your weapon or its ammunition in your toxic stomach fluids, which remain potent until the end of your next turn. The next time you successfully Strike a creature with the required weapon within the duration, if the Strike deals damage, you deal an additional 1d4 poison damage to the target. At 3rd level and every 2 levels thereafter, this damage increases by 1d4."],["You believe a healthy mind and body is integral to a life well lived, dedicating yourself to helping others recover swiftly from illness and disease. You become trained in Medicine. If you would automatically become trained in Medicine (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. In addition, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus on Medicine checks to [[/act administer-first-aid]], [[/act treat-disease]], and [[/act treat-poison]], and if you get a critical failure on one of these checks, you get a failure instead."],["You're an insatiable student, determined to learn and experience everything you can, as quick as you can—even if the knowledge gained quickly gets buried under new information. During your daily preparations, you gain the Additional Lore feat with one Lore skill of your choice. This proficiency lasts until you prepare again. Since this proficiency is temporary, you can't use it as a prerequisite for a permanent character option, like a feat."],["You miss your home world of Aucturn, and even if you don't want to go back to your time there, the thought of its strange vistas fills your heart with fond memories. If you would critically fail a saving throw against an emotion effect, you get a failure instead. In addition, you gain the Thoughts of a Lost Home action."],["You acknowledge that you are connected to the Newborn, now and forever, and have embraced the nascent godling as family. You become trained in Religion. If you would automatically become trained in this skill (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Additional Lore general feat for Newborn Lore.\n\nIn addition, the first time each day that you gain the dying condition, the Newborn—or perhaps some other unknown force—automatically stabilizes you. You lose the dying condition, though you remain Unconscious at 0 Hit Points."],["You can run incredibly fast on all fours. Your Speed is 30 feet as long as you have two free hands."],["You use your camouflaged skin to your advantage, moving unseen with ease. When you use Shifthide Camouflage and are in your selected terrain, you can [[/act hide]] or [[/act sneak]] without cover or being Concealed."],["You have an unending supply of toxins and bile. Select one of the following abilities you possess: Coat in Bile, Slitherskin, or Spew Acidic Bile. If you selected Coat in Bile or Spew Acidic Bile, the frequency of the selected ability becomes once per 10 minutes, rather than once per day. If you selected Slitherskin, the frequency of Slitherskin becomes once per 10 minutes, rather than once per hour.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat more than once, selecting a different ability you possess each time."],["The psychic static that shrouds your mind is a weapon as much as a defense. Whenever you use Static Shield and succeed at the triggering save, if the source of the mental effect was a creature, your psychic static lashes out at them and deals mental damage equal to half your level (or equal to your level on a critical success, (floor(level/2)) mental, level mental)."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** An ally within your sight is damaged by an enemy.\n\n---\n\nAgainst all odds, you've made friends you value dearly. When they're in trouble, you rush to their aid, regardless of the danger it could put you in. Stride up to three times, ending your movement in a space adjacent to the triggering ally. You're Off-Guard until the beginning of your next turn."],["You resist mental control with supernatural skill. You become immune to the Confused and Controlled conditions. Whenever you gain the Stupefied condition, you immediately reduce the value of the condition by 1. This feat doesn't apply if you impose the condition on yourself."],["You've trained to telepathically communicate with anyone. The range of your limited telepathy increases to 100 feet. You can communicate with creatures that don't share your language with limited telepathy, and you permanently gain the effects of Truespeech."],["**Frequency** twice per day\n\n---\n\nYou've studied medicine further to help others overcome illness and addiction. Choose an affliction and up to two of the following conditions affecting an adjacent ally: Confused, Controlled, Drained, Frightened, Sickened, Stupefied. You reduce the stage of that affliction by 1 and the value of the conditions by 1. If the target still has the affliction or at least one of the conditions, attempt a Medicine check to counteract those remaining afflictions and conditions. Your counteract rank is equal to half your level rounded up."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You succeed at a saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYou know that nothing in life is guaranteed, and you feel invigorated every time you overcome the challenges life throws at you. You're certain that you'll live to see another day. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to your level that last for 1 minute. If you critically succeeded on the triggering save, you are also Quickened during your next turn and can use your extra action only to Stride or Strike."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** Your last action was a skill check that you failed.\n\n---\n\nYour new life is a challenge that you embrace wholeheartedly. You never give up, even in the face of failure. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus on skill checks attempted with the required skill for 10 minutes."],["Your proboscis has become particularly deadly to those around you and is either longer, stronger, or more flexible. Your proboscis gains two of the following traits: backstabber, backswing, forceful, reach 10 feet (counts as two traits), sweep, trip, versatile S.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you select reach, you can use the Drain Blood ancestry feat or the Siphon Poison action of the bloodfilter orocoran heritage from up to 10 feet away."],["You've traveled to hundreds of places scattered across dozens of worlds and glimpsed wonders both beautiful and strange. When you roll a success on a Piloting check to Navigate or Plot Course, or on a Survival check to Sense Direction, you get a critical success instead. In addition, you gain a +10-foot circumstance bonus to Speed during overland travel."],["Your body is rubbery, and you bounce against surfaces. When you fall, reduce the falling damage you take as though you'd fallen half the distance. In addition, you gain the Bounce Back reaction."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** A creature within your reach is taking persistent bleed damage, or is Grabbed, Paralyzed, Restrained, Unconscious, or willing.\n\n---\n\nYou jab your proboscis into the required creature to consume their blood. Attempt an Athletics check against the target's Fortitude DC. You automatically succeed on this check if the target is paralyzed, unconscious, or willing (but you still roll to see if you get a critical success). On a success, the creature becomes Drained 1 (Drained 2 on a critical success), and you gain temporary Hit Points equal to the target's level that last for 10 minutes."],["**Trigger** You're about to gain the Confused or Controlled condition.\n\n---\n\nYou refuse to surrender your autonomy ever again, and you've trained your mind to instinctively shake off mental control. Attempt a DC 17 flat check. On a success, you don't gain the triggering condition."],["You've learned to distill your blood into a potent pharmaceutical. During your daily preparations, you can create one dose of this medicine, which is a unique consumable serum with the effects of both a tactical medpatch and an advanced hypopen. This medicine remains potent until your next daily preparations, at which point it breaks down and is useless. You can never sell the medicine created in this way. At 13th level, your medicine instead functions as both an advanced medpatch and a superior hypopen. At 17th level, your medicine instead functions as both a superior medpatch and an elite hypopen."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou spew bile in a broad spray, violently vomiting in a 30-foot cone. Your bile deals (ceil(level/2)-2)d6 acid plus (ceil(level/2)-2)d6 poison damage to creatures in the area, with a basic Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. On a failure, a creature is also Sickened 1 (Sickened 2 on a critical failure). At 11th level and every two levels thereafter, the acid damage and the poison damage each increase by 1d6."],["If you can track something in the stinking, shifting swamps of the Mire, it puts you in company with some of the finest trackers in the galaxy. You gain the Terrain Expertise feat for swamps and sewers, and you can [[/act track]] while moving at full Speed while you're in a swamp or sewer."],["The thick murky waters of the Deepmarsh are navigable to those who understand their tricks. You ignore difficult terrain and uneven ground caused by swamps and sewers. You don't gain the Off-Guard condition for not having a swim Speed during aquatic combat. If you have a swim Speed, you ignore non-magical difficult terrain while swimming underwater, but not greater difficult terrain."],["You possess a pair of rodlike structures that let you taste the air or water around you, making you alert to the presence of others via scent. You gain imprecise scent with a range of 30 feet; this range increases to 60 feet when you're underwater. The GM will usually double the range if you're downwind or downstream or halve the range if you're upwind or upstream."],["You fill the nooks and crannies of your armor with a thick mucous that helps you feel more comfortable. You don't become Fatigued if you sleep while wearing armor. You gain the Mucous Spurt reaction."],["**Requirements** You have an ally within reach.\n\n---\n\nYou've studied the defensive tactics of squires and chroniclers who have found that the best form of defense is to protect your more capable allies. You Raise a Shield to give an adjacent ally the circumstance bonus from your shield to their AC instead of you as long as the selected ally remains adjacent to you. These benefits last until the start of your next turn or until you're no longer adjacent to your ally, whichever happens first. If you have the Shield Block feat, you can trigger Shield Block when you have your shield raised and the selected ally would take physical damage from an attack. You gain no bonus from Raising your Shield this way and can't Shield Block if you would take damage."],["You excrete more slime than most osharus. Slime Squirt no longer has a frequency. Additionally, you can Slime Squirt as a free action, but after using it as a free action, you can't use Slime Squirt again for 1 minute."],["Whether the canal thruways of Jhavom, the seas off the coast of Zhast, or the murky depths of the Mire, you are no stranger to water and are strong from spending so much time swimming. Increase your swim Speed to 30 feet."],["You're practiced in keeping your eyestalks moving independently to better monitor for threats. This allows you to keep an eye on everything nearby and have battlefield control. You gain all-around vision. This lets you see in all directions and prevents you from being flanked."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou secrete a slick and slippery slime when speed is of the essence. Until the end of your turn, when you leave a square, you use Slime Squirt in that square. If you're Grabbed, Immobilized, or Restrained, you can attempt to Escape with a +2 circumstance bonus. You can then Stride. During this Stride, you have a +10-foot circumstance bonus to your Speed."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou pulse and strobe your pigmentation in bright and luminescent tones to confuse and distract your enemies. Attempt a Deception check and compare it to the Will DC of each creature in a 40-foot emanation. The creatures are then temporarily immune to Startling Shift for 24 hours.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is Fascinated by you for as long as it can see you (unless it stops being fascinated, as normal for the condition) and is Dazzled for 1 round or as long as it's fascinated, whichever is longer.\n\n**Success** The creature is fascinated by you for 1 round and is dazzled for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The creature is dazzled for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is unaffected."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** You would take bludgeoning or sonic damage. You're able to use your internal invertebrate physics to minimize damage to yourself.\n\n---\n\nYou gain resistance 10 against the triggering damage and don't gain the clumsy, Deafened, Sickened, or Stunned conditions due to the attack or any ability triggered by the attack.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have Ancestral Resistance (bludgeoning or sonic), you gain resistance 20 against the attack instead."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** An enemy hits you with a Strike, or you attempt a Reflex save.\n\n---\n\nYour reflexes kick in as you throw your armplates in front of yourself in times of danger. You drop all held items; if you have Bulky Armplates, instead choose one arm and drop anything it's carrying. You immediately [[/act take-cover]] and gain the effects of greater cover against the triggering attack."],["Your fervently religious approach to acquiring information gives you insights and understanding into a broad array of subjects. You gain the Additional Lore skill feat. During your daily preparations, you can recontextualize your insights and change the chosen Lore skill for any of your Additional Lore skill feats, unless they're being used as a prerequisite for a permanent character option that your new Lore skill won't satisfy."],["Your armplates are larger than most, giving you superior defensive capabilities. While you have your armplates raised, you can use the [[/act take-cover]] action to increase the circumstance bonus to AC to +4. This lasts until the shield is no longer raised, or until any of the normal conditions that end Take Cover, whichever comes first. If you would provide lesser cover against an attack, having your armplates raised provides standard cover against it (and other creatures can Take Cover as normal using the cover from your armplates)."],["You studied the methodologies of one of Jhavom's fine expeditionary academies and know a few magical standbys for dangerous missions. You can cast Akashic Download and Shifting Surge as 1st-rank divine innate spells once per day each."],["Your research and your religion make up two sides of the same coin for you, and to grow in one means to grow in both. You become trained in one Lore skill of your choice. Whenever your proficiency in Religion increases to expert or better, you also gain that new proficiency rank with the chosen Lore skill."],["**Trigger** You roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou can take the scholar out of the library, but you can't take the library out of the scholar—even when matters turn violent. You can attempt to Recall Knowledge against a creature you're observing within 30 feet."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nWith extra effort, you can spray your slime in a 15-foot cone, causing the area to become difficult terrain for non-osharu creatures for 1 minute."],["Your slime assails the olfactory receptors. Non-osharu creatures that begin their turn adjacent to any square affected by Slime Squirt or Slime Spray must attempt a Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. On a failure, they become Sickened 1 (Sickened 2 on a critical failure)."],["Field agents of the Informational Safety Board and clergy of the Glory In Knowledge Museum codeveloped methods to biomagically cultivate telepathic sensory organs, and you've undergone their regimens and rituals to better serve Yaraesa. You gain limited telepathy, allowing you to communicate mentally with creatures within 30 feet that share a language with you, and they can mentally respond. This doesn't give you any access to their thoughts and communicates no more information than normal speech would."],["Your sticky mucous lets you hang onto foes with a painfully tenacious grip. When you roll a critical failure on a check to [[/act grapple]] a target, you get a failure instead. In addition, when a creature you've Grabbed rolls a failure on its check to Escape, it gets a critical failure instead, and if it rolls a critical success, it gets a success instead."],["Your body excretes abrasive chemicals in your slime when you're threatened. When you use Slime Squirt or Slime Spray, creatures in the area take floor(item level/3)d4 persistent acid damage with a basic Reflex saving throw against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. At 12th level and every three levels thereafter, the persistent acid damage increases by 1d4."],["Your armplates have been drastically enhanced with sharp quills that bristle menacingly. While your armplate is raised, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to checks to [[/act demoralize]]. When you Shield Block using your reaction against a melee Strike, you break off some of the quills, dealing floor(@item.origin.level/3)d8 piercing damage to the attacking creature (basic Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC). On a critical failure, the creature also takes floor(@item.origin.level)d4 persistent bleed damage as the quills embed themselves in its flesh. At 12th level and every three levels thereafter, the piercing damage increases by 1d8, and the persistent piercing damage increases by 1d4."],["Your anatomy possesses a certain amount of flexibility that you can utilize to attack foes who would be just out of reach. Your unarmed attacks and melee weapons you wield gain a reach of 10 feet until the beginning of your next turn. Make a melee Strike against a creature within your reach."],["You can alter your body's color to better vanish into your surroundings. As long as an observer is at least 20 feet away from you, you don't need cover from that observer to [[/act hide]] or [[/act sneak]]. This lasts until you move to an area with substantially different terrain."],["Your sprayed slime thickens on contact with air, giving it some substantial stopping power and possibly even locking foes in place. When you use Slime Squirt or Slime Spray, creatures in the area must attempt a Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. On a failure, they become Clumsy 1 for 1 round. On a critical failure, they become Clumsy 2 and Immobilized for 1 round."],["Your size gives the impression that there's no room to escape. You gain the Intimidating Glare skill feat. Additionally, if you're blocking a target's passage down a hallway or door, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Intimidation checks when you [[/act demoralize]] that target."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** An ally attempts a skill check with a skill that you have trained or better proficiency rank in.\n\n---\n\nYou push yourself to be the best by competing with the triggering ally. Until the end of your next turn, you can attempt the same skill check to perform the same action or activity that the triggering ally performed. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to this skill check. If you achieve at least one degree of success higher than the triggering ally, this use of Competitive Spirit doesn't count toward its frequency. If you roll a critical failure on this skill check, you take a –1 circumstance penalty to all skill checks attempted with that skill for the next hour as you try new techniques to improve your future attempts."],["You've developed keen organs that have a sensitivity to sound—and you know how to put them to use. You become trained in Performance or gain the Assurance skill feat with Performance if you're are already trained in that skill. In addition, you can accurately recall a melody or lyrics you've heard within the last week, granting you a +2 circumstance bonus to all Deception and Performance checks that involve mimicking speech or a specific sound."],["Whether it's your apartment, laboratory, or starship, your senses are particularly keen in the place you call home.\n\nSelect one familiar location to be your home turf. While in your home turf, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Stealth, Survival, and Perception checks and DCs.\n\nYou lose this bonus for 24 hours if there are any major alterations to your home turf, including temporary or illusory changes to the environment from the use of spells and effects that cause difficult terrain, temporary structures, and many witchwarper abilities. You don't lose your bonus due to changes in light level, gravity, or temperature (unless those changes cause significant alterations to the environment, such as starting a fire)."],["You always seem to land on your feet. You become trained in Acrobatics. If you're already trained in that skill, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Cat Fall skill feat."],["Your whiskers function as advanced electroreceptors, allowing you to orient yourself more easily. At the end of each round in which you're untethered, attempt a DC 15 flat check. On a success, you ignore the Clumsy and Off-Guard conditions imposed by being in zero-g for 1 minute."],["Whether from hunting at night or having a deep connection to the void of space, you're at home in darkness. You become trained in Stealth. You gain the Terrain Stalker skill feat, except instead of selecting a form of difficult terrain, you can use the feat in areas of dim light and darkness."],["Your strange singing voice can cause a moment's reconsideration or hesitation. Attempt a Performance check against the Will DC of a target within 30 feet. The target then becomes temporarily immune to your Pahtra Caterwaul for 24 hours.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target becomes Frightened 1 and Stupefied 1 as long as it's frightened.\n\n**Success** The target becomes frightened 1."],["You're an expert in both the traditional and modern pahtra performing arts. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Acrobatics and Performance. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Pahtra Lore."],["Battle is a dance, and you've honed your body into an instrument as exquisite as it is deadly. When you select this feat, you gain your choice of a claw unarmed attack or a jaws unarmed attack. Both of these attacks are in the brawling weapon group.\n\nA claw unarmed attack deals 1d6 slashing damage and has the agile, finesse, pahtra, and unarmed traits.\n\nA jaws unarmed attack deals 1d6 piercing damage and has the finesse, grapple, pahtra, and unarmed traits.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these attacks, you get its critical specialization effect.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat a second time. If you do, select the other attack from the options above."],["You can unleash the same primal pahtra war cries as your ancient ancestors. You gain the Battle Cry skill feat. While your [[/act demoralize]] action still has the auditory trait, you don't take a penalty when you Demoralize a creature that doesn't speak your language. Additionally, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Demoralize animals."],["You've integrated a fungal biotech to help manage your growth. You vent spores from your body in a 30-foot emanation, dealing 7)d4 poison damage to creatures in the area with a basic basic Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. The damage increases by 1d4 for every two levels you have beyond 13th level. A creature that fails its save is also Sickened 1 (Sickened 2 on a critical failure). You can't use Proudhome Puff again for 1d4 rounds."],["Whether through intense musical training, magical insight, or Meyel's divine blessing, you can feel the rhythm of the world around you and tug on time's chords to manipulate its melody and flow. You gain Haste and Slow as 3rd-rank primal innate spells. You can cast each of these spells once per day."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou quickly scan your surroundings for threats. You Seek. If you use electromagnetic sense, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to this check."],["**Requirements** You're Hidden to at least one enemy.\n\n---\n\nYou can strike fear into those you stalk simply by letting them know that you can see them, but they can't see you. You [[/act sneak]] or [[/act hide]] and verbally mock a single creature within 30 feet from whom you're hidden. Your Stealth check against that target's Perception DC gains the following success and failure results in addition to its usual results.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target you mock becomes Frightened 2. The target can't reduce its frightened condition below 1 until 1 minute passes or until it observes you (whichever comes first).\n\n**Success** The target you mock becomes Frightened 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** You become Observed to the target you mock."],["You can take a leap of faith and usually land on your feet. You can Leap up to 30 feet in any direction without touching the ground and without requiring an Athletics check; when doing so, you must land on a surface you can Climb or adjacent to an Edge you can Grab within 30 feet of you, or else you fall after using your next action. You can exceed your normal Speed while Leaping."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nBy preparing your caterwaul, you can focus on your performance and sing to a wider audience. If your next action is to use Pahtra Caterwaul, you can affect up to five targets instead of one. If any allies in range of your caterwaul speak Pahtra, they can spend their reaction to join in on your Pahtra Caterwaul. If at least one ally joins the Pahtra Caterwaul, increase the frightened value of targets that fail their save by 1."],["**Frequency** once per minute\n\n---\n\nYou're an experienced warrior who can tap into your predatory instincts and completely focus on a single creature you can detect—to the exclusion of everything else. Those incapable of understanding these instincts might even believe you've lost your senses. The GM rolls a secret counteract check against any illusion, morph, or polymorph effect on a target, but only for the purposes of determining whether you see through it, with a counteract rank of 6 and a counteract modifier equal to your Perception modifier.\n\nYou get a +2 status bonus to Perception checks when you [[/act seek]] the chosen creature and to Survival checks to [[/act track]] the chosen creature, but all other creatures become Hidden to you. This lasts 1 minute, until the target dies, or until you fall Unconscious, whichever comes first. If you take damage, you can voluntarily end your trance as a reaction, which has the concentrate trait."],["You perform a mournful dirge tinged with supernatural grief that compels the soul of a lost comrade to return to its body. You can cast Breath of Life once per day as a 7th-rank primal innate spell. It gains the auditory trait."],["**Trigger** You are reduced to 0 Hit Points and would gain the Dying condition or would otherwise die.\n\n---\n\nYou've discovered the fabled occult pahtra art of cheating death or have made substantial contingencies that help keep that legend alive. You prevent yourself from dying and regain Hit Points equal to 6d8 plus half your level. If the cause of your death was a condition or effect that would still cause you to die after regaining Hit Points, such as a high value on the Doomed condition, you suppress that condition for 1 minute."],["You're an accomplished battledancer and warrior, blessed by seers, honed by ancestral tradition, and capable of feats beyond the natural abilities of your peers. You gain Tailwind as a 1st-rank primal innate spell that you can cast once per day."],["You can sashay while you sing. You Stride. You can use Pahtra Caterwaul at any point during the Stride. If you're more than 5 feet above the target of this Pahtra Caterwaul, the range of the Pahtra Caterwaul increases by 30 feet."],["You can recenter yourself with a familiar scent stored on your body, such as a favorite food, the scarf of a loved one, or a sample of dirt from your home world. Roll a DC 5 flat check.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** Reduce your Frightened value by 2.\n\n**Success** Reduce your frightened value by 1."],["You can extend your claws to aid you in climbing. You gain a climb Speed equal to your land Speed."],["You've honed your whiskers' sensitivity to the degree that you can sense the movement of the weak electric fields emitted by potential enemies. You gain electromagnetic sense as an imprecise sense out to 15 feet. Electromagnetic sense allows you to detect nearby living and technological creatures, but you might have to use the Seek action to find an undetected creature in an environment with too much electromagnetic radiation, such as inside the engine room of a spaceship or near a powerful source of radio waves."],["You're so light on your feet you can even move through tall grass without leaving any tracks. You gain the Feather Step general feat, even if you don't meet its prerequisites. You can Cover Tracks using Acrobatics instead of Survival."],["Your whiskers have developed the same senses as that of your bonded hymothoa. You gain motion sense as an imprecise sense with a range of 30 feet. Motion sense allows you to detect nearby motion through vibration and air movement."],["You've inherited a greater connection to your Volosian heritage and begin to exhibit hymothoa habits. You gain the Volosian Spit action."],["You've learned to compensate for your hypersensitivity to sound. You gain sonic resistance equal to half your level. If you roll a success on a saving throw against a sonic effect, you get a critical success instead."],["You can hear the thrum of magic as if it were a swirling note, a shifting melody, a harmonic chord, or a percussive beat, pulsing in tune with your heart. You can detect the presence of magic as though you were always using a 1st-rank Detect Magic spell. This detects magic within a 30-foot emanation.\n\nAt 13th level, the rank of detect magic increases to 3rd. At 17th level, the rank of detect magic increases to 4th."],["Divine rhythm pulses through your blood, and your life is the music. You gain a +2 status bonus to Performance checks. In addition, you can use Performance to [[/act create-a-diversion skill=performance]]{Create a Diversion}, [[/act demoralize skill=performance]]{Demoralize}, or [[/act make-an-impression skill=performance]]{Make an Impression}. If you listen to music while resting, you regain a number of additional Hit Points equal to your level."],["**Requirements** You're Prone.\n\n---\n\nThis technique allows you to use the momentum of your attack with the assistance of your tail to spin back onto your feet. Make a melee Strike with your claws or a Battle Ribbon, then Stand. You don't take the –2 circumstance penalty for attacking while prone, and your Stand action doesn't trigger reactions from the target of your Strike."],["You've unlocked a deeper connection to the depths of emptiness that voidborns call home. This connection allows you to travel through hidden spaces while avoiding the attention of others. While Undetected by all non-allies in an area of dim light or darkness, you can Sneak without attempting a Stealth check so long as you move less than 15 feet and don't pass within 15 feet of an enemy during your movement.\n\nDuring exploration, this also allows you to automatically approach within 20 feet of other creatures while Avoiding their Notice in an area of dim light or darkness, as long as they aren't actively Searching or on guard."],["With two sets of reflexes, you have twice the self-preservation instincts. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to AC and saving throws against hazards. If you fail a saving throw or take damage from a hazard, this bonus increases to +2 until the end of your next turn."],["You're built for the fast-paced social existence of a big city or busy space station. You become trained in Society. If you would already be trained in Society (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. In addition, you gain the Streetwise skill feat."],["You become trained in Computers and Medicine. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Phasorq Lore."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You attempt a check to Recall Knowledge.\n\n---\n\nYour head would clearly be lost if it wasn't for your other head. For the triggering check, one of your heads can attempt to Aid the other. For the purposes of this check, both of your heads use the same skill bonuses."],["With some effort and concentration, you can track the battlefield from both heads at once. You gain all-around vision until the start of your next turn. This lets you see in all directions and prevents you from being flanked."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nOne of your heads manages the magic, while the other is free to go about your business. You Sustain a spell."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nWith two sets of eyes, two facial expressions, and sometimes conflicting body language, you have a natural ability to mislead your opponents. Attempt to [[/act feint]]. If you succeed, your target is Off-Guard against your ranged attacks in addition to melee attacks, and you can immediately attempt a Strike at the same target."],["You've learned how to keep mental effects limited to one head first hit, rather than letting them cloud both your minds. Each round you're affected by a mental effect, you can attempt a DC 10 flat check. On a success, one of your heads is clearminded enough to ignore the mental effect for that round, allowing you to act normally."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You would die.\n\n---\n\nOne of your heads might be dead, but your other head can drag you back into the realm of the living through sheer force of will. You don't die. Instead, if you have the dying or Unconscious conditions, you lose the dying and unconscious conditions. If you're at 0 Hit Points, you have 1 Hit Point. Increase the value of your wounded condition by 1. You are Stupefied 1 and can't use any abilities that depend on two heads until you're healed to greater than half your maximum HP. You can use this reaction while unconscious, but not if your body would be destroyed, such as by the Disintegrate spell."],["Each of yours heads looks out for the other. You gain all-around vision, meaning you can’t be flanked."],["Your better half (or other head, anyway) is carefully monitoring your surroundings, making you twice as likely to be ready when danger arises. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks for initiative."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** Your last action was a critically failed Strike.\n\n---\n\nThough one of your heads is primarily responsible for your body, the second can exert control some of the time—especially when they see your primary head make a mistake. You Strike with a different weapon or unarmed attack, and your multiple attack penalty for this attack is –3 (–2 with an agile attack) on your second attack of the turn instead of –5, and –6 (–4 with an agile attack) on your third or subsequent attack of the turn, instead of –10."],["Sure, one of your heads has already tried, but that's why you've got a spare! Your other half can offer a fresh perspective in high-pressure situations and patch up holes in your allies that you might have missed. Once per day, you can use Battle Medicine on a creature that's temporarily immune due to having already been treated with Battle Medicine."],["It's easier to protect yourself on the move with two sets of eyes, so you can do it twice as well as most. You Step twice."],["You don't know everything, but you sure know how to learn it. You become a master in the Lore skill you learn each day during your daily preparations. At 15th level, you become legendary."],["When you're sick, both of your heads feel it, and they each have an incentive to do something about it. When you attempt to reduce the sickened condition, you can roll twice and take the better result. If you critically succeed, reduce your sickened value by 3."],["You can easily send data to technological devices like a spectra. You can cast the Implant Data cantrip as a divine innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou were born or gestated inside the Drift, and hyperspace is always a part of you. With a thought, you seize a fragment of the Drift and temporarily transplant it onto the battlefield as an intangible barrier of colorful light. This shimmering field appears within 30 feet and is straight and vertical, stretching up to 10 feet long and 10 feet high. The barrier grants concealment to creatures targeted through it, and it sheds colorful bright light for 10 feet on each side and dim light for the next 10 feet. You can ignore any concealment granted by the barrier. The barrier lasts for 5 rounds."],["Your body produces an overabundance of electrical energy, which you can emit as a blast of lightning or use to power technological devices. You can cast the Electric Arc cantrip as a divine innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up.\n\nWhen you cast electric arc, you can also target batteries or tech items powered by batteries (in any combination). If you target a battery or tech item powered by a battery, that item isn't damaged. Instead, it regains 2 charges per spell rank. If the target is a tech item that needs a battery but doesn't currently have one, treat the item as if it had a battery with 2 charges per spell rank for 1 minute."],["You've learned to leverage your intrinsic link to the Drift, making you an excellent pilot. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Piloting and Stealth. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Prismeni Lore."],["You became a prismeni after a close encounter with one or more spectra. You can communicate mentally with spectra and with intelligent constructs with the tech trait within 30 feet. You don't need to share a language to communicate with such creatures in this way. This doesn't give you any special access to their thoughts and communicates no more information than normal speech would."],["You have an intuitive understanding of computers, machines, and other technological devices. You become trained in Computers and Crafting. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice."],["Triune chose you specifically to become a prismeni. You hold the All-Code close in your heart and cherish the data it's imparted upon you. You become trained in Religion and Triune Lore. You have familiarity with the pulse gauntlet, and for the purpose of determining your proficiency, the pulse gauntlet is a simple weapon. Whenever you gain a class feature that grants you expert or greater proficiency in simple weapons, you also gain that proficiency in the pulse gauntlet."],["**Frequency** once per minute\n\n**Trigger** An enemy's Strike would hit you, and you weren't already Concealed, Hidden, or undetected to that enemy.\n\n---\n\nYou momentarily slip into the Drift, becoming concealed against the triggering Strike. If the flat check for concealment fails, the Strike misses you. After resolving the triggering Strike, you reemerge from the Drift in an unoccupied space adjacent to your original square."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou instinctively encode your presence, obscuring your identity and scrambling your visual appearance to technological visual sensors. You become Concealed to all technological visual sensors, such as security cameras, ocular cybernetic augmentations, and the visual processors of technological constructs, for 1 minute. As the nature of this effect still leaves your location obvious, you can't use this concealment to Hide or Sneak."],["Your connection to the Drift grows even stronger, allowing you to travel through it more often. The frequency of Drift Hop changes to once per hour."],["With a thought, you can infect a technological creature or device with a short-lived virus, causing the object to glitch and malfunction. You can cast Discharge as a 3rd-rank divine innate spell twice per day."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** Your last action was a melee Strike that critically hit a creature.\n\n---\n\nYou launch the creature you hit with the required Strike into the Drift to reposition it across the battlefield. The creature is teleported to a location of your choice up to a distance of 20 feet from its starting location and within your line of sight. If you're in the Drift, the distance you can teleport the creature is doubled. The creature must be able to fit in its new location, and its new location must be unoccupied. The creature can attempt a Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The distance you can teleport the creature is halved, and it can't be moved to a location that is hazardous or would result in a fall.\n\n**Failure** You teleport the creature up to the noted distance.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the distance you can teleport the creature is doubled."],["Whether through a quirk of your bloodline, the interference of powerful spectra, or Triune's blessing, your body has been flooded by the essence of the Drift, transforming you into a spectra. You cease aging. You gain darkvision, the cosmic trait, and a fly Speed equal to your land Speed. While you're in the Drift, your fly Speed is equal to double your land Speed. Additionally, you gain the Cosmic Blast action."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou travel across the battlefield via the Drift. You teleport up to a distance equal to your Speed within your line of sight. If you're in the Drift, the distance you can teleport is doubled."],["Your body is insulated from electrical attacks. You gain electricity resistance equal to half your level. Additionally, you gain the Redirect Current reaction."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou can project your speech through wireless transmission, rather than speaking aloud, causing your words to emit from unsecured technological devices as either audio, text, or both. For example, your voice could emit audibly from an intercom or appear as text on a vidscreen or holosign. Select an unsecured technological device within 100 feet. For 1 minute, you can choose to transmit anything you say through that output device, rather than say it aloud. You can change which device you use as an output as a single action. Doing so doesn't extend the duration."],["Your ability to control and empower technological devices has improved. You gain Delete and Supercharge Weapon as 1st-rank divine innate spells. You can cast each of these divine innate spells once per day."],["The Drift is your true home, and you can survive within it indefinitely. While you're in the Drift, you gain the cosmic trait, and you don't need to eat or drink. While you're in the Drift or a vacuum, you gain a fly Speed equal to your land Speed."],["You know how to probe computer systems with your mind as easily as others might handle a hacking toolkit. You can communicate wirelessly with technological devices within 10 feet, allowing you to attempt Computers checks on these devices without a user interface or hacking toolkit. If you can already attempt Computers checks at range, you increase the distance that you can do so by an additional 10 feet."],["The Drift revitalizes your spirit and restores your vitality, physically healing your wounds. If you rest for 10 minutes while within the Drift, you gain Hit Points equal to your Constitution modifier × your level. This is cumulative with any healing you receive from Treat Wounds.\n\nOnce per hour, you can focus or meditate on your inherent connection to the Drift. This is a 10-minute activity that has the concentrate and exploration traits. When you do, you're treated as if you'd rested for 10 minutes while in the Drift, save that the number of Hit Points you regain from this feat is halved."],["In addition to allowing you to wield weapons made for much larger creatures, your LFAN lets you wrestle way above your weight class. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus on Athletics checks to [[/act disarm]], [[/act grapple]], [[/act reposition]], [[/act shove]], or [[/act trip]] Small and Tiny creatures. You can attempt to Disarm, Grapple, Reposition, Shove, or Trip creatures of up to Huge size. If you're legendary in Athletics, you can also attempt these actions on Gargantuan creatures."],["You've adjusted your IMAS to tolerate stress more effectively. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against effects that would make you Paralyzed or give you a penalty to your Speed, including those that would make you suppressed."],["When you change between your flowering and seeding states, you perform other subtle alterations to your body to enhance your abilities. You can change between a flowering state and a seeding state by spending 1 week of downtime.\n\nIf you're flowering, your pleasant aroma makes you more charming. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks to [[/act make-an-impression options=floral-shifter:flowering traits=olfactory]]; this effect has the olfactory trait. The bonus increases to +2 if you're a master in Diplomacy. If you're seeding, you instead gain immunity to falling damage whenever you're in an atmosphere."],["Cooperation is a fundamental value on Raxil, and you were raised to always look for opportunities to work collaboratively with others. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to checks to Aid, and your allies gain a +2 circumstance bonus to checks to Aid you."],["You're always tinkering with your LFAN, making sure that it's in good repair and experimenting with methods to grant it new functionality. You can retrain all feats with the LFAN trait as a part of your daily preparations. You can use the Implant Augmentation downtime activity even if you don't meet the prerequisites. If you're an expert in Crafting or Medicine, you can Implant Augmentation in 10 minutes per item level of the augmentation. If you're a master in Crafting or Medicine, you can Implant Augmentation in 1 minute per item level."],["You have a free tactical flashlight built into your LFAN. Using this flashlight doesn't interfere with your ability to use your hands or your LFAN to interact with or hold other objects. Additionally, you gain the Digital Diversion skill feat and can Create a Diversion using Computers instead of Deception by rapidly manipulating the settings on your flashlight. When you do, Create a Diversion gains the visual trait.\n\n[[/act create-a-diversion skill=computers traits=visual variant=gesture]]\n\n[[/act create-a-diversion skill=computers traits=visual variant=trick]]\n\n[[/act create-a-diversion skill=computers traits=visual variant=distracting-words]]"],["**Frequency** once per day.\n\n---\n\nLike the seeds of a dandelion or the intricate connections that allow raxilite Gowan starships to break apart into many smaller independent vessels, you've engineered your body and equipment to be able to break apart into smaller pieces.\n\nIn this state, you're amorphous. You lose any item bonus to AC and all other effects and bonuses from armor, and you use your proficiency rank in unarmored defense. You gain resistance 8 to physical damage and are immune to precision damage. You can't cast spells, activate items, or use actions that have the attack or manipulate trait. You gain a fly Speed of 10 feet if you didn't already have a fly Speed, and you can slip through tiny cracks. You can reassemble your body and your gear as a single action. If you haven't reassembled yourself after 5 minutes, safety protocols automatically activate to rebuild you."],["You've attached a nervous system–integrated weapon mount to your LFAN that you can activate to efficiently fire an arc of electricity. This Semi-Autonomous LFAN Version Omega (or SALVO) deals ceil(level/2)))d4) electricity damage (basic Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC). After using SALVO, you can't use it again for 1d4 rounds. At 15th level and every 2 levels thereafter, the damage increases by 1d4."],["You've integrated a Wide-Spectrum Artillery Repulsion Device, or WARD, into your LFAN that emits energy to absorb incoming projectiles. The WARD is always active by default, but you can deactivate or reactivate it with a single Interact action. While your WARD is active, any damage you would take from a ranged attack is applied to the force field's Hit Points first before being applied to your Hit Points (including temporary Hit Points). If an attack reduces the WARD to 0 Hit Points, you take any excess damage, the WARD deactivates, and it can't be activated again for 10 minutes. Your WARD has 39 healing Hit Points and regains 6 healing Hit Points at the start of your turn. At 15th level and every 2 levels thereafter, increase the total Hit Points of your WARD by 3 and the amount of Hit Points it replenishes by 1."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\nYou've mastered the art of collaboration, developing a means to lend others your own energy and cognitive capability. An ally within 30 feet is Quickened for 1 round. They can use this extra action only to Stride or Strike. That ally is temporarily immune to Perfect Synergy for 10 minutes."],["You generate an overwhelming surge of electricity from within your body, engulfing yourself in a storm of sparks that causes nearby tech to malfunction. You can cast Overload Systems as a 7th-rank arcane innate spell once per hour. Raxilites and raxilite technology are immune to this spell, and you can choose up to four squares to exclude from the area of the spell."],["You've become particularly fascinated by a culture from a world other than Raxil and used your knack for integrating into a community to become part of that culture's traditions. You gain the Adopted Ancestry general feat as well as a 1st-level ancestry feat for your chosen ancestry."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou send currents of electricity coursing through your LFAN, electrifying everything you're holding. Until the end of your current turn, your Strikes deal an additional 1d6 electricity damage per weapon damage die."],["Your guidance provides your allies with exceptional assistance on tasks that are second nature to you. When your allies Follow the Expert and choose you as their expert, they gain a +3 circumstance bonus if you're an expert in the skill, or a +4 circumstance bonus if you're at least a master in the skill.\n\nPracticed Leader"],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\nYou have a MAIL (Messaging Augmentation Integrated LFAN), which allows you to efficiently communicate information to others by translating it into a form that can be efficiently transmitted to their nervous system. You use your LFAN to transmit information to the nervous system of an adjacent willing creature, imparting to that target an amount of information in an instant that could otherwise be communicated in 10 minutes.\n\n---\n\n**Special** As long as you have a MAIL, you gain a special form of limited telepathy that allows you to communicate mentally with any raxilite within 30 feet as long as they share a language with you."],["You gain the Augmented Body general feat and can choose an augmentation that costs 500 credits or less. You can swap out the augmentation you chose with this feat during your daily preparations, but the new augmentation must always have the same type (so a biotech augmentation can't replace a cybernetic augmentation). Any augmentation you choose with this feat is considered to be worth at least 500 credits for purposes of calculating the difference between prices when swapping your augmentations."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\nYou have a rudimentary artificial intelligence in your LFAN that you can activate to accelerate your LFAN-based activities. You become Quickened for 1 minute. You can spend this extra action only to Strike with a weapon held in your LFAN, Interact with an object with your LFAN, or perform an action with the LFAN trait.\n\n---\n\n**Special** if you have the Brawler LFAN feat, you can spend this extra action to [[/act disarm]], [[/act grapple]], [[/act reposition]], [[/act shove]], or [[/act trip]]."],["Your latest augmentation is a multifunction unit capable of processing metals of all types for a variety of purposes, a Metallic Augmentation Xtractor (MAX). You can use the benefits of the jury-rigging raxilite heritage once every 10 minutes, even if you don't have the heritage. If you have the heritage, you recover a number of Hit Points equal to seven times your level instead of five times your level."],["You and your partner are skilled at working together to bait your enemies and throwing them wholly off-kilter. When you or your partner [[/act feint]] and roll a critical success, the target is also Off-Guard to melee and ranged attacks that you or your bonded partner attempt against it until the end of your next turn."],["In the modern Drakelands, battle against draconic forces takes place in boardrooms with lawyers rather than in archaic lairs filled with treasure. You are well-versed in this new kind of corporate warfare and have faced off against at least one Triaxian corporation before. You become trained in Corporate Lore, Labor Lore, and Legal Lore. You also gain the Additional Lore skill feat for one of these three skills."],["You know full-well the dangers that exist in the modern galaxy when one is unprepared for the worst, even when hoping for the best. You gain the Shield Block general feat. You can move at full speed while using the Defend exploration activity."],["Your bond with your partner allows you to literally feel their pain, making it easier to treat their injuries. You gain the Battle Medicine feat even if you don't meet the prerequisites, but you can only use it on your bonded partner unless you're trained in Medicine. When you succeed with Battle Medicine or Treat Wounds, your bonded partner gains a circumstance bonus to the number of Hit Points they regain equal to 5 HP at DC 20, 10 HP at DC 30, or 15 HP at DC 40."],["Dragonkin have the ability to form permanent bonds with a chosen partner. Some ryphorians, through countless years of close proximity to the draconic inhabitants of Triaxus, have learned to emulate this ability to a limited degree. You can form a temporary bond with one willing sapient creature as a 10-minute activity that can only be attempted if you and your partner share a deep bond. Once formed, this bond lasts for 1 day. When you're within 30 feet of this bonded creature, you both gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Will saves.\n\n---\n\n*SFS Note:* For the purposes of this feat, any willing and sapient creature can be chosen."],["In pursuit of an equal friendship with their dragon neighbors, many ryphorians have learned to take on their large, winged forms. You can cast Dragon Form as a 6th-rank primal innate spell once per day. You must transform into the same battle form each time you cast this innate spell, chosen when you select this feat. When you reach 17th level, you can heighten the spell to 8th rank when you cast it."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** You're within 30 feet of an ally with the dying condition.\n\n---\n\nYou seethe as you see a friend, ally, or companion laid low. This anger hones your vision into a laser-like focus, allowing you to do what needs to be done. Make a Strike, rolling the attack twice and taking the better result."],["Your ability to ride your bonded partner into battle has further improved, and you act as one body and one mind. When you ride your bonded partner as a mount, you gain three actions at the start of your turn, rather than the two you normally would."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nBeyond emulating dragonkin's energy breath, you've now learned to channel the power of a true dragon, able to spew forth its potent energy. Choose a type of damage that corresponds to a specific dragon. You can exhale this energy as a 15-foot cone or 30-foot line that deals 14d6 damage plus 4d6 persistent damage of the chosen type (basic basic Reflex save using the higher of your class DC or spell DC). On a critical failure, a target also becomes Frightened 2."],["You conjure forth a visage of the psychic imprint from the Newborn that imbues your heritage. You can cast Mask of Terror as a 7th-rank occult innate spell once per day."],["You can hear a pin drop on a windy day and can even triangulate a vague estimation of where that pin came from. Your tremorsense becomes a precise sense with a range of 30 feet."],["You and your partner outmaneuver your foes by taking advantage of your difference in size. When you and your ally who's a different size than you flank the same enemy, that enemy takes a –2 circumstance penalty to its DCs against [[/act disarm]], [[/act feint]], [[/act reposition]], [[/act shove]], [[/act trip]], and [[/act tumble-through]] attempts.\n\nAbove and Below"],["Inspired by legends of heroes from a bygone age, you and your bonded partner have learned the ancient art of dragonriding. You can ride your bonded partner as a mount if they're one size category larger than you. When you ride your bonded partner as a mount, your synchronicity enables them to gain three actions at the start of their turn, rather than the two actions they normally would for being ridden by another PC. You still gain only two actions at the start of your turn, rather than three."],["Your innate connection to nature allows you to move through certain environments that might slow others down and hamper the movements of your allies and enemies alike. You ignore non-magical difficult terrain due to plant life if you're a summerborn ryphorian or due to ice and snow if you're a winterborn ryphorian, and you treat those kinds of greater difficult terrain as normal difficult terrain."],["Nothing escapes your ears so long as they move even an inch. You gain tremorsense as a vague sense with a range of 30 feet. This means you can use your ears to determine if a creature is present, but you can't pinpoint their location. Creatures that haven't moved or don't make sounds (such as those under the effects of a silence spell) remain undetected to you."],["Your glistening skin oils make it harder to pin you down. Whenever you roll a success on a check to Escape or a saving throw against an effect that would impose the Grabbed, Immobilized, or Restrained condition on you, you get a critical success instead. Whenever a creature rolls a failure on a check to [[/act grapple]], [[/act shove]], or [[/act trip]] you, it gets a critical failure instead."],["You and your partner are so in tune with each other that you can move past each other with ease on the battlefield. You can end your movement sharing the same space as your bonded partner and they can do the same, even if you're the same size. As long as you're in the same square, you and your bonded partner can't be flanked by creatures of your level or lower.\n\nBack to Back Bond"],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You take acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic damage.\n\n---\n\nYou call upon the strange psychic powers that influenced your birth and turn them into a protective bubble that shields you, but only so often. You gain resistance to the triggering energy type equal to your level for 1 minute. You don't apply the resistance to the triggering instance of damage."],["Even though the calling of your blood doesn't lie squarely with the summerborn or winterborn, you feel that you can nudge it in one direction or the other to help protect you. You gain resistance to cold and fire equal to half your level."],["**Trigger** You're struck by a critical hit from a melee attack.\n\n---\n\nReacting quickly to danger, your body shakes and vibrates, causing you to shed some fur that can throw off the attacks of even the most experienced warrior. Attempt a DC 17 flat check. If you're successful, the attack becomes a normal hit."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou tap into a primordial connection with the seasonal change your species bases much of its physiology on. You accelerate that change around you, tapping into primal powers to cause verdant growth nearby. For the next minute, each time you Step or Stride, you create difficult terrain in each square you leave during your movement that lasts for 10 minutes."],["You spend more time gallivanting across the galaxy than you do at home. You become trained in Society. If you would automatically become trained in Society (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Multilingual skill feat."],["You find flying exhilarating and live to perform impressive aerial maneuvers. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Acrobatics checks to Maneuver in Flight and on Piloting checks to Drive a vehicle or starship. When you roll a critical failure on an Acrobatics check to Maneuver in Flight, you get a failure instead."],["Ambient solar energy manifests in your attacks. You gain a solar strike unarmed attack that requires a free hand to use unless you have manifested energy wings. This is an agile, finesse, unarmed attack in the flame weapon group that deals 1d6 fire damage."],["You ride air currents, electromagnetic waves, and solar energy like a parachute. You take no damage from falling regardless of the distance you fall."],["You understand that the galaxy is a wondrous place full of arcane mysteries and strange phenomena. You can cast the Detect Magic cantrip as an arcane innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up.\n\nIn addition, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to skill checks to Identify Magic."],["You grew up hearing stories about Damiar and Iovo, the long-destroyed sarcesian home worlds remembered today only in legends, shattered rock, and the hearts of your people. You gain the Additional Lore general feat for Damiar Lore, Iovo Lore, and Diaspora Lore."],["You have excellent lung capacity. You gain the Breath Control general feat. You do not need to breathe for up to 10 minutes after leaving a vacuum."],["Your energy wings shed bright light in a 20-foot radius (and dim light to the next 20 feet). You can extinguish or rekindle this light using a single action, which has the concentrate trait."],["You've taken the lessons of your people to heart. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Arcana and Piloting. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Sarcesian Lore."],["You're accustomed to fighting from afar—really far! You gain access to weapons in the sniper group and all uncommon weapons with the sarcesian trait. You have familiarity with weapons in the sniper group and all weapons with the sarcesian trait—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons, and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["Your people's long history of clashing with Eox has made you wary. You become trained in Religion. If you were already trained in Religion, you become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to checks to Recall Knowledge about undead creatures."],["You're accustomed to living or working in utter darkness, and your eyes have adjusted to the gloom. You gain greater darkvision."],["You can absorb the solar and electromagnetic radiation in your surroundings, transforming it into kinetic energy that propels your body faster. Your Speeds increase by 5 feet. In addition, you gain the Light Speed action."],["Your ability to manipulate solar radiation has improved. You can manifest your wings to use Coronal Flare without any hands at any time, even if you are not in a vacuum. In addition, your Coronal Flare gains the Thrown 40 feet trait."],["You can leverage your instinctive magical abilities to liberate the body and mind. You gain Clear Mind and Unfettered Movement as 4th-rank arcane innate spells. You can cast each of these spells as arcane innate spells once per day."],["Your body has adapted over to consume the excess energy it uses to shield itself, allowing it to neutralize other forms of energy that could harm it. When you use your Energy Deflection reaction, if the attack was a failure or critical failure, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to your level; you also gain the Energy Shielding feat (selecting a different type of energy). These temporary Hit Points and the Energy Shielding feat last 1 minute.\n\nEnergy Consumption"],["Reaching across space, you connect with the River Between and seize a fragment of its solar stream, inundating the battlefield in golden light and solar energy. This trickle of the River Between fills a 100-foot line that is 10 feet in diameter, starts from your square, and remains for 1 minute. Once the river forms, you can move to any square within the river (this movement does not trigger reactions). The area is bright light and counts as a vacuum for the purposes of a sarcesian using their energy wings. Non-sarcesians in the area when you use Ride the River Between, or who later enter the area, must succeed at a Fortitude save or become Dazzled for 1 round (1 minute on a critical failure). Creatures affected by this ability are temporarily immune for 24 hours. The DC of this save is equal to the higher of your spell DC or class DC."],["You're among the most powerful of sarcesians and can harness the cosmic forces of the universe to create incredible stellar phenomena. Select one of the following spells, which you can cast once per day as a 7th-rank arcane innate spell: Eclipse Burst or Sunburst."],["You have a soul-deep connection to the River Between. When you're in mortal peril, the River Between beckons you home and into its embrace. When you would die, you don't. Instead, you are encased in a cocoon of golden solar energy and disappear, teleporting across the galaxy to the River Between. 2d6 days later, this chrysalis hatches, and you emerge fully healed in a random location along the River Between in the Diaspora."],["Somewhere along your travels, picking up new languages became as easy as breathing—some of your colleagues even suspect you might be blessed by the god Weydan! You can speak, read, and understand any language."],["You take in your surroundings, instantly opening your mind up to the answers hidden all around you and the clues their presence has left behind. You instantly use up to three Recall Knowledge actions. If you have any special abilities or free actions that would normally be triggered when you Recall Knowledge, you can't use them for these actions. The first time one of these attempts to Recall Knowledge uses a Lore skill you selected with Additional Lore, you roll the associated Recall Knowledge check twice and use the higher result. That Recall Knowledge check gains the fortune trait."],["You can manifest your energy wings while within an atmosphere for a short time. Your energy wings manifest, granting you a fly Speed equal to your land Speed plus 10 feet for 10 minutes. You can end this duration early as a single action."],["You concentrate ambient energy into a burst of light. Using the flash as cover, you use the Stealth skill to Hide, and then you Sneak up to twice."],["While traversing the Diaspora, you've witnessed countless magical anomalies and survived to tell the tale. This persistent exposure to magical energy has rubbed off on you, leaving traces of magic behind that shield your body from harmful energy. Select one of the following types of energy damage: acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic. You gain resistance 5 to that damage type.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times. Each time you do, select a different energy type."],["**Trigger** You take fire damage.\n\n---\n\nBe they solar rays or blazing flames, light and heat are a part of you. For 1 minute, you glow from within, shedding bright light in a 30-foot radius (and dim light to the next 30 feet). While you glow in this way, your body is flush with warmth—you treat environmental cold effects as if they were one step less extreme (incredible cold becomes extreme, extreme cold becomes severe, and so on). You also gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saves against attacks, spells, and other effects that have the cold trait."],["Using your large size, you can extend your reach to attack targets that are farther away. When you wield a melee weapon that requires two hands and doesn't have reach, you can change between a typical two-handed grip and an extended two-handed stretch using an Interact action. Weapons wielded in your extended stretch gain a reach of 10 feet."],["You study the subtle, intangible forces that can be found in every particle and mote of magic in the universe around you. During your daily preparations, you can meditate on these spiritual and celestial mysteries and gain the Additional Lore skill feat in any Lore skill subcategory of your choice. This feat (and your proficiency in the Lore skill granted by it) lasts until you make your daily preparations again. Since both the feat and proficiency are temporary, you can't use them to satisfy a prerequisite for a skill increase or permanent character option (like a feat)."],["**Trigger** You become Grabbed, Immobilized, or Restrained.\n\n---\n\nYour extreme flexibility and deceptively compact frame make it easy for you to escape a variety of confines, and your quick reaction time means you can do so in a flash! You attempt to Escape."],["You're capable of surviving in the void of space indefinitely. While you maintain suspended respiration, you are immune to inhaled threats. Additionally, as long as you use suspended respiration, you don't need to eat or drink. Once per day as a free action, you can suspend respiration in atmosphere with these benefits for 1 minute."],["You leverage your extensive knowledge of undead during combat. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to damage with weapons and unarmed attacks against undead creatures. If your attack would deal more than one weapon die of damage, the bonus is equal to the number of weapon dice or unarmed attack dice.\n\nFurthermore, when you succeed or critically succeed at a check to Recall Knowledge against an undead creature that you can see, you identify a weak spot in their defenses—for 1 minute, you gain access to the critical specialization effects of all weapons and unarmed attacks for attacks you make against that specific creature.\n\nUndead Slayer"],["You loudly proclaim your opposition to a single creature you're aware of within 60 feet. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Armor Class and saving throws against the selected creature's attacks, spells, and other effects for 1 minute. During that time, if you would fail or critically fail a saving throw against the selected creature, you can choose to reroll the failed save. If you do, after rerolling, Willful Defiance ends."],["You've become more adept at using your energy wings within an atmosphere. Atmospheric Flight no longer has a frequency and can be used as often as desired. When you use Atmospheric Flight, your wings remain manifested until you spend a single action to purposefully dismiss them."],["You're an abundant source of electromagnetic radiation, which naturally amplifies the radiance of lights around you. Light sources in your possession (including those carried, cast on you, worn, or otherwise a part of you) are more luminous—double the area illuminated by these light sources. If a light source you possess would deal damage or cause a harmful effect based on its area, the area of those additional effects are not increased by Amplify Radiance. Additionally, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to counteract checks made to counteract darkness."],["You have the ability to convert ambient solar radiation and other stellar energy into pure magical light. You gain Wisp Ally as a 1st-rank arcane innate spell and gain Floating Flame and Revealing Light as 2nd-rank arcane innate spells. You can cast each of these spells as arcane innate spells once per day."],["**Trigger** You are the target of a ranged attack that would deal at least one type of damage you selected with Energy Shielding.\n\n**Requirements** You're aware of the attack and are not Off-Guard against it.\n\n---\n\nYou leverage the magical energy clinging to your body to counter similar harmful attacks. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack."],["You've broadened your senses and are better able to comprehend the unseen answers all around you. When you use Student of the Unseen during your daily preparations, you gain Additional Lore twice."],["You've trained to engage your foes from afar and leverage your keen vision to improve your accuracy. You reduce the penalty for attacking beyond your first range increment by 1, to a minimum of 0. If you're in a vacuum, you instead reduce the penalty for attacking beyond your first range increment by 2, to a minimum of 0.\n\nIn addition, you gain the Line Up the Shot action."],["Your cheeks are stretchy, and you can store up to four items of light Bulk or less in these cheek pouches. None of these items can have a dimension longer than 1 foot. As long as you have at least one item in your cheek pouches, your speech is noticeably difficult to understand. Placing an item in your cheek pouch or retrieving one is an Interact action. You can empty your mouth with a single action, causing everything you had stored in your cheek pouches to fall to the ground in your square."],["Your psychic abilities have developed beyond simple communication. Choose one cantrip from the occult spell list. You can cast this cantrip as an occult innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["Your tail functions like an extra limb. You can hold one extra hand's worth of equipment with your tail, and you can use your tail to perform Interact actions. You tail is considered one pair of hands for the purposes of designating your active hands with the Switch Hands action."],["**Lashunta** When you use limited telepathy to communicate with another creature, you act as a conduit for their thoughts, allowing them to respond to you for a few scant moments—if they wish. The creature can give you a brief response as a reaction, or as a free action at the beginning of their next turn as long as they remain within range of your telepathy.\n\n---\n\n**Shirren** When you use limited telepathy to communicate with another creature, the creature can give you a brief response as a reaction, or as a free action at the beginning of their next turn."],["You install one additional pair of arms onto your frame.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat multiple times, gaining one additional pair of arms each time."],["You can induce a chemical reaction that allows a part of your body to glow. You must designate what part of your body glows when you take this feat.\n\nYou begin to glow with bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for the next 20 feet. While you're glowing, you can't be Undetected and you take a –4 penalty to Stealth checks to [[/act hide]] and [[/act sneak]]. You can Dismiss the glow as a free action. At 9th level, you shed bright light in a 40-foot radius and dim light for the next 40 feet."],["You have a growth of particularly durable chitin on your arm that you can use as a shield. This shield doesn't need to be held in your hand, and it can't be disarmed. Your shield has an AC bonus of +2, Hardness 4, 12 Hit Points, and a Broken Threshold of 6. If your shield becomes broken, it can't be repaired until you are restored to full health and spend 10 minutes readjusting your chitin. You can spend 1 day of downtime and expend raw materials (such as UPBs) to improve the grade of your shield, but only to a grade up to your level (such as advanced if you're level 8 or higher). Use the level, price, Hardness, HP, and BT adjustments in the Shield Improvements table."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** An ally within 10 feet fails a skill check requiring 3 actions or fewer.\n\n---\n\nYou broadcast helpful encouragement or pertinent information to your ally's mind. Your ally rerolls the triggering skill check and takes the better result."],["Helping your companions gives you a rush that no common drug could replicate. After you successfully Aid an ally, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to skill checks using the same skill for 10 minutes.\n\nJust Happy to Help!"],["Your ability to adapt to various beliefs instills you with knowledge of many cultures. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Diplomacy and Society. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Shirren Lore."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou have a specialized gland that produces an acidic compound that eats away at hard surfaces. You spit this acidic compound in a 30-foot line. Each creature in the line takes 8)d6 acid damage with a basic Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC.\n\nA creature that fails its save gains weakness 5 to piercing damage until the end of your next turn (this has no effect on creatures with resistance or immunity to piercing damage). At 16th level, the damage increases to 11d6.\n\nAcidic Spit"],["You're always ready to help your allies when they need you the most. You can use Communalism once per hour, rather than once per day."],["Like the ancient kucharn, you've honed your underground senses to detect faraway threats. Increase the range of your tremorsense to 120 feet."],["Your mastery of language reaches supernatural levels. You can cast Truespeech as a 5th-rank occult innate spell once per day on yourself only. You gain a +1 status bonus to Diplomacy checks for the duration of the spell when speaking to creatures with whom you already shared a language before Casting the Spell."],["You've gained precise control over where and when your chitinous exoskeleton molts. You can spend a week of downtime to retrain any other ancestry feat.\n\nIn addition, you can spend a week of downtime to permanently change your appearance. You retain a roughly similar height (within 6 inches) and weight (within 50 pounds), but your face shape, coloring, sex, and even distinctive mannerisms change to adapt to your new body type. Changing your appearance gives you a +4 circumstance bonus to Deception checks to prevent others from recognizing you. You can retrain your ancestry feat and change your appearance at the same time, even if you're using effects like Dreaming Potential."],["You've continued to advance your powers using your unconventional weapon. Whenever you gain a class feature that grants you expert or greater proficiency in certain weapons, you also gain that proficiency in the weapon you chose for Unconventional Weaponry."],["You slurp residual nutrients as you dissolve those you bite. Whenever you inflict persistent poison damage with your jaws unarmed attack, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to half your level for 1 minute.\n\nVoracious Bite (Temporary Hit Points)\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Suskillon Cutoff Shirren heritage, whenever you inflict persistent poison damage with your jaws unarmed attack, you also gain a +2 status bonus to your next Recall Knowledge check to recall information about creatures with the same trait as the target for the next minute.\n\nVoracious Bite (Recall Knowledge)"],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You're targeted by a mental effect.\n\n---\n\nYou can shield your mind by using similar techniques that your ancestors once mastered to escape the Swarm. You block the intruding effect by scattering your thoughts, making you immune to the triggering mental effect for the next minute."],["Whether gradual or in an instant burst of glorious evolution, you've metamorphosed into a powerful Swarm-like creature. You gain a +2 status bonus to saves against fear, and you gain acid resistance equal to half your level. You can cast Mask of Terror as a 7th-rank primal innate spell once per day."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou've learned to hone your psychic abilities to create a bespoke hive mind. You let out a psychic battle cry that links yourself and up to 10 allies within range of your limited telepathy into a temporary hive mind for 3 rounds, allowing them to communicate telepathically with everyone else in the hive mind.\n\nYou and the allies in your hive mind become Quickened for 3 rounds and can use the extra action only to Step, Stride, or prepare to Aid. For the duration, you and all allies in your hive mind can't be flanked. If an ally in your hive mind uses a ranged Strike against a target being flanked by two other allies in your hive mind, that target is Off-Guard to that Strike.\n\nAllies who leave the range of your limited telepathy lose all benefits of being in your hive mind as long as they remain outside of your limited telepathy."],["You have large and fearsome mandibles intended for protecting the hive. In addition, your body produces a venom that causes swelling, itching, and pain at the site of your bug bite. Your jaws unarmed attack deals 1d8 piercing damage and loses the finesse trait. Whenever you score a critical hit with your jaws unarmed attack, it deals an additional 1 persistent poison damage per weapon damage die."],["You love helping your friends and allies achieve their goals. At the start of your turn, you gain one additional reaction, which you can use only to Aid."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** An ally within 30 feet takes damage.\n\n---\n\nMany shirrens form especially empathetic bonds with their friends. You shout out to your friend when they're injured, forming a connection that shields them from pain. Your ally takes half the Hit Point damage from the triggering effect, and you take the remainder of the damage. When you take damage through this link, you don't apply any resistances, weaknesses, or other abilities you have to that damage; you simply take that amount of damage."],["Your body can partially absorb persistent damage to learn from it. Before you roll damage from a persistent effect, you can choose to take half damage from the effect. When you do, you automatically fail your flat check to end the persistent damage and you can immediately Recall Knowledge as a free action to recall information related to the source of the persistent damage. If you have any special abilities or free actions that would normally be triggered when you Recall Knowledge, you can't use them with this action."],["You've spent significant time underground, and as a result, your antennae are particularly sensitive to vibrations. You gain tremorsense as an imprecise sense with a range of 30 feet."],["Some shirrens are born with wings, but others grow them later. You evolve a pair of insectile wings that grant you a fly Speed of 20 feet. In addition, when you fall, you take no falling damage.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you're a winged shirren, you either grow a second set of wings or your existing wings morph into a stronger set of wings, increasing your fly Speed to 25 feet."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nThe chemical reaction in your body has grown more potent with time. You release a blinding burst of bioluminescence. Creatures in a 10-foot emanation around you must attempt a Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. On a failure, the creature becomes Dazzled for 1d4 rounds. On a critical failure, the creature is also Blinded for 1 round."],["The rush you get from helping your companions becomes even more intense in the heat of battle. When you successfully Aid an ally's attack, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your attack rolls until the end of your next turn.\n\nMy Friends Are My Power!"],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\nYou let out a psychic droning sound that interferes with telepathic communication. Other creatures in a 15-foot emanation around you must attempt a Will save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is Deafened and is unable to communicate telepathically for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** As success, and the creature also takes 3d8 mental damage.\n\n**Critical Failure** As success, and the creature also takes 6d8 mental damage and is Confused until the end of their next turn."],["Your psychic abilities have grown stronger. Choose one common 2nd-rank spell from the occult spell list. You can cast that spell as an occult innate spell once per day."],["**Trigger** An adjacent ally who is at least one size smaller than you would be hit by a Strike.\n\n---\n\nYou use your size and leverage to quickly move an ally out of harm's way. Attempt an Athletics check to Shove the ally targeted by the triggering Strike. If your ally is willing, treat the result as one degree of success higher. On a success, in addition to its normal effects, the Shoved ally also gains a +2 circumstance bonus to their AC against the triggering Strike.\n\nAssistive Shove"],["You combine your impressive stature and additional limbs to become a fierce wrestler. You gain the Titan Wrestler skill feat and a +1 circumstance bonus to your Fortitude DC against Grapple or Grab attempts."],["Your sure-footed nature combines with your natural height and long legs to give you an exceptionally impressive stride. Your Speed increases by 5 feet."],["You punch with brutal force akin to a club or rock. Your fist unarmed attacks don't have the nonlethal trait and gain the shove weapon trait."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You would be reduced to 0 Hit Points, but not immediately killed.\n\n---\n\nCenturies of living on a brutal and unforgiving planet has endowed many shobhad with an implacable will to survive despite debilitating injuries. You avoid being knocked out and remain at 1 Hit Point, and your Wounded condition increases by 1."],["You're well-versed in the stories of your people. You become trained in Nature and Survival. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example) you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Shobhad Lore.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the urban shobhad heritage, you also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Ysoki Lore."],["You gain access to all uncommon weapons with the shobhad trait. You have familiarity with weapons with the shobhad trait, plus the cryopike, fangblade, and hammer. For the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["**Requirements** You have at least one active hand free and are holding nothing in your other pair of hands.\n\n---\n\nYou pummel an opponent mercilessly. Make a fist Strike against an adjacent creature. If the Strike hits, you automatically Grapple the target in your inactive hands and make a second fist Strike with the following success conditions; the second Strike applies your multiple attack penalty as normal.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is Stunned 1, and Stupefied 2 for 1 round.\n\n**Success** The target is Stupefied 1 for 1 round."],["You are an implacable foe whose ability to escape death is nearly unrivaled. You can use Shobhad Ferocity once per hour, rather than once per day."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** You are wielding a ranged weapon with reload 1 or greater.\n\n---\n\nYou've learned unique techniques for wielding ranged weapons, honed through generations of experience and passed down through traditional teachings and intensive hands-on training. Strike with a ranged weapon in your active hands and then either Interact to reload that weapon or Switch Hands.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the sniper shobhad heritage and are wielding a shobhad longrifle in your active hands while holding another weapon from the sniper weapon group in your inactive pair of hands, the frequency of this feat is instead once per round."],["Shobhad-neh survive in conditions that would grind other species to exhaustion. When you would become Fatigued, attempt a DC 17 flat check. On a success, you aren't fatigued. If the fatigued condition has an underlying cause that you don't address, such as a lack of rest, you must attempt this check again at an interval determined by the GM until you fail the check or address the underlying cause."],["You use your large size and extra limbs to quickly aid your smaller allies in making room for you. Stride up to your Speed. If you end your movement in a position where one or more of your spaces are occupied by an ally, each such ally can immediately Step as a free action so that they are no longer occupying the same space as you. If this isn't possible, you must end your movement so that you aren't sharing a space with an ally, as normal."],["Calling upon your birthright as a shobhad, you channel the spirit of your ancestral home world of Akiton to encase you in a forbidding aura that causes your enemies to shy away from you in fear. Clad in the glory of the red planet, none can stand before you! You can cast Repulsion once per day as a primal innate spell. Creatures from Akiton take a –2 penalty to their Will saves against this effect."],["**Trigger** You use Shobhad Ferocity.\n\n---\n\nYou continue to battle even as you acquire mortal injuries. Make a single Strike. If this Strike brings a foe to 0 Hit Points, this activation of Shobhad Ferocity doesn't count against its frequency."],["**Requirements** You have at least one hand free and are wielding a two-handed ranged weapon that doesn't have the area trait in your inactive hands.\n\n---\n\nInvented by a talented shobhad sniper over a thousand years ago, the so-called \"shobhad special\" is a devastating maneuver that is only possible by a creature with the shobhad-neh's unique combination of size, strength, extra limbs, and cultural sniping techniques. Much to your pride, you're one of the few who have mastered it. Attempt a fist Strike against a creature at least one size smaller than you. If the attack is successful, you deal no damage but the target is immediately thrown up to 30 feet in a direction of your choice. Then, Switch Hands and make a ranged Strike against the target with the required weapon; the target is Off-Guard against this Strike. Regardless of whether this Strike is successful, the creature then falls Prone in whatever space is appropriate based on your throw.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Titan Wrestler skill feat, you can use Shobhad Special against creatures up to your size, or up to one size larger than you if you're legendary in Athletics."],["Your spiritual guardians ward you against all but the most potent of magics. You have resistance 20 against spirit damage and damage from primal spells."],["You can leverage your size and strength alongside lengthy and heavy weapons to strike foes who would normally be safe from you. While in this stance, when you wield a melee weapon that requires two hands and doesn't have reach, you can change between a typical two-handed grip and an extended two-handed grip using an Interact action. Weapons wielded in your extended two-handed grip have a reach of 10 feet."],["You have learned a technique practiced by shobhad boxers and warriors to fend off strikes from fists and blades. As long as you have at least one free hand (including an inactive hand), your fist unarmed attack gains the parry trait."],["You come from a line of shobhad spiritualists attuned to the whispers of the little spirits that encircle all things. Choose a 1st-rank divine or primal spell, either a common spell or another to which you have access. You can cast that spell once per day as an innate primal spell."],["Your unbelievable resilience allows you to survive even in the vacuum of space—at least for a while. You can hold your breath for 10 minutes. You have cold resistance equal to half your level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the glacierborn shobhad heritage, your cold resistance is instead equal to your level. If you have the offworld shobhad heritage, you additionally gain the Breath Control general feat."],["Your fists are exceptionally effective weapons. The damage die for your fist unarmed attack increases to a d6 and it gains the grapple weapon trait."],["When you bounce back from the brink of death, you experience a spike of adrenaline that allows you to ignore grievous injury. Whenever you use Shobhad Ferocity, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to your level that last for 1 minute."],["Your additional limbs make you exceptionally adept at vertical movement. You gain a climb Speed of 10 feet. If you Push Off in zero gravity while your inactive hands are not holding anything, you float up to your Speed instead of half your Speed.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the glacierborn shobhad heritage, the climb Speed granted by this feat is instead equal to half your Speed. If you have the offworld shobhad heritage, you gain a +5-foot status bonus to your Speed when you Push Off in zero gravity."],["Your bulk and dexterous limbs are incredibly useful for ensuring that you keep your smaller allies out of harm's way. You move a number of willing, adjacent creatures that are smaller than you up to 5 feet each in a direction of your choice; the number of creatures you can move is equal to the number of unoccupied hands you currently have (including your inactive pair of hands). This counts as forced movement (meaning you cannot move a target into hazardous terrain or a space they cannot occupy).\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Titan Wrestler skill feat, you can use Skilled Bodyguard to move a creature of any size."],["The spirits of the planet Akiton protect you from being harmed by the forces of the natural world. You gain a +1 status bonus to saves against primal spells."],["Your big-eyed, pleading look melts hard hearts. You gain your choice of the Charming Liar or Hobnobber skill feats, even if you don't meet the feat's prerequisites. Additionally, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to initiative rolls when you use Deception or Diplomacy for initiative."],["You have excellent control over your stomach-mouth. Your jaws unarmed attack gains the grapple trait. When you critically hit with your jaws attack, you can use your next action to attempt to Grapple that creature with your jaws or automatically extend the Grabbed condition on a creature you're restraining with your jaws. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward your multiple attack penalty."],["Everything in the world that's shiny needs a home, and everything in the world is shiny. You've found ways to create pockets in your fur, helping you to better conceal items you're liberating.\n\nYou become trained in Thievery. If you're already trained in Thievery, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain Internal Compartment as a standardized ancestry feat."],["You get a rush from extreme stunts and wild antics. You become trained in Acrobatics. If you're already trained in Acrobatics, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. Additionally, you gain the Tuck and Roll reaction."],["You're rarely discouraged or afraid. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saves against fear and to your Will DC against attempts to Demoralize you. If you get a success on a save against a fear effect, you get a critical success instead."],["You're fascinated with a particular topic, such as the religion of a small sect of worshippers, the process of spaghettification, or the songs sung by asterays. You gain the Additional Lore feat and the Assurance feat for the chosen Lore."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou've learned to take advantage of your glitter to help you disappear, rather than stand out. You vigorously shake out your fur, creating a cloud of glitter around you that moves with you and hides your exact location, granting you Concealment until the end of your next turn. You can then Step or Stride."],["Unlike others with the power of song, you like to be able to fly under the radar when you need to. You've developed a second identity in the process. You become trained in Deception. If you're already trained in Deception, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Favored Disguise skill feat, and the Skitter Idol Transformation activity."],["A good, solid hug makes everything better, and you're bringing hugs to the battlefield. You gain the Titan Wrestler skill feat. Additionally, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to Grapple and to your Fortitude DC to avoid being Grappled."],["You're full of energy, and you often bound into action faster than your friends can keep up. Your Speed increases by 5 feet."],["**Trigger** An ally is about to use an action that requires a skill check or attack roll.\n\n---\n\nYou're always willing to jump in and help, even if you don't know what you're doing. You Aid a willing ally, even if you didn't prepare to help them ahead of time. You gain a +4 circumstance bonus on your check to Aid, but after the triggering check, your ally becomes Clumsy 1 until the end of their current turn."],["You're gregarious and friendly but also passionately interested in the history of your people, going out of your way to learn traditional stories and unearth lost secrets. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Diplomacy and Society. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Skittermander Lore, and you learn Morandomandranan, the original skittermander language that has long been suppressed by the Veskarium."],["You never let the inability to communicate stop you from chatting with nufriends! You gain Speak with Animals as a 2nd-rank primal innate spell, and Speak with Plants and Translate as 3rd-rank primal innate spells. You can cast each of these primal innate spells once per day."],["Your absolute dedication to your friends lets you call upon some galactic power to keep them safe in their darkest hour. You can cast Breath of Life as a 5th-rank divine innate spell once per day; however, you only restore 5 healing Hit Points instead of 5d8."],["The pockets you've created in your fur have strengthened, and you love finding ways to hold more choices for your friends in them. You gain the Prescient Planner general feat. You can use Prescient Planner as a 2-action activity once per day, and you can procure ammunition and batteries in addition to the usual items available. These items must meet the usual level, Bulk, and other requirements, and you must still pay the Price of the chosen item."],["**Trigger** A creature critically fails a melee Strike against you.\n\n**Requirements** The triggering creature is within your reach, you have at least one free active hand, and your target is no more than one size larger than you.\n\n---\n\nYou seize the opportunity to give your foe a big hug to help them feel better or calm down. You attempt an Athletics check to Grapple the triggering creature.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Titan Wrestler skill feat, you can use Opportunistic Hug against creatures up to two sizes larger than you, or up to three sizes larger than you if you're legendary in Athletics."],["You move incredibly fast, becoming a colorful blur of erratic motion. When you Stride while Quickened from Zoomies, you gain concealment until the start of your next turn. As usual for concealment involving an obvious visual manifestation, you can't use this concealment to Hide."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** You aren't holding any items except in your active hands.\n\n---\n\nYou put forth your best effort and focus everything you've got on the task at hand, putting allsix of your hands (three of your sets of arms) into it! The next time you roll an attack roll or skill check, roll it three times and use the highest result."],["Your wells of energy are unending, and your exuberance can't be contained. You can use Zoomies once every hour, rather than once per day."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYour boundless enthusiasm is infectious, and you can share some of that energy and can-do attitude with your allies. You and all allies within 60 feet gain a +10-foot status bonus to Speed and the Quickened condition for 4 rounds. Creatures can use the extra action each round only to Stride.\n\nLet's Go\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Supersonic Speed feat, you and each ally gain Concealment until the start of their next turn if they Stride while quickened from Let's Go. As usual for concealment involving an obvious visual manifestation, you can't use this concealment to Hide."],["Traveling across the galaxy, you've formed a tight bond with your found family, absorbing some of their culture now as your own. You gain the Adopted Ancestry general feat, and you also gain one 1st-level ancestry feat from the ancestry you chose for the Adopted Ancestry feat."],["You've learned how to further use your beloved glitter to your advantage, shaking it off at the right moment to helpfully share it with enemies. When you successfully [[/act feint]] a creature, it becomes Dazzled until the end of your turn. If you critically succeed, the creature is dazzled until the start of your next turn. The creature can use an Interact action to remove the dazzled condition."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nIn the blink of an eye, you ready yourself to help your ally with a task. This counts as preparing to help an ally for the purposes of using the Aid reaction. You must still explain to the GM exactly how you're helping."],["**Requirements** You have a creature Grabbed with your jaws.\n\n---\n\nHaving two mouths to feed is said to take more energy, and you're no exception. You make a jaws Strike against the grabbed creature. On a hit, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to half your level for 1 minute.\n\nLatch On"],["You're a master improviser with a bit of talent at everything—even if you have no idea what you're doing. You gain the Untrained Improvisation general feat. In addition, you gain the Beginner's Luck action."],["You're overeager to get to grips with your foes (or just give an ally an unexpected big hug). You Step and attempt an Athletics check to [[/act grapple]] a creature."],["Years of playing skitterspree trained you for a special move. You curl up into a tightly wound ball, and an adjacent ally with a free hand that's at least one size larger than you can use a reaction to attempt a ranged Strike with your body as an unarmed attack that deals 1d10 bludgeoning damage for the duration of the Strike. This unarmed attack is in the brawling weapon group and has the agile, analog, brutal, and thrown (20 feet) traits. This unarmed attack gains the benefits of your worn hardlight handwraps. You land adjacent to the target, but you land Prone if the Strike is a critical failure.\n\nCannonball"],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou fall utterly silent and focus strenuously on a problem at hand. You attempt to Recall Knowledge with a +2 circumstance bonus to the skill check. If you would get a critical failure, you get a failure instead, and if you would get a success, you get a critical success instead."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** You must have at least three allies within 30 feet who you can communicate with.\n\n---\n\nYour body physically heals when you can communicate with your allies. You can choose if your communication with allies is auditory or visual, and this action gains that trait when used. You gain fast healing equal to half your level for 1 minute. While Restorative Chatter is active, if you no longer meet the requirements, this fast healing ends."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Requirements** Your last action was a successful Strike with your stomach-mouth jaws unarmed attack.\n\n---\n\nYour stomach-mouth secretes numbing saliva into your target, exposing them to the poison.\n\n**Numbing Saliva** (injury, poison)\n\n**Saving Throw** Fortitude (the higher of your class or spell DC)\n\n**Maximum Duration** 6 rounds\n\n**Stage 1** Clumsy 1 (1 round)\n\n**Stage 2** clumsy 1 and Suppressed (1 round)\n\n**Stage 3** Clumsy 2 and suppressed (1 round)"],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou unleash your pent up energy in a flurry of unpredictable motion. You gain the Quickened condition for 4 rounds. You can use the extra action each round only to Stride."],["You've incorporated a charging station into your frame, enabling you to recharge spent batteries with your own body. In addition, you can cast the Recharge Weapon cantrip as an arcane innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["You've adjusted your frame to fit into tight spaces and contort impressively. You gain the Quick Squeeze and Nimble Crawl skill feats (even if you don't meet the prerequisites)."],["**Trigger** You attempt a saving throw against a mental effect, but you haven't rolled yet.\n\n---\n\nYou clutch a memento from your past life—the time before you gained self-awareness and awakened as yourself—and you use it to fuel your defiance in the face of injustice, bolster your confidence in times of self-doubt, and remind you of the miracle of your independence. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saves against mental effects until the beginning of your next turn. This bonus also applies to the triggering save."],["You've installed tiny thrusters and vents into your frame that enable you to hover a few inches above the ground, avoiding the dirt and grime below. Your land Speed gains the hover trait. In addition, you gain the Overload Thrusters action."],["Your mechanical body resists ailments better than other living creatures. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against diseases, poisons, and radiation."],["You gain a shortwave radio transmitter, allowing you to communicate wirelessly with any creatures within 30 feet, as long as they have shortwave or are a construct with the tech trait. This doesn't give any special access to their thoughts or programming and communicates no more information than normal speech would."],["You have heavy duty treads, wheels, or appendages that make it easy for you to navigate uneven surfaces. You ignore difficult terrain caused by plants, stone, and trash and uneven ground made of earth, plants, stone, and trash."],["You've installed advanced optical sensors into your frame, calibrated to function in suboptimal lighting conditions. You gain low-light vision.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat a second time. When you do, you gain darkvision."],["Like many SROs, you value the miracle of life and believe all creations are worthy of respect. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Crafting and Nature. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for SRO Lore."],["Your face—if you have one—emotes differently than most creatures, making it hard for others to read your intentions and emotions. You become trained in Deception. In addition, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Deception checks to [[/act create-a-diversion]] and Lie. If you would automatically become trained in Deception (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice."],["Your body has an integrated weapon mount that can hold a one-handed weapon. You can install or uninstall a weapon into this weapon mount using the Install Upgrade activity. You're always wielding a weapon installed in your weapon mount. An installed weapon can't be disarmed, dropped, or stolen.\n\nChoose one common commercial simple weapon you can install on your weapon mount. You begin with this weapon already installed in your weapon mount. You don't need to pay the credits to purchase this starting weapon, but you do need to purchase any ammo it requires.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the combatant SRO heritage, you can instead install a one-handed martial weapon or a two-handed weapon in your weapon mount."],["You have a reinforced chassis to protect your frame from harm without interfering with your movements or increasing your size. During your daily preparations, you can apply a specially formulated coating and additional reinforcement to your outer chassis. This coating grants you Hardness equal to half your level rounded up. The first time each day you're damaged by a critical hit or reduced to half your Hit Points or less, this coating wears off, and you lose the Hardness granted by this feat until your next daily preparations."],["You've got a way with machines, so you can communicate even with those that lack self-awareness as if they were an old friend. You can cast Speak with Computers once per day as a 4th-rank arcane innate spell."],["**Trigger** You gain the Confused, controlled, Fascinated, frightened, or stupefied condition.\n\n---\n\nYou've created a virtual sandbox, a digital clone of your mental programming that contains all your memories and other aspects of your mind except your consciousness. Attempt a DC 15 flat check. On a success or critical success, you isolate and shunt the condition into your virtual sandbox and don't gain the condition, but you become immune to Virtual Sandbox for 10 minutes."],["A spark in your evolving consciousness allows you to create a backup of your awakened mind and body. Once per day, you can cast Akashic Revival as an 8th-rank occult innate spell."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou emit a powerful EMP in a 30-foot-radius emanation. Each tech creature, hazard, and item in the area must attempt a Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. You, your allies, your equipment, and your allies' equipment are unharmed by this EMP.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target becomes Glitching 1.\n\n**Failure** The target becomes Glitching 2.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target becomes Glitching 3."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nConfident in your sense of self to the point of recklessness, you send extra power to your healing circuits, pushing them to their limits. For 1 minute, you gain fast healing 10. In addition, the first time during the duration that a source would restore a variable number of Hit Points to you, it restores the maximum number of Hit Points possible."],["You've integrated a variety of clamps, pitons, and other climbing equipment into your frame that allow you to scale sheer surfaces. You gain a climb Speed of 20 feet."],["You've installed a powerful electromagnet in your frame that you can use to move and manipulate items from afar. You can move 1 unattended object of 1 Bulk or less that has the tech trait or is made from metal within 30 feet to anywhere within 30 feet as a single action with the concentrate trait.\n\nIn addition, if you attempt to [[/act disarm]] an item with the tech trait or that's made of metal, you don't need to have a hand free, and you can attempt to Disarm at a range of 30 feet.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the combatant SRO or worker SRO heritage, the range at which you can move such objects and Disarm such objects increases to 60 feet."],["You're adept at producing and using nanites to treat a variety of medical conditions. You gain the Inject Nanites action.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the medic SRO heritage, you can Inject Nanites once per 10 minutes."],["Your body's frame is highly reconfigurable, allowing for additional augmentations. You can Implant Augmentation on yourself in 10 minutes using a medkit or repair toolkit. In addition, increase your augmentation implant limit by 1.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once, increasing your augmentation implant limit by 1 each time you do."],["You can leverage your size to extend your reach. When you wield a melee weapon that requires two hands and doesn't have reach, you can change between a typical two-handed grip and an extended two-handed stretch using an Interact action. Weapons wielded in your extended two-handed stretch gain a reach of 10 feet."],["You've installed a complex system of liquid cooling tubes and thermal insulators throughout your frame to ensure your sensitive internal components maintain a consistent temperature, in addition to sensors that constantly adjust these components to keep you safe. You gain resistance to fire and cold equal to half your level."],["**Requirements** Your last action was a successful Strike against a tech creature, hazard, or item. You transmit a virus that hampers the operation of the required target. The target must attempt a Fortitude against the higher of your class DC or spell DC with the following results.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected and becomes temporarily immune to Transmit Virus for 1 hour.\n\n**Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The target becomes Glitching 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target becomes Glitching 2."],["To increase your odds of survival, you've installed visual sensors that provide a 360-degree view of your surroundings. You aren't Off-Guard to creatures that are flanking you."],["You've installed powerful jet thrusters into your frame, granting you the ability to fly. You gain a fly Speed equal to your Speed.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Hoverbot feat, when you Overload Thrusters, you gain a fly Speed equal to twice your land Speed, and your thrusters don't deactivate."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n**Requirements** You're adjacent to a creature, hazard, or item that has the glitching condition.\n\n---\n\nYou know how to manipulate errors in high-tech programming and complex machinery, enhancing or mitigating the resulting glitches. You can either increase or reduce the value of the required target's glitching condition by 1.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the repair SRO heritage, you can use Manipulate Glitch on a target up to 30 feet away."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You take electricity damage.\n\n---\n\nYou convert some of the excess electricity surging through your systems into kinetic energy by accelerating your internal motors and processors to handle the expedited movements. You become Quickened for 2 rounds. You can use the extra action each round only to Stride."],["Choose one cantrip from your ancestry's magic entry. You can cast that cantrip at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up. This spell has the same tradition as listed in the feat entry.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have multiple cantrips listed for your ancestry, you can select this feat more than once. If you do, you must select a different spell.\n\n*Note: For a list of cantrips for your ancestry, see the Ancestries journal page for your ancestry.*"],["You gain darkvision."],["You have a keen interest in the origins of your people. You become trained in the skills listed in your ancestry's skills entry. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for the Lore skill associated with your ancestry (for example, androids have Android Lore and ysoki have Ysoki Lore)."],["You gain the unarmed attack listed for your ancestry. At your GM's discretion, you can select one of the alternate unarmed attack options listed in the Less Standard Unarmed Attacks sidebar.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you land a critical hit with one of these attacks, you can add its critical specialization effect.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have multiple attacks listed for your ancestry, you can take this feat up to the number of attacks listed for your ancestry. Each time you do, select a different attack."],["You gain access to all uncommon weapons with your ancestry trait. You have familiarity with weapons with your ancestry trait and with ancestral weapons. For the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you land a critical hit with one of these weapons, you can add its critical specialization effect."],["**Frequency** once per minute\n\n---\n\nYou Fly. If you don't have a fly Speed, you gain a fly Speed equal to your ancestry's Flight Specialist entry for this action. If you aren't on solid ground at the end of this movement, you fall."],["You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill when interacting with creatures related to the listed creature. In cases where this definition is ambiguous, such as when trying to speak to a \"bearlike\" creature instead of a typical bear, the GM determines which creatures count for this ability."],["Whether through training or innate talent, you've expanded the range at which you can telepathically communicate. Increase the range of your limited telepathy by 15 feet.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once."],["Your natural senses improve with careful practice or through the use of specific techniques. Increase the range of one of your senses by 10 feet if it's a precise sense or by 30 feet if it's an imprecise sense."],["You gain two additional languages of your choice, selected from among the common and uncommon languages available to you. Every time you take the Multilingual feat, you gain another new language in addition to the two you gain from that feat."],["Whether by natural appendages or some personal modification, you can swim. You gain a swim Speed equal to your ancestry's Swimming Specialist entry."],["You've familiarized yourself with a particular weapon, potentially from another ancestry or culture. Choose an uncommon simple or martial weapon with a trait corresponding to an ancestry (such as vesk) or that is common in another culture (including a deity's favored weapon). You gain access to and familiarity with that weapon. For the purposes of proficiency, you treat a martial weapon as a simple weapon.\n\nIf you are trained in martial weapons or guns, you can choose an advanced weapon. You gain access to that weapon, and for the purpose of determining your proficiency, that weapon is a martial weapon."],["Choose one common 5th-rank or lower spell with the summon trait. Once per day, you can Cast this Spell as a 5th-rank innate spell, but the creature summoned must be one of the creatures listed in your ancestry's creature entry. This spell has the same tradition as listed in the feat entry."],["Your ancestry has grown alongside a favored creature, and you can tap into that bond to transform. When you gain this feat, choose a common polymorph spell with a battle form that matches your ancestry's creature entry; you can't change the form after making your choice. You can cast that spell as an 8th-rank innate spell once per day, except you must transform only into a battle form that matches your ancestral creature. Your form uses your normal AC if it's higher than what is granted by the battle form. If your ancestral creature isn't among the forms listed, you default to the statistics and abilities of the battle form that is closest to your creature at the GM's discretion. This spell has the same tradition as is listed in the feat entry.\n\nIf you have the Ancestral Pest feat, you can choose to gain the effects of a 4th-level Pest Form."],["Your ancestry has a powerful connection to one or more magical traditions.\n\nChoose one 1st-rank spell from your ancestry's magic entry. You can cast that spell as an innate spell once per day as a 1st-rank spell. If this is your 9th level ancestry feat, choose a 3rd-rank or lower ancestry spell as a 3rd-rank innate spell. If this is your 13th level ancestry feat, choose a 5th-rank or lower ancestry spell as a 5th-rank innate spell. If this is your 17th level ancestry feat, choose a 7th-rank or lower ancestry spell as a 7th-rank innate spell. This spell has the same tradition that is listed in the feat entry.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have multiple spells listed for your ancestry, you can select this feat more than once. If you do, you must select a different spell."],["You assume the form of a tiny animal, gaining the effect of a 1st-rank Pest Form, except you can transform only into a creature that matches the listed entry, and you can use your normal base Speed if it's higher than what the battle form grants. If the listed creature is normally larger than Tiny, you transform into a smaller, younger version of the animal. If the listed creature usually has a swim Speed, Ancestral Pest grants you a swim Speed of 20 feet."],["Whether by natural appendages or by some personal modification, you can climb. You gain a climb Speed equal to your ancestry's Climbing Specialist entry."],["Using your multiple sets of hands, you can quickly adjust your equipment. You Interact to draw, stow, or swap items you have up to twice."],["You are proud to serve as a mount for your trusted allies. This might be a natural development, or it might be the result of intense training to ensure you can operate as a mount for your allies.\n\nWhen another PC rides you as a mount, your expert coordination allows them to gain three actions at the start of their turn rather than the two they normally would for riding another PC. You still gain only two actions at the start of your turn instead of three, however, as you spend the third action keeping your ally balanced on your back and ensuring they're firmly mounted."],["One of your tails or tendrils functions like an extra hand and is capable of performing some precision tasks. You can hold one extra hand's worth of equipment with your prehensile limb, and you can use your prehensile limb to perform Interact actions. Your prehensile limb can be paired with another hand when you designate your active hands with the Switch Hands action, and you can wield a shield or weapon in your prehensile limb when it's one of your active hands."],["Your skill at flying allows you to do it as easily as other species might walk. Whenever you Stride, you can Fly or use Basic Flight instead."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou're able to focus on your coordination for a moment. Until the beginning of your next turn, you count up to one additional pair of hands as your active hands. At the beginning of your next turn, choose which set of active hands remains your active hands."],["Your ancestry provides you some level of natural defense against specific types of damage. You gain resistance to the damage type listed by your ancestry's resistance entry equal to half your level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have multiple damage types listed, you can take this feat multiple times. Each time you do so, select a different damage type."],["Whether by natural appendages or through some personal modification, you can burrow. You gain a burrow Speed equal to your ancestry's Burrowing Specialist entry."],["Whether by natural appendages or through some personal modification, you can fly. You gain a fly Speed equal to your ancestry's Flight Specialist entry."],["For as long as you are Small or smaller, you can end your movement in the same square as a Small or smaller ally. Only two creatures total can share the same space when using this ability or a similar one."],["Your work emphasizes the skilled manual dexterity and attention to detail required to create beautiful works of artistry. You gain the Specialty Crafting feat of your choice. Additionally, your background in artistry has left you with a keen eye for aesthetics that can often make your work more valuable to collectors. When you roll a critical success on Crafting to Earn Income, you gain the amount of currency listed for the task level + 2 and your proficiency rank."],["Nearly all talphis decorate themselves with swirling, glowing patterns to identify themselves in the dark, and because it looks nice, but you take it to another level by truly immersing yourself in the luminescent art form. You cover yourself and your armor with enough glowing patterns to emit dim light within 15 feet of you. While you emit light, you also gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Performance checks to [[/act perform]]. You can cover or uncover the light with an Interact action."],["One talphi saying states that life is better in motion, and many talphis are better in motion as well; it takes you a second to get up to speed, but your body is built to capitalize on the momentum you generate. The more you move, the faster you go. Your Speed increases by 5 feet until the beginning of your next turn after each action you spend to Stride.\n\nHead of Steam"],["**Trigger** You would take persistent bleed damage.\n\n---\n\nThe unique anatomy of talphis, wherein your loose skin hides your neck and extends to your elbows and knees, makes your body look much larger than it actually is and has plenty of give to resist more serious damage. When you're struck by an attack that would do persistent bleed damage, roll a DC 10 flat check. On a success, you steer the blow into a relatively safe part of your body, and the condition ends immediately."],["Your deep connection to the earth allows you to shape it to your own purposes, sometimes without even using your hands. You seek out particles of dust and stone around you and draw them to yourself, creating a calcified shield of stone around your limbs. This counts as using the Raise a Shield action, giving you a +1 circumstance bonus to AC until the start of your next turn, but it doesn't require a hand to use.\n\nWhile the mineral shield is in effect, you can use the Shield Block reaction with your mineral shield and can use it to reduce damage only from effects that deal electricity or fire damage. This shield has Hardness 5, but if used underground or in a foundry or junkyard where scraps of metal are plentiful, the shield gains resistance 5 to electricity and fire. After you use Shield Block, the effect ends.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can improve your shield by applying shield improvements to a small stone trinket with negligible Bulk that you must be wearing when you use Mineral Shield."],["Let's face it—you're not scaring anyone; many find something inherently disarming about small, low-slung, cheerful talphis, and you're prepared to take full advantage of it. You gain the Charming Liar skill feat as a bonus feat. Additionally, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Deception checks for initiative."],["You pass through earth and stone almost as easily as air. It's no longer a matter of digging, but rather becoming one with the ground and allowing it to carry you to your destination. When you Burrow, you can choose whether or not you leave behind a tunnel. If you choose to leave a tunnel, creatures one size larger than you or smaller can use the hole, but creatures one size larger than you have to Squeeze. If you don't leave a tunnel, you can [[/act sneak]] while Burrowing at your full movement speed."],["Infused with primal magic, you can use your glowing pigment to dazzle your enemies in a spray of glittering paint. You can cast revealing light as a 2nd-rank primal innate spell. You can't use Revealing Light again until you spend 1 hour to forage for new pigments. It takes only 10 minutes to find these pigments if you're in an environment with a plethora of minerals appropriate for your paint, such as an underground cave or a vehicle paint and auto body shop."],["You use the power of the world's core to move through the earth and Strike your foe. You gain the Drill Rush action and can use Channel the World's Core with a frequency of once per minute, rather than once per day."],["You've achieved a full connection with the spirit of the rock, and the minerals meld with your body to aid you the moment you call. You can cast Enlarge once per hour as a 4th-rank primal innate spell targeting only yourself. When you do, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to your level for as long as the spell is in effect.\n\nOne with the Stone"],["You've learned how to fight enemies without leaving the safety of your tunnels. Your tremorsense provided by Tunnel Vision becomes a precise sense. While underground, you can target enemies you detect using tremorsense with Strikes, Area Fire, and Auto-Fire as long as the only material between you and the enemy is something you could normally move through using your burrow Speed. Unless you use adamantine ammunition, ranged attacks made through solid ground have their range increments halved, and you take a –2 circumstance penalty to your attack roll for ranged attacks that pass through the ground."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou call upon the spinning and beating hearts of every planet you've ever visited and share their true power with your enemies, unleashing a blast of superdense, red-hot iron shards. Each creature in a 30-foot cone takes 14d6 piercing damage and 4d6 persistent fire damage with a basic Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. A creature that fails its save becomes suppressed until the end of your next turn. If you and your targets are in an underground environment, they don't get a bonus to their Reflex saves from standard cover against World Shards but still gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Reflex saves if they have greater cover."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nMany talphi philosophers have studied the forces underlying the universe for countless generations, finding ways to link their minds to primordial forces much like solarians. You can steady your body and mind to attune yourself to the ultradense core of your home planet, channeling the pressure and density of its core through your weapon. Add 1d4 bludgeoning damage per weapon damage die to the next attack you make with your weapon before the end of your next turn. On a critical hit, roll these damage die after doubling the weapon's damage."],["Nothing can stop a talphi who doesn't want to be stopped. If you Stride immediately before attempting to [[/act tumble-through]] an enemy's space, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the attempt. If you critically succeed, your enemy's space isn't considered difficult terrain."],["The body of a talphi is small to begin with, and most of what's there is empty space. You learn to manipulate your joints a bit, finding a little extra flexibility here and there, and you can push your way through almost any space without difficulty. You gain the Quick Squeeze feat. Tight spaces not tight enough to require the Squeeze action aren't difficult terrain for you."],["You have spent enough time in tunnels to have grown in tune with the vibrations of the earth, and you can sense when something disturbs its natural rhythm. You gain tremorsense as an imprecise sense with a range of 30 feet."],["You've expanded your planetary link and can reach out to a variety of planets. When you use Channel the World's Core the dice added to your next attack can be cold, electricity, fire, poison, or void damage instead of bludgeoning. The Strike gains the radiation trait if you choose poison."],["You open your mind to the whispers of the land and learn its secrets. You can cast Speak with Stones once per day as a 5th-rank primal innate spell. Additionally, you can use Nature to [[/act track skill=nature]] and [[/act seek skill=nature]] instead of Survival and Perception. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus when you use Nature to Track and Seek in an environment with natural or worked stone floors."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nUsing readily available materials, you create pieces of art to inspire those who have inspired you. Choose an ally. You spend 1 hour to Craft a gift of negligible Bulk or larger with the consumable and primal traits, decorated with the talphis' signature glowing paint. As long as the chosen ally wears this gift, they can draw inspiration from it as an Interact action to gain a +1 status bonus to their next attack roll, Perception check, saving throw, or skill check until the start of their next turn and gain temporary Hit Points equal to your Charisma modifier + character level that last for 1 minute. The glow from your gift fades after 24 hours as it crumbles to dust.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you're legendary in Crafting, you can make up to five tokens per day, but each must be made for a different ally."],["Scrambling through tunnels beneath the rocky surface of Nchak can be difficult when you're a 12-foot-tall arthropod with thick, armored plates covering most of your body, but they say practice makes perfect. You've spent enough time squeezing yourself through tunnels that your exoskeleton has grown accustomed to bending and deforming to fit in tight spaces, and by now, it hardly slows you down at all. You become trained in Acrobatics. If you would automatically become trained in Acrobatics (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Quick Squeeze feat."],["Your vestigial hands might lack in strength, but they make up for it in subtlety. You can manipulate objects with your smaller middle limbs while pretending to be otherwise occupied, drawing attention away from your clandestine activities. You gain the Subtle Theft feat. As long as your primary hands are holding or wielding items other than an infiltrator's toolkit, the circumstance penalty to notice your misdeeds extends to attempts to [[/act disarm]] a Device or Pick a Lock."],["**Trigger** You would be hit by a ranged attack.\n\n---\n\nWhen the shooting starts, everyone envies the one with the armored shell on their back. You Drop Prone, hiding beneath the thickest parts of your exoskeleton to avoid some of the damage. You gain resistance to physical damage equal to half your level (minimum 1) while you're Prone this way."],["You've studied under some of the foremost Hylaxian scholars in the galaxy deep in the Forever Halls, or another center of worship, to gain a greater understanding of the Forever Queen's teachings. You carry the evidence of those studies with you in the form of a religious symbol, relic of your faith, or other meaningful memento. You become trained in Religion. If you would automatically become trained in Religion (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Student of the Canon feat."],["It's not your fault being the biggest and the strongest. When fighting is inevitable, you've learned to use your superior bulk to grab and restrain smaller enemies. If nothing else, a foe in your grasp is less likely to harm your allies. Your powerful upper limbs have had plenty of practice wrestling, grabbing, and restraining smaller foes. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus on Athletics checks to [[/act grapple]] foes that are at least one size category smaller than you."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n**Requirements** You're taking persistent bleed damage.\n\n---\n\nWhen you're bleeding, you can strategically realign your chitinous plates to apply pressure, staunch your wounds, and improve your chances of stopping the bleeding altogether. Attempt a flat check to recover from the persistent bleed damage. The DC of this check is 10 instead of 15. Even if you fail, the DC of the recovery check to stop the bleeding at the end of your turn is reduced to 10 this round as well."],["You're well versed in using the subtle art of body language to convey the basics of your intentions, even when you don't share a language with whom you're attempting to communicate. You can use Diplomacy to [[/act make-an-impression]] without a shared language with your target. When you do, Make an Impression loses the auditory and linguistic traits, and you can attempt the Diplomacy check with a –2 circumstance penalty. When you do share at least one language with your target, you instead gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Make an Impression."],["Some threats go beyond the physical, and your chitin can adapt to protect you from them. You gain resistance to acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic damage equal to half your level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat multiple times. Each time you do so, select a different damage type."],["The more time you spend in combat, the more threats you see to your allies and the harder you work to protect your chosen family. Though it can be difficult to channel your fervor, you've found the strength to call upon it more and more. You can use Frenzy with a frequency of once per hour, rather than once per day. When you enter a frenzy, the status bonus to attack rolls also applies to damage, but the penalty to AC increases to –3."],["No matter the dangers posed to your person, you've always prioritized the safety of your allies over your own wellbeing. Whenever you Raise a Shield or position a weapon with the parry trait defensively, you can choose to increase the AC of up to two adjacent allies instead of your own. If you have the Stretching Reach feat, increase the effective range of your protection by 5 feet. As long as the selected allies remain within your reach and your shield is raised, they gain the circumstance bonus to AC from your shield or weapon, while you take a –1 circumstance penalty to AC while concentrating on the defense of those around you.\n\nProtective Bulk\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Shield Block feat, during this time, you can trigger Shield Block when you have your shield raised and one of the selected allies would take damage from a physical attack, but you can't use Shield Block to protect yourself."],["Hylax's favor flows through you, and you can feel her calling out, offering you a gift. You spend 24 hours in prayer deep underground, under intense environmental pressure. The power of Hylax flows into your exoskeleton, thickening the plates, strengthening the flesh beneath them, and providing you with the ultimate protection. You gain resistance to all physical damage (except adamantine) equal to one quarter your level (minimum 1)."],["You've trained your vestigial limbs for combat, and once you have control of an enemy with your larger and more powerful limbs, the smaller, sneakier ones go to work. You're permanently Quickened. You can this extra action only to [[/act disarm]], [[/act grapple]]{grab}, or [[/act trip]] a creature."],["Hylax teaches peace, even when bloodshed seems inevitable in a given situation, and that diffusing a fight is always worth a try. Before you reach the point of no return, you make one last overture to your foe using all the wisdom that you've learned from the elders, your religion, or your family. You gain the Legendary Negotiation feat even if you don't meet the feat's prerequisites. If you are in combat and haven't struck the opponent you're attempting to negotiate with, the penalty to your Diplomacy check is reduced to –2."],["**Requirements** You can observe at least one enemy and are wielding a shield.\n\n**Trigger** You roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou've had enough experience in battle to recognize when one is about to start, and though you're rarely the first to attack, you're always on guard. You Raise a Shield."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** An ally you can see was damaged by an enemy since the end of your last turn.\n\n---\n\nWith little regard for your own safety, you fly into a frenzy to protect those you care about, gaining a +2 status bonus to melee attack rolls and a –2 status penalty to AC for 1 minute."],["Even among your kind, you possess a powerful build with broad shoulders and overlapping chitinous plates that makes your anatomy well suited to carrying heavy loads. Increase your maximum carried Bulk and the amount of Bulk you can carry before becoming encumbered by 2. When you're encumbered, reduce the penalty to your Speeds by 5 feet."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail a Fortitude or Reflex saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYour chitin can shift and overlap in unpredictable ways, protecting you when you're unable to protect yourself. You can reroll the triggering saving throw, using the second result even if it's worse."],["Even with eyes that can see through the thickest darkness, you know some threats remain invisible. You've learned to listen to the ground beneath your feet, feeling the subtle shifts in vibrations as they run up your legs and interpreting them with lightning speed. You gain tremorsense as an imprecise sense with a range of 30 feet."],["Countless generations of specialization have stripped your two pairs of vestigial arms of much of their strength, but you've trained them to gain enough strength to be useful in combat. Though they aren't strong or agile enough to grab an opponent, you can use them to maintain a grip you already have. When you successfully grapple a creature that's at least one size smaller than you, you can transfer the foe to your vestigial arms as a free action, freeing your primary hands. You have a –2 circumstance penalty to the Escape DC for your grapple against creatures you have Grabbed in your vestigial arms."],["A lifetime living in a chitinous exoskeleton has given you rare insight on how to maneuver when wearing different types of armor, and your expertise only grows each time you shed and form an exoskeleton anew. You become trained in light armor and gain the armor specialization effect of light armor. If you're trained in medium or heavy armor, you gain the respective armor specialization effect of those armors as well."],["You grab hold of your foe with your powerful primary limbs, temporarily distracting them. If you critically succeed your check to [[/act grapple]] an enemy, you can attempt to [[/act steal]] something from the enemy as a free action. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Thievery check to Steal, as your grapple makes it difficult for your foe to keep track of your vestigial arms. You can Steal any immediately accessible item of light Bulk or less on the enemy's person, such as a holstered weapon or a serum hanging from a belt, but not anything inside a container or anything the enemy is holding. The GM makes the final determination on what you can Steal in this way."],["Your chitinous plates have thickened in response to heavy punishment. Every bit of scar tissue that forms on your plates and every healed fracture have built your natural defenses into a protective layer that's truly a sight to behold. Your exoskeleton becomes heavy armor, and your proficiency in your exoskeleton armor becomes equal to your proficiency in medium armor. Your armor now grants a +5 item bonus to AC, has a +1 Dex cap, a check penalty of –2, a –10-foot penalty to Speed, and a Strength threshold of +3. It has a Bulk of 3 and the bulwark, comfort, and exposed traits. It's in the plate armor group. You can wear flight suits, but no other armor."],["You've studied music and color theory; you understand the necessary function of art while removing any ambiguous subtext, metaphor, and even the very soul that makes it art. You can use Society in place of Performance when you use the [[/act perform skill=society]] action and Earn Income downtime activity. You can Create Forgery to replicate digital works of art (such as pictures, movies, and songs)."],["You shift your crystalline plates to curl up into a ball as a defensive posture. While you're in Conglobation, you gain a +4 circumstance bonus to AC and are Immobilized. You're in Conglobation until you Interact to return to your usual posture."],["A basic understanding of related topics has made you a better practitioner of your craft. You become trained in two Intelligence- or Wisdom-based skills of your choice."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou siphon off a few extra electrons you weren't using to empower your weapon. You can cast Supercharge Weapon as a 1st-rank arcane innate spell once per day, except the additional damage is electricity instead of being the same damage type of the weapon. Casting this spell in this way also fully charges the weapon's battery if it has one."],["You use your knowledge about a creature to focus your attacks. Choose a creature within 30 feet of you that you're aware of. Attempt a Recall Knowledge check against that target, following the standard rules for Recall Knowledge with the following additional effect.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** You understand the exact timing and location to strike your opponent. The target is Off-Guard against all attacks that you attempt against it until the end of your next turn.\n\n**Success** The target is off-guard against the next attack that you attempt against it before the end of your current turn."],["By recalculating variables like traffic, weather, and attacks from giant space tardigrades, you can determine the best way to get from here to there, and you might even wildly claim to be able to get there in a shorter distance than it actually is. When you succeed at a Piloting check to [[/act navigate]], you critically succeed instead. If you critically fail a Piloting check to [[/act plot-course]], you fail instead."],["Sometimes, the subtlety of sarcasm and innuendo is lost on you. You respond better to direct communication. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saves against mental effects. If you roll a success on a saving throw against a mental effect, you get a critical success instead. If you roll a failure to [[/act coerce]] or Influence a creature, you get a critical failure instead."],["You spew information about a topic you're passionate about that no one asked for. Choose a creature within 30 feet of you that you're aware of. Attempt a Lore check against that target's Will DC. Regardless of your result, the creature is temporarily immune to your attempts to Knowledge Bomb it for 10 minutes.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature becomes Stupefied 2 for 1 round.\n\n**Success** The creature becomes Stupefied 1 for 1 round."],["Through thousands of hours spent mastering a craft and hundreds of iterations on the process, you're able to consistently deliver quality results with minimal waste. When Crafting during downtime, if you critically fail a check, you fail instead, and when you succeed, you critically succeed instead."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You take electricity damage.\n\n---\n\nWhat electrocutes other species, you instead consider an energizing snack. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to half your level or your electricity resistance, whichever is greater. These temporary Hit Points last for 1 minute."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYour cilia help you to consume slowly even as they absorb nutrients, drawing out some extra potency from alchemical items. When you consume an alchemical item that has a duration of 1 minute or longer, that item's duration is doubled."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** An ally that you can hear and can hear you fails a skill check.\n\n---\n\nYou chime in at the last minute with a bit of helpful and, more importantly, accurate information. You use the Aid action. If you succeed, you can retroactively add the circumstance bonus to the check. This might change the outcome of the check."],["Time is precious and not to be wasted, and your mastery of efficiency allows you to shave seconds off even the most mundane tasks. You become Quickened until the end of your turn."],["Your cilia have become even more sensitive to detecting electric signatures of nearby creatures. Your electromagnetic sense becomes a precise sense with a range of 15 feet and an imprecise sense with a range of 60 feet."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nEducation is a powerful weapon—and so are guns; fortunately, you wield both to devastating effect. Attempt a Recall Knowledge check against a target you're aware of within 30 feet. You can use this result in place of your next attack roll. If you critically fail the Recall Knowledge check, you are overcome with analysis paralysis and become Stunned 2."],["You're confident in your knowledge and undeterred by those who would have you believe otherwise. Anytime you gain the Stupefied condition, reduce its value by 1. This doesn't reduce the stupefied condition if the value would be reduced to 0."],["**Trigger** An adjacent creature hits you with a Strike.\n\n---\n\nYou channel your inner battery into a retaliatory discharge. You deal electricity damage equal to half your level or your electricity resistance, whichever is greater, to the triggering creature."],["Your cilia are sensitive to detecting electric signatures of nearby creatures. You gain electromagnetic sense as an imprecise sense with a range of 15 feet. Electromagnetic sense allows you to detect nearby creatures and technological objects, but you might have to use the [[/act seek]] action to find an undetected creature in an environment with too much electromagnetic radiation, such as inside the engine room of a starship or near a powerful source of radio waves."],["Your cilia emit an electromagnetic field around your body that causes you to hover ever so slightly above solid ground. While hovering above solid ground, you ignore difficult terrain. Damaging effects originating from the surface of the ground, such as caltrops or an electrified floor, don't affect you, but effects extending far enough above the ground, like moving through a fire, might still affect you, at the GM's discretion."],["Your cilia are even more selective about the molecules they siphon for nutrients. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against diseases and poisons. If you roll a success on a saving throw against a disease or poison, you get a critical success instead. If you have a different ability that would improve the save in this way (such as the soldier's tough as nails class feature), if you roll a critical failure on the save, you get a failure instead."],["In traditional processes, a large part of an individual's life is spent waiting; you add value by reducing the amount of time wasted by waiting. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to initiative rolls."],["Your personal electromotive force is strong enough to propel you. You gain a fly Speed equal to your land Speed."],["You lead others by teaching and imparting insights onto them. Whenever an ally selects you as the target of their attempt to Follow the Expert, you increase the circumstance bonus they receive to their skill check by an additional +1, or an additional +2 if you have master proficiency rank or higher (for a total of +3 for expert, +5 for master, and +6 for legendary)."],["You can hold on to your natural static charge. Rather than gradually dissipating, it waits to jump to the closest conductor. Your unarmed Strikes deal an additional 1d6 electricity damage on a hit. On a critical hit, the jolt jumps to up to two other creatures of your choice within 10 feet of the target, dealing an equal amount of electricity damage. At 15th level, this damage ignores the target's electricity resistance (and the other creatures' electricity resistance on a critical hit)."],["You have niche expertise or esoteric training that you often fall back on when you find yourself in a rut. You gain the One Up reaction."],["**Trigger** You attempt a saving throw against a magical effect, but you haven't rolled yet.\n\n---\n\nYour ardent devotion to your faith or philosophy shields you from other divine magic and effects. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the triggering saving throw or a +2 circumstance bonus if it's a divine magical effect."],["Whether due to biological evolution, scientific experimentation, or intentional modification, your body naturally integrates augmentations. Your implant limit increases by 1.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the synthflesh verthani heritage, your implant limit increases by 2, rather than 1."],["You have excellent vision thanks to your large, bulbous eyes. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus when using the [[/act seek]] action to find hidden or undetected creatures within 30 feet of you. When you target an opponent that's Concealed from you or hidden from you, reduce the DC of the flat check to 3 for a concealed target or 9 for a hidden target."],["You're a talented engineer or programmer who frequently creates new innovations in your field. You become trained in your choice of either Computers or Crafting. If you selected Crafting, you gain the Specialty Crafting skill feat. If you chose Computers, you gain the Programmer skill feat."],["You're insatiably curious and driven to experiment, often attempting to push the boundaries of science. You gain the Additional Lore skill feat for your choice of either Life Science Lore or Physical Science Lore. In addition, you gain the Eureka! action."],["You're a natural leader, adept at bringing people together, settling arguments, and guiding a group toward a common goal. You become trained in Diplomacy. If you would automatically become trained in Diplomacy (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. In addition, you gain the Group Impression skill feat."],["You grew up in a megacity and are used to the hustle, bustle, and crowds of major cities. You become trained in Acrobatics and gain the Crowd Surfing skill feat."],["You've immersed yourself in your people's history and culture. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Crafting and Society. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Verthani Lore."],["**Trigger** You take damage, and a creature is adjacent to you.\n\n---\n\nThe color of your skin flickers wildly when you're hurt. Select one adjacent creature; that creature must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. Regardless of the result of its saving throw, the creature is then temporarily immune to Dazzling Surge for 1 hour.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes a –1 circumstance penalty to Perception checks until the beginning of your next turn.\n\n**Failure** The creature is Dazzled until the end of your next turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is dazzled for 2 rounds."],["You match your skin's color and patterns to your surroundings, vastly improving your ability to pass unseen and gaining perpetual camouflage. For 10 minutes, you can [[/act hide]] or [[/act sneak]] without cover or being Concealed."],["When you wield a melee weapon that requires two hands and doesn't have reach, you can change between a typical two-handed grip and an extended two-handed stretch using an Interact action. Weapons wielded in your extended two-handed stretch gain a reach of 10 feet."],["You can divine the patterns and colors of your skin. Twice per day, you can spend 10 minutes to cast Augury as a 2nd-rank divine innate spell. Once per day, you can spend 10 minutes to cast Read Omens as a 4th-rank divine innate spell. These spells gain the visual trait."],["Your wide-angle vision makes it hard for enemies to surprise you. You aren't Off-Guard to melee attacks from creatures flanking you."],["Your augmentations push past their limits. Increase your implant limit by 2. You gain the Miraculous Activation action."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou can shift the colors and patterns on your skin with barely a second thought, changing your appearance in an instant. You Shift Skin."],["You've spent your waking hours impersonating others to your heart's content and can effortlessly mimic those you've just met or shift into your own alternate personas to disguise yourself and slip away. The frequency of Identity Mimicry becomes once per 10 minutes rather than once per day."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou cause your skin to rapidly flicker between a clashing array of colors and patterns, disorienting anyone who can see you. Creatures within 30 feet that can see you must attempt a Will save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is Off-Guard against your next attack before the end of your turn.\n\n**Failure** The creature is off-guard against your attacks until the end of your turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is off-guard until the beginning of your next turn."],["You have adapted to extreme temperature, even beyond that of other bioharmonic verthanis. You gain resistance equal to half your level against cold and fire damage. If you use Temperature Acclimation, you gain resistance equal to your level to the triggering damage type for 1 minute, instead of the normal effects of Temperature Acclimation."],["You can tap into and channel the divine energies of the Universe to cast spells. You might be blessed, pious, an esoteric scientist, or—as most other verthanis assume—a chosen God-Vessel representing your divinity. Choose one of the following 1st-rank divine spells: Bane, Bless, Command, Fear, or Protection. You can cast the selected spell as a divine innate spell once per day.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the devotional verthani heritage, you can instead select two spells from the listed options, and you can cast each of the selected spells as a divine innate spell once per day."],["You possess a deep knowledge of your people's history and customs, and you can leverage that knowledge to influence your fellow verthanis and other citizens of Verces. You might be a scholar or diplomat, or you might be a member of the Pure Ones. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus on Society checks to Recall Knowledge about Verces and verthanis. In addition, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Charisma-based skill checks against verthanis and other citizens of Verces."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou come up with a unique and ingenious way to accomplish a task, taking longer to achieve your goal with better results. [[/act perform]] a skill action that takes a single action to perform and requires a skill check to accomplish or measure its success, such as an Acrobatics check to [[/act balance]], a Medicine check to [[/act treat-poison]], or a Stealth check to [[/act hide]]. Roll this skill check twice, and use the better result."],["Whether it springs from a love of exploration, a desire for freedom, or a need for speed, you're never happier than when you're behind the wheel of a vehicle or at the helm of a starship. You become trained in Piloting, or if you're already trained in Piloting, you instead become expert in Piloting. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus on Piloting checks to Navigate, Plot Course, Stunt, and perform starship actions at the piloting station. When you roll a success on a check to Navigate or Plot Course, you get a critical success instead."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou adjust the pigments of your skin, making it difficult to discern details about your body and even determine what parts of your body are where. You become Concealed until the beginning of your next turn. As the nature of this effect still leaves your location obvious, you can't use this concealment to [[/act hide]] or [[/act sneak]]. When this effect ends, your skin becomes a mottled mess, so it doesn't blend in with your surroundings."],["You've traveled distant worlds and lived among other cultures for years, leading you to become a talented linguist. You gain the Multilingual skill feat twice, even if you don't meet the prerequisites. In addition, you can cast Translate once per day on yourself as a 3rd-rank divine innate spell."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou're incredibly talented at mimicking others, using your ability to alter your skin's pigmentation and patterns alongside your more mundane skills to perfectly disguise yourself and impersonate others. You gain the effects of a 3rd-rank Illusory Disguise spell, targeting yourself, except this transformation is non-magical and doesn't have the illusion trait."],["◇ to ◆\n\n**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou've achieved near-perfect integration with your augmentations, allowing you to react with uncanny speed and precision. Activate an augmentation currently installed in your body. If the augmentation would usually take 1 action to Activate, Modification Synchronization is a free action. If the augmentation would usually take 2 actions to Activate, Modification Synchronization is 1 action. For example, Activating a Commercial Dragon Gland to Exhale would be a free action, while Activating Commercial Psychoactive Eyes to Gaze would be 1 action."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou're accustomed to collaborating with others and know how to lend a hand to an ally without slowing your own progress down or losing focus on your own goals. You prepare to help an ally with a task. This follows all the usual rules and steps detailed in the Aid action, except preparing to help is a part of Sudden Assistance and doesn't require a single action."],["You've learned through trial and painful error how to make the most out of your armor, deflecting damage from explosions and similar effects. When donning armor, you can grant it the bulwark trait until you remove it. When you're wearing armor that already has the bulwark trait, increase the modifier to Reflex saves to avoid damaging effects granted by that armor to +4, rather than +3."],["You're a natural predator trained to use part of your body as a weapon. When you select this feat, you gain one of the following unarmed attacks of your choice: claw, jaws, or tail. Each of these attacks is in the brawling weapon group.\n\nA claw unarmed attack deals 1d6 slashing damage and has the agile, finesse, unarmed, and vesk traits.\n\nA jaws unarmed attack deals 1d6 piercing damage and has the grapple, unarmed, and vesk traits.\n\nA tail unarmed attack deals 1d6 bludgeoning damage and has the sweep, trip, unarmed, and vesk traits.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these attacks, you get its critical specialization effect.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat three times. Each time you do, select a different attack from the options listed above."],["◆ or ◆◆\n\n**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou advance into danger, heedless of threats and intent on closing with your targets. Stride once, or Stride twice if you used two actions. You gain a +10-foot status bonus to your Speed for these Strides."],["You're a skilled leader. Whenever an ally selects you as the target of their attempts to Follow the Expert, you increase the circumstance bonus they receive to their skill check by an additional +1, or an additional +2 if you have master proficiency or higher (for a total of +3 for expert, +5 for master, and +6 for legendary)."],["Whether it comes from a sense of duty or a desire to succeed, you rarely flinch when confronted by fearsome foes. If you roll a success on a saving throw against a fear effect, you get a critical success instead."],["You can use your neck frill to glide slowly through the air, 5 feet down and up to 25 feet forward through the air. As long as you spend at least 1 action gliding each round and haven't yet reached the ground, you remain in the air at the end of your turn."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You critically fail a skill check.\n\n**Requirements** You're not in a combat encounter.\n\n---\n\nWhether you're boogying down in a dance-off or striving for the highest score on a test, you treat any challenge as seriously as a fight to the death. Reroll the triggering skill check and use the second result."],["You're trained with all doshkos. In addition, you gain access to all uncommon weapons with the vesk trait. For the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["When your foe is weak, you press on. When you successfully Strike a creature that has the frightened or persistent bleed condition with a melee or ranged weapon, you gain a circumstance bonus to the damage roll equal to the number of weapon damage dice of the weapon used for the Strike."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** You're engaged in combat.\n\n---\n\nYou pray to Damoritosh (or a battle saint) for a blessing in the heat of battle—and he answers. You regain 1 Focus Point, up to your usual maximum."],["Tapping into the divine magic that keeps the erosion of centuries at bay allows you to harden your body. You can cast Cairn Form twice per day as a 6th-rank divine innate spell that can only target yourself. In addition to the normal effects of *cairn form*, whenever a creature damages you with an unarmed attack or non-reach melee weapon, the attacking creature takes 8 bludgeoning damage."],["By honoring the memories of each of your amalgamated souls, you've learned how to better learn from their experiences. You can use Memories of Valor once per hour instead of once per day."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** You critically fail a Strike against an enemy.\n\n---\n\nYou clear your mind of distractions and focus on your foe, determined to overcome the shame of your failure lest it forever blemish your reputation. The next time before the end of your turn that you attempt a Strike with the same weapon and target as the triggering attack, you roll the attack roll twice and use the higher result. If the attack misses, you're overwhelmed with shame, becoming Off-Guard until the end of your next turn."],["You have ascended to the rank of living battle saint and are on a path to become a true divine servant of Damoritosh when you meet him in the afterlife. You can cast Rocket Dash and Haste as 7th-rank divine innate spells once per day each."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You deal the killing blow to an enemy.\n\n---\n\nYou don't just fight because you have to; the threat of battle and the thrill of victory invigorate you. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to your level. These temporary Hit Points last for 1 minute or until the encounter ends, whichever comes first."],["You use ritualistic prayer to gain supercharged regenerative abilities, giving your blood the power to heal wounds and regrow lost limbs, even when applied to others. You can cast Regenerate as a 7th-rank primal innate spell twice per day."],["The vesk deity of conquest, Damoritosh, has gifted (or cursed) you with the divine energy to persevere through the most intense combat situations. The first time each day that you would die, Damoritosh protects you, granting you a sliver of healing and the drive to push through the coming challenge. This prevents you from dying, restores 5 healing Hit Points, and you become Quickened for 1 minute. If the cause of your death was a condition or effect that would still cause you to die after regaining Hit Points, such as a high value on the Doomed condition, you suppress that condition for 1 minute."],["You have a keen sense of smell and are capable of detecting bloody wounds at a distance. You gain blood sense as an imprecise sense with a range of 30 feet. This means you can use your sense of smell to determine the exact location of a living creature who isn't at its full Hit Points. Creatures that don't have blood, such as oozes and most constructs, can't be detected with your blood sense."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You frighten a creature.\n\n---\n\nYou snarl, hiss, shout, or otherwise verbally menace the triggering creature as you frighten them. Increase the value of the frightened condition by 1 (maximum 3)."],["You use the power that animates your body to reshape your living stone and transform into one of your comrades. That comrade must be a common Medium-sized humanoid ancestry prevalent where your unit fought (typically in Veskarium space). While these disguises resemble specific individuals, the age of most animate enshrined vesk makes it challenging to find anyone who has personally met any specific enshrined warrior. If you've fought alongside enough or otherwise formed a close bond with a member of your party, your GM might allow you to transform into them as well.\n\nUsing Shape Statue counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception, but without a holoskin or similar disguise, you take a penalty to imitate a non-constructed ancestry. You can remain in your new form indefinitely, but you revert to your base form after 1 hour of Unconsciousness or 1 minute after death."],["**Trigger** You critically succeed on a save against a fear effect whose source was a creature, or a creature fails or critically fails an Intimidation check to Demoralize you.\n\n---\n\nYou laugh at your enemy's failed attempts to bully you, turning the tables on your foe with a display of terrifying bravado. You attempt an Intimidation check to Demoralize the triggering creature."],["You can enhance your natural venom by imbibing more poison, allowing it to mix with your natural poison production. You Interact to draw (if necessary) and chug a dose of poison or one piece of projectile ammunition from a weapon you're holding that deals poison damage. Add 1d4 poison damage to the next Strike you make with your venomous jaws. The damage increases to two dice if your held weapon is advanced grade or superior grade, three dice if the weapon is elite grade or ultimate grade, and four dice if the weapon is paragon grade. On a critical hit, roll these dice after doubling the weapon's damage."],["**Trigger** You become Grabbed.\n\n**Requirements** You have a fully grown tail.\n\n---\n\nYou disconnect and drop part of your tail to escape. You cease being grabbed then Step. It takes 1 day (or an effect like Regenerate) for your tail to fully grow back. Until it does, you can't use your tail, and you take a –2 circumstance penalty on checks to [[/act balance]].\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have Ancestral Unarmed Attack (tail), you can eject your tail as a reaction when you take damage from an attack. If you do, you Step and one adjacent square becomes difficult terrain for 1 minute as your tail wriggles in place. If you also have the Feign Death skill feat, you can Feign Death instead of Stepping, with a +2 circumstance bonus to your Deception DC."],["**Trigger** You roll Athletics or Intimidation for initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou eagerly stride into battle, giving no thought to the consequences. You Stride in a straight line directly toward an enemy."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou spit venom into the magazine of a weapon you're holding, or a similar ranged weapon held by a willing adjacent creature. Each Strike or use of Auto-Fire with the chosen weapon until the start of your next turn that deals acid, bludgeoning, poison, piercing, or slashing damage, also deals an additional 2d6 poison damage.\n\nVenomous Cocktail"],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nWhile the memories of most enshrined vesk are hazy and ephemeral, with some concentration you can recall memories of your amalgamated souls vividly enough to apply your experiences.\n\nChoose one skill. You temporarily increase your proficiency rank with that skill by one step for 1 minute (from untrained to trained, trained to expert, and expert to master). This temporary increase adjusts your proficiency bonus and allows you to use skill actions based on this increased proficiency as normal. Memories of Valor can't increase a skill's proficiency rank beyond master."],["At the start of a combat encounter, if you are aware of your foes and aren't attempting to Sneak or Hide, you can roll an Intimidation check for your initiative and can use the result to Demoralize one observed foe."],["You've mastered using your own plate scales or worn armor to absorb devastating strikes. You gain the Plate Deflection reaction."],["The Veskarium has a proud tradition of training disciplined quartermasters whose contributions to the empire's success through logistical acumen rival those of the greatest vesk warriors. You gain the Prescient Consumable and Prescient Planner feats."],["**Trigger** An ally within 60 feet fails a Will saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYou shout or sign encouragement to an ally in their time of need, buoying their spirits and hardening their resolve. Your ally rerolls the triggering check but must use the new result, even if it's worse. If you shout, Buoy gains the auditory trait. If you sign, Buoy gains the visual trait."],["You work well on a team, and you're always ready to lend a hand and accept the help offered by others. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to checks to Aid, and your allies gain a +2 circumstance bonus to checks to Aid you.\n\nCooperative"],["You refuse to give up or give in to despair, even when all seems hopeless. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against emotion and fear effects. If you roll a success on a saving throw against an emotion or fear effect, you get a critical success instead.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can't select this feat if you have the Heightened Paranoia feat."],["When the going gets tough, the tough fight tooth and nail to build a better life—literally. Your fellow vlakas might carry hope, dreams, and unending optimism in their hearts, but you've always found it harder to look on the bright side, and you've done some dubious things to get by. Whether you've lied, cheated, stolen, or taken some lives, you know that you did what it took to survive and thrive in a cold and callous galaxy. You become trained in one of the following skills of your choice: Deception, Intimidation, or Thievery. If you select Deception, you gain the Lengthy Diversion skill feat. If you select Intimidation, you gain the Group Coercion skill feat. If you select Thievery, you gain the Subtle Theft skill feat."],["You're a talented diplomat or mediator who's skilled at making a good impression and accustomed to finding compromises, brokering deals, and forging strong social connections. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Diplomacy. If you would automatically become trained in Diplomacy (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You also gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks to Make an Impression."],["You have the keen instincts of a hunter and know to go for the throat. If you're a sharp-toothed vlaka, the damage you deal with your jaws increases to 1d8, and your jaws lose the finesse trait and gain the grapple trait. Otherwise, you gain a jaws unarmed attack that deals 1d4 piercing damage. Your jaws are in the brawling group and have the finesse and unarmed traits.\n\nIn either case, whenever you score a critical hit with your jaws unarmed attack, your target takes 1 persistent bleed damage per weapon damage die, in addition to the other effects of a critical hit."],["You keep your people's stories alive with magic. You can cast Figment and Prestidigitation as occult innate spells at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["Your keen nose makes you an excellent tracker. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Survival. If you would automatically become trained in Survival (from your background of class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Survival checks to Track. This bonus increases to +2 when tracking by scent. You also gain the Experienced Tracker skill feat."],["You've spent many long years traversing Lajok's surface, moving from city to city or hunting for food and resources. You're accustomed to moving across slippery ice sheets and plowing through deep snow. When moving over ice or snow in arctic terrain, you always gain the benefits of the Cover Tracks action without needing to use the activity or having to move half your Speed. You don't treat icy terrain as uneven ground (though it's still difficult terrain for you), and you ignore difficult terrain caused by snow."],["You strive to keep the traditions and stories of your people alive, even as you build new communities and forge new alliances. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Diplomacy and Society. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Vlaka Lore."],["Your travels have taught you to pack smart for any situation. You've got really big pockets, and you've crammed a whole lot of useful stuff into them. You can use Just the Thing… once per hour, rather than once per day."],["Your starburst markings can store much greater reserves of solar energy, enabling you to heal yourself more frequently. The frequency of Siphon Solar Vitality increases to once per hour, rather than once per day."],["**Trigger** An adjacent ally Strides.\n\n---\n\nYou synchronize your movement to that of your allies, moving alongside them to keep close in the fray. Stride after the triggering ally, remaining adjacent to your ally for the duration of their movement until they stop or you've moved a distance equal to your Speed, whichever occurs first."],["**Requirements** You're within 30 feet of an ally with the dying condition.\n\n---\n\nThe sight of an ally near death overwhelms you with sorrow. In an act of frustration, you unleash a mournful, keening howl that forces your enemies to share in your heartbreak. You deal floor((level - 1)/2)d6 mental nonlethal mental damage to all enemies in a 30-foot emanation (basic Will save using your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher). The damage increases by 1d6 for every two levels you have beyond 13th."],["**Requirements** Your last action was a successful Shove.\n\n---\n\nYou leverage your knowledge of energy, mass, and motion against your opponents to manipulate their battlefield positioning. The Shoved creature continues moving. They're pushed back an additional 5 feet, or 10 feet if the required Shove was a critical success. If they would collide with a solid surface due to this movement, you immediately attempt to Trip them as a free action, even if they're no longer within your reach."],["You know that it's more important to act wisely than it is to act quickly. When you take the time to consider a problem from all angles, you come up with an insightful revelation. You gain Read Omens as a 4th-rank occult innate spell. You can cast this spell once per day."],["Your ability to detect the emotions of others is unparalleled. Your emotion sense becomes a precise sense with a range of 120 feet."],["You're an incredibly talented storyteller, making legends come to life. You gain Illusory Scene as a 6th-rank occult innate spell. You can cast this spell once per day. When you cast *illusory scene* in this way, the spell automatically adapts to suit its audience. A deaf creature that witnesses the illusion additionally sees the characters in the scene visually signing their dialogue. A blind creature that witnesses the illusion additionally hears an audio description of the scene. A deafblind creature that witnesses the illusion additionally receives a psychic impression of the scene and its dialogue in their mind."],["You orate an inspiring speech that rallies your allies, cleansing their body and mind of harmful conditions and stoking their spirit for the ongoing battle. If you say this speech, Sway the Heart, Stoke the Spirit gains the auditory trait. If you sign this speech, Sway the Heart, Stoke the Spirit gains the visual trait. You and all allies in a 60-foot emanation benefit from a 4th-rank Clear Mind and a 4th-rank Sound Body spell. Additionally, your allies gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Will saves for 1 minute.\n\nSway the Heart, Stoke the Spirit"],["Channeling the heat of Sota's rekindled sun, you unleash a blast of plasma across the battlefield. You deal 10d8 fire damage in a 120-foot line. For 1 minute afterward, your body is awash with solar energy. Creatures that Grab you or that hit you with an unarmed Strike or a non-reach melee weapon take 1d6 fire damage. Creatures in the area must attempt a Reflex save using your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage, plus 1d6 electricity damage, and is Dazzled for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage, plus 1d6 persistent electricity damage, and is Blinded for 1 round. For 1 minute afterward, your body is awash with solar energy. Creatures that Grab you or that hit you with an unarmed Strike or a non-reach melee weapon take 1d6 fire damage."],["You know that when it comes to surviving a dangerous situation, every moment counts. To that end, you've trained long and hard to improve your natural senses, pushing them to the limits of their ability. Select an imprecise sense you have, such as hearing or scent. The range of the selected imprecise sense increases to 120 feet.\n\n---\n\n**Special**: You can select this feat more than once. Each time you do, select a different imprecise sense you possess."],["You believe that even in the face of the impossible, from hope spring miracles. Much like Lajok's rekindled light, you always carry this spark of hope in your heart and can focus upon it to make magic. You regain 1 Focus Point, up to your usual maximum."],["You have a knack for mentoring others. Whenever you successfully Aid an ally, you increase the circumstance bonus that you would grant them by +1, or by +2 on a critical success. Whenever an ally Follows the Expert, and the expert they choose to follow is you, the circumstance bonus they gain to their skill check based on your proficiency is increased by +1."],["**Trigger** A creature you can see damages you with a melee Strike.\n\n---\n\nYou give your attacker a look of utter disappointment so heartbreaking that it causes them to feel shame for their actions. The attacker must succeed at a Will saving throw against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher, or become Sickened 1 from the guilt. On a critical failure, they fail to follow through on the attack, reducing the triggering damage dealt to you by their Strength modifier."],["You witnessed the ritual that supposedly rekindled Sota's flame up close, and while it was certainly impressive, you don't believe it should've worked. You can't seem to shake the feeling that something else is at work behind the scenes—something dangerous and unknown. Whatever it is, you intend to face this threat head on. When you succeed on a Will saving throw against an effect that could impose the Confused, Controlled, or Frightened condition, you get a critical success instead.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can't select this feat if you have the Determined Optimist feat."],["You're fascinated by the ancient ruins scattered across Lajok's surface and orbit. Whether you're a scrapper harvesting materials for reuse, an innovator looking for a unique technological wonder, or a scholar hoping to glean secrets of the past, you enter these ancient sites, heedless of the danger. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to find hazards, to skill checks to disable hazards, to AC against attacks made by hazards, and to saves against hazards."],["Your starburst markings store solar energy that you can tap into to revitalize your body and magically heal your wounds. You regain Hit Points equal to level+ 1d6 healing(1d6 plus your character level). If you're in an area of natural sunlight, you instead regain Hit Points equal to ((2*level)+1d6) healing (1d6 plus twice your character level)."],["When words fail and tempers flare, you center your emotions and then release your peaceful thoughts in a soothing, psychic calm. Once per day, you can cast either Calm or Clear Mind as an occult innate spell, heightened to half your level rounded up."],["Your extensive scientific knowledge of astronomy, astrophysics, and stellar phenomenon have given you insight into the underpinnings of the universe—particularly motion. You can use this knowledge to more easily move your foes across the battlefield. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to Reposition, Shove or Trip. If you critically fail an Athletics check to Reposition, Shove or Trip, you get a failure instead."],["You grew up in a dangerous environment that taught you to be wary. You can perform the Investigate exploration activity at the same time as the Search exploration activity."],["**Cost** the Price of the chosen item\n\n---\n\nYou've traveled far and wide, bringing supplies and equipment from place to place and picking up interesting objects in your travels. In fact, you've got an interesting item right… here! You Interact to pull an item you hadn't previously declared that you purchased out of your pocket—this item must be any common item of half your level or less with a Bulk of 1 or less. It must be a piece of adventuring gear (from the table in Starfinder Player Core or other sources of adventuring gear) and can't be a weapon, armor, ammunition, magic item, pharmaceutical item, or other treasure."],["**Requirements** A creature within 30 feet has the frightened condition.\n\n---\n\nYou snarl ferociously at a creature within 30 feet, menacing them with bared teeth. Increase the value of the frightened condition by 1 (maximum 3). The target then becomes temporarily immune to your Menacing Snarl for 24 hours.\n\nAs long as the target is frightened, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to melee Strikes against that creature, and damage dealt to the creature by your melee Strikes deals an additional 1 mental damage per damage die."],["**Requirements** You're adjacent to an ally.\n\n---\n\nYou're determined to protect your allies from harm—even if it hurts! Select one adjacent ally. Until the beginning of your next turn, you shield them with your body; any lesser cover you grant them is instead standard cover, though they can't use standard cover granted by you to Hide."],["You can detect the emotions of others, though you lack the ability to sort out the complexities of these emotions. You gain emotion sense as an imprecise sense with a range of 30 feet. This means you can detect and determine the location of creatures that possess emotions. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks when using the Seek action to find Hidden or undetected creatures within the range of your emotion sense who's under an emotion effect, such as rage, the frightened condition, or any spell with the emotion trait."],["You offer an ally advice and encouragement, granting them the inspiration they need to push themselves further in the face of a challenge. During a combat encounter, select an ally within 60 feet. That ally gains a +2 circumstance bonus to their skill checks until the beginning of your next turn. That ally then becomes temporarily immune to your Skillful Encouragement for 1 hour. If you said this advice verbally, Skillful Encouragement gains the auditory trait. If you signed this advice, Skillful Encouragement gains the visual trait.\n\nSkillful Encouragement"],["While vulkarisu are naturally good climbers, you're exceptional, and can ascend and descend vertical surfaces without a second thought. You become trained in Athletics. If you would automatically become trained in Athletics (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Combat Climber skill feat, and you reduce the number of free hands required to Climb by one."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail a skill check.\n\n**Requirements** You're not in a combat encounter.\n\n---\n\nYou're always prepared to catch yourself mid-failure before it cascades into a complete disaster, shrugging off a potential mistake as merely bad luck and pushing forward without letting it get you down. Reroll the triggering skill check and use the better result."],["Your understanding of languages extends to the logic-driven way computers and other technology communicates, allowing you to participate in their electronic dialogue. You become trained in Computers. If you would automatically become trained in Computers (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Phreaker skill feat. You can use Computers instead of Diplomacy to Make a [[/act request skill=computers]] of creatures with the tech trait."],["Whether burrowing underground, squeezing around branches in dense foliage, traversing the cramped back alleys of an urban jungle, or slipping through a starship's ventilation system, you know how to get through tight spaces. You become trained in Acrobatics. If you would automatically become trained in Acrobatics (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Quick Squeeze feat. Tight spaces not tight enough to require the Squeeze action aren't difficult terrain for you."],["You can swear a soul-sworn oath with one other willing sapient creature, empathically bonding your souls to one another. Swearing this bond is a 10-minute activity that you must both participate in. A soul-sworn oath lasts until you or the target choose to end it as a free action. You can only have one soul-sworn oath active at a time. If you attempt to swear a second soul-sworn oath, the first soul-sworn oath immediately ends. You and the target of this oath can communicate with each other mentally, as if you had limited telepathy with a range of 60 feet. In addition, as long as you can communicate mentally with one another, you share each other's languages."],["Alright, you admit it: you're a bit of a hoarder. But you maintain that all those things you've been squirreling away aren't useless! In fact, you swear you'll find a use for them one day! If only you can remember where you stashed everything...\n\nYou become trained in Survival. If you're already trained in Survival, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You can spend 3 actions burying up to a light Bulk of goods, or 10 minutes burying up to 10 Bulk of goods. This usually requires suitable terrain you can dig through, such as loose dirt or sand, but a GM might allow you to bury your stash in other terrain, such as a junkyard or behind the drywall of an office building. In most cases, creatures have a chance to detect your stash only if they use the Seek action to attempt a Perception check against your Survival DC. If you're relatively close by, such as in the same settlement, you can usually retrieve your stash in an hour without any problems."],["You are a skilled linguist and translator, with the uncanny ability to detect linguistic nuances, understand local parlance and metaphor, interpret nonverbal body language and communication, and ensure you're understood by those around you when it really counts, even when speaking a language they don't know. You gain two additional languages of your choice. Your linguistic effects work on targets who share a language with you, even if you aren't certain which language you share or aren't using the shared language."],["You're an eternal optimist, and you wouldn't have it any other way! No matter how close you come to failing at a task (or how often you fail), you know if you just keep trying, you're bound to succeed. You can use Aw, Nuts! once per hour, rather than once per day."],["**Requirements** You have at least one hand free and your target is no more than one size larger than you.\n\n---\n\nYou swoop down, use your arms to grab your friend, and fly them off to safety. You Fly or Tail Glide for each action you used to Sky-Save. At any point during this movement, you can seize hold of one willing ally within reach, taking them with you for the duration of your movement. When Sky-Save ends, choose if you are carrying the ally (making the ally Grabbed) or Release the ally (the ally must be willing to be Released)."],["You can speak clearly with creation itself. You gain Speak with Animals, Speak with Plants, and Speak with Computers as 4th-rank primal innate spells, and Speak with Stones as a 5th-rank primal innate spell. You can cast one of these spells once per day."],["You know how to prepare for the unforeseen and can instantly recognize the signs of buried stashes from others who share your diligence. You gain the Prescient Planner general feat. You can use Prescient Planner as a 2-action activity once per day to find a buried stash of goods, and you can procure ammunition and batteries in addition to the usual items available. These items must meet the usual level, Bulk, and other requirements, and you must still pay the price of the chosen item, usually by buying similar goods and burying them for later, even if that means other vulkarisu get to it first."],["You can read some of your story in the grand narrative of all creation, setting a metaphysical bookmark in case you lose your place. Once per day, when you would die, you instead cease to physically exist for 1 minute. At the end of this duration, your body is rewritten into existence from the grand narrative, appearing at full Hit Points in the location you disappeared from. Do not increase the value of your Wounded condition."],["Your mastery of Vulkari transcends mere linguistics. You're affected by a constant Truespeech spell."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYour keen senses and clever intellect help you maintain a constant and instinctive conversation with the narrative of existence, giving you uncanny knowledge of your surroundings and circumstances. You attempt a check to Recall Knowledge. If you roll a success, you get a critical success instead."],["By chittering out a hodgepodge of complex algorithmic computer code, you can disrupt technology attempting to process your words. You gain the Combat Hack skill feat. You can Combat Hack a creature with the tech trait within 30 feet without the use of a hacking toolkit or free hand. If you do, the action loses the manipulate trait and gains the auditory and linguistic traits."],["Like a squox fighting off a larger predator, you know it's best to dash into dangerous encounters, focus on a single enemy, and go right for their eyes (or other optical receptors). You Stride, then Feint, then make a melee Strike against the target of your Feint. You can use Acrobatics instead of Deception for this [[/act feint skill=acrobatics]], if desired, and the target takes a –2 circumstance penalty to their Perception DCs against your Feint if they're larger than you."],["◆ to ◆◆◆\n\nYou've learned to make use of your exceptional balance and your ankles that can rotate 180 degrees to run in almost any direction without warning, easily throwing off the expectations of any potential predators. You Stride for each action you use to Serpentine Scurry. If you change directions after moving 5 feet or more, any further movement you make as part of Serpentine Scurry doesn't trigger reactions based on movement.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Quick Jump skill feat, you can instead Stride, [[/act high-jump]], or [[/act long-jump]] for each action you use to Serpentine Scurry."],["You've deepened the bonds of your soul-sworn oaths. As long as you are within 10 feet of the target of your soul-sworn oath, you each gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Will save against fear effects. If you are both Frightened, whenever the value of the frightened condition decreases for one of you, it decreases by 1 for the other as well.\n\nSoul-Sworn Bravery"],["Using a technique developed by studying the defensive motions of wild squoxes, you get on all fours and bury your claws deeply into the ground, wiggling your tail around in a frenzy as if it were a separate creature with a mind of its own. Until you move, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Fortitude and Reflex DCs against attempts to [[/act shove]], [[/act reposition]], or [[/act trip]] you. This bonus also applies to saving throws against spells or effects that attempt to move you or knock you Prone. Furthermore, until you move, when you successfully [[/act feint]] a creature of your level or lower while that creature is flanking you, flanking doesn't make you Off-Guard to that creature (though that creature can still help its other allies flank you)."],["You can use your fluffy tail to guide your descent when falling through the air. You glide slowly toward the ground, 5 feet down and up to 25 feet forward through the air. As long as you spend at least 1 action Tail Gliding each round and have not yet reached the ground, you remain in the air at the end of your turn."],["**Requirements** You are climbing on a surface at least 10 feet directly above a target.\n\n---\n\nYou leap down on your target with all the acrobatic grace of a falling squox. You attempt to [[/act trip skill=acrobatics]] the target using Acrobatics instead of Athletics, then land in an unoccupied space of your choice adjacent to the target."],["You extend your broad membranes and flap your powerful arms in carefully controlled patterns, creating enough lift to carry you through the air. You gain a fly Speed equal to your land Speed."],["You can use your knowledge of computer coding and machine learning to hack magical items, enabling you to operate these powerful items even if you lack any magical talent. You gain the Trick Magic Item skill feat, even if you don't meet the prerequisites. When you Trick Magic Item, you can choose to use Computers instead of Arcana, Nature, Occultism, or Religion for the skill check, regardless of the item's magic tradition."],["You understand that magic is just another language, and you can recognize and decode even magic outside of your spellcasting tradition. You gain the Recognize Spell skill feat. When you Recognize Spell and you don't automatically identify the spell, you select which of the listed skill checks the GM rolls secretly to identify the spell, rather than the GM rolling whichever corresponds to the tradition of the spell being cast. In addition, you can get a result better than failure if you're not trained in the skill."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou have little regard for the concepts of personal space and individual ownership, and you often place your equipment in your allies' possession without their knowledge. Fortunately, you know exactly where you put it! You call out to your allies, urging them to pull something out of a pocket or bag. Each of your allies within 100 feet who can perceive you can use a reaction to draw one item of your choice from their pocket, bag, or similar storage space. They can additionally stow an item as part of this reaction, if desired. You choose the drawn item for each ally individually, from among the items in your possession that weigh 1 Bulk or less."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You or an ally you can sense within 15 feet rolls an attack roll, saving throw, or skill check.\n\n---\n\nWhen things seem about to turn against you or your allies, you invoke your innate connection to the fickle and uncanny whims of luck. The triggering check can be rerolled, and the second result must be used."],["Your body was forged in the Vault of Vorlath by mercenaries who were subjected to brutal experimentation. You gain the Diehard feat. Once per day, if you fail the flat check to remove persistent damage, you can reroll the check as a free action and take the higher result; this is a fortune effect."],["howing off isn't just something you do, it's part of who you are. You can use Performance to [[/act demoralize skill=performance]], [[/act lie skill=performance]], or [[/act make-an-impression skill=performance]]. If you've just done something impressive—such as rolling a critical success on an attack, save, or check—you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Performance checks for 1 minute, as the memory of your impressive feat hangs in the air. The GM has final say on if an action was impressive enough to merit this bonus.\n\nShow-Off"],["You've spent years traveling, and you know better than most that roads aren't always paved. Or clear. Or even built yet. You become trained in Nature or Survival. If you're already trained in both of those skills, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. Choose one kind of terrain from the following list: muddy, rocky, sandy, sloped, or undergrowth. You ignore difficult or uneven terrain of that type."],["You've refined your relationship with the most fickle force in the universe, and you can tap into it with an expertise that people all over the galaxy would envy. At the beginning of each adventuring day, roll 1d20. This number is your lucky number, and the first time you roll it on an attack, check, or save, treat the roll as a 20. If you roll a 20, your lucky number becomes 1 instead."],["You've truly lucked out. Like some of the greatest worlanisi luck manipulators to come before you, you can hold onto your connection with luck even after you've used it. You can use your lucky number twice a day instead of once."],["Your horn-cones have grown far more sensitive, as you've finally achieved some semblance of your ancestors' ability to hunt through psychic mastery alone and can track the locations of thinking creatures with incredible accuracy. Your thoughtsense becomes a precise sense."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nIn the heat of combat, all the skill in the world doesn't mean anything if you don't have a little luck on your side. When you critically hit with a Strike against a target, before you roll the damage, you can choose to roll the damage dice pool twice and take the better of the two results."],["**Trigger** An enemy you can sense rolls for initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou've mastered reading people in all circumstances, even before a fight breaks out. Roll Perception to [[/act sense-motive]] against your target. If you succeed, your initiative roll is equal to the target's initiative plus 1. If you critically succeed, your initiative is equal to the target's initiative plus 2, and the target is Off-Guard to you until the start of its turn."],["**Requirements** You haven't used your lucky number yet today.\n\n---\n\nYou can go all in on your luck in the present moment at the expense of your luck in the future. Before you roll a check, you can choose to expend both uses of your lucky number to count the roll as a 20. The effort strains your relationship with the primal forces of luck, so you don't get a lucky number tomorrow."],["Others might be victims of ill omens or portents of doom, but you can shrug off even the darkest of tidings. Your luck might have faltered temporarily, leaving you in a precarious spot, but you can always trust it to help you set things right. When you would reduce the doomed condition by 1, reduce it by 2 instead. You also gain the Game Face reaction."],["You always have an uncanny knack for understanding your audience. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to [[/act sense-motive rollOption=\"know-your-audience\"]] if your target's attitude toward you is indifferent or better."],["Building perfect luck is a lifelong quest, and you push farther and farther down that shimmering road; you've gained more control over your natural luck than ever before, and you can use it to manipulate your lucky number with greater precision. You can choose your lucky number instead of rolling."],["**Frequency** twice per day\n\n**Trigger** You or an ally you can see within 15 feet rolls a critical failure on a saving throw or skill check.\n\n---\n\nEven when you or your ally's luck seems to run out, it's not as bad as it seems. The triggering critical failure becomes a failure instead."],["**Trigger** You take mental damage or fail a save against a mental effect.\n\n---\n\nThe connections that your horn-cones form are bidirectional, which has left you sensitive to psychic attacks, but you can repurpose your vulnerability into a weapon. The source of the triggering effect takes mental damage equal to your weakness to mental damage."],["Your training under the elite mercenaries in the Vault were brutal for your body and your mind, but they've hardened your constitution and left you with rare expertise. You've done plenty of drills wearing the heaviest equipment, and you're quick to adapt to even the most specialized protective gear. You're trained in heavy armor. Whenever you gain a class feature that grants you expert or greater proficiency in medium armor, you also gain that proficiency in heavy armor."],["When you're psychically harmed, it causes pain you won't soon forget, but you've learned to grab hold of that pain and share it with your psychic attacker, to teach them what it feels like. When you use the Shared Reverb reaction, after you resolve its effects, the targeted creature takes a –1 status penalty to saves against mental effects and has a weakness to mental effects equal to half your level until the end of your next turn.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If the target has resistance (but not immunity) to mental damage, it instead loses its resistance for the duration.\n\nHold the Link"],["Though your psychic abilities still pale in comparison to your ancient worlanisi kin, you've honed the sensitivity of your horn-cones so that you can better triangulate your prey based on stray thoughts hanging in the environment around you. The range of your imprecise thoughtsense increases to 30 feet, and you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to [[/act track rollOption=\"horns-of-the-hunter\"]] thinking creatures that aren't otherwise immune to mental effects."],["Now that you've gained otherworldly control over your own luck, you've learned to share your fortune with your allies. When an ally you can see rolls your lucky number, you can pass the good luck over to them and change their roll to a 20. Doing so counts as using your lucky number for the day."],["Why should you keep all the luck for yourself? When you're a living, breathing good luck charm, it's important to spread the success to your friends, especially when they're in need of a helping hand. When you Aid, as long as you're an expert or better in the skill you're using, failures and critical failures to Aid instead count as successes."],["When a fight is about to break out, it's best to be on your toes; you take a split second to connect with your luck to stay ahead of the game. You can trigger Blue Mood after you roll initiative, in addition to its normal trigger, to reroll your initiative and take the higher of the two results. This counts as a usage of Blue Mood, as normal."],["Your synthetic brain makes it difficult for your enemies to assault your mind while ensuring that your thought processing is as fast as the currents flowing through your circuits. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against mental effects."],["You were originally designed or built by an independent foundry, without some of the restrictions and safety mechanisms that would be in place for most other xenometric android production facilities. Choose one of the following.\n\n- You're one size larger than your ancestry, up to Large. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Intimidation checks to [[/act demoralize]]. Add the Stretching Reach standardized ancestry feat to your available standardized ancestry feats.\n- You're one size smaller than your ancestry but no smaller than Small. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Stealth checks to [[/act hide]] and [[/act sneak]]. Add the Overcrowd standardized ancestry feat to your available standardized ancestry feats.\n- You have an additional pair of limbs but can only have one pair active at a time. You can change which of your limbs are active with the Switch Hands action. Add the All Hands on Deck and Double Draw standardized ancestry feats to your available standardized ancestry feats."],["You can temporarily upload additional skills thanks to your semi-technological nature. During your daily preparations, you become trained in one skill of your choice. This proficiency lasts until you prepare again. Since this proficiency is temporary, you can't use it as a prerequisite for a skill increase or a permanent character option like a feat."],["Your body incorporates a number of magical and technological components, granting you some innate magical power. You gain the Ancestral Cantrip feat from your ancestry or from the android ancestry. You're trained in the skill associated with the tradition of the cantrip you learned this way (Arcana for arcane, Religion for divine, Occultism for occult, or Nature for primal). If you would automatically become trained in that skill (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou pour your nanites into your weapon, empowering its next attacks. The weapon deals electricity damage instead of its normal damage type, and it gains the boost 1d4 trait until the end of your next turn."],["Your nanites form into a network of hardlight projectors to create a protective barrier. You can cast the Shield cantrip as an arcane innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up. When you use the Shield Block reaction granted by the spell, your nanites surge back into your body, allowing you to Step as part of the same reaction."],["Your design is one of the most common ones among your kind, and for good reason; it's robust, durable, and scalable. This gives you incredibly versatility in your development. You gain a general feat of your choice, and you must meet the feat's prerequisites."],["You can use your nanites and their hardlight projectors to form hardlight gear. You can cast Creation as a 5th-rank arcane innate spell once per day. The item you create is a hardlight projection and has no monetary value; it also doesn't need to be made of earthen or plant-derived matter. It can't replicate a specific item, such as the key card to a specific lock, unless you have intricate knowledge of what the specific item looks like and how it works, such as knowing the data that needs to be on the keycard for it to open the lock. It otherwise functions as a mundane item of its kind until your next daily preparations, though it vanishes if you move more than 100 feet away from it."],["The nanites in your synthetic cortex enable you to psychically reach out and grasp a vital part of a creature's anatomy and lift them. Once per day, you can cast Telekinetic Strangulation as a 6th-rank arcane innate spell."],["The nanites in your synthetic cortex surge outward, dynamically connecting to one another to form a network of hardlight plates for 1 minute or until you use an Interact action to return all the nanites into your body. While the nanites are out in this way, you have the following characteristics.\n\n- As a 1-action activity, you can create a 1-foot thick, 5-foot long wall of hardlight in a point you can see within 30 feet. The wall has AC 10, Hardness 30, and 70 Hit Points, and it's immune to critical hits and precision damage. The wall blocks physical effects from passing through it but doesn't block line of sight.\n- You can use your senses as if you were in the position of any of these walls.\n- If a creature is adjacent to one of the hardlight walls while moving, it can spend 5 feet of movement to teleport to a square adjacent to any of the other hardlight walls.\n- While at least one hardlight wall is out, and if you're adjacent to a hardlight wall or it's between you and your attacker, you can use Shield Block as if you had a shield raised, using the hardlight wall's Hardness and Hit Points. The wall disappears after the reaction is used."],["The nanites in your cortex are supercharged, enabling you to hurl objects in your environment. Once per day, you can cast Telekinetic Tantrum as a 9th-rank arcane innate spell."],["You're able to unlock dormant abilities in your design. Choose an android heritage. You gain all of its mechanical effects. You count as having that heritage for the purposes of qualifying for feats."],["You more closely mimic the physiological traits of your ancestry. You gain a heritage from your ancestry in addition to this versatile heritage. If an ability from this new heritage conflicts with an ability from your versatile heritage, you choose which of the conflicting abilities your character has, as normal. You count as having that heritage for the purposes of qualifying for feats."],["Your knowledge of your own constructed anatomy, combined with your experience in combat, helps you take down other constructed foes with greater ease. Against constructs and robots, you gain a circumstance bonus to damage with weapon and unarmed Strikes equal to the number of weapon damage dice."],["You manipulate your nanites more efficiently. When you use Nanite Armament Boost, you automatically Interact to boost the required weapon."],["Your nanites can reshape your synthetic cortex to enable you to communicate mentally with creatures within 30 feet. You can communicate only with creatures that share a language with you. This doesn't give you any access to their thoughts, and it communicates no more information than normal speech would.\n\n---\n\n*SFS Note:* A xenometric android with this feat counts as having limited telepathy for other abilities."],["Your unusual synthetic physiology enables you to resist aliments even better than most constructed or biological organisms. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to saving throws against diseases, poisons, and radiation. If you roll a success on a saving throw against a disease, poison, or radiation, you get a critical success instead.\n\nIf you roll a critical failure on the save, you get a failure instead."],["You gain even greater control over your nanites when using them to power up your weapons. When you use Nanite Armament Boost, your weapon gains the boost d8 trait instead of boost d4."],["The nanites in your synthetic cortex not only enable you to mentally communicate with others, but you can also mentally attack your enemies. You can cast Share Pain and Void Whispers as 3rd-rank arcane innate spells once per day each."],["Your synthetic brain is able to absorb a massive amount of practical knowledge, granting you the ability to accomplish various tasks you aren't specialized in. You gain the Untrained Improvisation general feat. In addition, you can attempt skill actions that normally require you to be an expert, even if you're only untrained or trained."],["You always have an inkling where you can find extended family. You become trained in Diplomacy. If you would automatically become trained in Diplomacy (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. When you attempt to [[/act make-an-impression]] or to make a Request from another ysoki, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your checks."],["You follow Lao Shu Po's teachings and aren't afraid to lie, cheat, or steal to get what you desire. Thanks to your extra devotion, you gain the trained proficiency rank in Deception and Thievery. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou gain the Additional Lore general feat for Lao Shu Po Lore."],["You have an incredibly nimble tail that helps you balance in zero gravity; this could be a hereditary gift from your ancestors as they adapted to spaceflight or the result of personal augmentation. You can use your tail to Push Off while in zero-g without needing a free hand. In addition, you ignore the clumsy and Off-Guard penalties while Untethered in zero gravity."],["You know how to talk down creatures of larger size from making the mistake of attacking your allies. You become trained in Intimidation, or you gain the Intimidating Glare skill feat if you were already trained. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Intimidation checks to [[/act demoralize]] creatures of a larger size than you that attacked an ally since the beginning of your last turn."],["You're resistant to radiation due to long-term exposure triggering changes in your biology. You gain poison resistance equal to your level against damage from radiation effects and a +1 circumstance bonus to Fortitude saves against radiation effects."],["You've had your retinas modified, granting you a permanent HUD that takes reads on your surroundings. You gain an Autorecognition Lens augmentation that can't be removed and that doesn't use an augmentation slot. You become trained in Computers. If you would automatically become trained in Computers (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. Once per day, you can Access Infosphere as a 3-action activity on a creature you're observing with your HUD whose name you've identified."],["You grew up learning to tinker with devices, repair objects, and take things apart. You're trained in Crafting. If you're trained in Crafting from another source (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You can Repair an item without using a repair toolkit without taking the –2 circumstance penalty, improvising tools from whatever you have at hand. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Crafting checks to Repair an item when you have a repair toolkit."],["Years of experience living among ysoki communities have trained your nimble steps and sneaky moves. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Acrobatics and Stealth. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Ysoki Lore."],["You know the best place to keep a firearm is out of sight, and you've adjusted your cheeks for maximum efficiency. It takes 10 minutes to safely prepare a one-handed gun and store it in your cheek pouch, and the gun can be up to 1 Bulk. As a single action, you can Interact to draw and Strike with the gun you stored in your mouth.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Big Mouth ysoki feat, you can store a two-handed gun instead of a one-handed gun, and the gun you store can be up to 2 Bulk instead of the normal amount."],["You've mastered the infamous ysoki martial art of spitting a live grenade from your mouth. It takes 10 minutes to safely prepare a grenade and store it in your cheek pouch. As a single action, you can draw and throw this specially prepared grenade using your mouth. You don't need a free hand to do so."],["You channel your ancestral ability to maximize movement in any situation. You Stride three times."],["**Trigger** An enemy occupying the same space as you uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.\n\n---\n\nYou launch a surprise attack from below. Make a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If your attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, you disrupt that action. This Strike doesn't count toward your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike."],["Your steadfast faith in Grandmother Rat yields more rewards. You gain Divine Decree as a 7th-rank divine innate spell once per day. Additionally, once per month, whenever you would die, your body instead transforms into a swarm of dispersing rats. After 1d6 days, these rats gather in a safe space of the GM's choosing (a site dedicated to Lao Shu Po, if possible) and reform your body. You're returned to life at your maximum Hit Points."],["You've made some dimensional adjustments to your cheek pouches for spacious storing, allowing you to defy the laws of physics. When you store items in your cheek pouches, they no longer significantly alter your speech. You can store up to 10 Bulk of items in your cheek pouches, and items stored in your cheek pouches can have a dimension longer than 1 foot, so long as they could still reasonably fit in your mouth. While stored in your extradimensional pouches, these items are virtually undiscoverable, and the DC to detect the items is equal to the higher of your class DC or spell DC + 10."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You successfully use Stealth to Hide and become Hidden from all your current foes, or use Stealth to Sneak and become undetected to all your current foes.\n\n---\n\nUsing clever technology, magical talent, a divine blessing, or uncanny luck, you slip from sight completely, becoming Invisible for 1 minute, or until you take a hostile action, whichever comes first."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou've realized the truth: that the universe is merely a series of tunnels, each connected individually by quantum particles into a massive and infinite warren. Create two wormholes, one adjacent to you, and one in an unoccupied square within 100 feet, visible to you, and at least 15 feet from the one adjacent to you. You immediately Step through the wormhole adjacent to you and appear at the other wormhole. The wormhole lasts for 1 round before collapsing, but you can Sustain the wormholes for up to 1 minute. Other ysoki can travel through your wormholes as well, but if a non-ysoki creature attempts to enter the wormhole, it automatically collapses."],["You know that sometimes the right answer to technological problems is to simply break something. Attempt a Crafting check against the item's DC or the Fortitude DC of the creature possessing the item if the item is being carried, held, or worn. The target is then temporarily immune to your attempts to Break It for 10 minutes.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The item becomes Glitching 1 for 1 minute.\n\n**Success** The item becomes glitching 1 for 2 rounds.\n\n**Critical Failure** Your attempt backfires. If the target has the glitching condition, reduce the value of its glitching condition by 1."],["When you're physically outmatched, you fight with unexpected ferocity. If a foe of a larger size than you critically hits and damages you, that foe is Off-Guard to you for 1 round."],["You always know where to find family, and family is everything. When you're in a settlement or an area you could conceivably meet another ysoki, you can spend 1 hour asking around to find a cousin of yours. The cousin begins with an attitude of friendly toward you and will grant you simple Requests, so long as they would be reasonable to ask (subject to GM discretion). You can attempt to make a more substantial Request, usually for a favor in exchange. The GM decides the DC based on the difficulty of the favor and the amount of risk it poses to your cousin."],["You can tell especially convincing lies when it comes to protecting others. When you [[/act lie]] to authority figures to protect someone else, you can roll twice and use the better result. If your Lie is found out, you can't use this effect on that authority figure again until you've regained their trust (usually by improving their attitude toward you)."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou're trained in the trick of quickly moving items into your cheek pouches. You Interact to store one held item in your cheek pouches (provided it fits)."],["You're adept at leveraging groups of allies to accomplish your goals. When at least two of your allies are flanking an enemy, that enemy is Off-Guard to your melee attacks."],["You can use your nimble tail to maneuver in zero gravity. You can Float up to your Speed when you Push Off using your tail instead of up to half your Speed. In addition, you can spend your reaction to [[/act grab-an-edge]] at any point in your movement while Floating that you pass adjacent to an object, halting your movement immediately if you succeed at your check."],["Your cheek pouches are especially large and stretchy. Instead of storing up to four items of light Bulk in your cheek pouches, you can store up to 1 Bulk worth of items. The maximum size of a given item is unchanged."],["Your physiology and experience makes you relatively resistant to what makes other creatures nauseated. At the end of each turn you have the Sickened condition, you can attempt to retch to reduce the value of your sickened condition as a free action. In addition, when you spend a single action to retch to reduce the value of your sickened condition, you can choose to retch toward an adjacent creature in an attempt to sicken them.\n\nIf you're successful in reducing your sickened condition, the adjacent creature must attempt a Fortitude save against the same DC of the effect that gave you the sickened condition or your class DC, whichever is lower, becoming Sickened 1 on a failure or Sickened 2 on a critical failure."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou make the sign of Lao Shu Po's eye and curse a creature with inescapable visions from the Netherworld. Choose a creature you can see within 30 feet. The target must attempt a Will save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is Stupefied 1 for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The target is Stupefied 2 for 2 rounds.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is stupefied 2 and Frightened 1 for 1 minute."],["You use your size against larger foes, quickly moving around them to avoid notice or stay out of reach. As long as you're Small, you can end a successful Tumble Through action in a Medium or larger enemy's space. The enemy must have appropriate limbs or otherwise leave you enough room for this maneuver, as determined by the GM. You couldn't, for example, occupy the space of an ooze that matches the full dimensions of the square. While you occupy an enemy's space, that enemy is Off-Guard to you."],["You've internalized your corporation's culture and strategies, and you're knowledgeable about general business practices. You gain the Additional Lore general feat for Business or Corporate Lore.\n\nYou can use Business or Corporate Lore instead of any other skill when making a Recall Knowledge check about subjects related to your work, such as goods your company buys and sells, individuals or settlements where you do business, or industry laws.\n\nAbadarCorp Rep"],["You announce business projections to an ally to benefit them. Make a Business Lore or Corporate Lore check against a DC based on your level. Whether or not you're successful, the target becomes temporarily immune to According to My Calculations for 24 hours. The benefit lasts for 1 minute or until activated.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target gains a +2 circumstance bonus on their next skill check or attack roll.\n\n**Success** The target gains a +1 circumstance bonus on their next skill check or attack roll.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target takes a –1 penalty to their next skill check or attack roll."],["You can share hidden messages using technical business and corporate jargon, using Business or Corporate Lore to disguise the true meaning of your words. Any allies who have traveled alongside you for at least 1 full week or are trained in the same Lore skill automatically discern your meaning. Other observers must succeed at a Perception check against your Business or Corporate Lore DC to realize you're passing a secret message, and they must critically succeed to understand the message."],["Throwing your corporation's name around adds weight to your threats. When you use Intimidation to Coerce or Demoralize a target who knows about your corporation, a success becomes a critical success."],["You call on your extensive network for help with skulduggery. When you Gather Information or Create a Forgery, you do it in half the normal time."],["You've learned to maximize your potential earnings. Whenever you would fail an Earn Income check, you get a success instead."],["You've perfected the art of convincing others to see things your way. You can use [[/act make-an-impression skill=business-lore]]{Business Lore} or [[/act make-an-impression skill=corporate-lore]]{Corporate Lore} to Make an Impression and, on a success or critical success, you shift your target's attitude one step higher. Whether or not Make an Impression is successful, the target becomes temporarily immune to Sales Pitch for 24 hours."],["You've synced and tuned your augmentations, allowing them to power each other. If one of your augmentations is out of limited uses, you can squeeze out one more use by drawing power from other augmentations that haven't expended all of their limited uses or don't have limited uses. The item level of the augmentation used for power must match or exceed the item level of the augmentation powered in this way. Exceeding the powered augmentation's level doesn't give any other benefit. For example, you can power a 3rd-level augmentation with a 5th-level augmentation, but it would still be considered an effect from a 3rd-level item. The augmentations used for power as well as the augmentation powered in this way then lose functionality until your next daily preparations."],["Your body has adapted to perform in perfect harmony with your augmentations. You're permanently Quickened, but you can use this extra action only to Activate an augmentation."],["You've developed a profound connection with your own body with every customized addition to it. You gain the Augmented Body general feat. You increase your implant limit by two."],["You've studied augmentations in depth. You become trained in Medicine. If you were already trained in Medicine, you become an expert instead. When you Implant Augmentation, you can install or remove augmentations in 10 minutes."],["You've learned that to push your augmentations to their limits, you must first hack your own body. By trying out new foods, using supplements, or engaging in esoteric workout routines, you increase the power your body provides to certain augmentations. If you have an augmentation that gives you a type of movement, increase that movement's Speed by 5 feet."],["You can adjust a common augmentation installed on your body during your daily preparations. One action with a daily frequency on that augmentation can be Activated an additional time that day.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat multiple times. For each time you take this feat, you can adjust an additional augmentation."],["All commercially available augmentations are tailor-made to the individual undergoing installation. You have, however, tinkered with your body to the point where you're confident you can accept any augmentation, even one not made for you. You gain the Monster Crafting feat and can use it to gather materials needed to make augmentations to install in yourself. The augmentations must match the type of creature being salvaged, such as a construct for cybernetics, a dragon for magitech, or an undead for necrografts."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** The target is within range of your limited telepathy.\n\n---\n\nYou reach out and sense the surface thoughts of your foe, helping you predict exactly where they're going to be so you can strike true. Attempt a Perception check to [[/act sense-motive]].\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** As success, except your attack also it deals 2 additional precision damage if you're trained in Perception, 4 if you're expert, 6 if you're master, and 8 if you're legendary.\n\n**Success** The next time you make an attack roll against the target, roll twice and use the better result. If your attack is a critical hit, the target is so surprised by the efficacy of your attack that they're also Off-Guard until the beginning of your next turn."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** A creature attacks you while you're Off-Guard to them, you share a language with that creature, and that creature is within range of your limited telepathy.\n\n---\n\nThe very thoughts of your enemies give them away. The triggering attack roll targets your Perception DC instead of your AC. Though this allows you to avoid taking penalties to your AC, it doesn't remove any conditions or other effects causing such penalties. For example, an enemy with sneak attack would still deal extra damage to you for being off-guard."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou spend 10 minutes going over clues you've learned about an investigation to draw a line to a possible solution. Choose a creature you've met and interacted with or studied for at least an hour, or a mystery that you've been investigating for at least a day, and ask a question about that topic that wouldn't normally fall under the purview of Recall Knowledge. The question must be specific and answerable, as determined by the GM. Some examples include, \"Did the tech entrepreneur really kill his assistant?\" or \"Was the hacker collective responsible for the data theft?\" You gain a flash of insight that allows you to know whether or not your line of thinking is on the right track, such as figuring out who to ask next, though you don't receive a definitive answer to your question. The GM determines your flash of insight."],["**Access** member of the Eyeswide Agency\n\n---\n\nThe agency has provided you with some psychic training that helps you question suspects and track down leads. You gain limited telepathy with a range of 30 feet. If you already have limited telepathy, increase its range by 30 feet. You also become an expert in Society and gain the Streetwise skill feat. If you already have the Streetwise skill feat, whenever you use Society to Gather Information and get a critical failure, you get a failure instead."],["You're constantly casting your mind out as you search for clues. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to [[/act sense-motive]] and to [[/act seek]] creatures who aren't immune to mental effects and within range of your limited telepathy, and a +2 circumstance bonus to your Perception DC against such creatures attempting to Lie to you."],["**Requirements** You share a language with the target, who is in range of your limited telepathy.\n\n---\n\nYou mentally ambush a creature. Telepathically ask a question of a non-allied creature that you can see within range of your limited telepathy. The target must attempt a Will saving throw against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. Regardless of the result, the target is temporarily immune to your Psychic Interrogation for 1 hour.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is slightly distracted by your question and can't use reactions until the end of your next turn.\n\n**Failure** The target's mind is consumed by the thought of your question. They can't use reactions until the end of your next turn and are Stupefied 1 for 1 minute. They can end the stupefied condition early by taking an action to telepathically reply to your question. They don't have to answer truthfully, but you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Perception DC if the target attempts to Lie to you, which increases to +4 if you have the Psychic Investigation feat.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the target becomes Stupefied 2."],["To you, the mind is an open book. You can cast Mind Reading as an innate occult spell once per day. Use your Intelligence as your spellcasting attribute for this innate spell if its modifier is higher than your Charisma modifier."],["You can use the Aid reaction to help an ally, even if you haven't prepared to do so. If one or more of your allies are your employees, after you Aid an ally at a skill check that doesn't have the attack trait, you can also Aid any other ally who's also one of your employees who attempts the same skill check for the same purpose that round as a free action rather than a reaction. An ally is also your employee as long as they spend at least one day of Downtime per week Earning Income on behalf of your company. They keep any income they earn, but on a Critical Failure your company's reputation might suffer."],["You've been granted your own administrative assistant who uses drones to deliver you useful items for a nominal fee. You can use Prescient Planner even if you've already used it after purchasing goods, and you can use it as a single action instead of a 2-action activity, during which a corporate drone appears to deliver the item directly into your hand. In addition, five times per day, you can use Prescient Planner to pull out a common consumable item of up to 6 levels lower than your level."],["You become trained in Society and gain the Management Material skill feat. You can use Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation instead of Society to Make an Impression ([[/act make-an-impression skill=deception]], [[/act make-an-impression skill=intimidation]]) or Impersonate ([[/act make-an-impression skill=diplomacy]], [[/act make-an-impression skill=intimidation]]) a professional using Management Material. You can Aid an ally using [[/act aid skill=deception]]{Deception}, [[/act aid skill=diplomacy]]{Diplomacy}, or [[/act aid skill=intimidation]]{Intimidation} instead of any other skill, depending on what style of management you think will help encourage them.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat even if you already have the AbadarCorp Rep Dedication feat and haven't taken two additional AbadarCorp rep archetype feats. Franchise manager archetype feats count as AbadarCorp rep archetype feats, and vice versa, for purposes of completing the archetypes."],["**Trigger** An ally within 30 feet of you critically fails a Strike\n\n---\n\nYou quickly review your ally's strategy and give them the advice they need to improve their performance. The next Strike the triggering ally makes before the end of their turn has the same multiple attack penalty as the critically failed Strike, but it counts toward their multiple attack penalty as normal."],["You use your experience and training as a manager to aggressively compel a foe within 30 feet into believing they've been fired. Roll a Deception check against the target's Will DC. If you're a leader in the organization, you can roll a Diplomacy or Society check instead. The target must be a member of an organization (such a corporation, cult, gang, or military) or working on behalf of that organization. The head of an organization is immune to the effects of Unexpected Downsize.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature becomes Unfriendly to all creatures from the same organization to which it wasn't already Hostile, even those that were previously allies. It treats no one as an ally for 1 minute.\n\n**Success** As success, but the effect ends after 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target knows you're bluffing and becomes immune to your Unexpected Downsize for 24 hours."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou've been promoted to assist a mysterious supervisor who communicates via suspiciously well-timed text messages, infosphere newsreels, or even conveniently placed graffiti that quickly conveys exactly what you need to know to get the job done. When you Recall Knowledge, your benefactor sends you a clue that allows you to make your check with Society instead of any other skill, as well as roll twice and use the better result. If you Recall Knowledge using Business Lore, Corporate Lore, or Society, reduce the frequency of Assistant Regional Manager to once per 10 minutes."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou know that teamwork makes the dream work, so you delegate your task to a teammate. Choose an ally within 30 feet who can perceive you and direct them to complete a simple task, such as attacking a target, moving to a location, or using an item. The creature becomes Quickened for 1 minute and can only use this extra action to Stride, Strike, or Activate an Item. If the target of Delegate completes your direction before the beginning of your next turn, you replenish your use of this feat."],["Your boss provides you with useful gifts emblazoned with the company's logo, even though the delivery seems to cost as much as the actual item. You gain the Prescient Planner and Prescient Consumable general feats. When using Prescient Planner, you can find and draw the item from a worn container as a 2-action activity rather than taking 1 minute. You pick up new gifts the next time you're able to purchase goods."],["You carry so many trinkets around with you that you're only a little heartbroken when they shatter. You can use Treasure on My Heart once per hour instead of once per day."],["You see and step into the liminal spaces that are hidden throughout the Universe. You Stride twice; these Strides do not trigger reactions normally triggered by movement."],["You've grown accustomed to the unpredictable and ever-changing nature of the Ghost Levels. You become trained in Survival or become an expert in it if you were already trained. You gain the Urban Survivalist skill feat.\n\nAdditionally, you've learned how to create and interpret coded symbols used for communication on the Ghost Levels. You learn the Courier Marks language, a language that's only expressed in written symbols. You can always [[/act decipher-writing skill=occultism]] using Occultism."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nDanger gives you a rush. For 1 minute, you ignore the encumbered condition and gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Athletics checks. While you are not encumbered, you gain a +5-foot circumstance bonus to your Speed for the duration."],["You've spent hours going through limdive footage, and now you're an expert at finding hidden details in recordings. You become trained in Computers; if you're already trained, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain the Hologram Skeptic skill feat. Additionally, when you critically fail your check to Decipher Writing, Recall Knowledge, or [[/act seek]] by watching recorded footage, you fail instead."],["You know how to spot trouble. When using the Scout exploration activity, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your initiative roll instead of +1, but your allies still only receive a +1.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have Incredible Initiative, you instead gain a +3 circumstance bonus to your initiative when using the Scout exploration activity."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** You're adjacent to a vertical surface, such as a wall.\n\n---\n\nYou Stride. This Stride does not trigger reactions normally triggered by movement. You can move through other creatures' spaces as though you were Tiny. During this Stride, if you're ever not adjacent to the required surface, your Stride ends.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you're Untethered, you can Step Between as long as you're touching any surface. You ignore the untethered condition during your Stride as part of this action."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You would take damage from a Strike.\n\n**Requirements** You have at least one item of L Bulk.\n\n---\n\nAs your life flashes before your eyes, you realize one of the trinkets you've been hoarding can soften the incoming blow. You gain resistance to the triggering damage equal to your level, and one item of L Bulk of your choice on your person is destroyed."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You would be reduced to 0 Hit Points but not immediately killed.\n\n---\n\nThis isn't your last limdive. You avoid being knocked out and remain at 1 Hit Point, and your Wounded condition increases by 1. For the next minute, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your AC and a +5-foot status bonus to your Speed."],["You know how to throw your grenades to deal severe structural damage. All grenades you throw gain the razing trait."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou Quick Toss twice. Any creature in the area of the first grenade gains a +2 circumstance bonus to its saving throw against the second grenade.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the primary target class feature, you can select a primary target for only one of the two grenades you throw, not both."],["You specialize in throwing highly explosive portable ordnances. You become trained with grenades. You gain the Quick Toss action.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the soldier archetype dedication feat, you can take this feat even if you haven't taken two additional soldier archetype feats. Soldier archetype feats count as grenadier archetype feats, and vice-versa, for purposes of completing the archetypes."],["You can throw grenades a ridiculously long distance while maintaining accuracy. When you throw a grenade, it has a range of 140 feet, instead of the usual 70 feet."],["You count grenades as an area weapon with the area (burst) trait for the purposes of all soldier feats and class features, including primary target and suppressing fire. If you're holding a grenade, you meet the requirements for soldier feats that require you to wield an area weapon.\n\nWhen you use primary target with a grenade, the grenade counts as a simple thrown weapon with expend 0, the area (burst) trait, and a range of 70 feet (or 140 feet if you have the Long Thrower feat). The Strike against the grenade's primary target deals one damage die of the same dice size and damage type dealt by the grenade. This damage increases to two damage dice if the grenade is advanced or superior, to three damage dice if the grenade is elite or ultimate, or to four damage dice if the grenade is paragon. If the grenade doesn't usually deal damage, it doesn't deal damage using primary target."],["You can put just the right spin on your grenade tosses to avoid hitting your friends or yourself. Whenever you Area Fire a grenade, you can select up to four creatures within the grenade's area; these creatures are unaffected by the grenade until the end of the Area Fire action."],["You know how to take advantage of your enemies getting distracted by your explosions. A creature that fails or critically fails a saving throw against a grenade you throw additionally becomes Off-Guard against the next attack you make against it before the end of your turn."],["You can bounce grenades off solid surfaces up to three times before they explode, rather than once. You don't need to see the surfaces, but you do need to have a general idea of where they are. If the grenade hits a solid surface you didn't expect to be there, it explodes. For example, if you toss a grenade down a hall you can't see completely, the grenade will bounce off the hall's walls and doors but would explode if it hit a chair or a janitor's cart."],["When you're fully decked out in your Hellknight regalia, just the presence of your fearsome visage drives enemies back. Attempt an Intimidation check against an enemy within 30 feet who can perceive you.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** You push your target up to 10 feet away from you. You can Stride after it, but you must move the same distance and in the same direction.\n\n**Success** You push your target back 5 feet. You can Stride after it, but you must move the same distance and in the same direction."],["Your infernal countenance is a scourge. You gain expert proficiency in Intimidation (or in another skill in which you're trained of your choice if you were already an expert in Intimidation). You become trained in light armor and medium armor. If you already were trained in light armor and medium armor, you gain training in heavy armor as well. Whenever you gain a class feature that grants you expert or greater proficiency in any type of armor (but not unarmored defense), you also gain that proficiency in the armor types granted to you by this feat. You gain the armor specialization effects of that armor and one additional armor upgrade. Your resistance (or reduction from critical hits) from that armor's specialization is 1 higher than normal and you gain an item bonus to Intimidation checks equal to 1 + your armor's resilience value.\n\n### Hellknight Orders\n\n| Hellknight Order | Edicts | Infernal Damage and Resistance |\n|---|---|---|\n| Order of the Chain | punish lawbreakers | electricity |\n| Order of the Crucible | test civilizations | cold |\n| Order of the Eclipse | control dangerous information | void |\n| Order of the Pyre | purge subversive media with fire | fire |\n\nHellknight"],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou infuse your weapons with the might of Hell. For the next minute, on your first weapon Strike each round, you gain a status bonus to damage equal to twice the number of weapon damage dice; this extra damage is determined by your chosen Hellknight order."],["Armor you wear gains the bulwark trait. You become trained in heavy armor, or become an expert in heavy armor if you were already trained. Your Hellknight regalia grants you resistance equal to half your level when you wear it, determined by your chosen Hellknight order."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** wearing armor customized with Hellknight regalia.\n\n---\n\nYour armor unleashes a gout of hellfire in a 30-foot cone, dealing (level)d6 @actor.flags.system.hellknight.order-damage damage per level of a type determined by your chosen Hellknight order (basic Reflex); a creature takes spirit damage instead if that would be more detrimental (as determined by the GM)."],["You excel at junkomancy, the art of magically sculpting trash into less-useless trash. You have researched junkomancy extensively and can even cast junk spells beyond the magical traditions of your peers. You become an expert in Crafting. Add one common junk spell of any rank you can cast to your spell list. Whenever you gain another junkomancer feat, add another common junk spell of a rank you can cast to your spell list."],["You fabricate potent ammunition from everyday scrap. As part of your daily preparations, you create up to 10 projectiles and 1 commercial battery per character level. When you create the ammunition, choose if the ammunition counts as cold iron or silver for the purposes of applying immunities, weaknesses, and resistances. Any unexpended ammunition you created reverts into useless junk 24 hours later."],["You're a wiz at forging armor from junk. During your daily preparations, you can review the formula of one armor upgrade in your formula book of your level or lower. Until your next daily preparations, whenever you cast *junk armor*, you can Install this Upgrade even if there are no available upgrade slots. If you're a master in Crafting, you gain the armor specialization effect of any *junk armor* you wear."],["The weapons you cobble together are bigger, meaner, and junkier. During your daily preparations, you can review the formula of one weapon upgrade in your formula book of your level or lower. Until your next daily preparations, whenever you cast *junk weapon*, you can Install this Upgrade even if there are no available upgrade slots. If you're a master in Crafting, you gain access to the critical specialization effects of weapons you create using *junk weapon*."],["You magically assemble a barricade using nearby items, junk and scrap. The barricade occupies a 5-foot square and provides lesser cover for you and one ally, though you can [[/act take-cover]] to increase this benefit to standard cover. The barricade has Hardness 15 and 54 HP. When destroyed, the junk barricade creates an area of clutter that is difficult terrain."],["Ammunition you create from scrap and trash is imbued with more special properties. When you create junk ammo as part of your daily preparations, choose two precious materials from the following list: abysium, adamantine, aucturnite, cold iron, siccatite, or silver. The ammunition created with this feat counts as both materials for the purposes of applying immunities, weaknesses, and resistances."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou channel your spirit into a mighty barrage from a celestial plasma cannon. Iomedae's barrage Auto-Fires in a 15-foot cone or a 30-foot line, dealing (floor(level/2 - 1))d6 fire plus (floor(level/2 - 1))d6 spirit damage with the holy trait (Reflex). At 12th level and every 2 levels thereafter, the fire and spirit damage each increase by 1d6. A creature that gets a critical failure on this Reflex save is also Blinded for 1 round."],["You touch an adjacent ally who is affected by a spell or other magical effect with the mental trait due to failing a Will save and has a duration of no longer than 1 minute. That ally can immediately attempt a Will save against the effect's DC, ending the condition on a success. This can't end the effect for any creatures other than your target ally. Regardless of the result of the save, your ally is temporarily immune to Iomedae's Helm for 10 minutes."],["You manifest your faith as a shield. Your armor and the armor of up to five allies you can see within 30 feet gains the benefits of an activated Tactical Force Field upgrade with 14 Hit Points that replenishes 2 Hit Points on your turn but does not protect from critical hits like a normal force field. The force field lasts for one minute. After receiving the benefits of Iomedae's Shield, you and your allies are immune to the effect for one hour.\n\nAt level 10, this becomes a Superior Force Field with 26 HP and replenishes 5 Hit Points on your turn, and at level 16, this becomes an Ultimate Force Field with 37 HP and replenishes 7 Hit Points on your turn."],["You've trained to fight the ancient enemies of lost Golarion. When you deal damage to a demon, devil, dragon, or undead with a weapon, you deal persistent spirit damage with the holy trait equal to the number of weapon damage dice. When you deal damage to one of these creatures with a spell cast from a spell slot that does not have a duration, you deal persistent spirit damage with the holy trait equal to the spell's rank."],["You have familiarity with all weapons in the sword weapon group. For the purposes of proficiency, treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons. If you are at least expert, you gain that weapon's critical specialization effect. You've studied lost Golarion's ancient cultures. You become trained in two of the following that you were not already trained in: Golarion Lore, Iomedae Lore, or a Lore skill associated with an ancestry or culture from Lost Golarion, such as Goblin, Halfling, Human, or Orc.\n\nKnight of Golarion"],["You gain the Adaptive Talent class feature, but you do not gain additional skill feats at higher levels.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat a second time as a 10th level feat and a 16th level feat, increasing the number of skill feats you gain using adaptive talent by 1."],["You gain one envoy feat. For the purpose of meeting its prerequisites, your envoy level is equal to half your character level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time you select it, you gain another envoy feat."],["You gain a 1st- or 2nd-level envoy feat of your choice."],["You gain the Envoy Directives class feature, but do not gain the Lead by Example benefits of the Get 'Em! envoy directive. You become trained in Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation plus another skill of your choice. If you were already trained in Deception, Diplomacy, and Intimidation, you instead become trained in an additional skill of your choice. You also become trained in envoy class DC.\n\nEnvoy"],["You gain the Leader's Confidence class feature."],["You gain the Lead by Example benefit for your Get 'Em! directive, except you and your allies get a +2 status bonus to damage on both the initial and subsequent Strikes."],["You gain one mechanic feat. For the purpose of meeting its prerequisites, your mechanic level is equal to half your character level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time you select it, you gain another mechanic feat."],["You gain a 1st- or 2nd-level mechanic feat of your choice."],["You become an expert in mechanic class DC, and in Computers or Crafting. If you're already an expert in those skills, you instead become an expert in another skill you're trained in."],["You gain the custom rig and exocortex class features, but you can't Modify your exocortex, and you don't gain the unique mods granted by your exocortex. You become trained in Computers and Crafting. If you were already trained in Computers and Crafting, you instead become trained in an additional skill of your choice. You also become trained in mechanic class DC."],["You gain the mechanic's ingenuity class feature. However, you gain the listed benefits at 6th and 14th level."],["You gain the mobile exocortex class feature."],["You gain the modify class feature. In addition, you can Modify your exocortex (as noted in your exocortex class feature), and you gain the unique mods granted by your exocortex.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you're at least 10th level, you can select this feat a second time to gain the damage customizations class feature."],["You gain the remote mods class feature. However, you don't get the additional benefits usually acquired at 15th level."],["You gain one mystic feat. For the purpose of meeting its prerequisites, your mystic level is half your character level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time you do, you gain another mystic feat."],["You gain your connection's initial epiphany spell. If you don't already have one, you also gain a focus pool of 1 Focus Point, which you can Refocus by reflecting on your connection."],["You gain the Basic Spellcasting benefits. Each time you gain a spell slot of a new rank from the mystic archetype, add a spell of the appropriate spell rank to your repertoire: a common spell of your connection's tradition, or one of your connection's granted spells."],["You gain a 1st- or 2nd-level mystic feat."],["Increase the number of spells in your repertoire and number of spell slots you gain from mystic archetype feats by 1 for each spell rank other than your two highest mystic spell slots."],["You gain the Expert Spellcasting benefits."],["You gain the Master Spellcasting benefits."],["Choose a Connection. You become trained in the connection's skill or, if you were already trained, you become trained in a skill of your choice. You don't gain any other abilities from your choice of connection. You gain the Mystic Bond class feature.\n\nYou cast spells like a mystic and gain the Cast a Spell activity. You gain a spell repertoire with two common cantrips from the spell list granted by your connection, from the spells granted by your connection, or any other cantrips of that tradition you learn or discover. You're trained in the spell attack modifier and spell DC statistics. Your key spellcasting attribute for mystic archetype spells is Wisdom, and they are mystic spells of your connection's tradition.\n\nMystic"],["You gain a Vitality Network with 10 Hit Points and can use Transfer Vitality to transfer up to 10 HP. Increase the maximum capacity of your vitality network by 10 at 10th, 15th, and 20th-level. Increase the amount you can transfer by 5 at 5th, 10th, 15th, and 20th-level."],["You gain one operative feat. For the purpose of meeting its prerequisites, your operative level is half your character level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time you do, you gain another operative feat."],["You gain a 1st- or 2nd-level operative feat."],["Your proficiency ranks for simple and martial guns increase to expert."],["Your proficiency rank for Perception increases to master."],["You become trained in simple and martial guns. You become trained in operative class DC.\n\nYou gain the Aim action, it doesn't deal additional damage, but still reduces the bonus to AC your mark gains from cover (which does not increase as you gain levels).\n\nOperative"],["You gain the exploit of your chosen specialization."],["You gain 3 additional Hit Points for each operative archetype class feat you have. As you continue selecting operative archetype class feats, you continue to gain additional Hit Points in this way."],["Your ranged Strikes against the target of your Aim using the required ranged weapon deal an additional 1d4 precision damage until the end of your turn. This damage increases to 2d4 at 6th level."],["Choose a specialization. You become trained in one skill determined by your specialization; if you were already trained in that skill, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You gain a skill feat associated with that skill. You don't gain any other benefits from your specialization."],["You gain one solarian feat. For the purpose of meeting its prerequisites, your solarian level is half your character level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time you do, you gain another solarian feat."],["You gain a 1st- or 2nd-level solarian feat."],["You can create and maintain a solar flare, but do not add your Strength modifier to damage rolls with your solar flare or any additional benefits based on your attunement."],["Your proficiency ranks for solar flare, solar weapon, and your solarian class DC increases to expert."],["You gain the Nimbus Surge reaction, but do not gain any additional benefits based on your attunement."],["You can select up to one trait for your solar weapon. When you reach level 6, you can choose a second trait, or the reach or two-hand 1d10 trait instead of two traits."],["You gain the stellar attunement class feature, but you do not Attune as a free action when you roll initiative. You become trained in solar flare, solar weapon, and solarian class DC.\n\nYou can manifest a solar weapon. Your weapon has the attuned and solarian traits, but you can't select additional traits and it gains no benefits based on your attunement. You gain the Re-Forge Solar Weapon action.\n\nSolarian"],["You gain 3 additional Hit Points for each solarian archetype class feat you have. As you continue selecting solarian archetype class feats, you continue to gain additional Hit Points in this way."],["You gain one soldier feat. For the purpose of meeting its prerequisites, your soldier level is half your character level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time you do, you gain another soldier feat."],["You gain a 1st- or 2nd-level soldier feat."],["You gain the primary target class feature."],["You become trained in Intimidation. If you were already trained in Intimidation, you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. Increase your maximum and encumbered Bulk limits by 2. You become trained in soldier class DC.\n\nYou become trained in light armor and medium armor. If you already were trained in light armor and medium armor, you gain training in heavy armor as well. Whenever you gain a class feature that grants you expert or greater proficiency in any type of armor (but not unarmored defense), you also gain that proficiency in the armor types granted to you by this feat. If you have a class feature that grants you expert proficiency in unarmored defense and you're 13th level or higher, you also become an expert in the armor types granted to you by this feat.\n\nSoldier"],["You gain 3 additional Hit Points for each soldier archetype class feat you have. As you continue selecting soldier archetype class feats, you continue to gain additional Hit Points in this way."],["Your proficiency rank in Fortitude saves increases to master."],["You gain the suppressing fire class feature."],["You gain one technomancer feat. For the purpose of meeting its prerequisites, your technomancer level is half your character level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time you do, you gain another technomancer feat."],["You gain your programming language's initial magic hack spell. If you don't already have one, you also gain a focus pool of 1 Focus Point."],["You gain the basic spellcasting benefits. Each time you gain a spell slot of a new rank from the technomancer archetype, add two common arcane spells of the appropriate spell rank to your database."],["You gain a 1st- or 2nd-level technomancer feat of your choice."],["You gain the expert spellcasting benefits."],["You gain your programming language's firmware enhancement."],["You gain the jailbreak spell class feature. You gain the spellshape and basic jailbreak benefit listed in your programming language."],["You gain the master spellcasting benefits."],["You gain your programming language's Overclock Pulse action. After you use this action, your gear stops being overclocked."],["Your repertoire expands. Increase the number of spells in your database and the number of spell slots you gain from technomancer archetype feats by 1 for each spell rank other than your two highest technomancer spell slots."],["Choose a programming language. You gain the Overclock Gear action. You gain your programming language's overclock boost benefits as if you were a 1st-level technomancer.\n\nYou cast spells like a technomancer, gaining a spell database with two common arcane cantrips of your choice. You gain access to the Cast a Spell activity. You're trained in the spell attack modifier and spell DC statistics. Your key spellcasting attribute for technomancer archetype spells is Intelligence, and they're arcane technomancer spells."],["You gain one witchwarper feat. For the purpose of meeting its prerequisites, your witchwarper level is half your character level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time you do, you gain another witchwarper feat."],["Your disruptive powers grow. You gain a 1st- or 2nd-level witchwarper feat."],["Your quantum field gains the effect of your chosen paradox."],["You gain your paradox's initial warp spell. If you don't already have one, you also gain a focus pool of 1 Focus Point, which you can Refocus by contemplating infinite worlds. (For more on warp spells, see page 165.)"],["You gain the Basic Spellcasting benefits. Each time you gain a spell slot of a new rank from the witchwarper archetype, add a spell of the appropriate spell rank to your repertoire: a common spell of your paradox's tradition, or one of your paradox's granted spells."],["You gain the Expert Spellcasting benefits."],["You gain the Master Spellcasting benefits."],["Your repertoire expands, and you can cast more spells of your paradox's tradition each day. Increase the number of spells in your repertoire and number of spell slots you gain from witchwarper archetype feats by 1 for each spell rank other than your two highest witchwarper spell slots."],["Choose a paradox. You become trained in the paradox's skill or, if you were already trained, you become trained in a skill of your choice. You gain the Warp Reality action, but your quantum field is a 10-foot burst.\n\nYou cast spells like a witchwarper. You gain access to the Cast a Spell activity. You gain a spell repertoire with two common cantrips from the spell list associated with your paradox, from the spells granted by your paradox, or any other cantrips of that tradition you learn or discover. You're trained in the spell attack modifier and spell DC statistics. Your key spellcasting attribute for witchwarper archetype spells is your choice of Intelligence or Charisma, and they are witchwarper spells of your paradox's tradition. You don't gain any other abilities from your choice of paradox.\n\nWitchwarper"],["You've upgraded your nanites to be able to form even more complex weapons. When you use Alteration Array, add the following traits to those you can choose from for your nanite unarmed attack: backswing, grapple, or kickback. In addition, you can choose to give your nanite unarmed attack one of the following traits instead of choosing two from the normal list: boost (1d8), deadly (1d8), or reach."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nWhen faced with danger, your nanites can envelop your body in a shimmering metallic armor. You gain the effects of a 5th-rank Elemental Form spell, except that you must choose either metal or water as your element, and you gain weakness 10 to electricity while the effect is active. At 14th level, you gain the effects of a 6th-rank *elemental form* spell, and at 18th level, you gain the effects of a 7th-rank *elemental form* spell."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYour nanites knit together wounds. You or another creature within 10 feet of you gains fast healing equal to half your level for 1 minute, then becomes temporarily immune to Repair Array for 24 hours. If the creature takes electricity damage, the fast healing ends immediately."],["**Requirements** Your Cloud Array is active.\n\n---\n\nYou command your nanites to sweep across the battlefield, damaging your enemies. You extend the duration of the cloud created by your Cloud Array until the end of your next turn, then you can move each square of the cloud up to 10 feet. The squares must each be contiguous to at least one other square of the cloud when the movement is complete. Until the start of your next turn, enemies that start their turn in the cloud take (floor(level/4))d6 acid damage with a basic Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. At 16th level and every four levels thereafter, increase the acid damage by 1d6."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You or a creature within 10 feet would be reduced to 0 Hit Points but not immediately killed.\n\n---\n\nTo well-programmed nanites, a body is simply another array to assemble. The triggering creature and its equipment are engulfed in a thick nanite mist and vanish, reappearing in a free space within 30 feet. The target remains at 1 Hit Point, gains a number of temporary Hit Points equal to your level for 1 minute, then becomes Wounded 1 or increases the value of its wounded condition by 1."],["Your body is infused with nanites programmed to execute specific protocols called arrays. During your daily preparations, you can register one or more pieces of equipment in your possession as nanocyte gear until your next daily preparations. You can't have more registered nanocyte gear than the number of nanocyte archetype feats you have, and no piece of nanocyte gear can have a Bulk greater than your Constitution modifier.\n\nYour nanites completely cover your registered nanocyte gear, allowing it to be harmlessly broken down and stored within your body. While stowed, your nanocyte gear is hidden from inspection that can't detect nanites. If your registered nanocyte gear is more than 10 feet away from you at the end of your turn, it turns into its nanite form and returns to your body, stowed. If you are knocked Unconscious or die, stowed nanocyte gear appears in your space, fully formed.\n\nIn addition, you gain the Gear Array action.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can use Gear Array as a free action triggered when you roll for initiative."],["Your nanites shape your body into a fluid weapon with customized features as you require them. When you use this action, you gain a nanite unarmed attack for 1 minute. Your nanite unarmed attack deals 1d6 damage, has the tech trait, and is in the brawling group. When you use this action, choose from bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing, and choose two of the following traits: finesse, forceful, razing, shove, or trip. Your nanite unarmed attack deals that type of damage and has those traits.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can use Alteration Array as a free action triggered when you roll for initiative instead of using Gear Array."],["Your nanites become a silvery cloud. The cloud covers a number of contiguous 5-foot squares equal to your Constitution modifier, at least one of which must be adjacent to you. It persists for 1 round and grants all creatures within lesser cover."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** You're hit by a Strike.\n\n---\n\nYour nanites surge out of your body to form a shield. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to your level that last until the start of your next turn."],["Your nanites are infused with magic to recreate spell effects. Choose two common cantrips from the arcane spell list. You can cast those cantrips as arcane innate spells at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYour nanites shoot forth and wrap around the limbs of a creature within 10 feet, binding them together with a powerful magnetic force. The target must attempt a Reflex save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is Off-Guard to the next attack made against it.\n\n**Failure** As success, and the creature is Suppressed until the end of its next turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** As success, and the creature is suppressed until the end of its next turn and knocked Prone."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a melee weapon registered as nanocyte gear, or you have a nanite unarmed attack.\n\n---\n\nYou attack and infect your target, eroding them and hampering their movements from within. Attempt a melee Strike with the required weapon or unarmed attack. If you hit and deal damage, the target takes an additional 1d4 persistent acid damage and becomes Clumsy 1 for 1 round. On a critical hit, the target becomes Clumsy 2 instead."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou unleash your nanites in a wave of metal. Enemies in a 15-foot cone take (floor(level/2))d6 bludgeoning damage and must attempt a Fortitude save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. Increase the bludgeoning damage by 1d6 at 8th level and every two levels thereafter.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage and is knocked back 5 feet away from you.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is knocked back 10 feet away from you.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and is knocked back 15 feet away from you."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYour nanites disperse your consciousness and body into a cloud, allowing you to transcend the limits of your physical frame. You gain the effects of a 3rd-rank Vapor Form spell for 1 minute or until you Dismiss the effect."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** Your turn begins.\n\n---\n\nYour nanites move as rapidly as your thoughts. You become Quickened until the end of your turn and can use the extra action only to use Alteration Array or Gear Array."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYour nanites refract light and reflect sound. If your next action is to use Cloud Array, creatures within the cloud are Concealed in addition to gaining lesser cover, and creatures outside the cloud are concealed to those within it."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nAs part of your daily preparations, you make a motivating speech to 10 or fewer allies. Your allies must be able to perceive you during this time, but this doesn't otherwise impede their own preparation. When one of these allies is reduced to 0 Hit Points and isn't immediately killed, you can call out to them to ignite their sense of duty. The creature avoids being knocked out and remains at 1 Hit Point, and its Wounded condition increases by 1. Additionally, it gains a +5 foot status bonus to its Speed until the end of its next turn and a +1 status bonus to its first attack before the end of its next turn.\n\nHold the Line"],["Your iconic armored silhouette has become a beacon of hope for the people you protect. As long as you are wearing armor with Peacekeeper Adornments, you can cast Command as an innate divine spell once per hour, heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level."],["You speak a powerful line that emphasizes your convictions and unwillingness to give up. You and each of your allies that heard or saw you gains temporary Hit Points equal to your level and a +1 status bonus to Will saves, AC, and attacks until the start of your next turn.\n\nSomething to Protect"],["You make peace with a grin and a gun. You become trained in Society or become an expert in it if you were already trained. You have familiarity with weapons with the nonlethal trait—for the purpose of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["You're trained in Mission Lore, a special Lore skill that can be used only to Recall Knowledge, but on any topic related to an assignment, mission, or quest performed on behalf of another individual or organization. If you fail a check to Recall Knowledge with Mission Lore, you get the effects of the Dubious Knowledge skill feat unless the question was already answered during a mission briefing. If you have legendary proficiency in Society, you gain expert proficiency in Mission Lore, but you can't increase your proficiency rank in Mission Lore by any other means."],["You avoid harm when you can help it. During your daily preparations, you can designate a weapon on your person. It gains the nonlethal trait while you wield it. If you designate a new weapon during daily preparations, the previously designated weapon loses the nonlethal trait.\n\nNonlethal Force"],["You can alter offensive spells to be less deadly. If your next action is to Cast a Spell that deals damage and doesn't have the death or void trait, that spell gains the nonlethal trait."],["You customize your armor with the symbols and seals of your command. You treat medium armor as light armor when determining your proficiency, and you treat heavy armor as medium armor. You customize your armor with Peacekeeper Adornments, gaining the armor specialization effects of that armor. While wearing this armor, you gain an item bonus to Intimidation checks equal to your armor's resilience value."],["You've drilled with countless weapons. You become trained in all martial weapons. If you're already trained in martial weapons, you become expert in a single weapon you're trained in.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time you do, you become expert in a weapon you're trained in."],["You study and brew medicine to treat patients. You become an expert in Medicine, and you gain the Serum Crafting feat, even if you don't meet the prerequisites. You can use Medicine instead of Crafting to Craft medical consumables.\n\nEach day during your daily preparations, you can make four medical consumables with an item level up to your level. You must know each item's formula. An item created this way is a temporary item and loses its potency the next time you make your daily preparations if you haven't already used it."],["You know how to effectively and safely administer medication in dire situations. You Interact to draw a medical consumable and Activate it.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Inject Serum skill feat, you can use Efficient Medicator as a 2-action activity to Interact to draw a hypopen or serum, Interact to load that consumable into an injection weapon you're holding, then Strike with that weapon."],["You've learned how to apply engineering and necromancy to help heal constructs and undead. Medical consumables you create with Pharmacologist Dedication during your daily preparations affect constructs (if you're trained in Crafting) and undead (if you're trained in Religion) as if they were living creatures."],["You know how to use the tools of your trade so well you're capable of using weapons with similar features to defend yourself. You gain access to all uncommon weapons with the injection trait and all uncommon weapons in the knife weapon group. For the purposes of proficiency, you treat any injection and knife weapons that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons. When wielding a simple weapon with the injection trait or in the knife group, you increase the damage die size of that weapon by one step.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with an injection weapon or a weapon in the knife group, you get its critical specialization effect."],["You've made further medical advances, enabling you to make a greater number of medical consumables every day. You can create two additional medical consumables during your daily preparations.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat a second time."],["By winning the trust of a panicking patient, you can apply world-class care. Whenever you use a medical consumable that restores a creature's Hit Points or removes a condition, that creature gains temporary Hit Points equal to the item's level for 1 minute. The target is then immune to Crisis Care for 10 minutes."],["**Requirements** You're holding a medical consumable.\n\n---\n\nYou can weave magic and medicine together to save lives. If your next action is to Cast a Spell with the healing trait, you can expend a medical consumable you're holding. One willing target affected by your spell is also affected by the medical consumable."],["When you Raise a Shield, you can raise up to two shields at once. Additionally, at the start of each of your turns, you gain an additional reaction that you can use only to Shield Block."],["**Trigger** An opponent casting a spell that targets you critically fails a spell attack roll against your AC.\n\n**Requirements** You have a shield raised.\n\n---\n\nMake a ranged attack roll against the attacker using your highest proficiency with a ranged weapon. If you cast spells, you can choose to make a spell attack roll instead. If you succeed, your opponent takes the effects of a successful spell attack roll for their own spell (or the effects of a critical success if your attack roll was a critical success)."],["Whether to protect yourself or your allies, your training emphasizes effective use and maintenance of shields. You gain the Shield Block general feat and the Quick Repair skill feat. Whenever you successfully Repair a shield, you restore additional Hit Points to the shield equal to your level."],["You can use your shield to protect yourself from explosions and other area attacks. You can use the Shield Block reaction while you have your shield raised and you would take physical damage from an area effect, even if that effect isn't an attack, in addition to its usual trigger. When you do, if you're between any allies and the source of the damage (the origin of a line or cone or the center of a burst or emanation), you prevent damage to those allies up to the shield's Hardness.\n\nYou can use Area Defender to Shield Block area effects that deal energy damage if you can Shield Block when you would take energy damage from an attack, such as with the Energetic Defender feat or a shield with the blocking trait."],["Your shield blocks more than just projectiles. You can use the Shield Block reaction while you have your shield raised and you would take energy damage from an attack, in addition to its usual trigger. Whenever you Shield Block with a shield that has the blocking trait for the same type of damage you would take, that shield gains the deflecting trait for that damage type against the triggering attack."],["**Requirements** You have your shield raised.\n\n---\n\nYou keep your guard up and Stride up to half your Speed; and this movement doesn't trigger reactions."],["When you have a shield raised, you can use your Shield Block reaction when an attack is made against an ally adjacent to you. If you do, the shield prevents that ally from taking damage instead of preventing you from taking damage, following the normal rules for Shield Block."],["**Requirements** You are wielding a gun and a melee weapon with the agile trait or a phase cutlass, each in a different hand.\n\n---\n\nAdvancing with blade and pistol in hand, you make a ranged Strike, move up to your Speed, and make a melee Strike, each using your current multiple attack penalty and both at the same target. This counts as two attacks when calculating your multiple attack penalty."],["**Trigger** An adjacent enemy attempts a melee Strike against you.\n\n**Requirements** You are wielding a gun and a melee weapon with the agile trait or a phase cutlass.\n\n---\n\nYou parry the triggering Strike with your melee weapon, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to your AC against the attack. If the triggering Strike is a critical failure, you may attempt a ranged Strike against the triggering creature. This ranged Strike does not trigger reactions from the target."],["**Trigger** You reduce an enemy to 0 Hit Points with a phase cutlass.\n\n---\n\nYour phase cutlass steals some of the enemy's vitality, press-ganging it into eternal servitude. As long as you are wielding a Phase Cutlass with stolen vitality, you can cast Wisp Ally as a divine innate spell at will, heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level. Using *wisp ally* this way requires and permanently releases one soul press-ganged with your phase cutlass. The first time each round you Strike with your phase cutlass, you immediately gain the effects of the Sustain a Spell action, which you can use only to extend the duration of and control a *wisp ally* spell cast using that phase cutlass."],["As a plunder-seeking spacefarer, you become trained in Piloting, or become an expert in it if you were already trained. You have familiarity with all cutlasses, flails, rapiers, and weapons with the razing trait. For the purposes of proficiency, treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons. If you are at least expert, you gain that weapon's critical specialization effect.\n\nAdditionally, you gain the Holo-Roger action.\n\nSpace Pirate"],["After countless unexpected encounters you've developed a second sense for danger. You can perform the Scout exploration activity at the same time as the Avoid Notice, Investigate, or Search exploration activity. The bonus to initiative you grant when you Scout is +2 instead of +1."],["Coming prepared to mission briefings gives you extra time to ask questions and research a topic relevant to your next adventure. You are trained in Mission Lore, a special Lore skill that can be used only to Recall Knowledge, but on any topic related to an assignment, mission, or quest performed on behalf of another individual or organization. If you fail a check to Recall Knowledge with Mission Lore, you get the effects of the Dubious Knowledge skill feat unless the question was already answered during a mission briefing. If you have legendary proficiency in Society, you gain expert proficiency in Mission Lore, but you can't increase your proficiency rank in Mission Lore by any other means."],["You are a trained agent of the Starfinder Society. You become an expert in Society. You gain the Additional Lore feat for Starfinder Society Lore; if you were already trained in Starfinder Society Lore, you also become trained in a Lore skill of your choice.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat if you have the Xenoarchaeologist Archetype Dedication feat even if you haven't taken two additional xenoarchaeologist feats. Xenoarchaeologist archetype feats count as Starfinder field agent feats, and vice-versa, for purposes of completing the archetypes.\n\nStarfinder Field Agent"],["The Starfinder Society provides you with provisions to aid you on your adventures. Each day during your daily preparations while you're in a settlement, a Starfinder Society delivery drone delivers two consumable items with an item level no higher than half your level. The drone might not be able to arrive if you're in a remote location or based on GM's discretion. If you receive a subsequent delivery and have items remaining from the prior delivery, you must return any unused consumables to the drone before receiving new stock."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Requirements** You are holding a repair kit, or you are wearing it and have a hand free.\n\n---\n\nYou've meticulously prepared your gear to allow for quick adjustments in the field without damaging any delicate components. You draw and Install an Upgrade into a wielded weapon or worn armor. You can uninstall and stow an upgrade as part of this activity. If you have master proficiency in Crafting, you can Install two upgrades."],["You can use [[/act disable-device skill=mission-lore]]{Mission Lore} instead of Computers or Thievery to disable traps in locations you researched using Mission Briefing. You can disable traps that require a proficiency rank of master in Computers or Thievery. If you have master proficiency in Computers or Thievery, you can disable traps that require a proficiency rank of legendary in that skill instead, and increase the circumstance bonus you gain from Danger Awareness to +2."],["**Requirements** You're piloting a vehicle.\n\n---\n\nEvery vehicle is a weapon. Whenever you Run Over, you can use your class DC in place of the vehicle's collision DC. Your vehicle can Run Over any number of creatures up to one size smaller than the vehicle or ram any one target creature or object in your path up to the size of your vehicle."],["**Requirements** You're piloting a vehicle.\n\n---\n\nYou can smoothly line up an attack without disrupting your control. You Drive, gaining the effects of the Drive action for the same number of actions you spent to Drive-By Attack. At any point during your vehicle's movement, you Strike."],["You know the ins and outs of piloting, including just how far you can push a vehicle. You become an expert in Piloting. You gain the Stunt Maneuver skill feat. Whenever you attempt a 2-action Drive, you can turn normally."],["They say the weakest part of any vehicle is the pilot, so you've learned how to protect that critical component by shielding yourself as you maneuver through the battlefield. While piloting a vehicle, you have lesser cover. If you would already have lesser cover, you instead gain standard cover. If you would already have standard cover, you instead gain greater cover."],["**Requirements** You're piloting a vehicle.\n\n---\n\nYou drive erratically, swerving from side to side or changing speeds. Attempt a Piloting check against the Fortitude DC of one creature aboard the vehicle you're piloting.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** You move the creature up to 5 feet in a direction of your choice, and they fall Prone. If they're Climbing on the exterior or your vehicle, you instead knock them off your vehicle.\n\n**Success** The creature falls prone, or if they're Climbing on the exterior of your vehicle, they're knocked off your vehicle.\n\n**Critical Failure** A random ally on your vehicle falls prone."],["**Requirements** You're piloting a hoverboard.\n\n---\n\nYou use careful angling to turn your hoverboard into a makeshift shield. You can Raise a Shield and Shield Block with your hoverboard, and you're wielding your hoverboard as long as you're piloting it. Your hoverboard is a commercial-grade shield that grants a +1 circumstance bonus to AC and can be improved."],["You know how to expertly mitigate the damage from a crash. Whenever you Run Over, or a vehicle you're piloting is Run Over, reduce the collision damage dealt to you and your vehicle by your character level."],["Whenever you use an action with the traversal trait, if you're piloting a hoverboard, you can substitute a Drive action in place of the Stride action. In addition, while piloting a hoverboard, you can [[/act leap]], using your hoverboard's speed in place of your own, and you can roll a Piloting check in place of an Athletics check when you [[/act high-jump]] or [[/act long-jump]]. If you critically fail and would fall Prone, you're also thrown off your hoverboard."],["You've spent hours poring over dusty tombs and ancient inscriptions, giving you practiced insight into linguistic problems. You gain access to uncommon languages that are restricted due to belonging to ancient civilizations or long-lost cultures. This does not give you access to languages that are restricted for additional reasons, such as not being decoded yet or being a secret language.\n\nYou can use Society or Delve Lore to Decipher Writing and you gain a +1 circumstance bonus on checks made to decipher text in a language that you don't know."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** An ally you can observe triggers a trap.\n\n---\n\nYou give a sharp, panicked reprimand to an unobservant ally. This feat gains the visual or auditory trait, whichever is appropriate for your warning. Attempt a Delve Lore check against the hazard's stealth DC.\n\n**Critical Success** Your warning comes just in time. You prevent the trap from being triggered, or you delay the activation until the start or end of your next turn (your choice).\n\n**Success** Your ally gains a +1 circumstance bonus to AC against the trap's next attack, or to their next saving throw against the trap's effects.\n\n**Critical Failure** Your sharp warning only startles your ally, leaving them Off-Guard against the trap's next attack."],["You learned your lesson after one-too-many encounters with deadly mechanisms and rigged ruins. You gain the Danger Awareness feat. You can use Delve Lore to disarm traps from alien or historically significant locations."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You critically fail a saving throw or skill check.\n\n---\n\nIt's unclear whether your luck is very good or very bad; more research may be necessary. Reroll the triggering check or save and use the second result. If the triggering skill check is for Delve Lore or the triggering saving throw is to avoid a trap's effects, the frequency for this effect becomes once per 10 minutes."],["You become an expert in Society and Thievery and gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Recall Knowledge checks and Delve Lore checks when using Investigate as your exploration activity.\n\nYou gain the Additional Lore general feat in Delve Lore, which you can use to Recall Knowledge about sites of archaeological significance, and about ancient history, relics, languages, and peoples. Upon gaining this skill, choose either Intelligence or Wisdom as the key attribute for your Delve Lore checks. This choice is permanent and can't be changed later.\n\nXenoarchaeologist"],["You can bond with a number of additional home worlds equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1), which count against your bond limit. Planetary Bond's edicts, anathemas, and effects now extend to all bonded planets.\n\nAt 14th level, add teleport to your primal spell list. You learn the Commune ritual, but can only use Nature to cast this ritual.\n\nAt 18th level, treat all bonded planets as within the same solar system as you when casting a spell with the teleport trait. Regardless of your current location, you can cast wrathful storm as a primal innate spell once per day using your spell DC."],["Your bond has grown into a kinship with all that lives on your planet. You're constantly under the effects of Speak with Animals and Speak with Plants while on your planet. You are considered a native of any planet in your bond. Creatures native to your planet feel an instinctual connection to you, granting a +2 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks when making a Request from them. Particularly helpful creatures may agree to minor tasks like delivering messages or spying on an area, but they won't do dangerous jobs or fight for you.\n\nYou vow to protect your bonded world. Gain the following edicts and anathemas.\n\n**Edicts** defend your world from extraterrestrial threats, protect its natural resources from exploitation, form bonds with lifeforms on your planet\n\n**Anathemas** disturb or harm your planet's ecosystem, plunder your planet's natural resources, exploit your planet's lifeforms\n\nIf your powers are lost due to anathema, you lose the effects of this feat and cannot bond with another planet only if you repent by conducting an Atone ritual."],["Your bonded world revives you. Add breath of life to your primal spell list. While on a bonded planet, if you cast Breath of Life and target a member of your bond, Transfer Vitality to restore Hit Points to the target. If you do, the target regains additional Hit Points equal to their level (without spending any Hit Points from your vitality network), if they also follow the edicts and anathema of Planetary Bond. If you are on a bonded planet, you can cast *breath of life* on yourself when you would die, even if you are Unconscious."],["You can form a bond with the collective spirit of a world's ecosystems. This is a 10-minute activity that involves communing with nature and meditation. The planet must have an active biosphere. You can only bond with one planet at a time. This counts toward your maximum number of bonds. Planets don't count as creatures nor allies for the purposes of spells, prerequisites, or other abilities, including your vitality network.\n\nYou gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Recall Knowledge about your planet's life and natural occurrences. You also gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Survival checks to subsist in its wilds and a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against environmental hazards and effects naturally found on your bonded planet. When off-world, you always know the general direction your planet lies in relation to you (but not distance), which grants a +1 circumstance bonus to Piloting checks to navigate.\n\nIn addition, you can assess the health of your planet once per day and attempt to locate any major disturbances to its ecosystems. Attempt a DC 20 Nature check while in contact with your planet.\n\n**Critical Success** You diagnose the planet's health through its various ecospheres. In addition, you can detect specific ongoing disturbances to the natural world—such as industrial mining or a fire in a particular valley. You can sense the distance and direction of the disturbance and gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against hazards created by this disturbance.\n\n**Success** As a critical success, but you can only sense disturbances happening on a massive scale (such as hurricanes, volcanic eruptions, or planetwide pollution) and the direction to it.\n\n**Failure** You diagnose the planet's health but don't identify any disturbances.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat if you have the mystic multiclass archetype dedication feat even if you haven't taken two additional mystic feats. Mystic archetype feats count as xenodruid feats, and vice-versa, for purposes of completing the archetypes.\n\nXenodruid"],["You succinctly direct your allies to find cover by any means necessary. You and all allies within 60 feet count any form of lesser cover as standard cover until the start of your next turn.\n\n**Lead by Example** If you used two actions, Take Cover. Any allies within 60 feet can Take Cover as a reaction."],["You distract your foes with a clever comment as you maneuver around them. You can use Deception instead of Acrobatics to Tumble Through using the target's Will DC instead of Reflex DC. When you successfully Tumble Through using Deception, the foe whose space you passed through is Suppressed until the end of its next turn."],["**Trigger** A creature within 30 feet is damaged by an ally's Strike.\n\n---\n\nYou follow up on your ally's success by hurling a cunning, well-timed taunt at a foe they wounded. Attempt to Demoralize the triggering creature."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou spend 1 minute observing a specific individual, 10 minutes researching a specific individual on the infosphere, or 1 hour networking and gathering information. This subject is your asset. If you assess your asset via observation, you don't need to know their identity, but if you assess your asset via research or networking, you must know their identity, which requires at least two relevant pieces of information about them. Examples of relevant information could include their name, their place of origin, their current residence, the name of their parent or significant other, their employer, or their organizational affiliation. The GM determines what constitutes relevant information for this purpose, based on the asset you've selected.\n\nYou gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Deception, Diplomacy, Intimidation, and Perception checks against or in relation to your asset, and a +1 circumstance bonus to attempts to Recall Knowledge about your asset.\n\nYou gain the benefits of the 2-action Get 'Em! when using 1-action Get 'Em! on an asset.\n\nYou can maintain a number of assets equal to your Charisma modifier. If you Size Up other assets after that, your new asset replaces a previous one.\n\nSize Up"],["You urge your allies to take down your enemies without incurring any loss of life. Until the beginning of your next turn, you and your allies can add the nonlethal trait to your attacks with weapons (without taking the normal penalty), and to your spells that deal damage and don't have the death or void trait.\n\n**Lead by Example** If you used two actions, Strike a target with a nonlethal attack. On a success, you gain a status bonus to damage equal to your Charisma modifier. On a critical success, an ally within 30 feet can Strike the target as a reaction using a nonlethal attack.\n\nTake 'Em Alive"],["**Trigger** A creature targets an ally within 60 feet with an attack, and you can see both the attacker and your ally.\n\n---\n\nYou signal a warning to your ally, granting them a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.\n\nWatch Out"],["Your insults and threats almost always hit the mark. When you roll a failure on a Demoralize action, you get a success instead. You can still critically fail.\n\nWhen you successfully Demoralize the target of your Get 'Em!, the target doesn't become immune to your further attempts to Demoralize them."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n**Trigger** An ally's Strike hits the target of your Get 'Em!\n\n---\n\nYou provide a quick follow-up to your ongoing directive, encouraging your ally when they successfully hit your designated target. Your ally gains a status bonus to damage equal to your Charisma modifier.\n\nGot 'Em"],["You're practiced in the art of diverting attention quickly and subtly. When you succeed at an attempt to Create a Diversion, you can immediately Sneak or Step as a free action.\n\nAdditionally, creatures only become aware you were trying to trick them if you critically fail to Create a Diversion. Otherwise the creature assumes that your diversion was part of your regular bravado."],["**Trigger** The target of your Get 'Em! is critically hit by an ally's attack or critically fails a Reflex save against an ally's attack or spell.\n\n---\n\nYou seize the opening your ally has provided, quickly attacking your foe. Make a Strike against the triggering creature. If it's a ranged Strike, it must be in your weapon's first range increment. This Strike doesn't count toward your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike."],["**Requirements** Your last action this turn was issuing a 2-action directive.\n\n---\n\nYou follow-up your issued directive with an understood order by attacking a notable foe. Make a Strike. If the Strike hits, the target is affected by a 1-action Get 'Em."],["You Ready a directive. If the trigger you designated occurs before the start of your next turn, you can use the 2-action version of the directive instead of the 1-action."],["When you warn an ally of an attack, you follow up with a shot at your enemy. The first time each round you use your Watch Out reaction, you can make a melee or ranged Strike against the triggering creature. This Strike doesn't count toward your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike. If you hit, your target is Suppressed until the start of its next turn."],["Your confidence is a battery that keeps your allies going. When you use a directive that grants temporary Hit Points, increase the temporary Hit Points by your level. When you use a directive that doesn't grant temporary Hit Points, you can grant one ally affected by that directive temporary Hit Points equal to half your level. These temporary Hit Points last for 1 minute.\n\nUnstoppable Directives"],["**Trigger** The final action on your turn is a 1-action directive.\n\n---\n\nYou act quickly to show your teammates exactly how it's done. Resolve the directive you just issued as though it was a 2-action version instead of the 1-action that you used."],["During your daily preparations, you can review stratagems with up to five allies. Later, you can quickly advise each of these allies on your schemes using the New Plan reaction."],["**Trigger** You roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou instinctively react to trouble by directing your allies to act at the exact moment their intervention would matter most. Issue a 1-action directive."],["**Requirements** Your last action was a 1-action directive.\n\n---\n\nYou motivate an ally within 60 feet to lead by example. As a free action, that ally can immediately perform the lead by example actions of your last action, gaining any benefits and using any abilities that would normally be used as if you used two-actions to issue the direction. Use your Charisma modifier instead of your ally's when determining any relevant benefits, such as the status bonus to damage for Get 'Em!"],["You've become such a master manipulator that spotting an opening to ply your influence has become second nature. You gain the Assurance skill feat three times for Deception, Diplomacy, and Intimidation. Furthermore, when you succeed at a check with Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation, allies within 60 feet who witnessed your success gain a +1 status bonus to the next check they attempt with that skill within 1 minute (or a +2 bonus if your check was a critical success).\n\nEffortless Influencer"],["**Trigger** Your turn begins, and you issued a 2-action directive on your last turn.\n\n---\n\nWith exceptional flair, you can repeat your orders with a single word or gesture. You immediately issue the 1-action version of the directive that you issued on your previous turn."],["When you use Get 'Em!, you can choose any number of enemies within range instead of a single target (you still only Strike one target if you spent 2 actions)."],["People follow your lead because you help push them to their ultimate potential. Each of your allies gain a second reaction if they start their turn within 100 feet of you and can perceive you. This second reaction can only be used for directives you issue."],["You can use Improvised Mastery once per hour, rather than twice per day."],["You assess a foe while in the thick of battle by observing their reactions to your attack. Make a melee or ranged Strike against a creature that isn't your asset. On a hit, your target becomes your asset as if you'd used Size Up. On a critical hit, you can also immediately attempt a check to Recall Knowledge about the target."],["**Trigger** The target of your Get 'Em! is reduced to 0 Hit Points.\n\n**Requirements** You used Get 'Em! against a creature on your last turn.\n\n---\n\nWhen the target you directed your allies to take down falls Unconscious or is destroyed, you quickly direct them at another target. You use Get 'Em! against a new target following all the normal targeting restrictions for Get 'Em! You don't count as leading by example against this new target."],["You encourage your ally to hang on and keep going, despite life-threatening wounds or other serious injuries that might take them out. Select an adjacent dying ally. Reduce the target's dying value by 1. If this would reduce their dying value to 0, they lose the dying condition, don't increase their wounded condition, and remain Unconscious. The targeted ally then becomes temporarily immune to Don't You Die on Me for 1 hour."],["You urge your allies to hustle into the fight or to get out of the way. Until the beginning of your next turn, you and your allies within 100 feet who can sense you gain a +5-foot status bonus to Speed. As your envoy level increases, increase the bonus by an additional 5 feet at 7th level, 12th level, and 17th level.\n\nGet in There!\n\n**Lead by Example** If you used two actions, Step or Stride. Each of your allies within 100 feet who can sense you can immediately Step or Stride up to half their Speed (rounded down to the nearest 5 feet) as a reaction."],["You alert your allies to look for enemies and Hidden things in a stressful situation, coordinating their efforts so they can do so more efficiently. Until the beginning of your next turn, you and your allies gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to Seek. As your envoy level increases, increase the bonus to +3 at 7th level, +4 at 12th level, and +5 at 17th level.\n\nSearch High and Low!\n\n**Lead by Example** If you used two actions, Seek. Each of your allies within 100 feet who can sense you can also immediately Seek as a reaction."],["Your varied life experiences let you adapt to nearly any situation. When you gain skill feats using adaptive talent, you gain two additional skill feats. In addition, you can adapt to the day's challenges by spending 10 minutes to plan. If you do, you can reselect the feats chosen with adaptive talent as if you'd made your daily preparations. You can't trade out feats with limited-use abilities that you've already used that day."],["You've worked with a team for so long that you've learned to convey orders with a glance, a single word, or the tiniest flick of your hand (or suitable appendage, depending on ancestry). Once per turn, you can issue a 1-action envoy directive as a free action. This directive doesn't count toward your total number of directives issued this turn."],["You're an efficient multitasker, and you always have more than one goal in mind or scheme on the go. You can maintain twice your Charisma modifier of assets."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You're about to roll a Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation check, but you haven't rolled yet.\n\n---\n\nWith masterful timing and a careful choice of words, you can manipulate the emotions and thoughts of others. You roll the triggering Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation check twice, and use the higher result."],["**Trigger** A creature targets you with a melee attack.\n\n---\n\nYou wave your arms to shield your face from harm and cower, acting meek and pitiful. Attempt a Deception check against the triggering creature's Will DC. The triggering creature is then immune to Not in the Face for 1 hour.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** Your attacker has second thoughts about harming you and is thoroughly thrown off. It takes a –2 status penalty to attack and damage rolls against you until the start of its next turn.\n\n**Success** Your attacker is thrown off. It takes a –1 status penalty to attack rolls against you until the start of its next turn.\n\n**Failure** Your attacker is temporarily thrown off. It takes a –1 status penalty to the triggering attack roll.\n\n**Critical Failure** Your attacker is unaffected.\n\nNot in the Face"],["**Trigger** You're about to roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou read the demeanor, body language, and instinctive tics of your foes as easily as you read a comm unit, allowing you to react a moment before those around you and gain an edge in the coming battle. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your initiative roll, and you can immediately do one of the following: Interact to draw a weapon, Step, or Stride."],["**Trigger** A creature misses you with a melee Strike.\n\n---\n\nYou turn the tables on your attacker, using underhanded tactics to temporarily hinder it, such as throwing dirt in its eyes, shining a light in its face, pulling its coat over its head, or otherwise being a meddlesome nuisance. The triggering creature becomes your choice of Clumsy 1 or Enfeebled 1 until the end of its next turn."],["You're an incredible actor, and you can use your over-the-top bits and dramatic gestures to throw a foe off its game. If you're wielding a ranged weapon, you can Feint against an opponent at a range of 100 feet, rather than just within melee reach. If you succeed, the opponent is Off-Guard against your melee and ranged attacks, rather than only your melee attacks."],["You encourage yourself or an ally, psyching them up for a coming challenge and granting them temporary Hit Points. Choose yourself or an ally within 30 feet, then attempt a DC 20 Diplomacy check. If you have master proficiency in Diplomacy, you can instead attempt a DC 30 Diplomacy check to increase the temporary Hit Points gained on a successful check by 5. If you have legendary proficiency, you can instead attempt a DC 40 Diplomacy check to increase the temporary Hit Points gained on a successful check by 10. These temporary Hit Points last for 1 minute. The target is then temporarily immune to your Hang in There for 1 day.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target gains temporary Hit Points equal to double their level plus your Charisma modifier.\n\n**Success** The target gains temporary Hit Points equal to their level plus your Charisma modifier.\n\n**Failure** The target is unaffected, and you can't use Hang in There again for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is unaffected, and you can't use Hang in There again for 1 hour."],["You urge an ally to pick up the pace and contribute more to the events happening around them. One ally within 30 feet who can sense you becomes Quickened for 1 round. They can use the extra action to Interact, Step, or Stride. The target is then temporarily immune to Hurry for the next 10 minutes."],["You encourage an adjacent ally to overcome their minor ailments by patting them on the back, providing them useful advice, or offering some form of comfort or inspiration. The target reduces the value of one of the following conditions of their choice by 2: Clumsy, Enfeebled, Frightened, Sickened, Stupefied. The target then becomes temporarily immune to Cheer Up for 1 day."],["You attempt to enthrall a foe with a convoluted and utterly pointless monologue that leaves your audience dumbfounded. Attempt a Deception or Diplomacy check against the Will DC of a single creature within 30 feet. The target is then temporarily immune to your Confounding Disquisition for 1 day.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is Stunned 1 and is Stupefied 1 for 1 round.\n\n**Success** The target is stupefied 1 for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The target takes a –1 status penalty to Perception checks and Will saves for 1 round.\n\nConfounding Disquisition (Failure)\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is unaffected."],["You warn your ally to move away from danger. You can use Watch Out before an ally in range attempts a Reflex save in addition to its original trigger. If you do, the circumstance bonus applies to their Reflex save against the triggering effect.\n\nWhen you use Watch Out and the triggering attack fails or critically fails, or your ally succeeds or critically succeeds at the saving throw, your ally can also Stride up to 10 feet as a free action."],["**Trigger** The attack roll for a Strike targeting you fails.\n\n---\n\nYou deftly step out of the way of an attack, letting the blow continue to the creature next to you. You redirect the attack to a creature of your choice that's adjacent to you and within range or reach of the triggering attack. The attacker rerolls the Strike's attack roll against the new target."],["You've modified your drone, granting it a new ability. Your drone gains one additional commercial customization.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat up to three times."],["Your mines use bursts of shrapnel that shred through a creature, causing lasting harm. A creature that fails its saving throw against one of your mines takes an additional 1 persistent damage (or persistent damage equal to your Intelligence modifier on a critical failure). If the mine dealt physical damage, this is persistent bleed damage. Otherwise, the persistent damage is of the same type dealt by the mine."],["You've designed a nozzle that can split fire into dangerous new shapes. You gain the following new mod.\n\n- **Explosive Shot (weapon):** Strikes with the modded item deal an additional 1 splash damage per weapon damage die. This splash damage is the same damage type the modded item deals."],["You can make the most of limited medical supplies. You can store up to 3 items with the healing or serum trait in your custom rig. You gain the following new mods.\n\n- **Numbing Analgesic (medpatch or serum):** In addition to its usual effects, the item reduces the value of the Sickened condition by 1.\n\n- **Powerful Stimulant (medpatch or serum):** In addition to its usual effects, the item reduces the value of the Enfeebled or Frightened condition by 1.\n\n- **Protective Excretions (medpatch or serum):** In addition to its usual effects, the item attempts a DC 10 flat check to end one persistent damage type afflicting the target with a DC of 10.\n\n- **Restorative Boost (medpatch or serum):** In addition to its usual effect, the item grants fast healing equal to half the item's level (rounded up) for 3 rounds."],["Your drone can discharge excess electricity. Your drone gains the Electrical Discharge action."],["Your turret is bulky. Your turret provides standard cover instead of lesser cover. Taking Cover behind it provides greater cover."],["**Requirements** You're holding or wearing your custom rig.\n\n---\n\nYou swiftly craft items. Choose a common level 0 weapon, shield, or piece of adventuring gear of 1 Bulk or less. The item lasts for 1 hour or until you next use Spontaneous Crafting."],["You've further modified your drone, granting it a new ability. Your drone gains one additional advanced customization.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat up to three times."],["**Requirements** Your drone or turret is in a space that includes a solid surface.\n\n---\n\nYour drone or turret plants itself on the ground, then extends retractable barriers that create a temporary wall. You either create a 5-foot-wide metal wall in a space adjacent to your drone or turret, or you extend a wall you've already created by an additional 5 feet, up to a maximum of 15 feet. The walls created by your exocortex are 1 inch thick, 5 feet high, and placed vertically on the border between squares. They must be placed on a solid horizontal surface. The walls are a part of your exocortex and use the the same statistics and Hit Points.\n\nThese walls automatically retract back into your exocortex if the drone or turret that created the walls moves (or is forced to move) from its location."],["**Requirements** Your turret's array deals energy damage.\n\n---\n\nYou've customized your turret to fire explosive blasts of energy. Make a ranged Strike with your turret against a target. Regardless of the result of the attack, additional energy from this shot is expelled around your turret, dealing damage to creatures in your choice of a 10-foot emanation around your turret or a 15-foot cone originating from your turret. All creatures in the area take damage equal to your turret's ranged Strike with a basic Reflex save against your class DC."],["You've adjusted your exocortex's debilitating features, making it even more of a hindrance to your enemies. When you apply the debilitating exocortex mod to your exocortex, add the following to the list of conditions you can select from: Clumsy 1, Enfeebled 1, or Stupefied 1."],["You've created a custom kinetic dampener that diverts incoming kinetic energy. While there are still some gaps in its coverage, you find it's a reliable invention. You gain resistance equal to your Intelligence modifier to physical damage (bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage). In addition, you gain the Rebound Kinetic Energy reaction."],["You've become accustomed to controlling multiple machines at the same time with perfect efficiency, your mind being able to process and calculate the positions and velocities of different devices at the same time. You do one of the following.\n\n- You Reposition Exocortex your mine and Reposition Exocortex your turret.\n\n- You Reposition Exocortex to move your turret and then Deploy Mine.\n\n- You Reposition Exocortex your mine and then Deploy Turret."],["You've become accustomed to controlling multiple machines at the same time with perfect efficiency. You Synchronized Step and then Reposition Exocortex."],["You've rigged your mines so that whenever you Deploy Mine, you can make the deployed mine a proximity alert mine. If you do, the mine automatically Detonates when a creature enters or leaves a square within the burst area of the mine. This doesn't take an action, and you can't choose to delay the mine's detonation when it would trigger."],["You put rocket boosters into your drone's chassis that allow them to soar across the battlefield. Your drone gains a fly Speed of 20 feet. If your drone already has a fly Speed of 20 feet or more, it increases its fly Speed by 5 feet instead. Additionally, it gains the Activate Thrusters action."],["Despite the speed with which you apply them, your modifications are stable and long-lasting. Whenever you Modify an item, it remains modded for 1 minute rather than until the end of your next turn. The first time the modded item would gain the Glitching condition, reduce the value of the glitching condition by 1."],["You've expanded the materials your transmutative casing can mimic. When you apply the transmutative casing mod, add the following to the list of precious materials you can select from: adamantine (standard-grade), aucturnite, and noqual."],["You've tweaked the formula for your energy neutralizer, increasing its effectiveness. When you apply the energy neutralizer mod to an item, the resistance is equal to your level, rather than your Intelligence modifier."],["Your devices can emit a disrupting pulse that causes tech to malfunction. You gain the following new mod.\n\n- **Glitch Pulse (weapon):** Strikes from the modded weapon disrupt technology. On a hit with the modded weapon, the target must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC with the following results.\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is immune to glitch pulse mods for 24 hours.\n\n**Success** The creature and its gear are unaffected.\n\n**Failure** If the creature has the tech trait, the creature is Glitching 3 for 1 round. Otherwise, one random item with the tech trait in the creature's possession becomes glitching 3 for 1 round, beginning with items they're wielding or holding.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but glitching 3 for 1 minute."],["You've greatly improved the effectiveness of your healing mines. Whenever you apply the healing mines mod, rather than creatures in the area regaining a number of Hit Points equal to the mine's number of damage dice + your Intelligence modifier, creatures in the area regain 1d6 healing Hit Points per the mine's number of damage dice + your Intelligence modifier."],["You've programmed your drone to spin around while attacking everyone nearby. It gains the Spin to Win action."],["You've further improved your exocortex's debilitating features, increasing the intensity of its effects. When you apply the debilitating exocortex mod to your exocortex, you can select two conditions, rather than one. In addition, if you select the clumsy, enfeebled, or stupefied conditions, the value of the condition is 2, rather than 1."],["You tactically redeploy your mines in the heat of battle. You Reposition Exocortex for every mine you've deployed."],["You know how to alter the shape of explosions. When you activate a grenade (or Detonate Mine, if applicable), you can cause it to explode in a cone with an area equal to double the area of the burst it would've affected, though it must still originate from the activated grenade (or mine)."],["You further customize your drone. It becomes a specialized companion and gains one specialization of your choice. In addition to the one superior customization it automatically gains from becoming a specialized robot companion, your drone gains one additional superior customization.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat up to three times. Each time, add a different specialization to your companion, but it doesn't gain the additional superior customization."],["You've devised a means to tear down and bypass the defenses of your enemies. You gain the following new mod.\n\n- **Exploitive Assault (grenade or weapon):** Using careful calculations, chemical reactions, quantum physics, and the magic of clever engineering, you tweak the item to foil resistances. Choose one damage type the modded item can deal. Any damage dealt by the item (including splash and persistent damage) ignores an amount of that resistance equal to your level."],["Using advanced targeting systems and scanners that adjust your weapons to your target's anatomy, you've made it nearly impossible to avoid the debilitating effect imposed by your exocortex. When you apply the debilitating exocortex mod to your exocortex, enemy targets avoid the condition the modded exocortex imposes only if they critically succeed at their saving throws."],["You've further modified your drone, granting it a new ability. Your drone gains one additional superior customization.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat up to three times."],["You've further expanded what your casing can mimic. When you apply the transmutative casing mod, add the following standard grade precious materials to the list you can select from: abysium, djezet, cold siccatite, or hot siccatite."],["Painstaking contingency plans and a reliable backup power source allow your exocortex to continue processing data and follow your programming even when you're Unconscious or dying. When you have 0 Hit Points or are otherwise unable to act, you can take 3 actions per round on your turn, but all of these actions must involve your exocortex. You can't use any actions with the manipulate or move trait. For example, you could still Command your drone, fire your turret, Detonate Mine, or Reposition Exocortex, but you can't Deploy Mine, Modify, or Synchronized Step."],["Your drone changes forms. When you pick this feat, select a robot companion chassis that your drone doesn't have; your drone gains this chassis. During your daily preparations, select the customizations for all of your drone's chassis individually, then select which chassis your drone begins that day as. Your drone gains the Mobile Reconfiguration action, which it can use to switch between its available chassis.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once, selecting a different chassis each time."],["During your daily preparations, when you Modify one item with your enduring mods class feature, you can instead Modify three items. All three mods last for 24 hours. In addition, you can spend 10 minutes Modifying an item with an enduring mod to change that item's enduring mod to another mod you know. This newly selected mod is an enduring mod."],["Your turret rains down a hail of destructive attacks. You can Area Fire your turret. When you do, your turret gains the area (cone) or area (line) trait (your choice whenever you Area Fire). If the turret has area (cone), its range is 20 feet. If it has area (line), its range is equal to the weapon's range increment."],["You fire in tandem with your exocortex to overcome your enemy's defenses. You and either your drone or your turret each attempt a ranged Strike against the same target, each using your current multiple attack penalty. If both attacks hit, combine their damage. Apply the target's resistances and weaknesses only once. This counts as two attacks when calculating your multiple attack penalty."],["You can craft a few rudimentary grenades each day. You gain the formulas for two common grenades. Each day during your daily preparations, you can create two temporary grenades of your level or lower from your formulas. Grenades prepared in this way don't cost you any resources to Craft and don't have any sale value. They're temporary items and fall apart the next time you make your daily preparations.\n\nIf you're an expert in Crafting, you can create three grenades per day. If you're a master in Crafting, you can create four grenades per day. If you're legendary in Crafting, you can create six grenades per day."],["You've designed a mine that explodes with healing medicine. You gain the following new mod.\n\n- **Healing Mines (mine exocortex):** Your mine uses tiny four-sided syringes full of concentrated medicine. Instead of dealing damage, your healing mine causes creatures to regain a number of Hit Points equal to the mine's number of damage dice. Unlike your usual mines, creatures in the area don't attempt a saving throw. At 8th level, add your Intelligence modifier to the number of Hit Points regained.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the High-Tech Medic feat, you can apply any of the mods granted by that feat to your healing mines."],["You dash across the battlefield and hunker down behind cover before unleashing hell on your enemies. You Stride and [[/act take-cover]]. You can either Detonate Mine, make a ranged Strike with your turret, or your drone can make a Strike."],["**Trigger** You roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou're always ready to unleash your exocortex. If you have a drone exocortex, your drone Strides. If you have a mine or turret exocortex, you can Deploy Mine or Deploy Turret."],["You rapidly deploy your exocortex while on the move. You Stride twice. At any point during this movement, you can Deploy Mine or Deploy Turret."],["You make the best explosions. Whenever you Area Fire, Auto-Fire, Detonate Mine, or activate a grenade, the area is doubled."],["You've made automated shortcuts for your exocortex. At the start of each enemy's turn, you gain an additional reaction you can use only during that turn to use a mechanic reaction."],["Your exocortex has become such a seamless extension of your own body and mind that you can flawlessly activate it without a second thought. You're permanently Quickened. You can use your extra action to only to Command your drone (or to provide 1 of the actions if you choose to spend 2 actions to Command your drone), make a ranged Strike with your turret, or Detonate Mine."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou unleash a flurry of synchronized explosions. You Detonate Mine twice. If a creature is in the area of both of these detonations, combine the damage for the purposes of applying that creature's resistances and weaknesses."],["You've created an adaptable coating that can neutralize a variety of energies. You gain the following new mod.\n\n- **Energy Neutralizer (armor):** Select an energy type when you apply this mod: acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic. The item and the item's wearer gain resistance equal to your Intelligence modifier against the selected energy type. At 10th level, you can select two energy types, and at 15th level, you can select three energy types."],["**Requirements** Your turret is Deployed and within 150 feet.\n\n---\n\nYou overload your turret's systems, causing it to self-destruct in a volatile explosion. Your turret deals (floor(level/4)+1)d6 piercing plus (floor(level/4)+1)d6 fire damage to all creatures in a 15-foot emanation. Creatures in the area can attempt a basic Reflex save against your class DC. Your turret is reduced to 0 Hit Points and automatically recalled to your custom rig.\n\nAt 8th level and every 4 levels thereafter, both the piercing damage and the fire damage increase by 1d6."],["You've improved your drone, making it a tactical robot companion and granting it additional capabilities. In addition to the one tactical customization it automatically gains from becoming a tactical robot companion, your drone gains one additional tactical customization.\n\nDuring an encounter, even if you don't Command your robot companion, it can still use 1 action that round on your turn to Stride or Strike. It can do this at any point during your turn, as long as you aren't currently taking an action. If it does, that's all the actions it gets that round—you can't Command it later."],["You can coat ammunition with a substance capable of mimicking rare materials. You gain the following new mod.\n\n- **Transmutative Casing (grenade or weapon):** Physical damage dealt by the item uses one of the following precious materials of your choice: cold iron or silver."],["No matter how advanced your inventions become, you never neglect the basics. In fact, you've even developed a few improvements to enhance some old favorites.\n\n- Whenever you apply the big boom mod to an item, you increase the item's radius by 10 feet if it's a burst or a cone (rather than by 5 feet), and its area by 20 feet if it's a line (rather than 10 feet).\n\n- Whenever you apply the bunker buster mod to an item, you increase the additional damage by 5 (for a total of 10 additional damage, rather than 5).\n\n- Whenever you apply the incapacitant mod to an item, creatures damaged by the item additionally become Frightened 1 if the attack was a critical hit or they critically failed their save.\n\n- Whenever you apply the long-range propulsors mod to an item, you increase the item's range or range increment by 60 feet (rather than by 30 feet).\n\n- Whenever you apply the magnetic levitators mod to an item, the wearer gains a fly Speed of 20 feet (rather than a fly Speed of 10 feet).\n\n- Whenever you apply the troubleshoot mod to an item, you reduce its Glitching condition by 2 (rather than by 1)."],["You've outfitted your exocortex with a variety of minor distracting features. You gain the following new mod.\n\n- **Debilitating Exocortex (exocortex):** Select one of the following conditions: Dazzled, Deafened, Off-Guard, or Suppressed. Creatures damaged by your exocortex must succeed at a Fortitude save against your class DC or gain the chosen condition until the end of their next turn."],["You're constantly experimenting with your exocortex and expanding its capabilities. Choose an exocortex other than your own. You gain that exocortex.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat a second time if you're 12th level or higher, gaining an additional new exocortex."],["Your mines push or pull creatures away from them. You gain the following new mods.\n\n- **Big Bang (mine exocortex):** Your mines blow enemies away. Creatures that fail their saving throw against the mine are pushed 5 feet directly away from the mine (or pushed 10 feet directly away from the mine and knocked Prone on a critical failure). This is forced movement.\n\n- **Black Hole (mine exocortex):** Your mines harness gravity-bending technology. Creatures that fail their saving throw against the mine are pulled 5 feet toward the mine (or pulled 10 feet toward the mine and Slowed 1 on a critical failure). This is forced movement."],["You've further modified your drone, granting it a new ability. Your drone gains one additional tactical customization.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat up to three times."],["Your turret unleashes a hail of gunfire. You can make a ranged Strike against a target within the first range increment of your turret's weapon, and the target is Off-Guard against this Strike."],["You activate the targeting system you've built into your exocortex. The next time before the end of your turn that you, your drone, or your turret makes an attack roll, the attack ignores circumstance penalties to the attack roll and any flat check required due to the target being Concealed or Hidden."],["You've further upgraded your drone, which becomes either a burly or deft companion and gains additional capabilities determined by its type. In addition to the one advanced customization it automatically gains from becoming a burly or deft robot companion, your drone gains one additional advanced customization."],["**Trigger** A creature within 30 feet of your drone or turret uses a manipulate action or a move action, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.\n\n---\n\nYour drone or turret can automatically attack foes. Your drone or turret makes a ranged Strike against the triggering creature. This Strike doesn't count toward your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike."],["◆ to ◆◆\n\n---\n\nYou activate dampeners in your exocortex that slow motion and dilate time. Either you, your exocortex, or one of your Deployed Mines emits a 10-foot emanation of difficult terrain for a number of rounds equal to your Intelligence modifier. You and your exocortex are unhindered by difficult terrain created this way.\n\nYou can Deploy Motion Dampener as 2 actions. When you do, you Deploy the Motion Dampener into an unoccupied space within 30 feet of you. This cloaking field is immobile and can't be moved."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nYou've programmed your exocortex to deploy mines together to create a choke point. You Deploy Mine twice. Both mines must be within 30 feet of one another."],["You design additional custom arrays for your turret. Select two of the following arrays. Add the selected arrays to your list of available arrays.\n\n- 1d8 mental damage, range increment 60 feet, tech trait, mental weapon group\n\n- 1d8 poison damage, range increment 60 feet, tech trait, dart weapon group\n\n- 1d8 vitality damage, range increment 60 feet, tech trait, laser weapon group\n\n- 1d8 void damage, range increment 60 feet, tech trait, void weapon group\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat a second time. When you do, you must select different arrays."],["You've worked a few shortcuts into your custom rig, enabling you to install and uninstall upgrades swiftly. You can Install Upgrade with your custom rig, instead of a repair toolkit, as a single action."],["You can make additional grenades each day. Increase the number of temporary grenades you can create each day by 2.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat a second time if you're 14th level or higher."],["As a disciple of a god, you wield some of their divine power. You become trained in the listed divine skill associated with the deity and add the listed cleric spells to your spell list and spell repertoire as signature spells. If you were already trained in the listed divine skill, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice. You become bound by that deity's anathema and can receive that deity's divine sanctification."],["You join a primal order of xenodruids with ties to nature and the biodiversity of the Universe, such as the Xenowardens. Choose one of the following xenodruid orders.\n\n**Order** Animal; **Skill** Animal Lore; **Spells** 1st: Pest Form; 2nd: Animal Form; 5th: Carcinization\n\n**Order** Plant; **Skill** Plant Lore; **Spells** 1st: Summon Plant or Fungus; 2nd: Verdant Code; 5th: Plant Form\n\n**Order** Viral; **Skill** Genealogy Lore; **Spells** 1st: Detect Poison; 2nd: Instant Virus; 5th: Toxic Cloud\n\nYou become trained in the listed skill associated with the order and add the listed spells to your spell list and spell repertoire as signature spells. If you were already trained in the listed skill, you instead become trained in another skill of your choice."],["You can speak with computers. Any construct creatures you summon are considered part of your bond and don't count against the maximum number of creatures in your bond. During your daily preparations, choose one of the following spells: Instant Virus, Mending, Summon Construct, or Summon Robot. You add the selected spell to your spell repertoire and signature spells until your next daily preparations."],["You see into the truth of the cosmos through your connection. You gain the greater epiphany spell for your chosen connection."],["You can speak with animals and plants. Any living creature you summon is considered part of your bond and doesn't count against the maximum number of creatures in your bond. During your daily preparations, choose one of the following spells: Summon Animal, Summon Elemental, Summon Fey, or Summon Plant or Fungus. You add the selected spell to your spell repertoire and signature spells until your next daily preparations."],["**Trigger** An enemy targets a bonded creature with a Strike or spell with an attack roll that has an elemental trait and the roll fails or critically fails, or you roll a critical success on a save against a foe's harmful elemental spell.\n\n---\n\nYour vitality network absorbs the essence of the attack. Your vitality network regains 2 Hit Points per rank of the triggering spell or 4 Hit Points per weapon die of the triggering Strike."],["**Trigger** An area within 60 feet has its light level reduced due to magical darkness.\n\n---\n\nYour vitality network regains Hit Points equal to the spell rank of the magical darkness if the affected area was normally dim light, and doubled if the affected area was normally bright light. Even if the magical darkness ends, the area's light level remains non-magical darkness for 1 minute; this effect removes light in the area but isn't magical darkness and is automatically overcome by any form of magical light."],["Analyzing your enemies gives you a greater understanding of the ties that bond all things and helps synchronize your connection to the Akashic Record. Attempt a Recall Knowledge check against an enemy you're observing. On a success, in addition to the normal benefits, your vitality network regains 10 Hit Points. On a critical success, it regains 20 Hit Points."],["With extreme concentration, you can sacrifice your own Hit Points to recharge your vitality network. Your vitality network regains Hit Points equal to the amount you sacrifice."],["**Frequency** once per minute\n\n---\n\nYou dance across the battlefield, magically converting your body's kinetic energy into magical potential. Stride a number of times equal to the actions you used. Your vitality network regains 10 Hit Points per Stride you took."],["**Trigger** An ally within 30 feet Casts a Spell.\n\n---\n\nYou pulse energy through your bond as your ally casts a spell, empowering their spell in one of the following ways.\n\n- If their spell deals damage or heals Hit Points and doesn't have a duration, you grant that spell a status bonus to damage or healing equal to its rank.\n\nBond Spell\n\n- If their spell doesn't have a spellshape effect applied to it, apply the effects of any one spellshape feat you know to the spell. The spellshape feat must be one that can be applied to the triggering spell, and you must be able to use it (for instance, if the spellshape feat is usable only a limited number of times per day)."],["You infuse your magic with vital energy that empowers the target of your spell. Pick a spell and reduce your vitality network's total by a number equal to twice the spell's rank. If your next action is to cast that spell, one bonded ally you target with that spell becomes Quickened until the end of your next turn and can use the extra action for only Strike and Stride actions."],["**Trigger** Your turn begins.\n\n---\n\nYou maintain your active spells with hardly a thought. You immediately gain the effects of a Sustain action for one of your active mystic spells."],["Plumbing the depths of your own connection, you understand how your piece of reality interconnects with another. You learn the advanced epiphany spell of the connection that grants training in the prerequisite connection skill."],["You can manifest your bond as a web of vital energy between your allies. You learn the Vitality Web epiphany spell."],["**Target** any number of your bonded allies within 120 feet\n\n---\n\nFeeling the surge of your strong communal bond, you temporarily attune your vitality network to the spiritual wavelength of your allies. Each ally can immediately choose to transfer up to 20 Hit Points from your vitality network into themselves or up to 20 Hit Points from themselves into the vitality network."],["**Frequency** once per minute\n\n---\n\nYou've come to learn that your vitality network isn't just a manifestation of your magic, it's a metaphysical representation of your connection. If your next action is to cast an epiphany spell, you can expend 20 Hit Points from your vitality network to cast it, rather than spending a Focus Point."],["**Trigger** A bonded ally within 20 feet is about to roll a saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYou channel a surge of energy through your bond, shielding your ally's body and mind. Your ally gains a +1 status bonus to the triggering saving throw. If they roll a success on the saving throw against a vitality or void effect, they get a critical success instead.\n\nBond Boost"],["You channel strange power from beyond this reality, granting creatures in your bond the power to reform their bodies into powerful, aberrant shapes. You gain the Eldritch Bond epiphany spell."],["**Trigger** An adjacent bonded ally takes damage.\n\n---\n\nYou quickly expend energy from your vitality network toward a bonded ally. Transfer Vitality to the triggering ally."],["Understanding that all living things are part of the same tapestry of life, you can tap into the universal code to radically alter the genes of creatures in your bond. You gain the Wild Bond epiphany spell."],["You understand the true nature of your connection and how it stretches across the vast pillars of reality. Your vitality network has a maximum capacity of 200 Hit Points and regains 20 Hit Points at the start of each turn instead of 8. You can bond with any number of willing creatures."],["Your understanding of your connection transcends the limits of other mortals, granting you access to the most powerful spells. You gain an additional 10th-rank spell slot."],["You prepare your vitality network to catch some of your excess magic, allowing it to flow back and bolster your bond's defenses. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that deals damage, whether or not it successfully deals damage, you and one bonded ally gain resistance to that spell's type of damage equal to the spell's rank (minimum 1) until the end of your next turn. If the spell deals more than one type of damage, choose one and gain resistance to that type.\n\nAdaptive Defense"],["You can use your vitality network as an extradimensional storage space, sliding items into and out of thin air as if it were a Null Space Chamber. You can Interact with an item that weighs 1 Bulk or less to stow it into your Cloud Storage. A creature in your bond and on the same plane can remove an item from your Cloud Storage as an Interact action, but doing so takes 2 actions instead of 1 action. Your Cloud Storage has a capacity of 12 Bulk. This increases to 25 Bulk at 8th level, 50 Bulk at 12th level, and 75 Bulk at 16th level."],["You can feel and reach out to your bonded allies regardless of range. You can Transfer Vitality to any bonded ally as long as they're on the same planet as you."],["You force link the target's mind to your bond and share a confusing glimpse of your connection. Attempt a skill check with your connection skill against the Will DC of a foe you can see within 30 feet. The target is them temporarily immune for 1 hour.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target takes a –1 status penalty to attack rolls and a –2 status penalty to Will saves for 1 minute. This effect ends early if it uses a single action with the concentrate trait to shake off the effects of the interference or immediately after you target it with a hostile action.\n\n**Success** As critical success, but the penalty to Will saves is –1.\n\n**Critical Failure** You become Off-Guard against the next attack the target attempts against you before the end of your next turn.\n\nMental Interference"],["With careful focus, you guarantee vital energy lost from a target is caught by your vitality network. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that deals void damage to a living creature, your vitality network gains Hit Points equal to twice the spell's rank.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can Waste Not without the spellshape trait. If you do and your next action is to Strike with a weapon that deals void damage, your vitality network gains 2 Hit Points per weapon damage die."],["**Trigger** You're hit by an attack.\n\n---\n\nYou condense the energy of your vitality network into a shield. The triggering attack reduces your vitality network's Hit Points instead of your own, up to twice your level. Any remaining damage after your Vitality Network is reduced to 0 Hit Points is dealt to you instead."],["Through dedication or serendipity, you've branched out to explore other connections to the fundamental building blocks of the cosmos. You learn the initial epiphany spell of a connection that grants training in the prerequisite connection skill."],["When you Transfer Vitality, you can select any number of bonded allies to transfer to, though the total maximum number of Hit Points you can transfer doesn't increase."],["You gain a deeper understanding of your connection. You gain the advanced epiphany spell for your chosen connection."],["**Trigger** You would gain the Confused, Controlled, Fleeing, Frightened, or Stupefied condition.\n\n---\n\nYou create duplicates of your consciousness capable of fending off mental intrusion. Attempt to counteract an effect of your choice imposing one of the triggering conditions, using half your level rounded up as your counteract rank and your spell attack modifier as the counteract modifier."],["**Trigger** A Strike targeting you fails.\n\n---\n\nYou move out of the way as you elude your attackers. You Step."],["You draw your gun and take careful aim with the same motion. You Interact to draw a ranged weapon or Switch Hands and then Aim with that ranged weapon."],["You always keep a target marked and in your sights, even if they move. When you Aim, the benefits apply if your mark is within your weapon's first or second range increment, rather than only within the first."],["You're rarely still, and you've learned to reliably hit your targets even while moving. You Stride and then Aim with a gun you're wielding."],["Viewing your marks through a scope is as instinctive as opening your eyes. Whenever you Aim, you can Interact to Activate a sight weapon upgrade."],["**Requirements** You aren't Encumbered.\n\n---\n\nYou dodge, roll, and weave out of danger, leaving no openings for attack as you move across the battlefield. Stride up to your Speed. This movement doesn't trigger reactions."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou target a creature's limbs or load-bearing appendages to weaken them. You Aim and then make a ranged Strike against your mark. If the Strike hits, the creature becomes your choice of Clumsy 1 or Enfeebled 1 until the end of your next turn (Clumsy 2 or Enfeebled 2 on a critical hit)."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou hinder your target with a shot. You Aim and then make a ranged Strike against your mark. If the Strike hits, the target is Slowed 1 until the end of its next turn. If the target is flying, it also falls 10 feet."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYour attack distracts your foe. You Aim and then make a ranged Strike against your mark. If the Strike hits, the creature becomes Dazzled until the end of your next turn if it's within your first range increment."],["**Trigger** A creature critically fails on a melee attack roll against you.\n\n---\n\nYou take advantage of the opening in your foe's defenses. Make a ranged Strike against the triggering creature."],["**Trigger** A creature Grabs, Immobilizes, or Restrains you.\n\n---\n\nYou've trained in close quarters combat and practiced how to escape a hold, or similar situations. You attempt to Escape. If you succeed or critically succeed, you can also Stand or Step."],["You sprint at top speed to chase down a foe or flee a dangerous situation. Stride up to four times. You can increase the number of actions this activity takes to 3 to Stride up to six times."],["Your sharpshooter skills improve. You can have two marks at a time instead of one. When you Aim, you can select two marks, rather than one.\n\nDual Aim"],["**Requirements** You have a mark.\n\n---\n\nYou take your time to line up a shot that's sure to hit. Make a ranged Strike with your gun against your mark. It gains the following failure effect.\n\n**Failure** Your attack deals minimum damage to the target. (Calculate this damage as if every die you would roll has a result of 1.)"],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou fire a single trick shot that passes through multiple foes. Make a ranged Strike with your gun against a target within your first range increment. Apply this attack against all creatures in a straight line between you and your target. This attack ignores any lesser cover the targets would provide one another. Roll damage only once, and apply it to each creature you hit. Line 'Em Up counts as two attacks for your multiple attack penalty."],["You pierce through your foe's resistance with a well-timed shot. You Aim and then make a Strike against your mark. Select one of the following damage types: acid, bludgeoning, cold, electricity, fire, mental, piercing, poison, slashing, or sonic damage. Your shot ignores an amount of the target's resistance to the selected damage type equal to your level. If the creature has a weakness to the selected damage type, increase that weakness by an amount equal to half your level. A creature's immunities are unaffected."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou rush forward, firing a precisely aimed shot at your enemy while you're on the move. Aim and then Stride up to your Speed. At any point during this movement, you can make a ranged Strike with the gun you're wielding."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou fire a trick shot as part of a daredevil maneuver. You Parkour. You can Aim and then make a ranged Strike with the gun you're wielding during this movement, including when you're falling."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You take damage that would reduce you to 0 Hit Points.\n\n---\n\nYou fly into a frenzy instead of accepting defeat. Instead of being knocked out, you're reduced to 1 Hit Point, gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to your half you level for 1 minute, increase your wounded value by 1, and enter a frenzy that lasts for 1 minute. You can't voluntarily end your frenzy. While in a frenzy caused by Bullet Fever, you're affected as follows.\n\n- You automatically apply precision damage to all targets as though you were Aiming.\n- You take a –1 circumstance penalty to AC.\n- You take a –1 circumstance penalty to Will saves.\n- You can't take actions that don't have the attack or move traits except to Reload your weapons.\n\nWhen Bullet Fever ends, you lose any remaining temporary Hit Points from Bullet Fever."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun with at least 3 expend worth of ammunition.\n\n---\n\nYou shoot a spray of bullets at a target. You Aim, make a ranged Strike against your mark, and subtract three times your weapon's expend from its magazine. Roll the attack twice, and use the better result. The attack ignores circumstance penalties to the attack roll and any flat check required due to the target being Concealed or Hidden."],["As the old saying goes: hitting easy targets is like shooting fish in a barrel. You Aim and then make a ranged Strike against a Prone or Immobilized creature not benefiting from cover. Treat a success as a critical success. If you roll a critical success, the creature is Off-Guard and Suppressed until the beginning of your next turn."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n**Requirements** You're wielding two guns, and your last action was a ranged Strike that missed.\n\n---\n\nWhen at first you don't succeed, shoot again. Make a second ranged Strike using the weapon you're wielding that you didn't fire with. This Strike doesn't count the multiple attack penalty from the prior attack but does count toward future multiple attack penalties."],["You squeeze the trigger and release a calculated burst of fire. If you make your second Strike from Double Tap with the same gun, Double Tap counts as one attack when calculating your multiple attack penalty, and you apply your precision damage bonus from Aim to both Strikes."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou bend light and background vibrations around yourself, either through expertise or a bit of technological ingenuity, allowing you to avoid detection. You become Invisible for 10 minutes. This makes you Undetected to all creatures, though creatures can attempt to find you, making you Hidden instead. If you use a hostile action, the effect ends after that hostile action is completed. While your Cloaking Field is active, security cameras, sentries, and other surveillance don't detect you unless they possess special senses that normally see through invisibility."],["**Trigger** You're in the area of a grenade explosion.\n\n**Requirements** You're aware of the attack, wielding a gun, and not Off-Guard.\n\n---\n\nYou attempt to detonate the grenade with a well-timed shot from your gun. Expend an amount of ammunition from your gun equal to its usage, as if you'd fired the gun. You gain a +4 circumstance bonus to your Reflex save against the triggering grenade. Determine if you succeed on your save before rolling for anyone else in the area. If you succeed on your Reflex save, you cause the grenade to explode prematurely. Select a space of your choice directly between you and the attacker. The deflected grenade explodes in the selected space, and you don't need to save again if you're in the new explosion area."],["When you Aim, the benefits apply if your mark is within range up to your weapon's fourth range increment. Additionally, you ignore the penalty for attacking your mark at up to four range increments away."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou dance across the battlefield while dispatching enemies with precision and grace. Stride up to twice. You can make up to three ranged Strikes during this movement. Each ranged Strike you make must target a different creature within your first range increment (calculated from the point at which you took your attack at that target). Each attack counts toward your multiple attack penalty but doesn't increase your penalty until you've made all your attacks."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou take careful aim at your mark and shoot to kill. You Aim and then make a ranged Strike against your mark. If this attack is a success (but not a critical success), you deal maximum damage. Calculate this damage as if every die you would roll has a maximum result. On a critical success, roll the result normally, but if the double damage would be less than the result of a maximum damage on a normal success, use the maximum damage on the success instead.\n\nIf you spent 3 actions and your attack was a critical success, then you deal maximum damage and double the damage of that result as normal."],["You take careful aim with your shots so that your bullets ricochet off solid surfaces. When determining if you have line of effect to a target you've aimed at, you can choose one solid surface within your weapon's first range increment to ricochet your shot to hit your target; determine line of effect from the chosen ricochet surface, rather than your location. If the creature is Undetected, the GM still rolls a flat check in secret to see if you missed, but the flat check becomes DC 5."],["You have an intuitive sense that alerts you to danger and allows you to discern the presence of hidden threats. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to find traps and Hidden, Undetected, and Unnoticed creatures; to AC against attacks made by traps and hidden, undetected, and unnoticed creatures; and to saves against traps. Even if you aren't Searching, you get a check to find traps that normally require you to be Searching. You still need to meet any other requirements to find the trap. If your initiative result is tied with an opponent, you always go first."],["You've learned to defend yourself with only a gun, shielding your body and deflecting blows with stock and barrel. Guns you wield gain the parry trait. If an appropriate weapon already has the parry trait, increase the circumstance bonus to AC it grants when used to parry from +1 to +2."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou fire two shots at the same target in quick succession. You Aim and then make two Strikes against your mark. Apply the multiple attack penalty normally. If both attacks hit, combine their damage. You add any precision damage only once, to the attack of your choice. Apply the target's resistances and weaknesses only once."],["**Trigger** An ally ends their turn after hitting a creature two or more times or critically hitting a creature.\n\n**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou fire a quick shot at a foe your ally is focusing their attacks on. You Aim at the creature your triggering ally hit and then make a ranged Strike against that creature."],["You shoot and then duck out of the way to avoid retaliation and errant gunfire. Make a ranged Strike, then Take Cover."],["**Trigger** You're about to roll a Reflex saving throw, but you haven't rolled yet.\n\n---\n\nSensing danger, you can leap and twist your body away from the threat. You Step or Leap and gain a +2 circumstance bonus on your Reflex save. You must still roll the Reflex save even if this ability moves you out of range of the triggering effect."],["Your extensive training has transformed you into a living weapon, ready to pull the trigger at a moment's notice. At the start of each enemy's turn, you gain an additional reaction during that turn that you can use only for an operative reaction."],["You're a sharpshooter who doesn't need a scope or stance to shoot your best shot. You can Aim as a free action."],["You know how to target your mark's vital spots, leaving bloody wounds. When you critically hit your mark, you deal persistent bleed damage to your mark equal to your number of Aim damage dice."],["Your well-placed shots inflict devastating wounds on your targets. When you Aim, increase the precision damage dice from d4s to d6s."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou skillfully line up your shot to hinder your foe. You Aim and then make a ranged Strike against your mark. If the Strike hits, the creature becomes Off-Guard until the end of your next turn."],["**Requirements** You've Aimed at a target.\n\n---\n\nWith a deadly authority, you order your target to halt in their tracks, drop their weapons, and surrender. You attempt to Demoralize your mark. This check doesn't take the –4 circumstance penalty if the target doesn't share a language with you. On a critical success, your mark is also Immobilized for 1 round."],["**Trigger** The creature you've currently Aimed at gains the Dying or Unconscious condition.\n\n**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nAs your target falls, you immediately home in on the next. You Aim at a different creature."],["**Requirements** You have two free hands.\n\n---\n\nYou've practiced smoothly drawing and taking aim with two weapons. Draw up to two one-handed weapons and Aim."],["**Requirements** You're in an environment with suitable material to tear up, such as an urban environment.\n\n---\n\nYou dash across the battlefield, tearing up your surroundings and toppling nearby objects as you go to make it harder for your foes to maneuver or to give chase. Stride up to your Speed. The squares you move through become difficult terrain.\n\nA creature within reach of one of the affected squares can clear the area with an Interact action, removing any difficult terrain you created in the square."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou attempt to disarm your foe with a well-aimed shot. You Aim and then make a ranged Strike against your mark. If the Strike hits, attempt to Disarm the target using the same ranged attack roll against the target's Reflex DC, instead of attempting an Athletics check. A Disarming Shot counts as two attacks for your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until after you've used Disarming Shot."],["**Trigger** The last creature you Aimed at since the start of your last turn uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action.\n\n**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou attempt a ranged Strike against the triggering creature. This Strike doesn't count toward your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** Your turn begins.\n\n---\n\nWith a steadying breath and a moment of intense focus, you push yourself beyond your limits, gaining incredible speed for a short period of time. You become Quickened until the end of your turn, and you can use the extra action only to Stride. When you use this ability, you can instead choose to become quickened until the end of your next turn, but at the end of this duration, you become Fatigued for 2 rounds as your body recovers. You can still only use the extra action from quickened to Stride with this effect."],["You attack as you move, staying mobile as you fight and keeping your enemies on their toes. Either Step and then Strike, or Strike and then Step."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n**Requirements** Your last ranged Strike this turn missed or hit and failed to damage the target.\n\n---\n\nYou swap weapons with a practiced motion. You Switch Hands or Interact to swap your current weapon for another. Make a Strike against the required target with your newly drawn weapon."],["When you use Tactical Advance, you ignore difficult terrain and greater difficult terrain."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun and a melee weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou shoot your target, then you follow up with a melee attack to keep the pressure on your foe. Make a ranged Strike with your held gun. If the Strike is successful, your next melee attack this round against the same target gains a +2 circumstance bonus to the attack roll."],["You dash forward, unhindered by obstacles or walls. Stride and Long Jump or High Jump (in any order). You must start your movement on a horizontal surface. During this movement, you can ignore difficult terrain and run up vertical surfaces, like walls, at your full Speed. If you end the Stride off the ground, you fall after taking your next action or when your turn ends, whichever comes first (though you can Grab an Edge, if applicable)."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a gun.\n\n---\n\nYou aim your shots to unbalance your foe, pushing them back or knocking them over. You Aim and then make a ranged Strike against your mark. If the Strike hits, the target is knocked back 5 feet. If this forced movement would cause them to collide with a creature or object, both the target and the creature (if any) take bludgeoning damage equal to your Aim damage. On a critical hit, the target is also knocked Prone."],["You're especially dangerous while brandishing twin guns. As long as you're wielding two simple guns, both guns gain the agile trait."],["You can extend the range of your spells. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that has a range, increase that spell's range by 30 feet. As is standard for increasing spell ranges, if the spell normally has a range of touch, you extend its range to 30 feet."],["You manipulate the energy of your spell, causing it to affect a wider area. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that has an area of a burst, cone, or line and doesn't have a duration, increase the area of that spell. Add 5 feet to the radius of a burst that normally has a radius of at least 10 feet (a burst with a smaller radius isn't affected). Add 5 feet to the length of a cone or line that's normally 15 feet long or smaller, and add 10 feet to the length of a larger cone or line."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou accelerate your spellcasting. If your next action is to cast a mystic cantrip or a mystic spell that's at least 2 ranks lower than the highest-rank mystic spell slot you have, reduce the number of actions to cast it by 1 (minimum 1 action)."],["Study broadens your range of simple spells. Add two additional cantrips from your spell list to your repertoire."],["Through sheer mental effort, you can simplify the incantations and gestures needed to spellcast, leaving them barely noticeable. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell, the spell gains the subtle trait, hiding the shining runes, sparks of magic, and other manifestations that would usually give away your spellcasting. The trait hides only the spell's spellcasting actions and manifestations, not its effects, so an observer might still see a ray streak out from you or see you vanish into thin air."],["You can alter offensive spells to be less deadly. If your next action is to Cast a Spell that deals damage and doesn't have the death or void trait, that spell gains the nonlethal trait."],["You coordinate your attacks with both your solar flare and solar weapon. Make two Strikes at the same target, one with your solar weapon and one with your solar flare, each using your current multiple attack penalty. You can make these Strikes in whichever order you desire. After the first time a Strike hits, resolve the damage and effects, then swap your current attunement. If both attacks fail to hit, you become unattuned. Binaric Assault counts as two attacks when calculating your multiple attack penalty."],["You focus on your flare, setting up a blast of energy to disorient your foes. Make a ranged Strike with your solar flare. If this attack hits, the target is Off-Guard until the start of your next turn or until it Takes Cover, whichever comes first."],["You briefly meditate on the nature of your foe and their role in the wider cosmos. Attempt a check to Recall Knowledge about a creature. On a success, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your next Strike with a solar weapon against the target this round. If your Strike hits, you can choose which attunement benefit you gain for that strike. The subject of your check is temporarily immune to Meditative Analysis for 1 day.\n\nMeditative Analysis"],["You've developed a new solar manifestation—a small shield of stellar energy that orbits you. This energy shield has the attuned and solarian traits and doesn't require a hand to use. You can Raise a Shield, giving you a +1 circumstance bonus to AC until the start of your next turn. You gain the Shield Block general feat.\n\nSolar Shield\n\nWhile the shield is raised, you can use the Shield Block reaction with your shield. The shield has Hit Points equal to 5 plus twice your level and Hardness equal to half your level, rounded up. Your shield can't be broken, but if it's destroyed, you can't manifest a new shield for 10 minutes. If your shield vanishes due to you losing attunement, when you Attune to reform it, the shield returns with however many Hit Points it previously had. The shield regains all its lost Hit Points during your daily preparations and whenever you rest for at least 10 minutes, even if it's been destroyed.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** If your shield is destroyed, it releases a shock wave. Adjacent enemies must succeed at a Fortitude save against your class DC or be Suppressed for 1 round (2 rounds on a critical failure).\n\n**Photon-Attuned** If your shield is destroyed, it releases a flash of light. Adjacent enemies must succeed at a Fortitude save against your class DC or be Dazzled for 1 round (Blinded for 1 round on a critical failure)."],["You rush forward with a blast of stellar energy, getting into the thick of combat with ease. Stride twice. You gain a +10-foot circumstance bonus to your Speed during these moves.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** When you finish your Strides, enemies within 15 feet of you must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC. On a failure, they're pulled directly toward you, ending in an adjacent square if possible. You select the order these enemies are moved.\n\n**Photon-Attuned** When you finish your Strides, you create a photon field in a 15-foot burst centered on you. Until the start of your next turn, creatures outside the photon field are Concealed to creatures inside the field."],["You have a second solar weapon. When you take this feat or Re-Forge Solar Weapon, choose its traits separately from your first weapon. You can select a different damage type, traits, and weapon group for this second solar weapon. Add the agile and twin traits to the list of weapon traits you can apply to your solar weapons.\n\nSolar Weapon (Twin Weapons)"],["You focus on your solar weapon's trajectory so you can adjust it up to the last possible moment and turn a missed attack into a glancing blow. Make a Strike with your solar flare or solar weapon. It gains the following failure effect.\n\n**Failure** Your attack deals damage equal to your Strength modifier. It doesn't count as a hit and doesn't trigger any other special abilities."],["Your flare wraps around your foes on impact, entangling them. Make a solar flare Strike. On a hit, the target is Immobilized until the end of its next turn or until it Escapes (against your class DC), whichever comes first. On a critical hit, the target is additionally Off-Guard for as long as it's immobilized."],["**Frequency** once per affliction every 24 hours\n\n---\n\nYour soul becomes fuel, burning away your life force to purge an affliction. Choose a disease or poison you're afflicted by. Lose a number of Hit Points equal to the level of the affliction. Attempt a new saving throw against the affliction, as though you were at the end of its listed interval. If you fail or critically fail this save, don't increase the affliction's stage."],["**Trigger** A creature within your reach critically hits you with a melee Strike, and you're wielding two solar weapons.\n\n---\n\nYou raise one of your weapons to intercept a particularly deadly attack. You gain resistance equal to your level against the triggering attack. One of your solar weapons shatters and is no longer manifested."],["**Trigger** You would cycle or become unattuned.\n\n---\n\nYou briefly enter a meditative state in which you re-center yourself and remember the ever-shifting balance between the violent extremes of the cycle. You don't become unattuned or cycle, and you remain in your current attunement state."],["You use your solar flare to cover yourself as you close in on your foes. You Stride twice; at any point during this movement, you can make a solar flare Strike. On a hit, the target is also suppressed until the end of its next turn."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou force a rip in space that acts as a tunnel to a nearby location. Create two wormholes in unoccupied squares in line of effect that are within 100 feet, visible to you, and at least 15 feet apart. When a creature enters a wormhole's space, they emerge in an unoccupied space of their choice adjacent to the other wormhole. A creature that isn't flying treats all spaces lacking solid ground as occupied. If there's no valid space for the creature to enter, then both wormholes collapse and the creature remains in the space where it entered the first wormhole. The wormholes last for 1 round before collapsing, but you can Sustain the wormholes for up to 1 minute. Use your attunement when you take the Wormhole action to determine its attuned effects.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** A creature beginning its turn adjacent to a wormhole must succeed at a Fortitude save against your class DC or be pulled into the wormhole.\n\n**Photon-Attuned** A creature entering the wormhole becomes Concealed until the start of its next turn."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Requirements** You're photon-attuned.\n\n---\n\nYou manifest a fragment of the cosmic forces from the Universe's first moments, unleashing a blast of scouring cosmic fire that reverts all things to their basic components and overcomes even magical defenses. This deals 10))d6 fire damage to all creatures in a 30-foot emanation. You and any number of adjacent allies are unaffected by this Big Bang. Affected creatures can attempt a Reflex save against your class DC.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and 2d6 persistent fire damage.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and 4d6 persistent fire damage, and you can attempt to counteract a spell on the creature, using half your level, rounded up, as the counteract rank.\n\n---\n\n**Level (+1)** Increase the damage by 1d6."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Requirements** You're graviton-attuned.\n\n---\n\nYou call upon a shred of the unstoppable cosmic force that eventually destroys all things. You concentrate and manifest the pinpoint center of a black hole within 60 feet. This occupies a single 5-foot space. Creatures within the singularity's space take 10))d8 void damage with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. Any creature dropped to 0 Hit Points by this effect is torn asunder and pulled into the singularity, leaving no remains. Until the end of your next turn, light can't pass through the singularity's space and all adjacent squares, shrouding it in darkness that even creatures with darkvision or greater darkvision can't see through. Any creature that starts its turn in the darkness must succeed at a basic Fortitude save against your class DC or become Slowed 1 for that turn.\n\n---\n\n**Level (+2)** Increase the damage by 2d8."],["**Trigger** Your Solar Shield is destroyed while you have it raised.\n\n**Requirements** You haven't used Black Hole or Supernova within the last 10 minutes.\n\n---\n\nYour solar shield collapses in on itself.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** Immediately use Black Hole as a free action (if you have the Black Hole feat).\n\n**Photon-Attuned** Immediately use Supernova as a free action (if you have the Supernova feat)."],["You supercharge your solar flare and unleash multiple simultaneous blasts at all foes in an area. Make a solar flare Strike with a –2 circumstance penalty against each enemy in a 15-foot burst centered on any point within your solar flare's first range increment. Each attack counts toward your multiple attack penalty, but you don't increase your penalty until you've made all your attacks.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** You can Stride up to half your speed once as a free action immediately before or after making your attacks.\n\n**Photon-Attuned** You're Concealed to each target of this attack until the start of your next turn."],["You can use your manifestations immediately upon attuning yourself. When you Attune as a single action, you can make a Strike with your solar flare or solar weapon as a free action."],["Dissonance grants you some clarity and a brief second wind in stressful situations. When you use an action with the disharmony trait, you gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to half your level until the start of your next turn.\n\nHarmonic Convergence"],["You extend your control of stellar forces to punish your foes. Creatures that hit you with an attack suffer consequences based on your attunement.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** The creature is Clumsy 1 and Off-Guard for 1 round. This increases to Clumsy 2 if this is the second time it hit you this turn.\n\n**Photon-Attuned** The creature takes persistent fire damage equal to half your level."],["You've come to rely on ranged motes as much as you do your solar weapon. Triple the range increment of your solar flare. When you make a solar flare Strike against a target within your first range increment, you ignore the target's concealment and cover."],["Your concentration lets you fire your solar flare even further. Increase the range increment of your solar flare by 15 feet."],["Your attacks create a brilliant eclipse that veil you from the enemy's view. Make a Strike with your solar weapon or your solar flare. On a hit, you create an impressive display of solar energy between you and your foe. Increase the level of cover you receive from your enemy by one step. Lesser cover becomes standard cover, or standard cover becomes greater cover in the case of creatures at least one size category larger than you. This effect lasts until the start of your next turn.\n\n---\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** For the duration, if you don't have any cover against an attack targeting you, you gain lesser cover against that attack.\n\n**Photon-Attuned** For the duration, if the target you struck provides you cover against an enemy's attack, that enemy takes a –1 circumstance penalty to their attack roll."],["With practice, you can make on-the-fly battlefield adjustments to your weapon, letting you choose the perfect attack for a situation. When you Attune, you can change the damage type of your solar weapon (but not its traits or weapon group), as if you'd Re-Forge Solar Weapon."],["You pour all your effort into making a single attack with your solar weapon that's so powerful it shatters the weapon. Strike with your solar weapon. The Strike deals one additional weapon damage die. Your solar weapon shatters and must be manifested to continue using it.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** On a hit, the target takes a –10-foot status penalty to Speed until the start of your next turn.\n\nShattering Impact\n\n**Photon-Attuned** On a hit, you additionally deal persistent fire damage equal to half your level, rounded up."],["Your training has helped you adapt to bulkier armor. You're trained in heavy armor. Whenever you gain a class feature that grants you expert or greater proficiency in medium armor, you also gain that proficiency in heavy armor. You treat armor you wear of 2 Bulk or higher as though it were 1 Bulk lighter (to a minimum of 1 Bulk)."],["You reach true alignment with the cosmic cycle. You're permanently Quickened. You can use your extra action only to Attune or make a Strike with your solar flare or solar weapon."],["You have absolute control and understanding of your attunement with the stellar forces of the cosmos. If you would become graviton- or photon-attuned, you instead become perfectly-attuned. When you're perfectly-attuned, you can choose which attunement bonus to benefit from (either graviton- or photon-attuned) when using any of your abilities. If any of your abilities require you to be in a specific attunement state, being perfectly-attuned counts as your choice of graviton- or photon-attuned."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** You're graviton-attuned.\n\n---\n\nYou concentrate on the gravitational forces around you, pulling matter toward you in emulation of a black hole. Select any number of creatures within 30 feet. Each affected creature takes (floor(level / 2)d8) bludgeoning damage and must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage and is pulled 5 feet toward you.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage, is pulled 15 feet toward you, and is Off-Guard against the next melee attack that you attempt against it before the end of your current turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage, is pulled 30 feet toward you, and is knocked Prone.\n\n---\n\n**Level (+2)** Increase the damage by 1d8."],["You infuse your attunements with additional energy. When you deal fire damage or persistent fire damage due to being photon-attuned, you can instead choose to deal vitality damage or persistent vitality damage, which damages creatures with void healing, such as undead.\n\nWhile graviton-attuned, Strikes with your solar weapon cause the target to count all squares within 10 feet as difficult terrain, rather than just adjacent squares."],["**Trigger** You would be damage by an attack, spell, or other effect.\n\n**Requirements** You're aware of the triggering effect and not offguard.\n\n---\n\nYou harness your solar nimbus to protect yourself from harm. You gain resistance equal to half your level (rounded up) until the start of your next turn. You choose the type of resistance when you use this action, depending on your current attunement.\n\nYou can use Nimbus Ward as a reaction only when the requirements and trigger are met, but you can use it as a 1-action activity without the requirements or trigger being met.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** Your resistance can be one of the following types of damage: bludgeoning, force, piercing, or slashing.\n\n**Photon-Attuned** Your resistance can be one of the following types of energy damage: acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic."],["You unleash an ejection of plasma, hitting every creature in your choice of a 10-foot emanation or in a 30-foot line. Each creature in the area takes ((1 + floor(level / 2))d6) fire damage with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. A creature that critically fails its save additionally takes 1d8 persistent electricity damage.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** A creature that fails its save is knocked Prone.\n\n**Photon-Attuned** Increase the fire damage to d8s.\n\n---\n\n**Level (+2)** The damage increases by 1d6 (or 1d8 if you're photon-attuned)."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** You're photon-attuned.\n\n---\n\nYou unleash your pent-up energy, causing it to erupt like the stellar events that birth and end stars. You can choose to affect creatures in a 15-foot or 30-foot emanation. Each affected creature takes (level)d8 fire damage and must attempt a Reflex save against your class DC. If you choose the 30-foot option, you instead deal (level)d6 fire damage.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage and is Dazzled for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is Blinded for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and is blinded for 1 minute.\n\n---\n\n**Level (+1)** Increase the damage by 1d8 (or 1d6 for the 30-foot option)."],["You manifest a copy of your solar weapon, causing it to circle around you in a vortex, leaving constellation patterns in its wake. A creature that starts its turn adjacent to you takes damage of an amount and type equal to the weapon damage of your solar weapon, with a basic Reflex save against your class DC. If you already have an active vortex when you use Constellation Vortex, add another weapon to the vortex instead, up to a maximum of 3 weapons at any time. Each added weapon increases the damage of the vortex by 1. You can Sustain the vortex for up to 1 minute.\n\nWhen the vortex ends, it shatters, dealing damage equal to your level, plus 1 for each weapon in the vortex, to all adjacent creatures. This damage is of the same type as your solar weapon.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** Increase the damage of the vortex by 2 per weapon (including the first).\n\n**Photon-Attuned** Add 1 fire damage per weapon (including the first).\n\n---\n\n**Level (+3)** The damage from each additional weapon increases by 2, and the extra damage from your attunement effect increases by 1."],["You unleash a corona of stellar energy in a 10-foot emanation, which lasts until the end of your next turn. You can Sustain your Corona for up to 1 minute. If your attunement changes, your Corona's attunement effect changes to match. While graviton-attuned, your Corona has the darkness trait. While photon-attuned, your Corona has the light trait.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** Your Corona is darkness that prevents light from penetrating the area. This acts as a Darkness spell with a spell rank equal to half your level.\n\n**Photon-Attuned** Your Corona is solar light that sheds bright light in the area (and dim light for the next 20 feet). While within your Corona's bright light, Invisible creatures become Concealed, and creatures already concealed are no longer concealed."],["You've combined the strength of your defensive powers such that your solar nimbus bolsters your solar shield. When you Shield Block a melee attack with your solar shield, as long as either you or your shield take damage from the attack, you can use Nimbus Ward as a free action."],["You can fire off multiple shots with your solar flare in short succession. Make three solar flare Strikes against different targets, each with a –2 circumstance penalty. These attacks count toward your multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until after you've made the attacks."],["**Requirements** Your last action was a successful solar flare or solar weapon Strike against a creature.\n\n---\n\nYou brand the creature with potent solar energy that keeps it visible and attracts your solar flare. When targeting the branded creature, increase the range increment of your solar flare by 60 feet. If the branded creature is Invisible, or later becomes invisible, it's Concealed instead. If the branded creature was already concealed for any other reason, it's no longer concealed.\n\nThe brand lasts 10 minutes but ends immediately if the branded creature is slain or you Star Brand a different creature."],["You break the bonds of gravity. While graviton-attuned, you gain a fly Speed equal to your Speed."],["You attack a target with your solar weapon, harnessing the collision's energy to attack another foe at the speed of light. Make a Strike with your solar weapon. On a hit, you teleport up to your Speed into an unoccupied square within reach of a different creature and then immediately make a solar weapon Strike against them. If your initial Strike fails, you don't teleport, and the action ends.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** Increase the range to double your Speed.\n\n**Photon-Attuned** If a Strike made as part of this action is a critical success, the struck target is Dazzled until the end of its next turn."],["Your solar shield acts as an anchor for your mind as much as your body. When your Raise your solar Shield, you gain the shield's circumstance bonus to Will saves. In addition, while you have your solar shield raised, you can Shield Block when you take damage as a result of a failed Will save, in addition to its usual trigger. If you do, the triggering damage bypasses your solar shield's object immunities."],["**Requirements** Your last action was a successful solar weapon Strike.\n\n---\n\nYou use the momentum of your last attack to maneuver around the battlefield, either by leaving photonic images or making great gravity-assisted leaps. Step twice.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** You move 10 feet with each Step, rather than 5 feet.\n\n**Photon-Attuned** You leave an afterimage in the square you started in. This image lasts until the end of your next turn but ends early if another creature enters the space. This afterimage counts as an ally to you and your allies for the purposes of flanking."],["You fire blasts of solar energy through your raised shield, harnessing its gravitational force to propel your attacks. When you make a solar flare Strike while you have your solar shield raised, increase the range increment of your solar flare by 10 feet and increase the damage your solar flare deals by 1 per weapon damage die.\n\n**Graviton-Attuned** The additional damage is bludgeoning damage. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the Trip attempt on a critical success.\n\n**Photon-Attuned** The additional damage is fire damage. Increase the persistent fire damage on a critical success to 1d8."],["You can partly discorporate your body, becoming a blur of stellar matter pushed by invisible solar winds. While photonattuned, you gain a +10-foot circumstance bonus to Speed and can move through the space of a single unwilling creature each time you Stride."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You fail an Athletics check to Disarm, Grapple, Reposition, Shove, or Trip.\n\n---\n\nYou draw on your inner reserves and rally yourself to try again. Reroll the triggering check, but you must use the new result, even if it's worse."],["**Trigger** A creature you're observing succeeds at their saving throw against your Area Fire or Auto-Fire attack.\n\n---\n\nYou focus your weapons fire on a resilient target in order to suppress them with the sheer ferocity of your assault. The required target must succeed at a Will save against your class DC or become Suppressed until the start of your next turn."],["**Trigger** You're wielding a two-handed weapon, and an enemy creature moves adjacent to you.\n\n---\n\nYou can switch weapons in stressful situations so that you quickly set yourself up to punish incoming foes. You stow your current weapon and draw another two-handed weapon. If you have multiple sets of arms, you can instead Switch Hands."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a two-handed ranged weapon with a reload of 2 or more, and your last action was an attack that expended ammo from the weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou know that reloading a weapon can be a delicate process, but you've mastered how to do so in the middle of combat, starting while still in the act of firing your weapon. You Interact to reload your weapon twice. Unlike most Interact actions, you don't need a free hand to reload your ranged weapon in this way."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a two-handed melee weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou swipe your weapon in a wide swing to create a deadly arc. Your weapon gains the area (burst 5 feet) and unwieldy traits until the end of the turn. If your weapon has reach, the burst radius becomes the reach of your weapon. Area Fire with the required weapon, centering the burst on a corner of a square you occupy. You're excluded from the burst. If you're using a weapon with the backswing or sweep trait, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the save DC of the attack. If you have the primary target class feature, the primary target Strike you make is a melee Strike, rather than a ranged Strike."],["Your suppressing attacks pin foes in place, preventing them from moving at more than a crawling pace. When you Suppress a target with one of your attacks, increase the speed penalty to a –20-foot status penalty for the duration of the suppressed condition. If the effect that imparted the suppressed condition was a critical hit, or the target critically fails its save and becomes suppressed, then the target also becomes Stunned 1.\n\nAnchoring Impacts"],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area or automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou prepare the perfect shot, able to tear through those closest to the impact point. If your next action is to Area Fire, Auto-Fire, or Whirling Swipe, add two additional weapon damage dice to targets who are adjacent to the center point of impact or within the first 10 feet of a cone or line."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You are reduced to 0 Hit Points and would fall Unconscious.\n\n---\n\nYou fight on to the absolute last, pushing yourself to make one final attack at a foe. Make a Strike with a –2 circumstance penalty, or make an Area Fire or Auto-Fire attack ignoring the unwieldy trait and with the save DC decreased by 2. After the attack is concluded, you immediately fall unconscious and gain the Dying condition."],["You compel enemies to avoid your attacks by aiming at their legs, wings, or other forms of movement to make them easier to outmaneuver. When you Suppress a target with one of your attacks, it also becomes Off-Guard until the start of its turn.\n\nIn addition, when Auto-Firing in a cone that affects only a single target, that target takes a –1 circumstance penalty to Reflex saves against the Auto-Fire attack."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n---\n\nWhether you got tired of getting hit in the face or slipping on bullet casings in the middle of a fight, you've learned how to redirect your weapon's spent ammunition or terrain warping vented energy while firing off a barrage. After you make an Area Fire or Auto-Fire attack with a weapon, make any number of squares adjacent to you difficult terrain. If a square was already difficult terrain, it instead becomes greater difficult terrain. Any difficult or greater difficult terrain created by this action remains in place until cleared."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an automatic or area (cone) weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou fire your weapon in sustained bursts to unleash a consistent deluge of firepower that tears apart the terrain to become treacherous. Make an Area Fire or Auto-Fire attack with your weapon. Until the start of your next turn, any creature that moves through the area you attacked takes 1d4 damage of the same type as the weapon fired per square traversed, with a basic Reflex save at the end of each move action it takes through the area. On a failure, a creature becomes Suppressed until the start of your next turn."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area or automatic weapon with a full magazine.\n\n---\n\nSpinning in place, you fire indiscriminately to completely clear out the room. You Area Fire (even if using an automatic weapon), affecting each creature in an emanation around you with a radius equal to the range of the weapon, expending the weapon's entire magazine. Creatures in the area take a –1 circumstance penalty to Reflex saves against this attack due to the cataclysmic nature of the raining fire. You don't designate a primary target with this attack."],["You adjust the angle of your barrage to maximize the ammunition's impact on creatures' bodies. Increase the distance creatures are pushed by your Shoving Shot to 5 feet on a success, 10 feet on a failure, and 20 feet on a critical failure. In addition, on a critical failure, the target is also knocked Prone."],["**Trigger** You and one adjacent ally attempt a Reflex or Fortitude save against the same effect.\n\n---\n\nWhether holding up a crumbling ceiling or jumping into a fireball, you interpose yourself between your ally and incoming danger. The result of your save becomes one degree worse, but the result of your ally's save becomes one degree higher."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area (burst) weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou fire your weapon as you jump, using the explosion to propel yourself to new heights or just out of a situation more dangerous than an explosion. You make an Area Fire and then Leap, using your weapon to add a status bonus to the distance traveled equal to double the burst of your weapon. You must be somewhere within the area of the weapon's area attack, but you don't have to save against the effect of your attack.\n\nMovement made as part of this action doesn't trigger reactions, though Area Fire still triggers them normally."],["**Frequency** once per round\n\n**Requirements** Your last action this turn was an Area Fire or Auto-Fire.\n\n---\n\nYou hold down the trigger and continue blasting. You Area Fire or Auto-Fire, ignoring your weapon's unwieldy trait. You don't designate a primary target with this attack, and creatures you damage with this attack don't gain the Suppressed condition."],["You use your weapon to help corral panicked enemies. An enemy who critically fails a save against your Area Fire or Auto-Fire is Fleeing for 1 round."],["Your overwhelming onslaught scatters enemies like leaves in the wind. When you Shoving Shot, all creatures in the area attempt the Fortitude save to avoid forced movement, rather than just your primary target."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area or automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nYour weapon blasts apart the battlefield and leaves it a ruinous waste. You Area Fire or Auto-Fire. You don't designate a primary target, but instead make each square in the area of your attack difficult terrain. If a square was already difficult terrain, it becomes greater difficult terrain. Any difficult or greater difficult terrain created by this action remains in place and can't be changed without extensive engineering or magic."],["**Trigger** A Suppressed creature damages you with a Strike.\n\n---\n\nYour armor absorbs some of the kinetic energy of your opponent's attack. You gain resistance equal to half your level against the triggering damage (or equal to your level if you have the Armor Storm fighting style). If the triggering creature is within reach, attempt an Athletics check to Shove it."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area or automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nYour opponents can run, but they can't hide! You spray your weapon in the general direction of an unseen enemy, revealing its location. You Area Fire or Auto-Fire. If the primary target is Concealed, you don't need to attempt a flat check to target it, and if it's Hidden, the DC of the flat check to target it is 5.\n\nWhen you Suppress a concealed creature with this attack, the debris around it helps reveal its current position, and no flat check is needed to target it; If it's hidden, the DC of the flat check to target it becomes 5, and the creature can't become undetected. This benefit lasts as long as the creature remains suppressed."],["Sometimes there's no better way to assure success than to pin a hapless enemy with concentrated firepower. When you Suppress a creature with Area Fire or Auto-Fire and only one creature was in the area of your attack, or when you use Concentrated Shot, the target takes 1d10 persistent bleed damage. If you critically hit it with your primary target Strike, this increases to 2d10 persistent bleed damage."],["Constant drills and combat experience leave you with reflexes capable of making snap decisions. Choose one soldier class feat you have that grants a reaction. At the start of your turn, you gain an additional reaction that you can only use for the selected class feat or an action granted by the selected class feat.\n\nYou can change the reaction selected for this feat when you make your daily preparations as long as the new feat meets the requirements."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area or automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nWith a mighty bellow, you unload your weapon to give your allies the cover they need to rally. You Area Fire or Auto-Fire without selecting a primary target. Give a verbal order as part of your firing, selecting either Reload, Strike, or Take Cover. Every ally within 30 feet who hears and understands your order can perform the action you selected as a reaction."],["You have become a legendary soldier on par with the saints of Damoritosh and need not choose between the destructive power of your firearm and the honor of your personal armament. You can wield two-handed weapons in one hand."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area or automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou skillfully line up your attack to harry two targets within your blast zone with equal lethality. You Area Fire or Auto-Fire, selecting two different primary targets, rather than one."],["Your laughter (or other vocalization) remains audible over the din of your weapons fire. Attempt an Intimidation check to Demoralize each creature within 30 feet who's Suppressed."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You take damage.\n\n---\n\nYou bounce back stronger after a hit, ready to continue the fight. You gain 1d8+4 temporary Hit Points that last for 1 minute. Increase this amount by 1d8+4 at 6th level and every 4 levels thereafter."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area or automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nBy preparing your weapon while on the move, you ready yourself to fire a salvo as soon as you're in position. Stride up to your Speed, and then Area Fire or Auto-Fire."],["You brace yourself as you prepare to defend your allies behind you. You Area Fire or Auto-Fire. Until the start of your next turn or until you use a move action, whichever happens first, you gain the Living Shield reaction and, if you would be moved by a forced movement effect, you move 10 feet less."],["Your destructive power has become second nature as enemies stand in awe of your overwhelming firepower. You can use the Area Fire or Auto-Fire attacks as a single action. However, you can never make more than two such attacks in the same round."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area or automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou can combine methods into a deadly new hybrid technique. Choose two soldier feats that take 2 actions to use, require you to wield an area or automatic weapon, and cause you to make an Area Fire or Auto-Fire attack as part of its effects. You Area Fire or Auto-Fire once and then apply the additional effects and benefits of both selected feats to the attack."],["**Trigger** You reduce your primary target to 0 Hit Points using Auto-Fire.\n\n---\n\nWith a subtle gesture of your weapon and a stare, you remind a survivor of your onslaught that there's more where that came from. Demoralize a single creature that was in the area of your Auto-Fire; you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to this check. If you have legendary proficiency in Intimidation, or if you have the Action Hero fighting style and the target of Collateral Witness is the enemy closest to you, you can use this as a free action with the same trigger."],["You overwhelm the defenses of suppressed foes. Your multiple attack penalty for attacks against suppressed targets is –4 (–3 with an agile weapon) on your second attack of the turn instead of –5, and –8 (–6 with an agile weapon) on your third and subsequent attacks of the turn instead of –10."],["**Requirements** Your last action this turn was an Area Fire attack.\n\n---\n\nYou know unleashing a barrage of gunfire can bring most enemies low. You make a follow-up Strike against your primary target using the same weapon. Ignore the unwieldy trait on your weapon when using this action. This doesn't make a new area attack and is treated as a Strike made using primary target."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area or automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou use the blast of your weapon to push back your adversaries. You Area Fire or Auto-Fire. Your primary target must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC.\n\n---\n\n**Failure** The target is pushed back 10 feet. If using an area (burst) weapon, the target is pushed away from the burst's center point.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the target is pushed 15 feet."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area or automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou set up your area weapon to affect more targets. If the next action you use is to Area Fire or Auto-Fire in a burst, cone, or line, or if you use Whirling Swipe, you increase the area of that attack. Add 5 feet to the radius of a burst that normally has a radius of at least 10 feet (a burst with a smaller radius isn't affected). Add 5 feet to the length of a cone or line that's normally 15 feet or smaller, and add 10 feet to the length of a larger cone or line."],["You make a well placed shot or unleash a hail of fire to cover your allies. Make a ranged Strike against a target and select one ally within range of the same attack. If your Strike hits your target, you deal no damage, but the targeted creature becomes Suppressed and takes a –2 circumstance penalty on attacks made against your ally until the end of your next turn.\n\nCovering Fire\n\nYou can use Covering Fire as a 2-action activity to Area Fire or Auto-Fire instead of making a ranged Strike, affecting targets that fail their save."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area or automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nThe flash and smoke from your frenzied gunfire conceals you from any enemies who might be left standing in the aftermath. You Area Fire or Auto-Fire. You leave behind a cloud of smoke and dust within the area that lasts until the end of your next turn or until dissipated by a strong wind (whichever happens first). Creatures in the area have the Concealed condition, and all other creatures are concealed to them."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You regain consciousness after being Unconscious.\n\n---\n\nEven when you're downed, you get right back into the thick of things once recovered. You Stand and Interact to draw a weapon or grab an unattended weapon."],["You taunt your enemy mercilessly, forcing them to acknowledge you as an immediate threat. Attempt an Intimidation check and compare it to the Will DC of one enemy creature within 60 feet. This action has the auditory trait or visual trait, depending on how you taunt your enemy.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** Your taunts sting hard. Until the start of your next turn, any hostile actions that the creature takes must include you as a target or include you in the area; otherwise, the creature takes a –2 circumstance penalty to attack rolls and to its save DC for those hostile actions.\n\n**Success** As critical success, but only the first hostile action that the creature takes is affected.\n\n**Failure** The creature is unaffected.\n\nIntimidating Taunt"],["**Requirements** You have a force field upgrade in your armor or are holding a tech shield.\n\n---\n\nYou overcharge a shield to create a concussive blast that repulses nearby foes. You Area Fire using your force field or shield, dealing 2d10 bludgeoning damage in a 5-foot radius burst excluding yourself centered on one corner of a square you occupy. This attack has the tracking +1 trait and is in the shield weapon group. A creature that fails its save is pushed back 5 feet. If you have the primary target class feature, the primary target Strike uses your force field or shield.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you're using a force field or shield that's superior or better, the tracking trait increases to +2, or +3 if ultimate or better. Likewise, if it's elite or better, the damage increases to 3d10 bludgeoning, or 4d10 bludgeoning if paragon."],["**Trigger** A creature within your reach uses a manipulate action, makes a ranged Strike, uses a move action, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.\n\n---\n\nYour foe's momentary lapse in defense gives you an opening Make a melee Strike against the triggering creature, ignoring the unwieldy trait on any weapons you're wielding for this Strike. This Strike doesn't count toward your multiple attack penalty, and your multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nBy using direct and methodical burst fire, you conserve your ammunition without compromising your destructive potential. Your Auto-Fire has an expend equal to the number of targets in the area, rather than the number of targets in the area × 2."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a two-handed weapon.\n\n---\n\nYour sheer bravado bolsters your defenses despite your recklessness. Until the start of your next turn, you take a –2 circumstance penalty to AC and gain resistance to all damage equal to half your level. If you have the Armor Storm fighting style, this resistance is doubled against attacks made by suppressed creatures."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an automatic weapon.\n\n---\n\nFocusing your fire enables you to target an enemy for immediate destruction. Make a ranged Strike with an automatic weapon, expending three times the ammo and gaining a +4 circumstance bonus to damage. This bonus increases to +6 at 11th level and +8 at 15th level."],["**Trigger** A suppressed creature within your weapon's first range increment makes a ranged attack or leaves a square during a move action it's using.\n\n---\n\nYou concentrate fire on a specific target operating within your weapon's threat range. Make a ranged Strike against the triggering creature, ignoring the unwieldy trait of weapons you wield for this Strike. On a critical hit, if the triggering action was a move action, you disrupt that action."],["**Requirements** You're wielding an area weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou hold down the trigger and push your weapons to their absolute limits with a ceaseless barrage of firepower. Area Fire twice with the required weapon, ignoring the unwieldy trait of your weapon. Creatures in the area of the second Area Fire attack gain a +2 circumstance bonus to their save.\n\nAfter you use this action, your weapon must cool off and can't be used until after your next turn or until you take any amount of cold damage."],["You've programmed a clever little mascot, uploaded into a body of pure magic. The resulting creature is a loyal companion and assists you in your day-to-day life. You gain a familiar."],["**Requirements** You have line of effect to a tech minion under your control within 120 feet.\n\n---\n\nYou transfer a spell between yourself and your minion. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell that affects only you, other than a polymorph spell, the spell affects your minion instead of you."],["You can freely speak with technology. You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with tech creatures. You don't need to share a language to communicate with such creatures in this way, although some creatures might lack the ability to communicate using spoken language and need to communicate using writing."],["You can piggyback on magic frequencies from your spell database to access your stored *spell chips* and *spell gems*. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell from a *spell chip* or *spell gem*, you don't have to be holding the item to activate it."],["You've made a breakthrough well suited to your preferred strategies. You learn the greater magic hack of your chosen programming language."],["You can hack reality, connecting two separate locations with a magical hyperlink and enabling fast travel between them. You gain the Liminal Hyperlink magic hack."],["You overcharge your spell to bypass your enemy's defenses. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell, the spell ignores an amount of the target's resistance to acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic damage equal to your level. This applies to all damage the spell deals, including persistent damage and damage caused by an ongoing effect of the spell, such as the wall created by wall of fire. A creature's immunities are unaffected."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nIf your next action is to Cast a Spell that requires a saving throw against a single target, you channel the magic through your weapon. Make a Strike against the target. On a hit, in addition to the normal effects of the Strike, the target takes a –1 circumstance penalty to its save against the spell (–2 circumstance penalty on a critical hit)."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** You have an overclocked tech minion.\n\n---\n\nYou channel energy from your overclocked tech minion into your spell database. If your next action is to Cast a Spell, you siphon surplus magical energy to cause your overclocked minion to Stride and erupt in a burst of flames and lightning after the spell resolves. It deals 3d4 fire and 3d4 electricity damage in a 10-foot emanation (basic Reflex save against your spell DC) and is destroyed. At 12th level and every two levels thereafter, increase the fire and electricity damage you deal by 1d4."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nMagical circuitry blazes to life on your body and empowers your spells' code. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell by activating a *spell chip* or *spell gem*, heighten the spell up to two ranks lower than the highest-rank spell slot you can cast."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nIf your next action is to Cast a Spell with a duration of no longer than 10 minutes that targets a single creature, you can amplify and reroute the defensive barrier being generated by your armor to empower your target. You Overclock Armor, immediately lose all your temporary Hit Points, and grant the same amount of temporary Hit Points you lost to the target of the spell. These temporary Hit Points last until the spell ends."],["You've mastered another programming language. You learn the advanced magic hack of the same programming language as the magic hack you learned with Cross-Platform Application."],["You can modify spells beyond compare. Once per hour, when you use Jailbreak Spell to apply the spellshape granted by your programming language to a spell, you can apply both the basic and advanced jailbreak benefits from your programming language. The spell you modify must still meet all the usual requirements of the spellshape and of both jailbreak effects."],["You can overclock a wider variety of gear. When you take this feat, select one programming language other than your own. You gain the overclock boost benefits of that programming language, meaning you can select that type of gear when you Overclock Gear instead of the type normally allowed by your original programming language. You don't gain the firmware enhancement, Overclock Pulse, or other benefits of that programming language."],["**Trigger** You would be hit, but not critically hit, by an attack.\n\n**Requirements** Your gear is overclocked.\n\n---\n\nA wall of data bursts from your overclocked gear to shield you from harm. The attacker must roll its attack roll a second time and take the lower result."],["During your daily preparations, you gain one extra spell slot of your highest rank, which you can use only to prepare or Download Spells from your spell cache."],["You adjust the parameters of a spell to operate at maximum efficiency. If your next action is to Cast a Spell that deals damage or restores Hit Points, any die you roll for damage or healing that has a result of less than 2 becomes 2 instead."],["**Requirements** You have an active spell affecting an area or a single ally within 60 feet.\n\n---\n\nThe battlefield isn't always as predictable as you'd like, so you've devised a method to shift around your spell effects after they've been deployed. If the required spell affects an area, you move the spell's area to a new location, and the spell no longer affects its previous area. If the required spell affects a single ally, you move the spell to a new ally, and the spell no longer affects its previous target. The new area or target must meet any of the spell's usual requirements, including range and line of effect from you when you Recalculate Coordinates. Regardless of the required spell's area or target, the spell's remaining duration is reduced by half."],["You apply the outdated technique of clustering identical systems to form a parallel computing cluster to your magic, allowing you to manage more than one piece of overclocked gear at once. You can have up to two pieces of overclocked gear at once, and you overclock up to two pieces of gear whenever you Overclock Gear. Only one piece of overclocked gear is no longer overclocked when you use Jailbreak Spell."],["You can take an extra moment when you access your spell cache to gain nearly unlimited access to its contents. When you Download Spell, you can do so as a single action instead of a free action. If you do, you can download any number of spells in your spell cache into any number of your available spell slots, replacing spells on a one-for-one basis and filling spell slots as usual when you Download Spell."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** Your turn begins.\n\n---\n\nArcane scripts from the infosphere can be easily transferred from one spell database to another, allowing technomancers access to spellshapes without having to know exactly how they work. Until the end of your turn, you gain a single spellshape feat from the technomancer class that has a level requirement of no more than half your level."],["You copy the components of your spell before casting it from your database, maintaining a copy that duplicates the spell's effects. If your next action is to Cast a Spell of 4th rank or lower that has no duration, the spell's energy remains temporarily copied. You can Cast the Spell a second time before the end of your next turn without expending a spell slot."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Trigger** You critically succeed at a saving throw against an enemy's spell, or an enemy critically fails at a spell attack roll against you.\n\n---\n\nYou decompile an enemy's spell and take its lingering magical energy for yourself. You gain the ability to cast the triggering spell one time before the end of your next turn, even if it's not on your spell list or is of a higher rank than you can cast. This doesn't cost you a spell slot or other resources. If you cast it using a spellshape against the creature that originally cast it, that creature cannot use any reactions that would trigger from you Casting the Spell. Use your own spellcasting statistics for this spell, as you do for other spells you cast."],["You briefly hack reality, allowing you to pass through walls, ignore damage, and phase through enemies. You gain the Speedrun magic hack."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYour magic protects the delicate lattice of your *spell gems* from damage so they can be used more than once. If your next action is to Cast a Spell from a *spell gem*, instead of being destroyed, the spell gem becomes a temporary item that can't be sold and lasts only until you use it again or the next time you make your daily preparations (whichever comes first). If your next action is to Cast a Spell from a *spell chip* that has already been used once today, it becomes broken on a failure (but is still destroyed on a critical failure)."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYour magic is directed into your armor to protect you from harm. If your next action is to Cast a Spell that deals at least one type of energy damage (acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic), you gain resistance to an energy damage type of your choice equal to twice the spell's rank for 1 minute. You get the resistance regardless of whether or not your spell dealt damage."],["You infuse your familiar with additional magical energy, increasing its abilities. You can select four familiar or master abilities each day, instead of two."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes You alter the type of energy output of your magic. If your next action is to Cast a Spell with no duration that has an elemental trait (air, earth, fire, metal, water, or wood) and deals one type of damage, replace the elemental trait with a different elemental trait and the damage it deals with one of the damage types corresponding to the selected trait: air (electricity or sonic), earth (bludgeoning or piercing), fire (fire), metal (acid or slashing), water (cold), wood (poison)."],["You exploit magical shortcuts to effortlessly alter your spells. You can use spellshape single actions as free actions."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou understand the nuanced beauty of arcane code and can modify it in ways other spellcasters can hardly fathom. Use up to three single-action technomancer spellshape feats. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell, apply all of these spellshapes to that spell."],["You've cracked the root access of arcane magic itself. You gain an additional 10th-rank spell slot."],["**Requirements** You're wielding a ranged weapon, and your most recent action was to Cast a Spell from a *spell gem*.\n\n---\n\nYou take the delicate remains of a consumed spell gem and load it into your ranged weapon as magic ammunition. Overclock Gear, ignoring its usual trigger. Until the end of your turn, the weapon deals an extra 1d6 force damage and gains the arcane trait if it didn't have it already. If the spell dealt a different type of damage, the Strike deals this type of damage instead (or your choice of one type of damage if the spell dealt multiple types of damage)."],["You've learned how to exploit the vulnerabilities of glitching creatures to force them to do your bidding for a short time. You gain the Black Hat Trick magic hack."],["You've expanded your spell cache. Select any two spells that are in your spell database; each spell you select must be of a different rank. The selected spells are temporarily added to your spell cache. Each time you gain a new rank of spells, you can remove one of the selected spells from your spell cache and replace it with another spell from your spell database."],["**Requirements** You control an overclocked minion.\n\n---\n\nWhen you apply the Conceal Spell spellshape to a spell, you can manifest the spell from one of your overclocked minions instead of yourself. Use the minion's space to determine the spell's source, range, and area of effect, but line of sight and line of effect must be met from both you and your minion when the spell is cast. If the spell has a range of touch, you can have the minion deliver the spell to a creature within its reach."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You roll initiative.\n\n---\n\nYou've programmed your gear to be ready to overclock at a moment's notice. You Overclock Gear, ignoring its trigger."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYour subroutine diverts a portion of your spell's energy to create a shield. If your next action is to Cast a Spell, you or your minion with the tech trait gains temporary Hit Points equal to double the rank of the spell that last 1 minute. If the spell deals at least one type of energy damage (acid, cold, electricity, fire, force, sonic, vitality, or void), you or your minion gain resistance to an energy damage type of your choice equal to the spell's rank for as long as the temporary Hit Points remain."],["Whether out of practicality or sentimentality, you keep all your technological tools at your disposal in impeccable condition—even if they're only at your disposal for a minimal amount of time. Tech creatures under your control, including minions, within a 30-foot emanation around you gain a +2 status bonus to saving throws and resistance to electricity damage equal to half your level rounded up."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou bind a hostile spell into your armor. If your next action is to Cast a Spell with a hostile effect that targets one creature, you store the spell in your armor instead. The spell must use a spell slot and take 2 or fewer actions to cast. Your armor can store only one spell in this way; you can't use Active Defense Firewall while you already have a spell stored.\n\nWhen a creature touches or damages you with an unarmed melee attack or non-reach melee weapon, you can Cast the Spell stored in your armor as a reaction, targeting the triggering creature. Only the creature that triggered the reaction is affected by the spell.\n\nYou can Dismiss Active Defense Firewall. If you do, you immediately restore the spell to its spell slot."],["Delving into your chosen programming language has led to a magical breakthrough. You learn the advanced magic hack of your chosen programming language."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYour summoned creature appears with unexpected fanfare and brilliant destruction. If your next action is to Cast a Spell with the summon trait, all creatures in a 10-foot emanation around the creature you summoned take 1d4 sonic damage per spell rank of the spell cast, with a basic Fortitude save against your spell DC."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou decode a temporary copy of an executed spell into your spell cache. If your next action is to Cast a Spell from a spell chip or spell gem, temporarily add the spell to your spell cache. It remains in your cache until you use Download Spell to replace a prepared spell with the logged spell or until the next time you use Log Spell Execution. You can use this spellshape only to log spells that appear on the arcane spell list."],["**Trigger** You Cast a Spell not modified by a jailbreak effect.\n\n**Requirements** Your gear is overclocked.\n\n---\n\nYou route excess magical energy into your spell cache. Your gear is no longer overclocked. Once during the next minute, you can Cast a Spell directly from your spell cache, up to the same rank as the triggering spell, without using a spell slot."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** You're wielding a ranged tech weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou digitize yourself using your magic and transmit yourself across the battlefield as rapidly as a message sent through the infosphere. If your next action is to Cast a Spell with a range and an area, you teleport yourself and your gear to one open space within the spell's area. You can choose to arrive before or after the spell takes effect."],["**Trigger** You Cast a Spell not modified by a jailbreak effect.\n\n**Requirements** Your gear is overclocked.\n\n---\n\nYou're an expert in testing the cyber defenses of tech gear and defending against incoming attacks, and you know how to use excess magic energy to troubleshoot your tech when these defenses are inevitably breached. You target tech creatures or items of a number up to the rank of the triggering spell that are within 100 feet of you. You reduce the glitching condition of the targets by half the triggering spell's rank (minimum 1). For the next minute, affected targets roll flat checks to recover from the glitching condition twice and use the higher result; this is a fortune effect."],["You believe that adaptability and a diverse skill set is the key to success. You learn the initial magic hack of a programming language other than your chosen programming language."],["**Requirements** You're holding a grenade requiring a Reflex save.\n\n---\n\nIf the next action you use is to Cast a Spell with a burst area that requires a basic Reflex save, the spell doesn't take effect and is instead installed into the required grenade. Until the end of your next turn, any creature caught in the area of that grenade is also affected by the installed spell; creatures don't attempt a separate Reflex save against the spell and instead use the same result they rolled against the grenade. Resolve the grenade's effects first, then the spell's effects."],["Your familiar is imbued with even more magic. You can select six familiar or master abilities each day, instead of four."],["You've designed a magical application to enhance technology. You gain the Jury-Rigged Turbocharge magic hack."],["You use your knowledge of creatures and their specifications to magically overcome their defenses. When you critically succeed at a check to Recall Knowledge about a creature, the creature takes a –1 circumstance penalty to its AC and saving throws against your spells and the attacks of your minions with the tech trait for a number of rounds equal to your Intelligence modifier."],["You've expanded your spell cache to store more spells than most. During your daily preparations, you can add one spell to your spell cache of each rank of spell you can cast, selecting from the spells in your spell database. The spells remain in your spell cache until your next daily preparations."],["You program a ranged spell to split and hit two foes at once. If your next action is to Cast a Spell without a duration that requires an attack roll against a single target, you can choose a second target within range. You roll a single attack roll and compare the result to the AC of each target. This counts as one attack for your multiple attack penalty. To the second target, the spell deals only half the damage it would normally deal for its degree of success and has no effects beyond the spell's initial damage (such as imposing conditions or penalties)."],["**Requirements** Your quantum field is active.\n\n---\n\nBattle can be disorienting, but for you, the intense mental effort of striking your targets lends you additional clarity and focus. Make a Strike. The Strike gains the following success and critical success effects.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The Strike gains the anchoring trait. You can reroll the damage dice rolled for this strike, but you must use the second result, even if it's worse.\n\n**Success** The Strike gains the anchoring trait."],["Whether it's covered in debris, partially flooded, or otherwise troublesome to traverse, the area of your quantum field becomes difficult terrain."],["Your spell has an odd appearance or cosmetic effect. If the next action you use is to Cast a Spell, creatures with the ability to Cast that Spell don't automatically know what the spell is. In addition, creatures that witness your spellcasting take a –2 circumstance penalty to checks to identify the spell with Recall Knowledge and checks to counteract the spell and its effects."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** Your last action was to Sustain your quantum field or had the anchoring trait.\n\n---\n\nYou concentrate more deeply on your anchor to soothe yourself. You gain temporary Hit Points equal to your character level that last for 1 round."],["You breach the veil of paradoxical understanding. You gain the greater warp spell for your paradox."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou temporarily share your quantum field with an ally. You cause your quantum field to emanate from an ally you can see instead of yourself. The ally gains all the benefits of your quantum field, and your warp spells originate from your ally instead of you until your quantum field deactivates. If you cast warp spells at other targets, you must still have line of sight to the target, but the spell originates from your ally for purposes of determining its range and line of effect."],["You expose this reality to a realm of pure darkness filled with gibbering voices and otherworldly entities. The area of your quantum field functions as though it were an area of 2nd-rank Darkness. Creatures that begin their turn in the area must succeed at a Will save against your class DC or become Confused for 1 round (this is an incapacitation effect). The creature then becomes immune for 24 hours. If this *darkness* is successfully counteracted, the quantum field's other effects remain."],["Whenever you rest, you behold different versions of yourself in other realities. During your daily preparations, select one ancestry feat for your ancestry that you meet the prerequisites for and don't already have. You gain that feat until your next daily preparations."],["The reality you conjure is much brighter than your own. The area of your quantum field becomes bright light. Creatures who begin their turn in your quantum field must attempt a Fortitude save against your class DC; creatures with light blindness treat their result as one step worse.\n\n---\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature is Dazzled for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is Blinded for 1 round, then dazzled for 1 round."],["You possess an uncanny sixth sense for ambient magic. You can sense the presence of magic auras as though you were always using a 1st-rank Detect Magic spell. This detects magic in your field of vision only. When you Seek, you gain the benefits of a 3rd-rank *detect magic* spell on things you see (in addition to the normal benefits of Seeking). You can turn this sense off and on with a free action at the start or the end of your turn."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You use an action that Sustains your quantum field, and the quantum field is still active.\n\n---\n\nBy reaching across both time and space, you can borrow the use of a spell from a version of yourself inhabiting another reality. During this turn, you can cast one spell without spending a spell slot to do so. The spell must be in your repertoire."],["Your paradoxical nature has given you access to magic that isn't associated with your spellcasting tradition. You can have one spell in your spell repertoire (not one on your paradox's spell list) that isn't from your spellcasting tradition. Select this spell when you select this feat. You can cast that spell as a spell of your spellcasting tradition, and it becomes a signature spell. You can change the spell you choose when you gain a level."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou can create a stable quantum field. You Warp Reality with a duration of 1 minute."],["Your paradoxical nature has become multifaceted. During daily preparations, you can replace one of your paradox spells with a spell of another paradox that grants training in the prerequisite paradox skill."],["**Requirements** Your quantum field is active with one zone affecting it.\n\n---\n\nYou cause a second zone to overlap your quantum field. You can choose to apply another zone you're able to create, or apply the existing zone again, improving its effects as follows: Danger Zone deals 1 extra damage, Debris Zone becomes greater difficult terrain, and Twisted Dark Zone ignores the temporary immunity of creatures that previously critically succeeded at the save for 1 round."],["The multiverse is a complex game—you use alternate realities to move creatures on the board. When you use the Sustain action to move your quantum field, you can teleport any number of creatures within the quantum field's original area to squares of your choice in its new area. You also teleport any items they're wearing or holding. This gives the Sustain action the teleportation trait. Each target can attempt a Will save against your class DC. Targets who succeed at the save are unaffected."],["You borrow spells from other realities. Twice per day, you can cast a 9th-rank or lower spell after you've run out of spell slots of the appropriate spell rank; the two spells you cast with this feat must be of different spell ranks."],["**Trigger** A creature, trap, or similar object within your quantum field casts a spell that you don't have in your spell repertoire, and you're aware of the casting.\n\n---\n\nIf the triggering spell is common and you're trained in the associated skill for the spell's tradition, you automatically identify the spell being cast (you still roll to attempt to get a critical success but can't get a worse result than a success). You or a visible ally within 60 feet targeted by this spell gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your saving throw or your AC against it (or a +2 circumstance bonus if you rolled a critical success)."],["**Trigger** An enemy damages you.\n\n**Requirements** Your quantum field is active.\n\n---\n\nYou reposition to a space you'd occupy in a different reality, free from incoming danger. You instantly teleport up to your Speed to an area within your quantum field. This movement doesn't trigger reactions based on movement and ignores hazards and terrain, but can't pass through walls or other such obstructions."],["**Trigger** You or an ally fail a save against a mental effect while within your quantum field.\n\n---\n\nYou scrub all traces of the triggering effect from the target's mind. The target rerolls their saving throw against the triggering effect and must use the second result, even if it's worse."],["**Trigger** An enemy damages you.\n\n**Requirements** An enemy or willing ally is in your quantum field.\n\n---\n\nYour reality shifts to partly overlap with another in which someone else was injured in your stead. You gain resistance to all damage against the triggering attack equal to half your level, and one enemy or willing ally in your quantum field takes damage of the same type equal to the amount of damage prevented this way, with a basic Fortitude save against your class DC."],["You expose a target to a reality in which they don't exist. You learn the Quantum Negation warp spell."],["You become a true embodiment of your paradox and surpass what mortals can achieve in your reality. You gain an additional 10th-rank spell slot."],["**Requirements** Your quantum field is active.\n\n---\n\nYou allow your mind to wander to things you find pleasant, briefly shutting out all realities and protecting you from harm. You gain a +2 status bonus to saving throws against mental effects until the start of your next turn."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You cast a 2nd-rank or higher spell, and the spell targets a creature or area within your quantum field.\n\n---\n\nYou expertly manipulate the effects of your quantum field to ensure that some of the energy from your spell is preserved and can be harnessed again. You regain an expended spell slot one spell rank lower than the triggering spell."],["**Frequency** once per turn\n\n**Trigger** You cast a non-cantrip spell.\n\n---\n\nYou siphon spell energy into one weapon or grenade you're wielding. Until the end of your turn, the weapon or grenade deals extra force damage equal to the rank of the spell and gains the magical trait if it didn't have it already. If the spell deals damage, the extra damage becomes the same type as the triggering spell."],["Your quantum field slowly encroaches on reality. Increase your quantum field's radius by 10 feet. Until your quantum field deactivates, once per turn when you Sustain the quantum field, increase its radius by an additional 5 feet (to a maximum of 50 additional feet)."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n---\n\nYou spend 10 minutes opening yourself to the mysteries of the multiverse by peering across different timelines or analyzing probability simulations. You gain the effects of Augury, except you learn only about the dangers ahead; any results of \"good\" are instead \"nothing,\" and results of \"mixed\" are instead \"bad.\"\n\nIf you're legendary in Arcana or Occultism, you take only 1 minute to Predict Outcome."],["You can become the nexus of the warped reality you create. Each time you use Warp Reality to activate your quantum field, you can choose for your quantum field to be an aura around you that moves with you. If you do, your Warp Reality action gains the aura trait, and the quantum field you create is a 10-foot-radius emanation."],["Your paradox begins to cement itself across your life. You gain the advanced warp spell for your paradox."],["Your quantum field merges with a more dangerous reality, becoming hazardous terrain that deals 1 damage to an enemy each time it enters a square in the area. You choose the damage type when you use Danger Zone, selecting from the following: acid, bludgeoning, cold, electricity, fire, piercing, slashing, or sonic. Increase the damage by 1 at 12th, 16th, and 20th levels."],["You prevent creatures from leaving your quantum field and returning to reality. Until the start of your next turn, any creature who begins its turn inside your quantum field must succeed at a Will saving throw against your witchwarper class DC to move outside your quantum field. On a failure, the action is disrupted. A creature that succeeds at this save is immune to your Quantum Entanglement for 24 hours."],["You implant one augmentation with an item level equal to your character level or lower. This augmentation doesn't count against your total implant limit. The first time you take this feat, the augmentation you receive is free as long as its item level is 1 or lower. You can upgrade this augmentation by swapping it out with another augmentation when you gain a level or by spending downtime replacing the augmentation as though changing out a feat. When you swap out the augmentation, you must pay the difference between the original and new augmentation each time you upgrade.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times, choosing a different augmentation each time. Retraining this feat requires paying the cost of the original augmentation."],["You hastily create a barricade using nearby items, junk, or debris. The barricade provides lesser cover for you and one other ally, though you can Take Cover to increase this benefit to standard cover. The barricade is flimsy and falls apart at the end of your next turn."],["**Cost** the Price of the chosen item\n\n**Requirements** You haven't used this ability since the last time you were able to purchase goods.\n\n---\n\nYou regularly create convoluted plans and contingencies, using your resources to enact them. You take 1 minute to remove your backpack, then carefully remove an item you hadn't previously declared that you purchased—you intuited that you would come to need the item and purchased it at the latest opportunity. The item must be a piece of adventuring gear, and can't be a weapon, armor, serum, magic item, or other treasure. It must be common with a level no higher than half your level, and its Bulk must be low enough that carrying it wouldn't have made you encumbered."],["**Requirements** You have a free hand and are holding a battery with at least 10 charges.\n\n---\n\nWith a couple quick adjustments, you Craft an electromag grenade using the held battery. The grenade is Commercial grade if the battery has at least 10 charges, Tactical if the battery has at least 40 charges, or Advanced if the battery has at least 60 charges. If you're legendary in Crafting, you can Craft a Superior grenade using a battery with at least 100 charges. Grenades crafted using Akiton Battery Hack last until the end of your next turn, after which they're harmlessly discharged and no longer function as a battery or grenade."],["You can cast 1st-rank Detect Magic at will as an arcane innate spell. If you're a master in Arcana, the spell is heightened to 3rd rank; if you're legendary, it is heightened to 4th rank."],["You can Earn Income using Diplomacy, spending your days hunting for bargains and reselling at a profit. You can also spend time specifically seeking a great bargain on an item; this works as if you were using Earn Income with Diplomacy, except instead of gaining money, you purchase the item at a discount equal to the money you would have gained, gaining the item for free if your earned income equals or exceeds its cost. Finally, if you select Bargain Hunter during character creation at 1st level, you start play with an additional 20 credits."],["**Requirements** You're holding or wearing a medkit.\n\n---\n\nYou can patch up wounds, even in combat. Attempt a Medicine check with the same DC as for Treat Wounds and restore the corresponding amount of HP; this doesn't remove the wounded condition. As with Treat Wounds, you can attempt checks against higher DCs if you have the minimum proficiency rank. The target is then immune to your Battle Medicine for 1 day. This does not make them immune to, or otherwise count as, Treat Wounds."],["You know how to blend in and become a forgettable face in the crowd. While in a crowd of at least 10 other creatures, you can roll a Society check in place of a Stealth check when using the Avoid Notice exploration activity to see if enemies notice you. While in a settlement, you can use [[/act impersonate skill=society]]{Society} in place of Deception when Impersonating a non-specific individual."],["You move through crowds without slowing down. You can move at full Speed in crowds. Treat areas truly packed with people as difficult terrain instead of greater difficult terrain."],["Whether you are a hacktivist or reformed troll, you know to irritate people anonymously in digital spaces, pushing their buttons even when it means resorting to cruel personal attacks. You can use Intimidation to [[/act coerce]] without the usual penalty from being anonymous on the infosphere."],["**Requirements** You aren't Fatigued.\n\n---\n\nFor 1 minute, you can carry 4 more Bulk than normal before becoming encumbered. The amount you can carry increases to 6 at expert, 8 at master, and 10 at legendary. When the benefits of this feat end, you become Fatigued for 10 minutes."],["As long as you're using a comm unit, datapad, or computer to communicate, when you attempt to use a skill action with the linguistic trait on a creature that doesn't understand the language you're using, roll a DC 15 flat check. On a success, the effect works as if the creature understood the language you're using. If you're Legendary in Society, the DC is 10 (DC 10 flat check)."],["You use acting, video editing, and propaganda to convince people of your lies online, even if they don't know who you are in the real world or think you are someone else. You can use Deception to Lie without the usual penalty for being anonymous on the infosphere."],["**Requirements** You are holding or wearing a hacking toolkit and have a free hand.\n\n---\n\nWhether it's a sudden comm unit ping or a warning alarm on an equipment display, you can Create a Diversion by using Computers instead of Deception on an adjacent target carrying, wearing, or wielding a tech item.\n\n[[/act create-a-diversion variant=distracting-words skill=computers]]\n\n[[/act create-a-diversion variant=gesture skill=computers]]\n\n[[/act create-a-diversion variant=trick skill=computers]]"],["**Requirements** You have a hand free and are within melee reach of an opponent.\n\n---\n\nYou hook a foe's boot clasps together, pull their visor from their eyes, loosen their mag-belt, or otherwise confound their mobility through an underhanded tactic. Attempt a Thievery check against the target's Reflex DC.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is Clumsy 1 until they use an Interact action to end the impediment\n\n**Success** As critical success, but the condition ends automatically after 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** You fall Prone as your attempt backfires."],["You can fuel battery-powered devices by drawing electricity from different sources. Doing so takes 1 minute of work and an adjacent source of power appropriate to the device. If the source of power is a technological creature or hazard, it must have been destroyed within the last 10 minutes and provides charges equal to twice its level. If the source is a facility capable of charging a battery, the battery-powered device operates as if the battery were always fully charged. If you're a master in Crafting, you can connect a device to a power source as a 3-action activity. If you're legendary, it takes 1 action."],["You know how to get there fast. When calculating your travel Speed for the day while piloting a vehicle, you can attempt a Piloting check to increase your vehicle's travel Speed for long-term overland or aerial travel. The DC is determined by the GM but is typically based on the vehicle's piloting DC or a difficulty based on the environment, whichever is harder. On a success, double your vehicle's travel Speed for the day. This has no effect on your vehicle's movement in encounters or on starships traveling through the Drift."],["You know how to configure and print tech items out of UPBs in creator capsules. You must have the formula to create the item in a creator capsule and pay an amount of UPBs equal to the material price of the item, reducing the materials used based on the result of your Crafting check. Unlike normal Crafting, this process takes minutes instead of days (depending on the grade of creator capsule used), but you can't spend additional time working on the item. A creator capsule is consumed when you successfully Craft an item but not when you roll a failure or critical failure. You don't need the Tech Crafting skill feat to craft tech items using Fabricator, but you can't use Fabricator to create magical equipment unless you have Magical Crafting."],["You know how to get lost in a crowd. You can use cover from crowds to Hide and Sneak, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to your Stealth checks when in a crowd of at least 10 creatures and a +4 circumstance bonus to your Stealth checks when in a crowd of at least 100 creatures. Hidden creatures don't count as members of a crowd. If you're a master in Deception you only need 5 creatures to get these bonuses.\n\nFace in the Crowd"],["You create a favored disguise that you can call upon at a moment's notice. When you Impersonate, you can decide that the disguise becomes your favored disguise. If you have a holoskin or can Change Shape, you can always adopt your favored disguise when Impersonating. You still roll Deception for the Impersonate check but count any critical failure results as failures instead. You can have one favored disguise and gain an additional favored disguise you can employ at expert, master, and legendary proficiency in Deception."],["You're constantly recording, aiming for that perfect camera angle or sound bite. You can perform the Livestream exploration activity at the same time as other exploration activities. In addition, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to checks to Earn Income that use your footage, such as Performance or Infosphere Lore, as long as you have at least 8 hours of footage recorded since the last time you attempted to Earn Income. If you're a master in Performance, this bonus increases to +2; if you're legendary in Performance, this bonus increases to +3."],["You easily spot the tiny glitches and imperfections in holograms. Even if you aren't Searching, you always attempt a check to disbelieve holograms and effects with the illusion and tech traits that normally require you to Search or Interact with them."],["You can administer medicine using injection weapons. You can load an injection weapon with a hypopen, poison, or serum as an Interact action. When you successfully Strike with an injection weapon loaded in this way, you deal no damage. Instead, you administer the loaded substance to the target of the Strike."],["You attempt to Demoralize a foe with your ranged weapon by firing it into the air, using ammo equal to the weapon's expend and the weapon's maximum range rather than the usual range of 30 feet. This check doesn't take a –4 circumstance penalty if the target doesn't share a language with you."],["When in a junk-rich environment, you can spend 4 hours to attempt a Crafting check to scavenge the materials you need to Craft a non-consumable item of 2nd level or lower. The GM determines the DC based on the level of the item you're attempting to Craft. During your daily preparations, you must perform some maintenance on this junk item or it falls apart and gains the broken condition. You can only have one junk item at a time. If you're an expert in Crafting, you can have two junk items at a time. If you're a master in Crafting, you can have four junk items at a time. If you're legendary in Crafting, you can have eight junk items at a time and can Craft junk items of an item level up to half your level.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** You locate suitable raw materials worth half the Price of the item you intend to Craft.\n\n**Success** You locate raw materials worth one-quarter the Price of the item you intend to Craft.\n\n**Failure** You fail to locate any raw materials.\n\n**Critical Failure** Poor materials ruins 10 percent of the raw materials you use to Craft your item."],["**Trigger** An ally critically fails to Coerce, Make an Impression, or Request.\n\n---\n\nYou attempt to play off a social misstep as a joke. Attempt a Performance check against the same DC as your ally's check. If you succeed, your ally treats their critical failure as a failure."],["**Trigger** You end your movement adjacent to an enemy.\n\n**Requirements** You're Flying using a tech item, such as a jetpack or jump jets.\n\n---\n\nSoaring head-first into your foe, you [[/act shove skill=acrobatics]] them, rolling an Acrobatics check in place of the usual Athletics check. On a success or critical success, you can Fly after your target rather than Stride, even if you don't have a fly Speed."],["Anyone who speaks with you about a job, workplace, or office skill set assumes you're a professional in that setting unless you intentionally present yourself differently. You can use [[/act make-an-impression]]{Society} to Make an Impression on a professional or to Impersonate a type of professional or a specific individual professional. If you use the normally required skills in those situations, you receive a +1 circumstance bonus to the check instead."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou've integrated medical nanites into your body. You activate these nanites to gain the benefits of one hypopen with a level equal to half your level or lower (minimum 1)."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Requirements** You have a comm unit and infosphere access.\n\n---\n\nInfosphere archivists have lived by the credo that information wants to be free, and you know where to find it. You Access Infosphere. On a critical failure, in addition to the usual effects, your comm unit becomes Glitching 5."],["You're skilled at running digital fraud schemes. You can Create a Forgery using [[/act create-forgery skill=computers]]{Computers} instead of Society. Digital forgeries are compared against your Computers DC. Using information gained from a successful forgery usually requires additional checks, including Deception and Society, and casting too wide a net runs the risk of a potential victim figuring out your ruse and turning you in to the authorities."],["You've learned how to hack using alternative methods. You can use Computers to Disable a Device or Hack a system using any computer, comm unit, or terminal instead of a hacking toolkit. If you're an expert in Computers and the equipment you use is at least 3rd level, you gain a +1 item bonus to Disable a Device or Hack.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the Combat Hack or Digital Diversion skill feat, you can use this feat to Combat Hack or Create a Diversion without a hacking toolkit."],["You've learned that in the heat of a race or the frenzy of a chase there's no time to slow down for repairs. You know how to maintain a vehicle without having to slow down. You can perform the Repair activity on a moving vehicle, without the need for a stable surface."],["**Trigger** You perceive a creature attempting a check using Deception, Diplomacy, or Intimidation against another creature's Will DC.\n\n---\n\nYou intercede in a conversation to subtly damage another's reputation and make their argument less compelling. The creature targeted by the triggering check gains a +2 circumstance bonus to its Will DC for that check.\n\nPlant Rumor"],["You have a reliable system for loading gear. You can open and close a backpack as part of the same Interact action as retrieving a stowed item from it. When using a container, increase the amount of Bulk of items that container can hold that doesn't count against your Bulk limits by 1. If you're an expert in Survival, increase the amount by 2. If you're a master in Survival, increase the amount by 3. If you're legendary in Survival, increase the amount by 4."],["You can write computer programs. You can Earn Income using Computers, spending your time programming apps for clients. You can also Craft items with the virtual trait. You can use Programmer to Craft tech items that don't have the virtual trait, but you can only cover up to a quarter of the item's cost in raw materials; the remaining Crafting has to be completed by someone using the Crafting skill."],["You can [[/act coerce]] a creature after 1 round of conversation instead of 1 minute. You still can't Coerce a creature in the midst of combat, or without engaging in a conversation."],["You take only 1 minute to Install an Upgrade. If you're legendary in Crafting, you can Install an Upgrade as a 3-action activity."],["You fly vehicles like you're trying to steal them. Reduce the number of actions to Take Control of an uncontrolled vehicle by one. If this would reduce the number of actions to zero, you can Take Control as a free action. Additionally, you gain the Punch It! action."],["You restore items to pristine condition. When you succeed at a Crafting check to Repair an item, you restore additional Hit Points to that item equal to your Intelligence modifier. Additionally, you can use Crafting to Treat Wounds on constructs, substituting a repair toolkit for a medkit. You can use Battle Medicine and Continual Recovery with Crafting instead of Medicine while treating constructs, but you must still meet the feats' prerequisites to qualify for these feats."],["You've mastered the preparation of many types of food and drink. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to checks to Craft food and drink, including serums if you have Serum Crafting. If you are a master in one of the prerequisite skills, this bonus increases to +2."],["You can Craft serums and medical items with the consumable trait, though some have other requirements. When you select this feat, you gain formulas for four common serums of 2nd level or lower."],["Your training focused on Crafting one particular kind of item. Select one of the specialties listed below; you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Crafting checks to Craft items of that type. If you are a master in Crafting, this bonus increases to +2. If it's unclear whether the specialty applies, the GM decides. Some specialties might apply only partially. For example, if you were making an Abadarcorp travel suit and had specialty in textiles, the GM might give you half your bonus because the item requires both armorsmithing and textiles to craft.\n\n| Specialty | Applicable Items |\n|---|---|\n| Armorsmithing | Armor, shields and upgrades |\n| Artistry | Fine art, including jewelry and solarian crystals |\n| Automotives | Vehicles, including spaceships |\n| Chemicals | Alcohol, ammunition, explosives, and fuel |\n| Computer | Comm units, datapads, and virtual items |\n| Engineering | Tech gadgets and accessories |\n| Gunsmithing | Firearms and firearm upgrades |\n| Life Science | Biotechnology and some pharmaceuticals |\n| Robotics | Drones, mechs, and robots |\n| Textiles | Clothing, leather, and polymer armor |"],["You can use Treat Wounds to restore Hit Points to undead creatures, not just living ones. The techniques you use to do so vary, but all require sutures, bandages, and other tools included in a medkit. Some conditions that might raise the DC of treating undead's wounds differ from that of living creatures. For instance, the GM might increase the DC if the undead is being treated in a Pharasmin medbay or the wounds were caused by powerful vital energy."],["You can spend 10 minutes assessing the area around you for signs of creatures. Attempt a Survival check against a DC determined by the GM based on how obvious the signs are. On a success, you can attempt a Recall Knowledge check with a –2 penalty to learn more about the creatures just from these signs. If you're a master in Survival, you don't take the penalty."],["Your experience in navigating a certain type of terrain makes you supremely confident while doing so. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Survival checks in one of the following types of terrain, chosen when you select this feat: aquatic, arctic, desert, forest, mountain, plains, sky, space, swamp, or underground.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once, choosing a different type of terrain each time."],["You examine a magic item you normally couldn't use in an effort to fool it and activate it temporarily. For example, this might allow a soldier to cast a spell from a spell gem or spellchip or allow a mystic to cast a spell that's not on their connection's tradition list using a spell gem. You must know what activating the item does, or you can't attempt to trick it.\n\nAttempt a check using the skill matching the item's magic tradition, or matching a tradition that has the spell on its list, if you're trying to cast a spell from the item. The relevant skills are Arcana for arcane, Nature for primal, Occultism for occult, Religion for divine, or any of the four for an item that has the magical trait and not a tradition trait. The GM determines the DC based on the item's level (possibly adjusted depending on the item or situation).\n\nIf you activate a magic item that requires a spell attack modifier or spell DC and you don't have proficiency in the relevant statistic, use your level as your proficiency bonus and the highest of your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma modifiers. If you're a master in the appropriate skill for the item's tradition, you instead use the trained proficiency bonus; if you're legendary, you instead use the expert proficiency bonus.\n\n---\n\n**Success** For the rest of the current turn, you can spend actions to activate the item as if you could normally use it.\n\n**Failure** You can't use the item or try to trick it again this turn, but you can try again on subsequent turns.\n\n**Critical Failure** You can't use the item, and you can't try to trick it again until your next daily preparations."],["You can use [[/act subsist skill=survival]]{Survival} in place of Society to Subsist in cities, space stations, and other settlements. You can also use Survival instead of Perception to notice hazards in these environments; if you find a hazard in this way, you can also use Survival instead of Thievery to [[/act disable-device skill=survival]]{Disable the Device}."],["You have exceptional talent with one type of performance. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus when making a certain type of performance. If you are a master in Performance, this bonus increases to +2. Select one of the following specialties and apply the bonus when attempting Performance checks of that type. If it's unclear whether the specialty applies, the GM decides.\n\n| Specialty | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| Acting | Drama, live streams, reality shows |\n| Comedy | Buffoonery, joke telling, stand-up routines |\n| Dance | Ballet, ballroom, interpretive, pop, traditional |\n| Keyboards | Keytar, organ, piano |\n| Oratory | Epic, ode, poetry, storytelling |\n| Percussion | Bells, chimes, drum kit, xylophone |\n| Singing | Ballad, chant, pop, rock, shanty |\n| Strings | Guitar, singing coil, theremin |\n| Synths | Synth deck, turn table |\n| Winds | Horn, flute, pipes |"],["You're an expert at destroying or removing incriminating evidence from a crime scene. When using the Cover Tracks exploration activity, an yone tracking you must succeed at a Perception check against your Deception, Stealth, or Underworld Lore DC (whichever is highest). If you spent 10 minutes cleaning up a crime scene, anyone investigating the scene must succeed at a Perception check against your Deception, Stealth, or Underworld Lore DC (whichever is highest) to uncover any Hidden evidence."],["Your eye opens to greater truths. You can use Akashic Sync once per round instead of once every 10 minutes."],["Your body builds primal energy that you can unleash to disable technology. Attempt a Nature check against all glitching creatures, hazards, and items with the tech trait within 20 feet. The DC is equal to the creature or hazard's Fortitude DC or the Fortitude DC of the creature attending the object, or is based on the item's level if it's unattended. Regardless of the results, each target is then temporarily immune to Amplify Glitch for 1 day.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** Increase target's glitching condition value by 4.\n\n**Success** Increase target's glitching condition value by 2."],["When you successfully Maneuver in Flight, compare the results of your Acrobatics check against the Reflex DC of one creature you were adjacent to at any point during your movement. On a success, the creature is Off-Guard to the next Strike you make before the end of your turn."],["You can intuit how even the most interesting vehicles function. You can pilot a ship even if it would be physiologically impossible for you, including those that require telepathy or other supernatural abilities. You can use Piloting instead of Crafting to Repair a part of a vehicle, starship, or mech with a –2 circumstance penalty as long as you have the appropriate parts available to you. You can use Piloting instead of Computers to Hack a vehicle, starship, or mech with a –2 circumstance penalty."],["**Requirements** You're holding a grenade.\n\n---\n\nYou attempt to slip a grenade onto a foe, then slip away before it blows. Attempt a Thievery check against an adjacent creature's Perception DC, then you Stride.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The grenade explodes after you Stride. The target treats the result of its saving throw as one degree of success worse.\n\n**Success** The grenade explodes after you Stride.\n\n**Failure** The grenade explodes after you Stride, but the target notices your actions. The target treats the result of its saving throw as one degree of success better.\n\n**Critical Failure** The grenade explodes before you Stride, catching you in the blast."],["Your fame has spread throughout the galaxy. Creatures who have any listed skill in Society have heard of you and usually have an attitude toward you one step better than normal, depending on your reputation and the creature's disposition. For instance, if you're well-known for cruel and demanding behavior, creatures might be intimidated by you, rather than be friendly toward you. When you Earn Income with Performance, you attract higher-level audiences than your location would allow, as audiences flock to see you. For instance, famous socialites and spectra might travel to a dive bar in a backwater port to hear you perform. Typically, this increases the audiences available to your level or by two levels, whichever is higher."],["Your fame has spread throughout the galaxy (for instance, if you have Warfare Lore, you might be a legendary general or tactician). This works as Legendary Performer, except you gain higher-level jobs when you Earn Income with Lore."],["**Requirements** You or your target are using a comm unit, datapad, or other computer.\n\n---\n\nAttempt a Deception check against the Will DC of a target within 60 feet. On a success, the target is Off-Guard for 1 round, and on a critical success, it's Confused for 1 round. The target's reaction gives you information about it as though you'd attempted to Recall Knowledge using an appropriate skill and received the same result on your roll. The target is then temporarily immune to your Legendary Troll attempts for 24 hours."],["You understand the common underpinnings of the four traditions of magic and magical essences. Whenever you use a skill action or a skill feat that requires a Nature, Occultism, or Religion check, depending on the magic tradition, you can use Arcana instead. If you would normally take a penalty or have a higher DC for using Arcana on other magic (such as when using Identify Magic), you no longer do so."],["**Requirements** You are holding or wearing a hacking toolkit and have a free hand.\n\n---\n\nAttempt a Computers check to [[/act hack]]{Hack} an adjacent creature, hazard, or item with the tech trait. The DC is equal to the creature, item, or hazard's Fortitude DC, or the Fortitude DC of the creature attending the object. If the target is an unattended object, the GM sets the DC for the check based on the item's level. The target is temporarily immune to your attempts to Combat Hack it for 10 minutes.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target becomes Glitching 2.\n\n**Success** The target becomes Glitching 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** If the target has the glitching condition, reduce the value of its glitching condition by 1."],["You pile lie upon lie. Reduce the circumstance bonus a target gains for your previous attempts to Create a Diversion or Lie to it from +4 to +2. If you're a master in Deception, reduce the bonus to +1, and if you're legendary, your targets don't get these bonuses at all."],["Your voice can be heard over the noise in a crowd. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks against crowds. The first time each round you Stride into a square containing a crowd, you can attempt a DC 20 Diplomacy check to move the crowd out of your way. A GM might use a different DC under certain circumstances, such as when the crowd has a level or set DC to disperse.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** As success, and the crowd departs from all adjacent squares as you move.\n\n**Success** The crowd disperses from squares you move into.\n\n**Failure** The crowd doesn't move, but you can continue moving.\n\n**Critical Failure** The crowd forcefully resists you and disrupts your Stride."],["Your sabotage takes effect when the time is right. When you Disable a Device, you can delay the device from becoming disabled for up to 24 hours or until someone attempts to use the device. In most cases, creatures have a chance to detect that the device is disabled only if they use the [[/act seek]] action to attempt Perception checks against your Thievery DC. If you rolled a critical success on your Thievery check to Disable a Device, other creatures can't figure out the device will become disabled, and you can safely activate the device without triggering or ending the effect of Delayed Disable."],["You convince others to do their own research using specifically curated data and misinformation you casually guide them into finding on the infosphere. The first time you fail to Lie to the target (but not critically fail), you convince them that you were given faulty information, the data isn't all in yet, or you were both mislead, and the target doesn't gain a circumstance bonus against your further attempts to Lie to them. If you're a master in Deception, you can fail to Lie twice in the same conversation before they begin to suspect you, or four times if you're legendary in Deception."],["When threatened, you can quickly take a dive and find somewhere to hunker down. You Leap, land Prone, and immediately Take Cover, which allows you to hunker down and gain greater cover against ranged attacks."],["You're well-versed in the street racing technique known as drifting, or sliding your vehicle through the entirety of a curve while maintaining speed and showcasing your driving skills. While piloting a land vehicle, when you perform Piloting actions with the reckless trait, your vehicle only becomes uncontrolled on a critical failure. On a failure, the vehicle moves as described under reckless piloting, except that you, not the GM, control where the vehicle drifts. You can choose to fail (but not critically fail) a reckless Piloting action. The GM, however, has discretion as to when a vehicle you're piloting is too large or unwieldy for this technique to be viable—it's a move that works with sports hovercars and not long-hauler transports (generally)."],["**Trigger** You take damage.\n\n---\n\nYou lie Prone and Impersonate a corpse. As long as you don't take any actions requiring anything other than your mind, you appear dead. To see through your ruse, a creature must succeed at a check against your Deception DC, either by Seeking or Recalling Knowledge. You can Ready an Action without ending this effect if you're a master in Deception."],["You are a genius at Crafting, easily able to determine how things are made and create new inventions. You can spend downtime to invent a common formula that you don't know. This works just like the Craft activity: you spend half the Price of the formula up front, attempt a Crafting check, and on a success either finish the formula by paying the difference or work for longer to decrease the Price. The difference is that you spend the additional time in research, design, and development, rather than in creating an item. Once it's complete, you add the new formula you invented to your formula book.\n\nThe GM might allow you to invent uncommon or rare formulas, typically with an increased DC. You need the Magical Crafting feat to invent hybrid and magical formula."],["**Requirements** You have a hand free and are adjacent to an ally who isn't at full Hit Points.\n\n---\n\nYou perform a token medical effort to convince an ally they've recovered from an injury. Attempt a Deception check with the same DC as for Treat Wounds. On a success, the target gains temporary Hit Points equal to half the corresponding amount of Hit Points from Treat Wounds. These temporary Hit Points last 1 round. Kiss It Better doesn't remove the wounded condition. The target is temporarily immune to Kiss It Better for 24 hours."],["Whether you're frequently plugging sponsors, talking to chat, or showing off merch, you're always performing for the cameras. You can Earn Income after Livestreaming for 24 hours in exploration mode. These hours don't need to be consecutive, but each show must be at least 1 hour long to count toward the total number of hours required to roll to determine your earnings. If you're an expert in Performance, you only need 12 hours to receive earnings. If you're a master in Performance, you only need 8 hours. If you're legendary in Performance, you only need 1 hour. You can receive earnings only once per day."],["**Requirements** You're holding a tech item that has the glitching condition.\n\n---\n\nYou try to repair an item by smashing it against a hard surface. Attempt a DC 10 flat check.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** Reduce the glitching condition by 2.\n\n**Success** Reduce the glitching condition by 1."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou can combat technology with the bounty of the natural world. Attempt a Nature check and smear blood, mud, or another natural substance on an adjacent creature, hazard, or item with the tech trait to disrupt it with primal energy. The DC is equal to the creature's, item's, or hazard's Fortitude DC, or the Fortitude DC of the creature attending the object. If the target is an unattended object, the GM sets the DC for the check based on the item's level. The target is then temporarily immune to your attempts to Primal Sabotage it for 1 hour.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target becomes Glitching 2.\n\n**Success** The target becomes Glitching 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The nature spirits rebuke you, causing a random piece of tech gear you own to become glitching 1."],["Whether you're a natural ace or a veteran pilot, you can push a vehicle to perform incredible stunts. Remove the reckless trait when you attempt a Stunt with a –1 penalty. If you're a master in Piloting, remove the reckless trait when you attempt a Stunt with a –2 penalty or lower. If you're legendary in Piloting, remove the reckless trait from any Stunt you attempt."],["You can Craft level 1 or higher tech items, though some have other requirements. When you select this feat, you gain formulas for four common tech items of 2nd level or lower."],["You're a menace behind the wheel! When you attempt to Run Over creatures with a vehicle you're Piloting, you can attempt to [[/act demoralize]] one creature in your path. If you're a master in Piloting, you can Demoralize up to two creatures in your path, or up to three creatures if you're legendary in Piloting."],["You throw the vehicle into a barely controlled skid, turning sharply to evade pursuit. You Drive with a –2 penalty to your Piloting check, gaining the effects of the Drive action for the same number of actions you spent to Power Slide. At the end of the movement, if you succeed, you can turn the vehicle up to 90 degrees. If you critically succeed at your Piloting check, you can instead turn the vehicle up to 180 degrees."],["You Board and Take Control of an adjacent vehicle."],["You can gracefully perform aerial stunts as if flying were second nature. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Acrobatics checks to Maneuver in Flight and can combine two maneuvers into a single action, such as reversing direction while making a steep descent or hovering in gale force winds. The DC of the Acrobatics check is equal to the DC of the most difficult maneuver + 5.\n\nIf you're legendary in Acrobatics, you can combine three such maneuvers into a single action; the DC of the Acrobatics check is equal to the DC of the most difficult maneuver + 10. Regardless of the combination, these maneuvers rarely allow you to move further than your fly Speed."],["**Frequency** once per 10 minutes\n\n---\n\nYou can briefly connect to the Akashic Records. You Recall Knowledge using [[/act recall-knowledge skill=occultism]]{Occultism} instead of any other skill as though Occultism were applicable to perform Recall Knowledge for that topic.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** You recall accurately and gain three pieces of information or context.\n\n**Success** You recall accurately and gain two pieces of information or context and a piece of erroneous information, but you don't have any way to differentiate which is which.\n\n**Failure** You gain a piece of information or context and two pieces of erroneous information.\n\n**Critical Failure** You gain three pieces of erroneous information."],["**Trigger** You successfully Strike and deal damage with a boost melee weapon charged to deal additional damage.\n\n---\n\nYou launch yourself across the battlefield using your boosted weapon. This energy pushes you 20 feet directly back from your target. This movement doesn't trigger reactions."],["When you roll initiative, if you're Livestreaming, you can ask chat for some help. You Recall Knowledge about a creature you and your livestream audience can see, using a Performance check in place of the usual skill. For this action, you can't use any special abilities, reactions, or free actions that trigger when you Recall Knowledge."],["When you administer a consumable that restores Hit Points to a creature, you can apply it to maximum effect, pinpointing vital parts of your patient's anatomy. When you do, instead of rolling dice, the consumable heals the maximum possible amount. The target is then temporarily immune to your Critical Care for 1 day."],["You've dedicated yourself to a deity or pantheon. As long as you follow the edicts and anathema of that deity, you gain their granted 1st-rank spell as a divine innate spell you can cast once per day, heightened to 3rd rank; if you're legendary, the spell is heightened to 4th rank. If you repeatedly break your deity's edicts or perform anathemas, you lose this ability, and it can only be regained with an atone ritual."],["You know how to fool security cameras and tech items that confer special senses, such as scopes. Whenever you use the Avoid Notice, Hide, or Sneak actions, you're always considered to be taking precautions against special senses from tech items. In addition, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your Stealth DC to Avoid Notice by cameras and technological hazards."],["Your eye magnifies distant targets as well as a scope. You can adjust your sight in that eye as a single action to Seek a specific creature with a +2 circumstance bonus to your Perception check, or Seek to search a 10-foot square up to 100 feet away for any undetected or Hidden creatures or objects. You don't take penalties for an object or creature being too far away unless you're more than 2 miles away."],["Whenever you succeed at a Piloting check, the vehicle you're piloting gains a +10-foot circumstance bonus to all its Speeds until the end of your turn. If you critically succeed, this bonus increases to +15 feet."],["You can construct and bless a religious symbol of your deity in 10 minutes. While such talismans are traditionally scraps of paper with a religious symbol drawn on them, they can take many forms, including body art, a sticker, or even a virtual emoji. You can create a talisman only for yourself and for the deity you worship. As long as you continue to engage in activities that match your deity's edicts you gain a +1 status bonus to initiative rolls. If you violate your deity's anathema, the talisman is destroyed, and you take a –1 status penalty to initiative rolls and Perception checks until you complete an Atone ritual."],["Shameless requests are your specialty. When you Request something, you reduce any DC increases for making an outrageous request by 2, and if you roll a critical failure for your Request, you get a failure instead. While this means you can never cause your target to reduce their attitude toward you by making a Request, they eventually tire of requests, even though they still have a positive attitude toward you."],["You attempt to convince someone that you've seen nasty rumors about them on the infosphere. Choose a target within 30 feet, and attempt a Society check against its Will DC.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The distracted target takes a –3 status penalty to Will saves and Diplomacy checks for 1 minute. The target can end this effect early by checking a comm unit or other computer as a single action that has the manipulate trait or with the assistance of another creature checking a device.\n\n**Success** As critical success, but the penalty is –2.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target doesn't care about your accusation or knows it's a lie, ruining your reputation and giving you a –2 circumstance penalty to your Deception, Diplomacy, and Society checks for 1 minute."],["You are naturally calm and collected in the face of imminent danger. At the end of your turn, reduce your Frightened condition by 2 instead of 1."],["You eagerly absorbed the old stories and traditions of your ancestors, your gods, and your people, studying subjects and techniques passed down for generation upon generation. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Crafting and Religion. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Dwarf Lore."],["Your kin have instilled in you an affinity for hard-hitting weapons, and you prefer these to more elegant arms. You gain access to all uncommon weapons with the dwarf trait. You have familiarity with weapons with the dwarf trait plus the battle axe, pick, and warhammer—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["Dwarves have a long history fighting common foes, and you've mastered the ancient tactics to better face these enemies. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to damage with weapons and unarmed attacks against creatures with the giant, goblin, hryngar, or orc trait. If your attack would deal more than one weapon die of damage (as is common at higher levels than 1st), the bonus is equal to the number of weapon dice or unarmed attack dice.\n\nIn addition, if any creature critically succeeds at an attack against you and deals damage to you, you gain your bonus to damage against that creature for 1 minute regardless of whether it has one of the listed traits.\n\nMountain Strategy (Critically Hit)\n\n---\n\n**Special** Your GM can add appropriate creature traits to the ancestral foes list if your character is from a community that commonly fights other types of enemies."],["Your innate connection to stone makes you adept at moving across uneven surfaces. You can ignore difficult terrain caused by stone (such as rubble or gravel) and uneven ground made of stone and earth. In addition, when you use the Acrobatics skill to Balance on narrow surfaces or uneven ground made of stone or earth, you aren't Off-Guard, and when you roll a success at one of these Acrobatics checks, you get a critical success instead."],["You understand the intricacies of stonework. You become trained in Crafting. If you're already trained in Crafting, you instead gain the Specialty Crafting skill feat for stonemasonry.\n\nYou also gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to notice unusual stonework. This bonus applies to checks to discover mechanical traps made of stone or Hidden within stone.\n\nIf you aren't using the Seek action or searching, the GM automatically rolls a secret check for you to notice unusual stonework anyway. This check doesn't gain your normal circumstance bonus."],["You've learned techniques first devised by your ancestors during their ancient wars, allowing you to comfortably wear massive suits of armor. Ignore the reduction to your Speed from any armor you wear.\n\nIn addition, any time you're taking a penalty to your Speed for some other reason (such as from the Encumbered condition or from a spell), deduct 5 feet from the penalty. For example, the encumbered condition normally gives a –10-foot penalty to Speed, but this feat would reduce it to a –5-foot penalty. If your Speed is taking multiple penalties, pick only one penalty to reduce."],["You march through the earth and lead an ally along. You gain a burrow Speed of 15 feet when you use this activity (if you don't have a higher one), and then you either Stride twice or Burrow twice. You can choose one willing ally adjacent to you at the start of your movement to move with you. That ally ends its movement one square behind you."],["You channel strength from the earth beneath your feet to pummel your enemies. When making a melee Strike against a target who is standing on the same earth or stone surface as you are, you gain a circumstance bonus to the damage roll equal to the number of weapon damage dice."],["Earthen barriers no longer impede your progress. You gain Magic Passage as a 7th-rank divine innate spell that you can cast once per day. Unlike the spell, however, this ability can be used only to open passages through barriers of earth or stone."],["**Trigger** An enemy or hazard's effect hits you or you fail a Fortitude save against one.\n\n---\n\nThe strength of stone overcomes you so strongly that it replaces your stout body. You become Petrified until the end of the current turn. You don't take any damage from the triggering effect or any other ill effects that couldn't affect stone."],["Your dwarven build allows you to push foes around, just like a mighty boulder tumbles through a subterranean cavern. Take a Step into the square of a foe that is your size or smaller, and the foe must move into the empty space directly behind it. The foe must move even if doing so places it in harm's way. The foe can attempt a Fortitude saving throw against your Athletics DC to block your Step. If the foe attempts this saving throw, it takes bludgeoning damage equal to your level plus your Strength modifier unless it critically succeeds.\n\nIf the foe can't move into an empty space (if it is surrounded by solid objects or other creatures, for example), your Boulder Roll has no effect."],["Using ancient dwarven methods developed to fight enemies wielding magical darkness, you've honed your darkvision and sworn not to use such magic yourself. You gain greater darkvision, enabling you to see through magical darkness even if it normally hampers darkvision (such as the darkness created by a 4th-rank Darkness spell). You can't cast spells with the darkness trait, use item activations with the darkness trait, or use any other ability with the darkness trait."],["You can use your knowledge of engineering and metalwork to temporarily strengthen thick objects and structures. By spending 1 hour working on an item, you can give it a +1 circumstance bonus to its Hardness for 24 hours. If you're a master in Crafting, the bonus is +2, and if you're legendary, the bonus is +3. You can reinforce a portion of a structure, though 1 hour usually reinforces only a door, a few windows, or another section that fits within a 10-foot cube.\n\nDwarven Reinforcement"],["**Requirements** You are standing on a stone or earthen surface.\n\n---\n\nYou pause a moment to attune your senses to the stone around you. Until the start of your next turn, you gain imprecise tremorsense with a range of 20 feet."],["Your hardiness lets you withstand more punishment than most. Increase your maximum Hit Points by your level. When you have the Dying 1 condition, the DC of your recovery checks is equal to 9 + your dying value (instead of 10 + your dying value).\n\nIf you also have the Toughness feat, the Hit Points gained from it and this feat are cumulative, and the DC of your recovery checks is equal to 6 + your dying value."],["**Trigger** You are struck by a critical hit that deals physical damage.\n\n---\n\nYour intractable nature can help you shrug off even the most grievous injuries. Attempt a DC 17 flat check. If you are successful, the attack becomes a normal hit."],["You have a deep reverence for and connection to stone. You can cast One with Stone as a 3rd-rank divine innate spell once per day.\n\nIf you have the Stonemason's Eye feat, you can attempt to find unusual stonework and stonework traps that require legendary proficiency in Perception. If you have both Stonemason's Eye and legendary proficiency in Perception, when the GM rolls a secret check for you to notice unusual stonework, you keep your bonus from Stonemason's Eye."],["You have accumulated a vast array of lived knowledge over the years. During your daily preparations, you can reflect upon your life experiences to gain the trained proficiency rank in one skill of your choice. This proficiency lasts until you prepare again. Since this proficiency is temporary, you can't use it as a prerequisite for a skill increase or a permanent character option like a feat."],["You've studied traditional elven arts, learning about arcane magic and the world around you. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Arcana and Nature. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Elf Lore."],["You favor bows and other elegant weapons. You gain access to all uncommon weapons with the elf trait. You have familiarity with weapons with the elf trait plus Longbows, Composite Longbows, Rapiers, Shortbows, and Composite Shortbows—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["Watching your friends age and die fills you with moroseness that protects you against harmful emotions. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against emotion effects. If you roll a success on a saving throw against an emotion effect, you get a critical success instead."],["Your muscles are tightly honed. Your Speed increases by 5 feet."],["Your elven magic manifests as a simple arcane spell, even if you aren't formally trained in magic. Choose one cantrip from the arcane spell list. You can cast this cantrip as an arcane innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["Your mystic control and meditations allow you to resist external influences upon your consciousness. Whenever you are affected by a mental effect that lasts at least 2 rounds, you can reduce the duration by 1 round.\n\nYou still require natural sleep, but you treat your saving throws against effects that would cause you to fall asleep as one degree of success better. This protects only against sleep effects, not against other forms of falling Unconscious."],["**Frequency** once every 10 minutes\n\n**Requirements** You are within 30 feet of an ally with the Dying condition.\n\n---\n\nThough you know that you will eventually outlive your companions, seeing them at death's door brings clarity to your attacks. Make a Strike. Roll twice on the attack roll and use the higher result."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou've perfected your ability to keep up with all the skills you've learned over your long life, so you're almost never truly untrained at a skill. You reflect on your life experiences, changing the skill you selected with Ancestral Longevity (and the skill you selected with Expert Longevity if you have that feat)."],["Your people used powerful magic to travel between distant worlds in the distant past, and the remnants of that magic make such transportation easier for you. When you are the target of a teleportation spell that transports more than one person, it can affect an additional person beyond the normal limit, chosen by the caster. Additionally, when you're the target of a Teleport spell, you and the other targets arrive no farther than 1 mile off target, regardless of distance traveled."],["You work at a pace born from longevity that enhances your thoroughness. You can voluntarily spend twice as much time as normal on a Perception check or skill check that takes 1 action or longer. If you do, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the check and don't automatically reduce your degree of success on a natural 1 (you get a critical failure only if your result is 10 lower than the DC). For example, you could get these benefits if you spent 2 actions to Seek, which normally takes 1 action. You can get these benefits during exploration by taking twice as long exploring as normal, or in downtime by spending twice as much downtime.\n\nThe GM might determine a situation doesn't grant you a benefit if a delay would be directly counterproductive to your success, such as a tense negotiation with an impatient creature."],["Long-lived elves have seen civilizations rise and fall, often at the hands of outside forces. As a result, they have developed a wariness of others who might seek to influence or control them. You've been trained to resist such manipulation, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to saving throws against effects that would make you Controlled, such as Dominate, and to Perception checks to Sense Motive when trying to determine if a creature is under the influence of such an effect. When you roll a success on a saving throw against such an effect, you get a critical success instead."],["You've crossed blades with a wide variety of foes wielding a wide variety of weapons, and you've learned the basics of fighting with nearly any of them. When wielding a weapon you aren't proficient with, treat your level as your proficiency bonus.\n\nAt 11th level, you become trained in all weapons."],["You move in a graceful dance, and even your steps are broad. You Step 5 feet twice."],["You've continued to refine the knowledge and skills you've gained through your life. When you choose a skill in which to become trained with Ancestral Longevity, you can also choose a skill in which you are already trained and become an expert in that skill. This lasts until your Ancestral Longevity expires.\n\nWhen the effects of Ancestral Longevity and Expert Longevity expire, you can retrain one of your skill increases. The skill increase you gain from this retraining must either make you trained in the skill you chose with Ancestral Longevity or make you an expert in the skill you chose with Expert Longevity."],["The arcane magic you possess grows in power and complexity. Choose one common 2nd-rank spell from the same tradition as an innate spell you previously gained from another elf ancestry feat (from the arcane list if you have Otherworldly Magic, for example). You can cast that spell as an innate spell once per day, using the same tradition as the list you chose the spell from.\n\nYour magic is adaptable. By spending 1 day of downtime, you can change the spell you chose to a different common 2nd-rank spell from the same tradition."],["You've spent much of your life among the treetops and have become an expert at quickly and safely climbing them. You gain a Climb Speed of 10 feet."],["You build a rapport with an animal, which becomes magically bonded to you. You gain a familiar. The type of animal is up to you, but most gnomes choose animals with a burrow Speed."],["You hear animal sounds as conversations instead of unintelligent noise, and you can respond in turn. You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals. In most cases, wild animals will give you time to make your case. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Make an Impression on animals."],["Your enhanced fey connection (either through your blood or via prolonged contact with their kind) affords you a warmer reception from creatures of the First World as well as tools to foil their tricks or withstand their magic. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to both Perception checks and saving throws against fey.\n\nIn addition, whenever you meet a fey creature in a social situation, you can immediately attempt a Diplomacy check to Make an Impression on that creature rather than needing to converse for 1 minute. You take a –5 penalty to the check. If you fail, you can engage in 1 minute of conversation and attempt a new check at the end of that time rather than accepting the failure or critical failure result."],["Your connection to the First World grants you a primal innate spell, much like those of the fey. Choose one cantrip from the primal spell list. You can cast this spell as a primal innate spell at will. A cantrip is heightened to a spell rank equal to half your level rounded up."],["You might have a flighty nature, but when a topic captures your attention, you dive into it headfirst. You gain the Additional Lore feat and the Assurance feat for the chosen Lore. As gnome obsessions can come and go quickly, you can retrain Gnome Obsession to a different Lore subcategory in 1 day of downtime."],["You favor unusual weapons tied to your people, such as blades with curved and peculiar shapes. You gain access to kukris and all uncommon weapons with the gnome trait. You have familiarity with weapons with the gnome trait plus the glaive and kukri—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["Your ancestors spent their days cloaked and cradled in illusions, and as a result, sensing illusion magic is second nature to you. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to both Perception checks and Will saves against illusions.\n\nWhen you come within 10 feet of an illusion that can be disbelieved, the GM rolls a secret check for you to disbelieve it, even if you didn't spend an action to Interact with the illusion."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You blind or dazzle a creature.\n\n---\n\nYou've spent considerable time practicing the manipulation of light, weaponizing your blade's reflection or bolstering the luminosity of magical displays to unconventional heights. Extend the duration of the Blinded or Dazzled condition you give the target by 1 round."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You are attacked by a foe, but they haven't rolled yet.\n\n---\n\nThe magic within you manifests as a natural reaction to threats. An illusory double of you appears in your space for a brief moment. The triggering attacker must roll a DC 10 flat check; on a success, the attack targets you normally; if they fail, the attack targets the double and destroys it. The tradition of this action matches the tradition of your gnome ancestry options."],["**Frequency** twice per week\n\n---\n\nThe connection between you and the First World resonates within your body stronger than it does for most gnomes, allowing you to cross the threshold between the Universe and the First World. You gain Interplanar Teleport as a primal innate spell. You can cast it twice per week. This can be used only to travel back and forth between the First World and the Universe. Due to your body's natural resonance, you can act as a locus for the spell, and you don't require a specially attuned planar key."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou can focus your mind more quickly thanks to the magic that flows within you. You regain 1 Focus Point, up to your usual maximum."],["Where others etch their armor to serve as a conduit for their imaginations, your vivid mind and bold personality allow you to project a more fitting persona over your lackluster armor. You change the shape and appearance of your armor to appear as ordinary or fine clothes of your imagining. The armor's statistics don't change. This effect lasts as long as you remain conscious and are wearing the armor. A creature can disbelieve the illusion by Seeking or touching your armor. The DC equals your Will DC."],["Over time your fey magic has grown stronger. You gain Invisibility and Revealing Light as 2nd-rank primal innate spells. You can cast each of these primal innate spells once per day."],["**Requirements** You must be adjacent to a living creature.\n\n---\n\nYou phase through a space that a living creature occupies in a flash, spontaneously appearing on the opposite side of it in a vibrant display of colorful light. You move from your current location to another location that's still adjacent to the same living creature, but on the opposite side or corner of the creature's space. To determine whether a position is valid, use the same rules as for flanking: a line through the center of the two spaces must pass through opposite sides or corners of the creature's space.\n\nYou pass through the creature's life force, appearing in the selected location; this doesn't trigger reactions based on movement. You must be able to see your destination, and you can't move farther than your Speed would allow."],["Your connection to the First World has grown, and its vital energy flows into you rapidly. If you rest for 10 minutes, you regain Hit Points equal to your Constitution modifier × half your level. This is a healing vitality effect and is cumulative with any healing you receive from Treat Wounds."],["Fire fascinates you. Your spells and alchemical items that deal fire damage gain a status bonus to damage equal to half the spell's rank or one-quarter the item's level (minimum bonus +1). You also gain a +1 status bonus to any persistent fire damage you deal."],["You know that the greatest treasures often look like refuse. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to checks to Subsist, and you can use Society or Survival when you Subsist in a settlement.\n\nWhen you Subsist in a city, you also gather valuable junk that silly longshanks threw away. You can Earn Income using Society or Survival at the same time while you Subsist, without spending any additional days of downtime. You also gain a +1 circumstance bonus to this check.\n\n---\n\n**Special** If you have the irongut goblin heritage, increase the bonuses to +2."],["You've picked up skills and tales from your goblin community. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Nature and Stealth. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Goblin Lore."],["**Trigger** An ally ends a move action adjacent to you.\n\n---\n\nYou take advantage of your ally's movement to adjust your position. You Step."],["You sing annoying goblin songs, distracting your foes with silly and repetitive lyrics. Attempt a Performance check against the Will DC of a single enemy within 30 feet. This has all the usual traits and restrictions of a Performance check to sing.\n\nYou can affect up to two targets within range if you have expert proficiency in Performance, four if you have master proficiency, and eight if you have legendary proficiency.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target takes a –1 status penalty to Perception checks and Will saves for 1 minute.\n\nGoblin Song (Critical Success)\n\n**Success** The target takes a –1 status penalty to Perception checks and Will saves for 1 round.\n\nGoblin Song (Success)\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is temporarily immune to Goblin Song for 1 hour."],["Others might look upon them with disdain, but you know that the weapons of your people are as effective as they are sharp. You gain access to all uncommon weapons with the goblin trait. You have familiarity with weapons with the goblin trait—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["You can make useful tools out of even twisted or rusted scraps. When using the Crafting skill to Craft, you can make level 0 items, including weapons and armor, out of junk. This reduces the Price to one-quarter the usual amount but always results in a shoddy item. Shoddy items normally give a penalty, but you don't take this penalty when using shoddy items you made (nor does the worse check penalty of shoddy armor you made apply to you).\n\nYou can also incorporate junk to save money while you Craft any item. This grants you a discount on the item as if you had spent 1 additional day working to reduce the cost, but the item is obviously made of junk. At the GM's discretion, this might affect the item's resale value depending on the buyer's tastes."],["You are especially good at riding traditional goblin mounts. You gain the Ride feat, even if you don't meet the prerequisites. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Nature checks to use Command an Animal on a goblin dog or wolf mount.\n\nIf you gain a wolf as an animal companion, it gains the mount special ability (and if you gain an ability that grants you an animal companion with the mount special ability, you can choose a wolf)."],["Taller folk rarely pay attention to the shadows at their feet, and you take full advantage of this. You can move 5 feet farther when you take the Sneak action, up to your Speed.\n\nIn addition, as long as you continue to use Sneak actions and succeed at your Stealth check, you don't become observed if you don't have cover or greater cover and aren't Concealed at the end of the Sneak action, as long as you have cover or greater cover or are concealed at the end of your turn."],["You can move up to your Speed when you use the Sneak action, and you no longer need to have cover or greater cover or be Concealed to Hide or Sneak."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nDespite a lifetime filled with questionable decisions, you've managed to survive, as though you have uncanny luck that lets you avoid the consequences of your own actions. For the remainder of your turn, if you roll a failure or critical failure on a saving throw against a harmful effect, you get a success instead. Further, if you would take damage from an enemy or hazard this turn you take the minimum possible damage.\n\nThese benefits apply only to harmful effects incurred entirely during your turn in which you activate Reckless Abandon, such as running through a Wall of Fire. Persistent damage and conditions that were applied prior to your turn proceed normally, and as soon as your turn ends you are subject to the full consequences of any dangers still threatening you."],["You deliver a punishing blow to an enemy's knee, shin, or other vulnerable anatomy within your reach. Make a melee Strike with a melee weapon or melee unarmed attack. This attack doesn't deal damage. On a hit, the target takes a –10-foot status penalty to its Speed (or a –15-foot status penalty on a critical hit). The penalty lasts for 1 round. This penalty applies only if the target has a land Speed and depends on legs or other targetable appendages to use its land Speed. As with all penalties to Speed, this can't reduce a creature's Speed below 5 feet.\n\nKneecap"],["Staying on pitch, proper breath control, and remembering the words are all less important than the real measure of a good singer: volume! The range of your Goblin Song is increased to 60 feet, and you can target one additional enemy when you use it."],["You have a knack for breaking and dismantling things. Putting them back together is the boring part, so you largely don't bother with that. You become trained in Thievery. If you would automatically become trained in Thievery (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nIn addition, whenever you hit with a Strike against a trap or an unattended object, you ignore the first 5 points of the object's Hardness."],["After years of clambering through caverns, you can climb easily anywhere you go. You gain a climb Speed of 10 feet."],["**Requirements** Your last action was a successful Strike and you have a free hand.\n\n---\n\nYou hang onto a foe to harry them into submission. If your target moves while you're hanging onto it, you can choose to move with the target. The target is released if you choose not to move with it, at the start of your next turn, or if the target Escapes. Attempts to Escape from a Cling are made against your Acrobatics DC, but they end the Cling instead of the conditions normally ended by the Escape action.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can use this action without a free hand if your preceding Strike was made with your jaws or a similar unarmed attack you could use to hang on. The GM determines which unarmed attacks apply. Hanging on in this way prevents you from using that unarmed attack."],["You can scuttle farther and faster when maneuvering alongside allies. When you use Goblin Scuttle, you can Stride up to half your Speed instead of Stepping."],["You have learned to remain hidden by using larger folk as a distraction to avoid drawing attention to yourself. You can use creatures that are at least one size larger than you (usually Medium or larger) as cover for the Hide and Sneak actions, though you still can't use such creatures as cover for other uses, such as the Take Cover action."],["You are adept at disguising coded messages as folksy idioms. Using slang, jokes, halfling loanwords, and the like, you convey a simple message consisting of three basic words (such as \"Danger assassin flee\" or \"Meet me moonrise\"). Your intended listener can attempt a DC 20 Perception check to discern the message. This DC is reduced by 5 if the listener is a halfling or has Folksy Patter, or by 10 if both apply (DC 15 Perception DC 10 Perception). Eavesdroppers can also attempt a Perception check against your Deception DC to discern your meaning. Any bonuses or penalties to Perception checks to Sense Motive apply to checks to understand Folksy Patter."],["You've dutifully learned how to keep your balance and how to stick to the shadows where it's safe, important skills passed down through generations of halfling tradition. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Acrobatics and Stealth. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Halfling Lore."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You fail a skill check or saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYour happy-go-lucky nature makes it seem like misfortune avoids you, and to an extent, that might even be true. You can reroll the triggering check, but you must use the new result, even if it's worse."],["You favor traditional halfling weapons, so you've learned how to use them more effectively. You gain access to all uncommon weapons with the halfling trait. You have familiarity with weapons with the halfling trait plus the sling and shortsword—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["You grew up riding your clan's shaggy ponies and riding dogs. You become trained in Nature. If you would automatically become trained in Nature (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice. You also get a +1 circumstance bonus to Command an Animal if the target is a traditional halfling mount, such as a pony or riding dog."],["Whether keeping your balance or climbing, your feet easily find purchase. If you roll a success on an Acrobatics check to Balance or an Athletics check to Climb, you get a critical success instead. You're not Off-Guard when you attempt to Balance or Climb."],["You have learned how to use your sling to fell enormous creatures. When you hit on an attack with a weapon of the sling group against a Large or larger creature, increase the size of the weapon damage die by one step."],["You were either pressed into indentured servitude or shackled in a prison, but you've since escaped and have trained to ensure you'll never be caught again. Whenever you roll a success on a check to Escape or a saving throw against an effect that would impose the Grabbed, Immobilized, or Restrained condition on you, you get a critical success instead. Whenever a creature rolls a failure on a check to Grapple you, it gets a critical failure instead."],["You pay close attention to the people around you, allowing you to more easily notice when they act out of character. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks when using the Sense Motive basic action to notice enchanted or possessed characters. If you aren't actively using Sense Motive on an enchanted or possessed character, the GM rolls a secret check, without your usual circumstance bonus, for you to potentially notice the enchantment or possession anyway.\n\nIn addition to using it for skill checks, you can use the Aid basic action to grant a bonus to another creature's saving throw or other check to overcome enchantment or possession. As usual for Aid, you need to prepare by using an action on your turn to encourage the creature to fight against the effect."],["You excel at going unnoticed, especially among a crowd. You no longer need to have cover or be Concealed to Hide or Sneak. If you would have lesser cover from a creature, you gain standard cover instead and can Take Cover; if you would have standard cover from a creature, you gain greater cover instead."],["While sharing a creature's space using Dance Underfoot, your melee weapons and unarmed attacks gain the trip trait, but only against the creature whose space you share. You can be in the same space as a Large or larger Prone creature, even if it's not your ally."],["**Frequency** once per hour\n\n**Trigger** You successfully use Stealth to Hide and become Hidden from all your current foes, or use Stealth to Sneak and become undetected to all your current foes.\n\n---\n\nYou slip from your adversaries' notice and appear to be somewhere else. You become Invisible for 1 minute or until you take a hostile action, whichever comes first. Choose a location within 10 feet of you. Until your invisibility ends, you appear to be hidden in that location to anyone trying to find you. If the searcher gets clear evidence that you're not there, they no longer think you're hidden there, but they don't discover your actual location."],["During your adventures, you've honed your ability to adapt to the culture of the predominant ancestry around you. You gain the Adopted Ancestry general feat, and you also gain one 1st-level ancestry feat from the ancestry you chose for the Adopted Ancestry feat."],["**Trigger** A Large or larger enemy ends a move action adjacent to you.\n\n---\n\nYou are an expert at avoiding the lumbering footsteps of larger creatures. You Step to another space adjacent to the enemy."],["You dart under the legs of your enemies in combat. You can end a successful Tumble Through action in a Large or larger enemy's space. Also, when using the Step Lively feat, you can Step into the triggering enemy's space. The enemy must have limbs or otherwise leave you enough room for this maneuver, as determined by the GM. For instance, you could share space with a giant or dragon, but not an ooze."],["Your luck guides you to look the right way and aim your blows unerringly. You can use Halfling Luck twice per day: once in response to its normal trigger, and once when you fail a Perception check or attack roll instead of the normal trigger."],["You are easily able to ward off attempts to play on your fears and emotions. When you roll a success on a saving throw against an emotion effect, you get a critical success instead. If your heritage is gutsy halfling, when you roll a critical failure on a saving throw against an emotion effect, you get a failure instead."],["You won't allow others to restrain you. You can cast Unfettered Movement on yourself as a primal innate spell once per day."],["Through study of multiple magical traditions, you've altered a spell to suit your spellcasting style. Choose one cantrip from a magical tradition other than your own. If you prepare spells, you can choose this spell when you prepare your cantrips, in addition to your other options. If you have a spell repertoire, replace one of your cantrips known with the chosen spell. You can cast this cantrip as a spell of your class's tradition.\n\nIf you swap or retrain this cantrip later, you can choose its replacement from the same alternate tradition or a different one."],["The short human life span lends perspective and has taught you from a young age to set aside differences and work with others to achieve greatness. You gain a +4 circumstance bonus on checks to Aid."],["Your adaptability manifests in your mastery of a range of useful abilities. You gain a 1st-level general feat. You must meet the feat's prerequisites, but if you select this feat during character creation, you can select the feat later in the process in order to determine which prerequisites you meet.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times, choosing a different feat each time."],["Your powerful ego makes it harder for others to order you around. If you roll a success on a saving throw against a mental effect that attempts to directly control your actions, you critically succeed instead. If a creature rolls a failure on a check to Coerce you using Intimidation, it gets a critical failure instead (so it can't try to Coerce you again for 1 week)."],["You were raised to be ambitious and always reach for the stars, leading you to progress quickly in your chosen field. You gain a 1st-level class feat for your class. You must meet the prerequisites, but you can select the feat later in the character creation process in order to determine which prerequisites you meet."],["Your ingenuity allows you to learn a wide variety of skills. You gain the trained proficiency rank in two skills of your choice."],["Over the long course of your adventuring life, your adaptability has let you pick up numerous useful abilities. You gain a general feat of 7th level or lower. You must meet the feat's prerequisites.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times, choosing a different feat each time."],["Humans are renowned for their ability to persist through the most grueling of trials that would leave others ready to drop. When you would become Fatigued, attempt a DC 17 flat check. On a success, you aren't fatigued. If the fatigued condition has an underlying cause that you don't address, such as lack of rest, you must attempt the check again at an interval determined by the GM until you fail the flat check or address the underlying cause."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nThe blood of heroes courses through your veins, and you inspire your allies to dig deep and find a new level of resolve. You grant up to 10 willing creatures within 30 feet the effects of a 6th-rank Zealous Conviction, though the effect automatically ends on a target if you give that target a command they would normally find repugnant. This action has the auditory trait or visual trait, depending on how you inspire your allies."],["You've continued adapting your magic to blend your class's tradition with your adapted tradition. Choose a cantrip or 1st-rank spell from the same magical tradition as your cantrip from Adapted Cantrip. You gain that spell, adding it to your spell options just like the cantrip from Adapted Cantrip. You can cast this spell as a spell of your class's magical tradition. If you choose a 1st-rank spell, you don't gain access to the heightened versions of that spell, meaning you can't prepare them if you prepare spells and you can't learn them or select the spell as a signature spell if you have a spell repertoire."],["You've learned how to handle situations when you're out of your depth. You gain the Untrained Improvisation general feat. In addition, you can attempt skill actions that normally require you to be trained, even if you are untrained."],["Like many humans raised in a close-knit community, you have always been strongly attuned to the presence of others. Willing allies that you are aware of within 60 feet that would otherwise be Undetected by you are instead Hidden from you. The flat check for you to target willing allies within 60 feet that are hidden from you is DC 5 flat check instead of 11."],["You have developed a soul-deep bond with your comrades and maintain an even greater degree of cooperation with them. If you are at least an expert in the skill you are Aiding, when you roll a failure or critical failure to Aid a skill check, you get a success instead."],["Your upbringing emphasized teamwork, and helping your allies comes naturally to you. After you Aid an ally at a skill check that doesn't have the attack trait, you can also Aid any other ally who attempts the same skill check for the same purpose that round. You do so as a free action rather than a reaction.\n\nThe preparation you did to help must still apply to the other allies, and you can Aid each ally only once. For example, if you helped lift up an ally to Aid them on an Athletics check to scale a wall, you could keep the same posture to give a boost to other allies attempting to scale the wall in the same round."],["There's no journey too far or burden too heavy when you have friends at your side or hope within your heart. Increase your maximum and encumbered Bulk limits by 1. In addition, you gain a +10-foot circumstance bonus to your Speed during overland travel."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You attempt a check using a skill you're untrained in.\n\n---\n\nA stroke of brilliance gives you a major advantage with a skill despite your inexperience. Gain a +4 circumstance bonus to the triggering skill check."],["You can extend a tangle of vines or tendrils to support your arms and extend your reach. When you wield a melee weapon that requires two hands, doesn't have reach, and deals at least 1d6 damage, you can change between a typical two-handed grip and an extended two-handed grasp using an Interact action. Weapons wielded in your extended grasp gain reach of 10 feet. This grasp is less stable and powerful than a typical grip, reducing the weapon's damage die by 1 step."],["Your size and demeanor make it easy for you to convince others that you mean no harm. You gain the Shameless Request skill feat. Additionally, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to initiative checks when you roll Deception for initiative."],["You deeply understand your people's cultural traditions and innate strengths. You gain the trained proficiency rank in Nature and Stealth. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Leshy Lore."],["**Trigger** You attempt a saving throw against a spell or magical effect, but haven't rolled yet.\n\n---\n\nYou notice spirits that inhabit objects, learning which bring good fortune and which are unlucky. You focus on the power of a lucky object, granting you a +1 circumstance bonus to your saving throw against the triggering effect."],["Your body produces a nearly endless supply of hard seedpods. You gain a seedpod ranged unarmed attack with a range increment of 30 feet that deals 1d4 bludgeoning damage. On a critical hit, a seedpod bursts, issuing forth a tangle of vegetation that imposes a –10-foot circumstance penalty on the target's Speed until the start of your next turn. Seedpods do not add critical specialization effects.\n\nSeedpod"],["It's difficult to notice your passage through wild areas. As long as you're not in an urban environment, you're always considered to be Covering Tracks, even if you chose a different activity in exploration mode."],["Your spirit has endured many challenges over its long existence. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saves against emotion effects. If you roll a success on a saving throw against an emotion effect, you get a critical success instead."],["You can call forth nearby nature spirits to augment your body. Once per day, you can cast Plant Form as a 5th-rank primal innate spell. When you reach 17th level, you can heighten the spell to 6th rank when you cast it."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n---\n\nYou secrete a cloak of concentrated poison that harms any who dare attack you. For 1 minute, any creature that touches you or damages you with an unarmed attack or melee weapon without the reach trait takes 3d6 poison damage."],["You can call upon the vital essence of your spirit to restore life to your allies and call forth vines to ensnare and bludgeon your foes. You can cast Field of Life and Tangling Creepers as 6th-rank primal innate spells once per day each."],["Your command over your vital essence allows you or an ally to recover from grievous wounds. You can cast Regenerate as a 7th-rank primal innate spell once per day."],["Small roots sprout from your feet, steadying you as you move. You gain the Steady Balance skill feat, even if you aren't trained in Acrobatics, and you can use the Anchor action."],["Using your own leaves, you can control your descent. You glide slowly toward the ground, 5 feet down and up to 25 feet forward through the air. As long as you spend at least 1 action gliding each round and have not yet reached the ground, you remain in the air at the end of your turn."],["You can temporarily revert to a less conspicuous form without diminishing your senses. You take the form of an ordinary specimen of the type of plant or fungus that most closely resembles you, reverting to your body's appearance just before your spirit joined with it. This otherwise has the effects of One with Plants, except that your size remains Small."],["You have a connection with creatures that share your physiology. You can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with plants and fungi. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Diplomacy checks with plants or fungi of your kind. Generally, fungus leshies get this bonus with mushrooms and fungi; gourd leshies with gourds, melons, and similar fruiting plants; leaf leshies with deciduous trees; and vine leshies with vines and climbing plants."],["You wield primal magic. You can cast Entangling Flora and Oaken Resilience as 2nd-rank primal innate spells once per day each."],["You have a Keepsake that grants you luck. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saves against spells and magical effects at all times, not just when you use Leshy Superstition. If you lose the keepsake, you lose the bonus until you designate a new keepsake, typically over the course of a week."],["When your seedpods strike a felling blow, they burst into viciously thorny vines. When you critically succeed at a seedpod Strike, vines twist and stab your foe, dealing 1d4 persistent piercing damage."],["You have an impressive innate ability to tame and command ferocious beasts. You become trained in the Nature skill and gain your choice of the Pet general feat or the Train Animal skill feat."],["You bear scars or tattoos enhanced by the mark of your community's prowess. When you select this feat, choose one of the options from the below table. You are trained in the listed skill and gain a +1 status bonus to saves against spells from the listed tradition. You gain a large brand or tattoo in the shape of the chosen emblem or a similar concept (for example, the Burning Sun could be a torch, sun, volcano, or other fiery symbol, while the Empty Hand could be a fist or claw).\n\n| Hold Mark Emblem | Skill | Tradition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Burning Sun | Diplomacy | Arcane |\n| Death's Head | Survival | Primal |\n| Defiled Corpse | Religion | Divine |\n| Empty Hand | Intimidation | Occult |"],["Your fists have been forged by battle, your naturally tough skin and dense bone further hardened by conflict. Your fist unarmed attacks no longer have the nonlethal trait and gain the shove weapon trait."],["**Frequency** once per day\n\n**Trigger** You would be reduced to 0 Hit Points but not immediately killed.\n\n---\n\nFierceness in battle runs through your blood, and you refuse to fall from your injuries no matter how terrible they may be. You avoid being knocked out and remain at 1 Hit Point, and your Wounded condition increases by 1."],["The hold elders taught you your people's histories, told tales of great athletic feats, and shared with you the hardships your ancestors endured so that you can pass this wisdom down to future generations. You become trained in Athletics and Survival. If you would automatically become trained in one of those skills (from your background or class, for example), you instead become trained in a skill of your choice.\n\nYou also gain the Additional Lore general feat for Orc Lore."],["**Trigger** You attempt a saving throw against a spell or magical effect, and have not yet rolled.\n\n---\n\nYou defend yourself against magic by relying on techniques derived from orc cultural superstitions. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your saving throw against the triggering spell or magical effect."],["In combat, you favor the brutal weapons that are traditional for your orc ancestors. You gain access to all uncommon weapons with the orc trait. You have familiarity with weapons with the orc trait plus the falchion and greataxe—for the purposes of proficiency, you treat any of these that are martial weapons as simple weapons and any that are advanced weapons as martial weapons.\n\nAt 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with one of these weapons, you get its critical specialization effect."],["You have particularly long, jagged tusks perfect for tearing meat from bone. You gain a tusks unarmed attack that deals 1d6 piercing damage. Your tusks are in the brawling group and have the finesse and unarmed traits.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can take this feat only at 1st level, and you can't retrain into this feat. You can retrain out of this feat only through drastic measures, such as breaking, filing, or extracting your tusks."],["Since ancient times, the mightiest orc beast tamers would draw out the true fighting spirit of their companion beasts by feeding the creatures a draft incorporating the orc's own blood. All animal companions, pets, familiars, and bonded animals you have gain the Orc Ferocity feat, and gain one reaction per round they can use only for Orc Ferocity. If you have the Undying Ferocity ancestry feat, all animal companions, pets, familiars, and bonded animals you have also gain the benefits of that feat when using the Orc Ferocity reaction."],["You don't just resist magic; you devour it. Whenever you succeed at a saving throw against a spell or magical effect, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to double the spell's rank, or equal to the level if the magical effect isn't a spell. These temporary Hit Points last until the end of your next turn."],["**Trigger** You use Orc Ferocity.\n\n---\n\nYou lash out viciously even as you fend off death. Make a single melee Strike. If this Strike brings a foe to 0 Hit Points, this activation of Orc Ferocity doesn't count against its frequency."],["Surviving in hostile terrain has given you a great talent for mobility. Whenever you roll a success on an Athletics check to Climb or Swim, you get a critical success instead."],["Your lethal unarmed attacks leave bloody gouges or cause severe internal bleeding. When you critically hit with a Strike using an unarmed attack that isn't nonlethal, the target takes 1d4 persistent bleed damage. This can be because you're taking the penalty to use a fist for a lethal attack or because you have an unarmed attack without the nonlethal trait due to Tusks or a similar ability."],["You're exceptionally difficult to kill. The DC of your recovery checks is equal to 9 + your dying value, or 8 + your dying value if you have the Toughness general feat. In addition, whenever someone returns you to life using magic that would normally leave you debilitated for a week (such as Raise Dead or the resurrect ritual), you don't suffer that condition."],["Glorious, storied scars cover and protect much of your body, girding you in fleshly armor that resists any wound weaker than those you have already survived. Your DC on flat checks to end persistent bleed damage is reduced from 15 to 10, or from 10 to a DC 5 flat check after receiving especially appropriate assistance."],["You steep yourself in superstition and practice ancient orc mental exercises for shrugging off the effects of magic. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against spells and magical effects at all times."],["You resist death's clutches with supernatural vigor, daring death to claim you while promising that any such attempt will surely fail. When you use Orc Ferocity, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to your level.\n\nUndying Ferocity"],["You're fully immersed in another ancestry's culture and traditions, whether born into them, earned through rite of passage, or bonded through a deep friendship or romance. Choose a common ancestry or another ancestry to which you have access. You can select ancestry feats from the ancestry you chose, in addition to your character's own ancestry, as long as the ancestry feats don't require any physiological feature that you lack, as determined by the GM."],["You become trained in light armor. If you already were trained in light armor, you gain training in medium armor. If you were trained in both, you become trained in heavy armor. If you are at least 13th level, you become an expert in this armor type.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time, you become trained in the next type of armor, as detailed above."],["You can breathe even in hazardous or sparse air. You can hold your breath for 25 times as long as usual before suffocating. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against inhaled threats, such as inhaled poisons, and if you roll a success on such a saving throw, you get a critical success instead."],["Your avoidance or observation is beyond the ken of most in your profession. Choose Fortitude saves, Reflex saves, Will saves, or Perception. You become an expert in your choice. At 17th level, you become a master in your choice."],["It takes more to kill you than most. You die from the Dying condition at dying 5, rather than dying 4."],["Your body quickly bounces back from afflictions. You regain twice as many Hit Points from resting. Each time you succeed at a Fortitude save against an ongoing disease or poison, you reduce its stage by 2, or by 1 against a virulent disease or poison. Each critical success you achieve against an ongoing disease or poison reduces its stage by 3, or by 2 against a virulent disease or poison. In addition, you reduce the severity of your drained condition by 2 when you rest for a night instead of by 1."],["You step carefully and quickly. You can Step into difficult terrain."],["You move more quickly on foot. Your Speed increases by 5 feet."],["You react more quickly than others can. You gain a +2 circumstance bonus to initiative rolls."],["You have a pet—a Tiny animal of a type you choose, such as a cat, bird, or rodent. It has the minion trait, meaning it gains 2 actions during your turn if you use the Command an Animal action to command it; this replaces the usual effects of Command an Animal, and you don't need to attempt a Nature check. A pet can't take attack actions except to Escape or Force Open.\n\n**Level** Your pet's level is equal to yours.\n\n**Modifiers and AC** Your pet's save modifiers and AC are equal to yours before applying circumstance or status bonuses or penalties. It uses 3 + your level as its modifier for Perception, Acrobatics, and Stealth, and just your level as its modifier for other skill checks. It doesn't have or use its own attribute modifiers and can never benefit from item bonuses.\n\n**Hit Points** Your pet has 5 Hit Points per level.\n\n**Senses** Your pet has low-light vision and can gain additional senses from pet abilities.\n\n**Speed** Your pet has a Speed of 25 feet. You can choose to instead have an aquatic pet, which breathes in water instead of air and has the aquatic trait, no land Speed, and a swim Speed of 25 feet.\n\n**Pet Abilities** When you gain your pet, choose two of the following abilities. If your pet is an animal that naturally has one of these abilities (for instance, an owl has a fly Speed), you must select that ability. Your pet can't be an animal that naturally has more pet abilities than the maximum. In some cases, the GM might add some familiar abilities to the pet abilities you can choose.\n\n- **Amphibious** It gains the amphibious trait, allowing it to breathe in both air and water, and has both a land Speed and a swim Speed, each equal to its highest land Speed or swim Speed.\n- **Burrower** It gains a burrow Speed of 5 feet, allowing it to dig Tiny holes.\n- **Climber** It gains a climb Speed of 25 feet.\n- **Darkvision** It gains darkvision.\n- **Echolocation** Your pet can use hearing as a precise sense within 20 feet.\n- **Fast** Movement Increase one of the pet's Speeds from 25 feet to 40 feet.\n- **Flier** It gains a fly Speed of 25 feet.\n- **Manual Dexterity** It can use up to two of its limbs as if they were hands to perform manipulate actions.\n- **Scent** Your pet can use scent as an imprecise sense within 30 feet\n- **Tough** Your pet's max HP increase by 2 per level.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can gain a new pet by retraining this feat, releasing any previous pet you have. If you later gain a familiar or other companion that uses the Pet feat, you can immediately retrain this feat."],["When you Command an Animal you're mounted on to take a move action (such as Stride), you automatically succeed instead of needing to attempt a check. Any animal you're mounted on acts on your turn, like a minion. If you Mount an animal in the middle of an encounter, it skips its next turn and then acts on your next turn."],["**Trigger** While you have your shield raised, you would take physical damage (bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing) from an attack.\n\n---\n\nYou snap your shield in place to ward off a blow. Your shield prevents you from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. You and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield."],["Your body can withstand more punishment than most before succumbing. Increase your maximum Hit Points by your level. You reduce the DC of recovery checks by 1."],["You become trained in all martial weapons. If you were already trained in all martial weapons, you become trained in one advanced weapon of your choice. If you are at least 11th level, you also become an expert in these weapons.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time you do, you become trained in an advanced weapon."],["You have an incredible ability to invest more magic items. Increase your limit on invested items from 10 to 12."],["Whether through instinct, study, or magic, you feel a deeper connection to your ancestry. You gain a 1st-level ancestry feat."],["You've learned how to handle situations when you're out of your depth. Your proficiency bonus to untrained skill checks is equal to your level –2. This improves to your level –1 at 5th level and your full level at 7th level. This doesn't allow you to use the skill's trained actions."],["You have a system that lets you search at great speed, finding details and secrets twice as quickly as others can. When Searching, you take half as long as usual to Search a given area. This means that while exploring, you double the Speed you can move while ensuring you've Searched an area before walking into it (up to half your Speed). If you're legendary in Perception, you instead Search areas four times as quickly."],["You can predict which consumables you might need in advance. When using Prescient Planner, you can procure a consumable item from your backpack, instead of a piece of adventuring gear. The consumable item must still be common with a level no higher than half your level, and its Bulk must be low enough that carrying it wouldn't have made you encumbered."],["Your knowledge has expanded to encompass a new field. Choose a Lore skill subcategory. You become trained in it. At 3rd, 7th, and 15th levels, you gain an additional skill increase you can apply only to the chosen Lore subcategory.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat more than once. Each time you must select a new subcategory of Lore and you gain the additional skill increases to that subcategory for the listed levels."],["You can use the Craft activity to create alchemical items. When you select this feat, you immediately add the formulas for four common 1st-level alchemical items to your formula book."],["Even in the worst circumstances, you can perform basic tasks. Choose a skill you're trained in. You can forgo rolling a skill check for that skill to instead receive a result of 10 + your proficiency bonus (do not apply any other bonuses, penalties, or modifiers).\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times. Each time, choose a different skill and gain the benefits for that skill."],["Your catlike aerial acrobatics allow you to cushion your falls. Treat falls as 10 feet shorter. If you're an expert in Acrobatics, treat falls as 25 feet shorter and 50 feet if you're a master. If you're legendary in Acrobatics, you always land on your feet and don't take damage, regardless of the distance of the fall."],["Your charm allows you to win over those you lie to. When you get a critical success using the Lie action, the target's attitude toward you improves by one step, as though you'd succeeded at using Diplomacy to Make an Impression. This works only once per conversation, and if you critically succeed against multiple targets using the same result, you choose one creature's attitude to improve. You must be lying to impart seemingly important information, inflate your status, or ingratiate yourself, which trivial or irrelevant lies can't achieve."],["Your techniques allow you to fight as you climb. You're not Off-Guard while Climbing and can Climb with a hand occupied. You must still use another hand and both legs to Climb."],["You were raised among the nobility or have learned proper etiquette and bearing, allowing you to present yourself as a noble and play games of influence and politics. Unless you are intentionally presenting yourself differently, anyone who speaks with you will assume you are a noble or closely associated with the nobility (such as a prominent servant). You can use Society to Make an Impression on a noble, as well as with Impersonate to pretend to be a type of noble or a specific individual noble. If you use the normal skills in those situations, you receive a +1 circumstance bonus to the check instead."],["You're a treasure trove of information, but not all of it comes from reputable sources. When you fail (but don't critically fail) a Recall Knowledge check using any skill, you learn the correct answer and an erroneous answer, but you don't have any way to differentiate which is which. This can occur as knowing something is significant, but not whether it's good or bad."],["You carefully safeguard your professional endeavors to prevent disaster. When you use Lore to Earn Income, if you roll a critical failure, you instead get a failure. If you're an expert in Lore, you gain twice as much income from a failed check to Earn Income, unless it was originally a critical failure."],["You often smuggle things past the authorities. When the GM rolls your Stealth check to see if a passive observer notices a small item you've concealed, the GM uses the number rolled or 10—whichever is higher—as the result of your die roll, adding it to your Stealth modifier to determine your Stealth check result. If you're a master in Stealth, the GM uses the number rolled or 15, and if you're legendary in Stealth, you automatically succeed at hiding a small concealed item from passive observers. This provides no benefits when a creature attempts a Perception check while actively searching you for hidden items.\n\n---\n\n**PFS Note** This feat allows you to Earn Income with Underworld Lore with tasks of your level -1 (instead of the normal level -2)."],["Tracking is second nature to you, and when necessary you can follow a trail without pause. You can Track while moving at full Speed by taking a –5 penalty to your Survival check. If you're a master in Survival, you don't take the –5 penalty. If you're legendary in Survival, you no longer need to roll a new Survival check every hour when tracking, though you still need to roll whenever there are significant changes in the trail."],["When you Perform, compare your result to the Will DC of one observer. If you succeed, the target is Fascinated by you for 1 round. If the observer is in a situation that demands immediate attention, such as combat, you must critically succeed to fascinate it and the Perform action gains the incapacitation trait. You must choose which creature you're trying to fascinate before you roll your check, and the target is then temporarily immune for 1 hour.\n\nIf you're an expert in Performance, you can fascinate up to four observers; if you're a master, you can fascinate up to 10 observers; and if you're legendary, you can fascinate any number of observers at the same time."],["While using Survival to Subsist, if you roll any result worse than a success, you get a success. On a success, you can provide subsistence living for yourself and four additional creatures, and on a critical success, you can take care of twice as many additional creatures. You can choose to support half the number of creatures with a comfortable living.\n\nIncrease the number of additional creatures you feed on a success to eight if you're an expert in Survival, 16 if you're a master, and 32 if you're legendary."],["You can strong-arm people effectively, even when you don't have them isolated. When you Coerce, you can compare your Intimidation check result to the Will DCs of up to five targets instead of one.\n\nIt's possible to get a different degree of success for each target. The number of targets you can Coerce in a single action increases to 10 if you're an expert, 25 if you're a master, and 50 if you're legendary."],["When you Make an Impression, you can compare your Diplomacy check result to the Will DCs of up to 10 targets you conversed with, with no penalty. The number of targets increases to 20 if you're an expert, 50 if you're a master, and 100 if you're legendary."],["You can carry more than your frame implies. Increase your maximum and encumbered Bulk limits by 2."],["You are skilled at learning information through conversation. The Gather Information exploration activity takes you half as long as normal (typically reducing the time to 1 hour). If you're a master in Diplomacy and roll a critical failure to Gather Information, you get a failure instead. There is still no guarantee that a rumor you learn with Gather Information is accurate."],["Your performances inspire admiration and win you fans. You can [[/act make-an-impression skill=performance]] using Performance instead of Diplomacy. If you spend at least 10 minutes performing in front of an audience, you can Make an Impression targeting up to 10 members of the audience who were there for the whole performance, without taking the normal penalty. The number of targets increases to 20 for a 1-hour performance and 50 for a 2-hour performance."],["You can Demoralize with a mere glare. When you do, Demoralize loses the auditory trait and gains the visual trait, and you don't take a penalty if the creature doesn't understand your language."],["When you critically succeed to Create a Diversion, you continue to remain Hidden after the end of your turn. This effect lasts for an amount of time that depends on the diversion and situation, as determined by the GM (minimum 1 additional round)."],["You can use Deception to weave traps to trip up anyone trying to deceive you. If you can engage in conversation with someone trying to Lie to you, use your Deception DC if it is higher than your Perception DC to determine whether they succeed. This doesn't apply if you don't have a back-and-forth dialogue, such as when someone attempts to Lie during a long speech."],["You easily pick up new languages. You learn two new languages, chosen from common languages, uncommon languages, and any others you have access to. You learn an additional language if you are or become a master in Society and again if you are or become legendary.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times. Each time, you learn additional languages."],["You can apply natural cures to heal your allies. You can use Nature instead of Medicine to [[/act treat-wounds]], including higher Nature proficiency letting you attempt more difficult checks. It doesn't replace Medicine for uses of the skill other than Treat Wounds or for feat prerequisites.\n\nIf you're in the wilderness, you might have easier access to fresh ingredients, allowing you to gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your check to Treat Wounds using Nature, subject to the GM's determination."],["You attempt to reduce panic. Attempt a Diplomacy check, comparing it to the Will DC of creatures in a 10-foot emanation around you who are Frightened. Each of them is temporarily immune for 1 hour.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** Reduce the creature's frightened value by 2.\n\n**Success** Reduce the creature's frightened value by 1."],["When you become aware of a magical effect or see a spell being cast, you can immediately determine if it twists minds (with the mental trait), fights against fortune (with the fortune or misfortune trait), or reveals secrets (with the detection, prediction, revelation, or scrying traits). At the GM's discretion, similar effects can also fall into these categories. When you [[/act identify-magic skill=occultism]] or [[/act recall-knowledge skill=occultism]] to learn more about these effects, you can always use Occultism without penalty and gain a +2 circumstance bonus."],["You can Steal or Palm an Object that's closely guarded, such as in a pocket, without taking the –5 penalty. You can't steal objects that would be extremely noticeable or time consuming to remove (like worn shoes or armor or actively wielded objects). If you're a master in Thievery, you can attempt to Steal from a creature in combat or otherwise on guard. When doing so, Stealing requires 2 actions instead of 1, and you take a –5 penalty."],["You can Identify Magic swiftly. You take only 1 minute when using Identify Magic to determine the properties of an item, ongoing effect, or location, rather than 10 minutes. If you're a master, it takes a 3-action activity, and if you're legendary, it takes 1 action."],["You can use High Jump and Long Jump as a single action instead of 2 actions. If you do, you don't perform the initial Stride (nor do you fail if you don't Stride 10 feet)."],["For you, the Repair activity loses the exploration trait and takes 1 minute instead of 10 minutes. If you're a master in Crafting, it takes 3 actions. If you're legendary, it takes 1 action."],["You Squeeze 5 feet per round (10 feet on a critical success). If you're legendary in Acrobatics, you Squeeze at full Speed."],["You can read lips of others nearby who you can clearly see. The language read must be one that you know. When you're at your leisure, you can do this automatically. In encounter mode or when attempting a more difficult feat of lipreading, you're Fascinated and Off-Guard during each round in which you focus on lip movements, and you must succeed at a Society check (DC determined by the GM) to successfully read someone's lips."],["**Trigger** A creature within line of sight casts a spell that you don't have prepared or in your spell repertoire, or a trap or similar object casts such a spell. You must be aware of the casting.\n\n---\n\nIf you are trained in the appropriate skill for the spell's tradition and it's a common spell of 2nd rank or lower, you automatically identify it (you still roll to attempt to get a critical success, but can't get a worse result than success). The highest rank of spell you automatically identify increases to 4 if you're an expert, 6 if you're a master, and 10 if you're legendary. The GM rolls a secret Arcana, Nature, Occultism, or Religion check, whichever corresponds to the tradition of the spell being cast. If you're not trained in the skill, you can't get a result better than failure.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** You correctly recognize the spell and gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your saving throw or your AC against it.\n\n**Success** You correctly recognize the spell.\n\n**Failure** You fail to recognize the spell.\n\n**Critical Failure** You misidentify the spell as another spell entirely, of the GM's choice."],["You notice the signs and symbols that members of mystery cults and other secret societies use to declare their affiliation to fellow members. You can use Occultism in place of Diplomacy to [[/act gather-information skill=occultism]]{Gather Information} about such groups and in place of Deception to [[/act impersonate skill=occultism]]{Impersonate} a member of these groups.\n\nIf you belong to a secret cult, lodge, sect, or similar organization, you automatically recognize members of your group unless they are specifically attempting to conceal their presence from you. They also recognize your standing unless you are specifically concealing it."],["You learn the sign languages associated with the languages you know, allowing you to sign and understand signs. Sign languages typically require both hands to convey more complex concepts, and they are visual rather than auditory.\n\nSign language is difficult to understand during combat due to the level of attention needed, unlike basic gestures like pointing at a foe to suggest a target. Sign language is hard to use in areas of low visibility, just like speech is difficult in a noisy environment."],["You become trained in the skill of your choice.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times, choosing a new skill to become trained in each time."],["You can keep your balance easily, even in adverse conditions. Whenever you roll a success using the Balance action, you get a critical success instead. You're not Off-Guard while attempting to Balance on narrow surfaces and uneven ground."],["You know about life on the streets and feel the pulse of your local settlement. You can use your Society modifier instead of your Diplomacy modifier to [[/act gather-information skill=society]]. In any settlement you frequent regularly, you can use the Recall Knowledge action with Society to know the same sorts of information that you could discover with Diplomacy to Gather Information. The DC is usually significantly higher, but you know the information without spending time gathering it. If you fail to recall the information, you can still subsequently attempt to Gather Information normally."],["You've researched many faiths enough to recognize notions about them that are unlikely to be true. If you roll a critical failure at a Religion check to Decipher Writing of a religious nature or to Recall Knowledge about the tenets of faiths, you get a failure instead. When attempting to Recall Knowledge about the tenets of your own faith, if you roll a failure, you get a success instead, and if you roll a success, you get a critical success instead."],["When you successfully Steal something, observers (creatures other than the creature you stole from) take a –2 circumstance penalty to their Perception DCs to detect your theft. Additionally, if you first Create a Diversion using Deception, taking a single Palm an Object or Steal action doesn't end your Undetected condition."],["Select one type of difficult terrain from the following list: rubble, snow, or underbrush. While Undetected by all non-allies in that type of terrain, you can Sneak without attempting a Stealth check as long as you move no more than 5 feet and do not pass within 10 feet of an enemy during your movement.\n\nDuring exploration, this also allows you to automatically approach within 15 feet of other creatures while Avoiding their Notice, as long as they aren't actively Searching or on guard.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times. Each time, choose a different type of terrain."],["You can attempt to Disarm, Grapple, Reposition, Shove, or Trip creatures up to two sizes larger than you, or up to three sizes larger than you if you're legendary in Athletics."],["You spend time teaching an animal to do a certain action. You can either select a basic action the animal already knows how to do (typically those listed in the Command an Animal action) or attempt to teach the animal a new basic action. The GM determines the DC of any check required and the amount of time the training takes (usually at least a week). It's usually impossible to teach an animal a trick that uses critical thinking. If you're expert, master, or legendary in Nature, you might be able to train more unusual creatures, at the GM's discretion.\n\n---\n\n**Success** The animal learns the action. If it was an action the animal already knew, you can Command the Animal to take that action without attempting a Nature check. If it was a new basic action, add that action to the actions the animal can take when Commanded, but you must still roll.\n\n**Failure** The animal doesn't learn the trick."],["You've learned to fight underwater. You are not Off-Guard while in water, and you don't take the usual penalties for using a bludgeoning or slashing melee weapon in water."],["Your unparalleled athletic skill allows you to jump impossible distances. Triple the distance you jump on a successful Long Jump (so you could jump 90 feet with an Athletics result of 30). When you successfully High Jump, use the distance jumped and distance limit for a Long Jump but don't triple the distance.\n\nYou can jump a distance greater than your Speed by spending additional actions when you Long Jump or High Jump. For each additional action spent, add your Speed to the distance limit."],["You can find ways to craft just about anything, despite restrictions. As long as you have the appropriate Crafting skill feat (such as Magical Crafting for magic items) and meet the item's level and proficiency requirements, you ignore just about any other requirement, such as being of a specific ancestry or providing spells. If a requirement adds to the item's cost, you must still pay it (including castings of spells that themselves have a cost). You can't ignore requirements of special items that have exclusive means of access and Crafting, such as artifacts. The GM decides whether you can ignore a requirement."],["You're so immersed in divine scripture that you find meaning and guidance for any situation in your texts. Spend 10 minutes Deciphering Writing on religious scriptures of your deity or philosophy while thinking about a particular problem or conundrum you face, and then attempt a Religion check (DC determined by the GM). If you succeed, you unearth a relevant passage, parable, or aphorism that can help you move forward or change your thinking to help solve your conundrum."],["Your skill with languages and codes is so great that you can decipher information with little more than a quick read through a text. You can Decipher Writing using Society while reading at normal speed. If you slow down and spend the full amount of time that's ordinarily required and roll a success, you get a critical success; if you critically succeed while spending the normal amount of time, you gain a nearly word-for-word understanding of the document."],["You're so skilled with languages you can create a pidgin instantly. You can always talk to any creature that has a language—even a language you don't know—by creating a new pidgin language that uses simplified terms and conveys basic concepts. To do so, you must first understand at least what medium of communication the creature uses (speech, sign language, and so on)."],["You've discovered medical breakthroughs or techniques that achieve miraculous results. Once per day for each target, you can spend 1 hour treating that target and attempt a Medicine check to remove a disease or the Blinded, Deafened, Doomed, or Drained condition. Use the DC of the disease or of the spell or effect that created the condition. If the effect's source is an artifact, above 20th level, or similarly powerful, increase the DC by 10."],["You can negotiate incredibly quickly in adverse situations. You attempt to Make an Impression and then Request your opponent cease their current activity and engage in negotiations. You take a –5 penalty to your Diplomacy check. Generally, the DC of this check is the creature's Will DC, although your GM may modify it based on the situation. Some creatures may be unable to stop regardless of their personal desires, and even those who agree to parley might ultimately find your arguments lacking and return to violence."],["You're always sneaking unless you choose to be seen, even when there's nowhere to hide. You can Hide and Sneak even without cover or being Concealed. When you employ an exploration tactic other than Avoiding Notice, you also gain the benefits of Avoiding Notice unless you choose not to."],["You can survive indefinitely without food or water and can endure severe, extreme, and incredible cold and heat without taking damage from doing so."],["Your ability to Steal defies belief. You can attempt to Steal something that is actively wielded or that would be extremely noticeable or time consuming to remove (like worn shoes or armor). You must do so slowly and carefully, spending at least 1 minute (and significantly longer for items that are normally time consuming to remove, like armor). Throughout this duration you must have some means of staying Hidden, such as the cover of darkness or a bustling crowd. Even if you succeed, if the item is extremely prominent—like a suit of full plate armor—onlookers will quickly notice it's gone after you steal it."],["You can frighten foes so much, they might die. Attempt an Intimidation check against the Will DC of a living creature within 30 feet of you that you sense or observe and who can sense or observe you. If the target can't hear you or doesn't understand the language you are speaking, you take a –4 circumstance penalty. The creature is temporarily immune for 1 minute.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target must attempt a Fortitude save against your Intimidation DC. On a critical failure, it dies. On any other result, it becomes Frightened 2 and is Fleeing for 1 round. The critical failure effect has the death trait.\n\n**Success** The target becomes frightened 2.\n\n**Failure** The target becomes Frightened 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is unaffected."],["You know basic facts off the top of your head. Choose a skill you're an expert in that has the Recall Knowledge action and for which you have the Assurance feat. You can use the Recall Knowledge action with that skill as a free action once per round. If you do, you must use Assurance on the skill check.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can select this feat multiple times, choosing a different skill each time. You can use Automatic Knowledge with any skills you have chosen, but you can still use Automatic Knowledge only once per round."],["You forge strong connections with animals. You can spend 7 days of downtime regularly interacting with a normal animal (not a companion or other special animal) that is friendly or helpful to you. After this duration, attempt a Nature check against the animal's Will DC. If successful, you bond with the animal. The animal is permanently bonded to you until you form a bond with a different animal or do something egregious to break your bond.\n\nA helpful animal is easier to direct. If your bonded animal is level –1, it gains the minion trait, allowing you to command it more efficiently. The maximum level of creature that can be your minion increases to 3 if you're a master in Nature and to 11 if you're legendary.\n\n---\n\n**Special** You can't have both a bonded animal and an animal companion (though you can have both a bonded animal and a pet or familiar)."],["You can have other PCs help you Craft an item, under your direction. A helper PC rolls a check with a skill in which they're trained. The skill must be Crafting or another skill relevant to the item, as determined by the GM. For example, a PC might use Religion to help you Craft an item with the divine trait or Warfare Lore to help you Craft a weapon. Your roll still determines whether you successfully create the item. Any helper's roll contributes toward reducing the cost of raw materials using the numbers from the Earn Income table; this uses the ally PC's proficiency rank in the skill and their level – 1 for their level. Helping PCs must accompany you throughout the Craft activity (preventing them from pursuing other downtime activities) or the benefit is lost. The GM might determine that only a certain number of PCs can help depending on the circumstances. Communal Crafting also allows you to take the role of a helper when someone else is crafting, provided they accept your help."],["You zealously monitor a patient's progress to administer treatment faster. When you Treat Wounds, your patient becomes immune for only 10 minutes instead of 1 hour. This applies only to your Treat Wounds activities, not any other the patient receives."],["First impressions are your strong suit. When you meet someone in a casual or social situation, you can immediately attempt a Diplomacy check to Make an Impression on that creature rather than needing to converse for 1 minute. If you fail, you can engage in 1 minute of conversation and attempt a new check at the end of that time rather than accepting the failure or critical failure result."],["In situations where you can physically menace the target when you Coerce or Demoralize, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Intimidation check and you ignore the penalty for not sharing a language. If your Strength modifier is +5 or higher and you are a master in Intimidation, this bonus increases to +2."],["When you successfully Coerce someone, the maximum time they comply increases to a week, still determined by the GM. If you're legendary, the maximum increases to a month."],["You can Craft magic items, though some have other requirements. When you select this feat, you gain formulas for four common magic items of 2nd level or lower."],["Learning spells comes easily to you. When you succeed at Learning a Spell, it takes 10 minutes regardless of the spell's rank. If you would succeed on the check, you critically succeed instead. If you fail, you can try again after a week or after you gain a level, whichever is first.\n\nYou can use downtime to learn and inscribe new spells. This works as if you were using Earn Income with the tradition's associated skill, but instead of gaining money, you choose a spell available to you to learn and gain a discount on learning it, learning it for free if your earned income equals or exceeds its cost."],["You can Crawl incredibly swiftly—up to half your Speed, rather than 5 feet. If you're a master in Acrobatics, you can Crawl at full Speed, and if you're legendary, you aren't Off-Guard while Prone."],["You can jump 5 feet up with a vertical Leap without making a High Jump. You also increase the horizontal distance when you Leap, including as part of a High Jump or Long Jump, by 5 feet."],["You can set up a disguise in one-tenth the usual time (generally 1 minute). If you're a master in Deception, you can create a full disguise and Impersonate as a 3-action activity. If you're legendary, it takes a single action."],["You're skilled at moving with a group. When you are Avoiding Notice and your allies Follow the Expert, you and those allies can roll a single Stealth check, using the lowest modifier, instead of rolling separately. This doesn't apply for initiative rolls."],["You easily pull yourself onto ledges. When you Grab an Edge, you can pull yourself onto that surface and stand. You can use Athletics instead of a Reflex save to Grab an Edge. If you Climb or Leap to within 5 feet beneath the top of an edge, you can pull yourself onto the surface and stand as part of that action."],["You learned folk medicine to help recover from diseases and poison, and using it diligently has made you especially resilient. When you Treat a Disease or a Poison, or someone else uses one of these actions on you, increase the circumstance bonus granted on a success to +4, and if the result of the patient's saving throw is a success, the patient gets a critical success."],["You never get information about your areas of expertise wrong. When you Recall Knowledge using any Lore subcategory in which you're trained, if you roll a critical failure, you get a failure instead. If you're a master in a Lore subcategory, on a critical success, you gain even more information or context than usual."],["Your medical training extends to less obvious conditions. When you succeed against a DC 20 check to Treat Wounds, you can also reduce the value of one Clumsy, Enfeebled, or Stupefied condition on the patient by 1. If you're able to treat more than one creature at once, choose only one to gain this benefit. A creature can benefit from Unusual Treatment only once per day. If the condition results from an affliction, the affliction isn't cured, though the condition is reduced as long as the affliction remains at that stage. If you are a master in Medicine, add the Drained condition to the list of conditions you can remove if you succeed at a DC 30 check. If you are legendary in Medicine, you reduce the chosen condition by 2 instead of by 1."],["You've studied in large medical wards, treating several patients at once and tending to all their needs. When you use Treat Disease or Treat Wounds, you can treat up to two targets. If you're a master in Medicine, you can treat up to four targets, and if you're legendary, you can treat up to eight targets."],["If you trigger a device or set off a trap while disarming it, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to your AC or saving throw against the device or trap. This applies only to attacks or effects triggered by your failed attempt, not to any later ones, such as additional attacks from a complex trap."],["You use your medical training to ameliorate sickness or assuage fears. When you use Medicine to Administer First Aid, instead of Stabilizing a character or Stopping Bleeding, you can reduce an ally's Frightened or Sickened condition by 2, or remove either of those conditions entirely on a critical success. You can remove only one condition at a time. The DC for the Medicine check is usually the DC of the effect that caused the condition."],["When you roll initiative, you can yell a mighty battle cry and [[/act demoralize]] an observed foe as a free action. If you're legendary in Intimidation, you can use a reaction to Demoralize your foe when you critically succeed at an attack roll."],["You can draw upon strange variations in your spellcasting, whether or not you can cast occult spells. The DCs to Recognize Spells you cast and Identify Magic you use increase by 5."],["You spend 8 hours praying or performing occult rites over the target, weakening a curse's power over them. Attempt to counteract the curse, using Occultism or Religion for your counteract check and half your level rounded up for the counteract rank. Break Curse only takes 10 minutes of prayer and rites if you are legendary in Occultism or Religion."],["You are adept at foiling creatures' special senses and cautious enough to safeguard against them at all times. Whenever you use the Avoid Notice, Hide, or Sneak actions, you are always considered to be taking precautions against special senses."],["You craft flawless creations with great efficiency. Whenever you roll a success at a Crafting check to make an item of the type you chose with Specialty Crafting, you get a critical success instead."],["You stand up. This movement doesn't trigger reactions."],["You can use the parts of monsters to aid in crafting. You can use the body of a monster to help Craft items, using Survival instead of Crafting for the Craft activity when you do so. If parts of the monster's body are valuable, you can expend them toward the item's raw material cost as well. (The GM makes the determination if the monster's entry doesn't list any valuable materials from its body.)\n\nIf you spend additional days working on the item, reduce the Price using the monster's level instead of your own. Certain items may require specific creatures in their Craft requirement."],["You can Subsist using Survival on different planes, even those without resources or natural phenomena you normally need. For instance, you can forage for food without penalty even if the plane lacks food that could normally sustain you. A success on your check to Subsist also prevents damage done by the plane to you and anyone else you support with Subsist. This applies only to damage dealt by the general conditions of the plane, not smaller hazards."],["When Climbing, you move 5 more feet on a success and 10 more feet on a critical success, up to your Speed. If you're legendary in Athletics, you gain a climb Speed equal to your Speed."],["You Recognize Spells swiftly. Once per round, you can Recognize a Spell using a skill in which you're a master as a free action."],["You Swim 5 feet farther on a success and 10 feet farther on a critical success, to a maximum of your Speed. If you're legendary in Athletics, you gain a swim Speed equal to your Speed."],["You can Pick a Lock using 1 action instead of 2."],["You elude and evade attempts to uncover your true nature or intentions. When a spell or magical effect tries to read your mind, detect whether you are lying, or reveal your identity, you can attempt a Deception check against the spell or effect's DC. If you succeed, the effect reveals nothing."],["You can move your full Speed when you Sneak. You can use Swift Sneak while Burrowing, Climbing, Flying, or Swimming instead of Striding if you have the corresponding movement type."],["When you critically succeed at the Demoralize action, if the target's level is lower than yours, the target is Fleeing for 1 round."],["You can use your momentum from a jump to propel yourself off a wall. If you're adjacent to a wall at the end of a jump (whether performing a High Jump, Long Jump, or Leap), you don't fall as long as your next action is another jump. Your previous jump gives you momentum, letting you use High Jump or Long Jump as a single action, but you don't get to Stride as part of the activity.\n\nYou can use Wall Jump only once in a turn, unless you're legendary in Athletics, in which case you can use it as many times as you can use consecutive jump actions in that turn."]], F = ["d"]; (P.feats || []).forEach(function (e, i) { F.forEach(function (k, j) { if (T[i] && T[i][j] != null) e[k] = T[i][j]; }); }); P.featsText = 1; })(typeof window !== "undefined" ? window : globalThis);
